7+vas11yev1work@users.noreply.github.com> 1791458137 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791458137 +0200\n\nchore: add CLAUDE.md and Claude Code rules (#2538)\n\n## Description\nAdds project guidance for Claude Code:\n- `CLAUDE.md` covers the common commands (dev, build, validation,\nsingle-test runs, codegen), the backend proxy setup and the high-level\narchitecture (layers, bootstrap, modules + extension registry, GraphQL\ncodegen, Module Federation facade, i18n).\n- `.claude/rules/*.md` holds path-scoped conventions that load\nautomatically for matching files: architecture, data/GraphQL, i18n,\nmarkup, security, styles, tests, ui-kit, Vue/TypeScript.\n\nNo app code changes.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\n<!-- Put link to your task in Jira here -->\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2538-9b9a-9b9a9d23.zip\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx3tZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAI7cQACfSJ3TWZyyw0eYhArWxFomX\nxPjXhpt00exVnM1GgZ6YByKGhMDSlNaxKaeAT+jTGXTHfFyTVqOXHFq5TU+uTq8W\nWGT1sctGdEp2yUiCpE8IQHfyQfH24bpmIyXTr9spUe519tgTRbINr1Z12UTJroEG\nBrCP8WCTSpnwpoZhrbuqcXZwMJov9eaioCwHMt7+WW/yL/m1gR1XPE1wzQwmS9vM\nTlxAvFecmrWPhgM+FPxfnfE8lbD0iV65EpqsJ2vJoAVQLYSSBft6jiOV/1elbbmq\n8IwUAxMRvoZVAb1IgHzD907qr6gWzzX4MRptCHPh1y8zOKazKeI73hpRTClK2Jro\nTnX/muZRDGBH8vgyfjwNugNRFUUtV+TeiqJtvpqN4zKzZpXKpZ7s3lDP/HPwWXSv\nQXXnx+EpnZj+0KwGT+8ypSlRuHuCEc3CRkjlGm0NoLCsc3+rUMsFpM9vZyFfyzvm\nJH/54LBO6vJtKoe4+5285OVLh8yYoFVd2hZPJ9L52XYqcLZ6FC9KlF9mXCBh61Qa\nkdKyTyWps1z9VoCeSIyYYCfJqta+XwjsIoxW5nTkmjGkJLPklp0cPwtl6UAejdMA\nUR6koMDKopOt2LMi+Vr4fERFPDnRM6PxghgxL3kZRIdyCIV6jiXtmZpLLlO+LOiS\ntixsUBLPWxYdKjEta2mR\n=TvbK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T11:15:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/666b3945eb5cafc6eb1c067068223627eacf0be3","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDY2NmIzOTQ1ZWI1Y2FmYzZlYjFjMDY3MDY4MjIzNjI3ZWFjZjBiZTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/225fb8bb5aebc718ff1a65c3e4f09cd3e474998d","sha":"225fb8bb5aebc718ff1a65c3e4f09cd3e474998d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/225fb8bb5aebc718ff1a65c3e4f09cd3e474998d"}],"sha":"666b3945eb5cafc6eb1c067068223627eacf0be3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/666b3945eb5cafc6eb1c067068223627eacf0be3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/231671742?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kutasinaelena/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kutasinaelena/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kutasinaelena/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kutasinaelena/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kutasinaelena","id":231671742,"login":"kutasinaelena","node_id":"U_kgDODc8Hvg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kutasinaelena/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kutasinaelena/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kutasinaelena/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kutasinaelena/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kutasinaelena/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kutasinaelena","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/225fb8bb5aebc718ff1a65c3e4f09cd3e474998d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T08:31:32Z","email":"kutasina.elena@gmail.com","name":"Elena Kutasina"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T08:31:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"VCST-6206: theme-ci: stop opening a vc-deploy-dev PR for every PR (#2549)\n\n## What\n\nIn `theme-ci.yml`, the `deploy-cloud` job no longer runs on\n`pull_request`. It still runs for `dev` (on push and\n`workflow_dispatch`). On `dev` it uses `forceCommit`, so it commits\nstraight to `vcst-dev` without opening a PR. That behaviour does not\nchange.\n\n## Why\n\nBefore this change, every vc-frontend PR made `create-deploy-pr` open a\n`vc-ci` PR in\n[vc-deploy-dev](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-deploy-dev/pulls):\n- `VCST-XXXX-vcst-qa-deployment` into `vcst-qa`, for PRs based on `dev`;\n- `-vcst-dev-deployment` into `vcst-dev`, for all other PRs.\n\nNobody merges these PRs. On 2026-10-07 there were 168 open `vc-ci` PRs,\nand they hide the deployment PRs that people open by hand.\n\nJira: [VCST-6206](https://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6206)\n\n## What does not change\n\n- The PR build and the upload of the PR artifact to the `vc3prerelease`\nblob still happen. So a PR theme can still be deployed to any\nenvironment by hand.\n- You can still start `deploy-cloud.yml` manually through\n`workflow_dispatch`.\n- `auto-tests` and the Jira deployment push in the `ci` job are not\ntouched.\n\nThe module half of the same problem (a PR into `vcptcore-qa` for every\nmodule release) is handled in\n[VirtoCommerce/.github#109](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/.github/pull/109).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n[VCST-6206]:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6206?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ\nArtifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.60.0-pr-2549-1493-1493345b.zip\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2d37818a74aeca1923d59d398e47df1db44a6fe2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/2d37818a74aeca1923d59d398e47df1db44a6fe2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/225fb8bb5aebc718ff1a65c3e4f09cd3e474998d","verification":{"payload":"tree 2d37818a74aeca1923d59d398e47df1db44a6fe2\nparent f1130c7f8e1a95f53f726aeeb51d5dba978cc788\nauthor Elena Kutasina <kutasina.elena@gmail.com> 1791448292 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791448292 +0500\n\nVCST-6206: theme-ci: stop opening a vc-deploy-dev PR for every PR (#2549)\n\n## What\n\nIn `theme-ci.yml`, the `deploy-cloud` job no longer runs on\n`pull_request`. It still runs for `dev` (on push and\n`workflow_dispatch`). On `dev` it uses `forceCommit`, so it commits\nstraight to `vcst-dev` without opening a PR. That behaviour does not\nchange.\n\n## Why\n\nBefore this change, every vc-frontend PR made `create-deploy-pr` open a\n`vc-ci` PR in\n[vc-deploy-dev](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-deploy-dev/pulls):\n- `VCST-XXXX-vcst-qa-deployment` into `vcst-qa`, for PRs based on `dev`;\n- `-vcst-dev-deployment` into `vcst-dev`, for all other PRs.\n\nNobody merges these PRs. On 2026-10-07 there were 168 open `vc-ci` PRs,\nand they hide the deployment PRs that people open by hand.\n\nJira: [VCST-6206](https://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6206)\n\n## What does not change\n\n- The PR build and the upload of the PR artifact to the `vc3prerelease`\nblob still happen. So a PR theme can still be deployed to any\nenvironment by hand.\n- You can still start `deploy-cloud.yml` manually through\n`workflow_dispatch`.\n- `auto-tests` and the Jira deployment push in the `ci` job are not\ntouched.\n\nThe module half of the same problem (a PR into `vcptcore-qa` for every\nmodule release) is handled in\n[VirtoCommerce/.github#109](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/.github/pull/109).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n[VCST-6206]:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6206?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ\nArtifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.60.0-pr-2549-1493-1493345b.zip\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx1TkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXR8QAJMm9EUKJ4k3ZB3OlFjnx09a\nOsQoIW/hXLjQiqtWvOYaCn/nvBX4ZcnWISm0SJCmDvj/tXjnVIr3Z5d8GtJ/CLp+\n/kDAebAgzx7zwqSW6X2NMd2womncMHpPuyjsMieiYZTTDk3eE8XupsWAnYw0qWf6\nGhaa/gEUFdpyxfaxWbUmDxKwsdhXXbMhJChODNH1WuyyC05EVKJNVu/1KqsSp282\n4mZYL18stKRYQOzuBldzCVQg4vf8sFdsPB/6JeOXwrbC4AgBjcuEEmk312VfSI7V\nJE5uPQlRb6l3tzJ6KFQsHnsr0bzQvzesScknLWJ9zcZm7yp3QeYoovGb28rLkU9U\nD/Kh5WNN1pV8yxu7OezsNY5UfD7ztloBrakwfHQ522kSsXUFsCJaCePrHcw0IJXB\nu9Q+GkDfwwQUatjPD6kw1nybmL/vNTXaDXtbA+XrlwRTTZeV/RhiISUSREa0ezrx\nkLp4UptQoN7e72Y+ecKGGawKgeW4nQQGpO1iR2RoapxLqRf8Jc6f40lUiG9XxNTE\nELPcd6lETQz3xW1G4t0nkV7gkowuSFeyD3TgBxafm0cA632lC3oQwYNL1ffkxWJU\nw2Bxrs4E7xVfAzz4R79gOpE30S3HOHy4J1dY+Hi3+Gk+zEeM/RtmhaAPrZlc+wge\nZ0ZwVCNCbsfpxnK0y9xb\n=ZuKO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T08:31:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/225fb8bb5aebc718ff1a65c3e4f09cd3e474998d","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDIyNWZiOGJiNWFlYmM3MThmZjFhNjVjM2U0ZjA5Y2QzZTQ3NDk5OGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/f1130c7f8e1a95f53f726aeeb51d5dba978cc788","sha":"f1130c7f8e1a95f53f726aeeb51d5dba978cc788","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/f1130c7f8e1a95f53f726aeeb51d5dba978cc788"}],"sha":"225fb8bb5aebc718ff1a65c3e4f09cd3e474998d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/225fb8bb5aebc718ff1a65c3e4f09cd3e474998d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16372194?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/goldenmaya","id":16372194,"login":"goldenmaya","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzcyMTk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/f1130c7f8e1a95f53f726aeeb51d5dba978cc788/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-08T07:45:42Z","email":"mayapavlovna@gmail.com","name":"Maiia Diachkovskaia"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T07:45:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(VCST-5990): explain an out-of-range quantity in cart and quotes (#2533)\n\n## Description\n\nWith `allowZero: false` the quantity field could be invalid while\nnothing tied it to the text explaining why, which fails WCAG 3.3.1.\nResidual of VCST-5912.\n\nIn the cart, Chrome already reported the field as invalid on `dev`, from\nthe native `rangeUnderflow`, but the DOM had no `aria-invalid`. The red\nalert under the line was on screen, but nothing connected it to the\nfield, so the field had no description. This PR adds the description and\nmakes `aria-invalid` explicit.\n\n### Cart: the server stays the source of truth\nThe cart passes `disable-validation` on purpose: the typed quantity is\nsent, and the server answers with line validation errors, which the cart\nrenders as `VcAlert`s under the line.\n\n- The quantity input gets `aria-describedby` pointing at the line''s\nerror container whenever the line has errors.\n- It gets `aria-invalid=\"true\"` only when one of those errors is about\nthe quantity (`QUANTITY_VALIDATION_ERROR_CODES` in `shared/cart/enums`).\nA price or availability error describes the field without marking it\ninvalid.\n- Works in both `product_quantity_control` modes.\n\nThe code list comes from x-cart 3.1034.0 `CartLineItemValidator`, branch\nby branch:\n\n| In the list | Left out, and why |\n|---|---|\n| `PRODUCT_MIN_QTY`, `PRODUCT_MAX_QTY`, `PRODUCT_MIN_MAX_QTY`,\n`PRODUCT_EXACT_QTY`, `PRODUCT_QTY_CHANGED`,\n`PRODUCT_MIN_QTY_NOT_AVAILABLE`, `PRODUCT_PACK_SIZE_LIMIT`,\n`LINE_ITEM_LIMIT` | `PRODUCT_FFC_QTY`, `CART_PRODUCT_UNAVAILABLE`: about\nthe product; no typed quantity fixes them |\n| | `PRODUCT_QTY_INSUFFICIENT`: raised on the `CartProduct`\n(`ItemQtyAdjustmentValidator`), so its `objectId` never matches a line |\n\n`PRODUCT_PACK_SIZE_LIMIT` matters most: the validator checks pack size\nfirst in an if/else chain, so it is the only error the line gets.\n\nThis deliberately differs from AC 1 (\"before the value is committed\").\nBlocking the commit on the client would change cart behaviour, and the\nproduct owner chose to keep the server as the source of truth.\n\n### Translations\n`PRODUCT_PACK_SIZE_LIMIT` and `LINE_ITEM_LIMIT` had no\n`validation_error` keys, so every locale showed the raw English server\ntext (`\" Order in packs of 2\"`, leading space included). Both are now\ntranslated in all 13 locales and use the server''s `packSize` / `limit`\nparameters.\n\nThe pack-size text matches `ui_kit.add_to_cart.errors.pack_size`, so the\nproduct page and the cart say the same thing. **Visible change outside\nthe cart:** the product-page pack-size message is reworded in fi, it, zh\nand ja.\n\n### Quotes\nA quote row without a tier quantity renders 0. In stepper mode it is now\nvalidated on mount (`:validate-on-mount=\"$cfg.product_quantity_control\n=== ''stepper''\"`), so it announces `aria-invalid` plus the\n`positive_number` message. Button mode is left alone: VcAddToCart would\nmark it invalid there with no message to describe it.\n\n### ui-kit / shared, additive only\n- `VcQuantityStepper` and `VcAddToCart` get a new optional `aria` prop,\nforwarded to their `VcInput` (the same idiom as `VcInput`,\n`VcDateInput`, `VcDatePicker`). The stepper''s own `role`, `aria-label`\nand `aria-valuemin/max/now` always win.\n- `QuantityControl` gets a new optional `aria` prop, forwarded in both\nmodes.\n- The early return in `QuantityControl`''s `onMounted` now applies only\nwhen `allowZero` is set. Missions, add-to-cart and the catalog card are\nunchanged. The guard stays because the max rule would reject an\nuntouched 0 on negative stock; a test pins this.\n\n### Verification\n- Live app, QA backend, stepper mode:\n- min 2 / max 5 product, typed 1: the field gets `aria-invalid=\"true\"`\nand the description \"You can order from 2 to 5 item(s)\" (on `dev` it had\nno description).\n- pack-size-2 product (min 10 / max 20), anonymous cart, typed 11:\n`aria-invalid=\"true\"`, described by \"Order in packs of 2\"; in de,\n\"Bestellen in Packungen von 2\". Typing 12 removes both attributes.\n- Tests:\n- `cart-line-items.test.ts`: a quantity error, `PRODUCT_PACK_SIZE_LIMIT`\nand `LINE_ITEM_LIMIT` as a line''s only error, a non-quantity error, an\nerror on another object, no errors.\n- `useErrorsTranslator.locales.test.ts`: both new messages rendered with\nserver parameters in all 13 locales.\n  - `quote-line-items.test.ts`: stepper and button mode.\n- `quantity-control.test.ts`: mount validation, negative stock,\npassthrough in both modes.\n  - `vc-quantity-stepper.test.ts`: passthrough, own semantics win.\n\nEvery new behaviour was mutation-tested: removing it turns a test red, 3\nruns each.\n- 1908 tests pass across `client-app/shared`, ui-kit organisms,\n`modules` and the new locale test. `yarn validate:types` and `yarn\ncheck-locales` are clean. eslint on the changed files reports one error,\n`quote-line-items.vue:108`, which is already on `dev`.\n- Storybook: new `DescribedByExternalMessage` story (`allowZero: false`,\nvalue below the floor, AC 6), and `aria` argTypes on VcQuantityStepper\nand VcAddToCart.\n\n**Not verified:**\n- `LINE_ITEM_LIMIT` in a browser (it needs a quantity above 999999).\n- An editable quote with a missing tier quantity in the live app\n(covered by `quote-line-items.test.ts`).\n- Storybook axe on the new story.\n- A native-speaker check of the fi, it, zh and ja wording.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5990\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2533-7f07-7f07141a.zip\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Low Risk**\n> Additive ARIA and i18n with targeted mount-validation guard changes;\ncart quantity commit behavior is unchanged and behavior is heavily\ncovered by new tests.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Improves **WCAG 3.3.1** for cart and quote quantity fields by wiring\nserver and client validation messages to the input via\n**`aria-describedby`** and explicit **`aria-invalid`**, instead of\nshowing errors only as disconnected alerts.\n> \n> **Cart** keeps server-side validation as source of truth: line error\nblocks get stable IDs, `QuantityControl` receives computed ARIA from\n`getQuantityAria`, and **`aria-invalid`** is set only when the line’s\nerror code is in the new **`QUANTITY_VALIDATION_ERROR_CODES`** list\n(min/max/pack/limit, etc.); other line errors still describe the field\nwithout marking it invalid.\n> \n> **Quotes** enable **`validate-on-mount`** on the quantity stepper when\nthere is no tier quantity (0), so the invalid state is announced with\nthe local validation message; button mode is unchanged.\n> \n> **UI kit / shared**: optional **`aria`** prop on `VcQuantityStepper`,\n`VcAddToCart`, and `QuantityControl` (passthrough to the input; stepper\nspinbutton semantics still override conflicting consumer ARIA).\n**`QuantityControl`** only skips mount validation for untouched **0**\nwhen **`allowZero`** is true.\n> \n> **i18n**: adds **`PRODUCT_PACK_SIZE_LIMIT`** and **`LINE_ITEM_LIMIT`**\nunder `validation_error` in all storefront locales; aligns pack-size\ncopy with ui-kit in fi/it/ja/zh (visible on product pages too).\n> \n> Broad **unit tests** cover cart/quote ARIA behavior, aria passthrough,\nmount validation, and locale parameter substitution.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n7f07141adcf608aedfa346f6a4f06ae52cfca4ac. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"518c5138ded8be8a0fa6da6a2ce45104b226a864","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/518c5138ded8be8a0fa6da6a2ce45104b226a864"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/f1130c7f8e1a95f53f726aeeb51d5dba978cc788","verification":{"payload":"tree 518c5138ded8be8a0fa6da6a2ce45104b226a864\nparent 2b75c7de79e676a7bad40f05487fb7ee3fb89cee\nauthor Maiia Diachkovskaia <mayapavlovna@gmail.com> 1791445542 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791445542 +0300\n\nfix(VCST-5990): explain an out-of-range quantity in cart and quotes (#2533)\n\n## Description\n\nWith `allowZero: false` the quantity field could be invalid while\nnothing tied it to the text explaining why, which fails WCAG 3.3.1.\nResidual of VCST-5912.\n\nIn the cart, Chrome already reported the field as invalid on `dev`, from\nthe native `rangeUnderflow`, but the DOM had no `aria-invalid`. The red\nalert under the line was on screen, but nothing connected it to the\nfield, so the field had no description. This PR adds the description and\nmakes `aria-invalid` explicit.\n\n### Cart: the server stays the source of truth\nThe cart passes `disable-validation` on purpose: the typed quantity is\nsent, and the server answers with line validation errors, which the cart\nrenders as `VcAlert`s under the line.\n\n- The quantity input gets `aria-describedby` pointing at the line''s\nerror container whenever the line has errors.\n- It gets `aria-invalid=\"true\"` only when one of those errors is about\nthe quantity (`QUANTITY_VALIDATION_ERROR_CODES` in `shared/cart/enums`).\nA price or availability error describes the field without marking it\ninvalid.\n- Works in both `product_quantity_control` modes.\n\nThe code list comes from x-cart 3.1034.0 `CartLineItemValidator`, branch\nby branch:\n\n| In the list | Left out, and why |\n|---|---|\n| `PRODUCT_MIN_QTY`, `PRODUCT_MAX_QTY`, `PRODUCT_MIN_MAX_QTY`,\n`PRODUCT_EXACT_QTY`, `PRODUCT_QTY_CHANGED`,\n`PRODUCT_MIN_QTY_NOT_AVAILABLE`, `PRODUCT_PACK_SIZE_LIMIT`,\n`LINE_ITEM_LIMIT` | `PRODUCT_FFC_QTY`, `CART_PRODUCT_UNAVAILABLE`: about\nthe product; no typed quantity fixes them |\n| | `PRODUCT_QTY_INSUFFICIENT`: raised on the `CartProduct`\n(`ItemQtyAdjustmentValidator`), so its `objectId` never matches a line |\n\n`PRODUCT_PACK_SIZE_LIMIT` matters most: the validator checks pack size\nfirst in an if/else chain, so it is the only error the line gets.\n\nThis deliberately differs from AC 1 (\"before the value is committed\").\nBlocking the commit on the client would change cart behaviour, and the\nproduct owner chose to keep the server as the source of truth.\n\n### Translations\n`PRODUCT_PACK_SIZE_LIMIT` and `LINE_ITEM_LIMIT` had no\n`validation_error` keys, so every locale showed the raw English server\ntext (`\" Order in packs of 2\"`, leading space included). Both are now\ntranslated in all 13 locales and use the server''s `packSize` / `limit`\nparameters.\n\nThe pack-size text matches `ui_kit.add_to_cart.errors.pack_size`, so the\nproduct page and the cart say the same thing. **Visible change outside\nthe cart:** the product-page pack-size message is reworded in fi, it, zh\nand ja.\n\n### Quotes\nA quote row without a tier quantity renders 0. In stepper mode it is now\nvalidated on mount (`:validate-on-mount=\"$cfg.product_quantity_control\n=== ''stepper''\"`), so it announces `aria-invalid` plus the\n`positive_number` message. Button mode is left alone: VcAddToCart would\nmark it invalid there with no message to describe it.\n\n### ui-kit / shared, additive only\n- `VcQuantityStepper` and `VcAddToCart` get a new optional `aria` prop,\nforwarded to their `VcInput` (the same idiom as `VcInput`,\n`VcDateInput`, `VcDatePicker`). The stepper''s own `role`, `aria-label`\nand `aria-valuemin/max/now` always win.\n- `QuantityControl` gets a new optional `aria` prop, forwarded in both\nmodes.\n- The early return in `QuantityControl`''s `onMounted` now applies only\nwhen `allowZero` is set. Missions, add-to-cart and the catalog card are\nunchanged. The guard stays because the max rule would reject an\nuntouched 0 on negative stock; a test pins this.\n\n### Verification\n- Live app, QA backend, stepper mode:\n- min 2 / max 5 product, typed 1: the field gets `aria-invalid=\"true\"`\nand the description \"You can order from 2 to 5 item(s)\" (on `dev` it had\nno description).\n- pack-size-2 product (min 10 / max 20), anonymous cart, typed 11:\n`aria-invalid=\"true\"`, described by \"Order in packs of 2\"; in de,\n\"Bestellen in Packungen von 2\". Typing 12 removes both attributes.\n- Tests:\n- `cart-line-items.test.ts`: a quantity error, `PRODUCT_PACK_SIZE_LIMIT`\nand `LINE_ITEM_LIMIT` as a line''s only error, a non-quantity error, an\nerror on another object, no errors.\n- `useErrorsTranslator.locales.test.ts`: both new messages rendered with\nserver parameters in all 13 locales.\n  - `quote-line-items.test.ts`: stepper and button mode.\n- `quantity-control.test.ts`: mount validation, negative stock,\npassthrough in both modes.\n  - `vc-quantity-stepper.test.ts`: passthrough, own semantics win.\n\nEvery new behaviour was mutation-tested: removing it turns a test red, 3\nruns each.\n- 1908 tests pass across `client-app/shared`, ui-kit organisms,\n`modules` and the new locale test. `yarn validate:types` and `yarn\ncheck-locales` are clean. eslint on the changed files reports one error,\n`quote-line-items.vue:108`, which is already on `dev`.\n- Storybook: new `DescribedByExternalMessage` story (`allowZero: false`,\nvalue below the floor, AC 6), and `aria` argTypes on VcQuantityStepper\nand VcAddToCart.\n\n**Not verified:**\n- `LINE_ITEM_LIMIT` in a browser (it needs a quantity above 999999).\n- An editable quote with a missing tier quantity in the live app\n(covered by `quote-line-items.test.ts`).\n- Storybook axe on the new story.\n- A native-speaker check of the fi, it, zh and ja wording.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5990\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2533-7f07-7f07141a.zip\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Low Risk**\n> Additive ARIA and i18n with targeted mount-validation guard changes;\ncart quantity commit behavior is unchanged and behavior is heavily\ncovered by new tests.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Improves **WCAG 3.3.1** for cart and quote quantity fields by wiring\nserver and client validation messages to the input via\n**`aria-describedby`** and explicit **`aria-invalid`**, instead of\nshowing errors only as disconnected alerts.\n> \n> **Cart** keeps server-side validation as source of truth: line error\nblocks get stable IDs, `QuantityControl` receives computed ARIA from\n`getQuantityAria`, and **`aria-invalid`** is set only when the line’s\nerror code is in the new **`QUANTITY_VALIDATION_ERROR_CODES`** list\n(min/max/pack/limit, etc.); other line errors still describe the field\nwithout marking it invalid.\n> \n> **Quotes** enable **`validate-on-mount`** on the quantity stepper when\nthere is no tier quantity (0), so the invalid state is announced with\nthe local validation message; button mode is unchanged.\n> \n> **UI kit / shared**: optional **`aria`** prop on `VcQuantityStepper`,\n`VcAddToCart`, and `QuantityControl` (passthrough to the input; stepper\nspinbutton semantics still override conflicting consumer ARIA).\n**`QuantityControl`** only skips mount validation for untouched **0**\nwhen **`allowZero`** is true.\n> \n> **i18n**: adds **`PRODUCT_PACK_SIZE_LIMIT`** and **`LINE_ITEM_LIMIT`**\nunder `validation_error` in all storefront locales; aligns pack-size\ncopy with ui-kit in fi/it/ja/zh (visible on product pages too).\n> \n> Broad **unit tests** cover cart/quote ARIA behavior, aria passthrough,\nmount validation, and locale parameter substitution.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n7f07141adcf608aedfa346f6a4f06ae52cfca4ac. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqx0omCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAj40QACuUo9GqQmJMc7eDF6ZyhEBG\nI2HAq2hp/UgOFY8VY0dXnGJoav3lkz/zuVjUr/xC1Ned+EtcyOsc8yGalFH1MI5V\nScH5z24Zk2FGBPruDeeiu+cIo75cR2QX96ElOInKOuVn8YnVp7CP3+KDj4nLVSBt\nib4wdPT4GQceS1hhqnbk1zsjn+Ok4lXGQomm+6zZY0zVMsJP27ZP+udbd9zldvAC\nRTB8yVi9y8KXIw8m/czSMzRe/g4v4kWum/6dyYTGTaw4FwoiS3wQbIED/MFuvqPG\n/GX2onxlBkqYGC6xsxwTwf/jxksXqw6SIeT3eZbBY8Ngx1E7i8j6IHZoJZDH1k1e\n1Nf26U2E6JRAP9qWZsbTwJlmEILrbGWxKBMMuZdPsb2QCf4Ck5eyGzsOEAsCSd6H\nsX3OwrGekP3kbZiE9gBYJy8OuYVb877Uft9eBpBX60z0G1VlIW/GfPdkEg+KP1qF\nFJKtsj1j056sFj2iwqLGyJlf4ykFTG1yWiuPAI/fTgluMur2r1bXq85+RCtrJq+U\nuKh1aNV2yEWowIRM6CHx9skz4uWy0VpBSfjpoxWdD4u4e0J/Ds/D4Qj9LVvrYnA7\nVaACEqd7qbKxxjDhaltPLNBIc49vqCyThlr5GNCPba1Ul23ViEu7e5hnUXH3pip0\nFJyBszrxcss/1CU6BJKx\n=+4C3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-08T07:45:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"htt