n\n- Update `backend-packages.json` (platform 3.1073.0 → 3.1076.0, module\nbumps; PR-build blobs for SalesRep/XCart/Cart replaced by released\nversions).\n- Remove the orphaned `requestPasswordReset` query. The backend dropped\nthe deprecated `Query.requestPasswordReset` field (replaced by the\n`sendPasswordResetEmail` mutation in #2060), so the unused document made\n`yarn generate:graphql-types` fail validation. Nothing imported it.\n- Regenerate GraphQL types against the current backend.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\n<!-- Put link to your task in Jira here -->\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2547-e991-e991d431.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"be8e085c2eecc0079c84c3e0ff7975642c5ff326","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/be8e085c2eecc0079c84c3e0ff7975642c5ff326"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/a005f8bde61bd3288a28147f2242fdeea192c702","verification":{"payload":"tree be8e085c2eecc0079c84c3e0ff7975642c5ff326\nparent 702d1c1c7c72360aad8c3e22389ad653dc58df0e\nauthor Ivan Kalachikov <ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com> 1791370874 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791370874 +0100\n\nchore: update backend packages and graphql types (#2547)\n\n## Description\n\n- Update `backend-packages.json` (platform 3.1073.0 → 3.1076.0, module\nbumps; PR-build blobs for SalesRep/XCart/Cart replaced by released\nversions).\n- Remove the orphaned `requestPasswordReset` query. The backend dropped\nthe deprecated `Query.requestPasswordReset` field (replaced by the\n`sendPasswordResetEmail` mutation in #2060), so the unused document made\n`yarn generate:graphql-types` fail validation. Nothing imported it.\n- Regenerate GraphQL types against the current backend.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\n<!-- Put link to your task in Jira here -->\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2547-e991-e991d431.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxiZ6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUD0QAG27la+zxEjLdBzPj6QUFlCn\n05rs/f6gcCb9MyBXArnvCWqIBkG+TY3Zx3qncQCxrq+2IopgHxJij7PGIOq0zNHT\n981OoaGqbMrho55P1QG9ITGB7mb0w8aV8GL0vjOi/xr6MdtN9NYkO0sCs8/upGE0\nUsaGjQ0lZbrCOFolFgYxo2CoIbyWK8imSqebHXa/VebWCuAZZvjFeMwMTKm/3YMM\nzUw+742HfXv01qzu51RB5CMoKE54SkO66+RMvnmNOVhQ+VsqrGxozhlrJtQZrNWe\nWB8RChxHZlpz0HKw/oiMT3ckF7qyqKfRRdiz1cLsPNDlWyjPls1t9JL6HJfkKfYF\nFiMylbMkY12p0i17BKl0xztjZOM8QC9/Xf47rs+gIHCXt2yYRxEanQDOXdOrvbNc\npefdyowJwu7M+H/zYJ/AelkIYQ5SDo48SjWEod/AjAaHO9q0PbZoyUXhT9ZcwA6U\nhudqU+5lXtuRf2Iz2VEgCvlJ1AcMc2LWiNykPiQ8njfufYaklezYcOxWQunn3dnw\nm9PTstKuMB0+10AyDpYe3BOk3WpP7MbhDcquVKw96dLLXa+v1cluwjvE+/MuMNE/\nEZoZhpztkkx1x1gV7MeIGnCfDsRN3rdHhJryK3rCvywKPdiFWED9J28zdp8Cdfgt\n2MVdbvmwuGBYLVBmynQE\n=9MEP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T11:01:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/a005f8bde61bd3288a28147f2242fdeea192c702","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKGEwMDVmOGJkZTYxYmQzMjg4YTI4MTQ3ZjIyNDJmZGVlYTE5MmM3MDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/702d1c1c7c72360aad8c3e22389ad653dc58df0e","sha":"702d1c1c7c72360aad8c3e22389ad653dc58df0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/702d1c1c7c72360aad8c3e22389ad653dc58df0e"}],"sha":"a005f8bde61bd3288a28147f2242fdeea192c702","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/a005f8bde61bd3288a28147f2242fdeea192c702"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16372194?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/goldenmaya","id":16372194,"login":"goldenmaya","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzcyMTk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/702d1c1c7c72360aad8c3e22389ad653dc58df0e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T07:41:46Z","email":"mayapavlovna@gmail.com","name":"Maiia Diachkovskaia"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T07:41:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VCST-6001): adopt VcDateRangePicker in the sales-rep orders filter (#2519)\n\n## Description\n\nThe Sales Rep customer-orders filter hand-assembled its custom date\nrange from two single-date pickers, a separator and its own \"end before\nstart\" check. It now uses `VcDateRangePicker`, the same component as the\nstorefront''s `/account/orders` filter.\n\n### What changes for the user\n\n- **Desktop:** two labelled fields (Start date / End date) — the `split`\nlayout, with the picker''s `fieldset` / `group \"Date range\"` semantics,\n`aria-invalid`, `aria-haspopup=\"dialog\"` and an `aria-hidden` separator.\n- **Phone** (below `sm`, 640px): one combined field labelled \"Date\nrange\", as on the storefront.\n- **Range validity** (format, start ≤ end) is the picker''s own; the\nfilter''s hand-rolled order check and its `invalid_range` key are gone.\n- **Chip dates** use the same format as the inputs (`formatDateLocale`):\n`Start: 08/01/2026`, not `8/1/2026`.\n- **Contextual accessible names** instead of duplicates:\n- calendar buttons — \"Open calendar: Start date\" / \"Open calendar: End\ndate\"\n- clear buttons, wherever a split field is clearable — \"Clear: Start\ndate\" / \"Clear: End date\" (this filter clears through the calendar\nfooter instead, see below)\n  - chip close buttons — \"Remove filter “Start: 08/01/2026”\"\n\n### ui-kit — additive only\n\nAll new props are optional; without them every component renders exactly\nas before.\n\n- `VcInput`: `clearButtonAriaLabel` — accessible name of the clear\nbutton (falls back to \"Clear\").\n- `VcDateInput`: `clearButtonAriaLabel`, forwarded.\n- `VcDatePicker`: `clearButtonAriaLabel`, `calendarButtonAriaLabel`\n(falls back to \"Open calendar\").\n- `VcDateRangePicker` (`split`): passes both, built from each field''s\nlabel — `ui_kit.buttons.clear_field` /\n`ui_kit.accessibility.open_calendar_for`, new in all 13 locales. The\ncolon form (\"Clear: {field}\") never inflects the field name, so it holds\nfor any caller label; ja and zh keep their own word order, where the\nfield name is not inflected either.\n- `@vc-frontend/core` contract (`core-api/contract/index.d.ts`):\n`VcInput` gains `clearButtonAriaLabel` — VcInput is a facade export.\nAdded as the two lines `yarn build:core-types` generates for it, with\nthe patch bump it writes (`core-api/package.json` 0.1.1 → 0.1.2); the\nrest of that command''s output is drift already on `dev`\n(`validate:core-types` is red at the merge base too), so it is left out\nof this PR.\n\n> ⚠️ **Visible to storefront users:** the storefront `/account/orders`\ndate filter uses `VcDateRangePicker` in `split` layout, so its two \"Open\ncalendar\" / \"Clear\" buttons get the same contextual names. This is the\nfix VCST-5718 asks for.\n\n### Removed / changed in the sales-rep module (shipped in 2.57.0 and\n2.58.0)\n\nFor forks that styled or overrode these — nothing raises an error, they\nsimply stop matching:\n\n- `.sales-rep-orders-filters__date` — gone (it sat on each of the two\ndate pickers).\n- `.sales-rep-orders-filters__separator` — gone; the separator is now\nthe picker''s own, `aria-hidden`.\n- `.sales-rep-orders-filters__range` — moved from a flex-row wrapper\n`div` onto the `VcDateRangePicker` root (the `fieldset` in split, the\npopover root in combined); it now only sets the top margin.\n- `sales_rep.customer_orders.filters.invalid_range` — removed from all\n13 locale files; the picker''s own message replaces it.\n\n### Deliberate\n\n- **No clear button inside the fields.** The filter never had one on\n`dev`. With `clearable` on, both fields clip their value (content 102px\nin a 100px field — that is VCST-6002). Clearing the range goes through\nthe calendar footer (`show-footer`) instead.\n- The chip label keeps the old \"Start: / End:\" wording; only the date\nformat changed.\n\n### Follow-ups, not in this PR\n\n- The returns module assembles the same date filter by hand.\n- Storefront order chips still format dates with `d()`, not the input\nformat.\n- Quote style in es / it / pt: this module quotes with « », like its\nexisting strings; the global `locales/{es,it,pt}.json` use “ ”. Worth\nsettling one style per language.\n\n### Screenshots\n\n| | dev | this branch |\n|---|---|---|\n| Desktop filter | <img width=\"300\" alt=\"6001-desktop-before\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c4ee6c17-3e1a-4eb8-94c8-f1f229a9cd86\"\n/> | <img width=\"300\" alt=\"6001-desktop-after\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0f9401af-e5a3-47d1-88f1-b65e4df207cd\"\n/> |\n| Chips | <img width=\"480\" alt=\"6001-chips-before\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/99ca7b48-2b26-4155-9883-0c41f7c43d76\"\n/> | <img width=\"480\" alt=\"6001-chips-after\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6d53fedd-177c-4f28-88e4-74114121a417\"\n/> |\n| Mobile, 390px | <img width=\"260\" alt=\"6001-mobile-before\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a4c95cc8-9ed3-4386-a290-aa5281f02cff\"\n/> | <img width=\"260\" alt=\"6001-mobile-after\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d209dc51-9e68-4fc1-868e-2ba2642dbfe3\"\n/> |\n\nCalendar on the phone: <img width=\"260\" alt=\"6001-mobile-calendar\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/78d0ab73-6266-407b-a15e-e73fa7c545a5\"\n/>\n\n### Verification\n\neslint and `validate:types` clean, `check-locales` clean. Unit tests:\nfilter component, customer-orders page, `VcInput`, `VcDatePicker`, the\nrange picker''s per-field names (new\n`vc-date-range-picker.names.test.ts`); 1241 tests green across\n`client-app/modules/{sales-rep,federated}`,\n`ui-kit/components/molecules/{input,date-input}`,\n`ui-kit/components/organisms/{date-picker,date-range-picker}`,\n`ui-kit/utilities` and `shared/account`. Browser: desktop and a 390px\nmobile viewport against a mocked Sales Rep backend; desktop split,\nchips, the out-of-order error, footer Clear and Escape re-checked\nagainst the QA backend with a real Sales Rep account. PORT_TO_MF.md\nlists the new non-facade imports.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6001\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2519-c7ad-c7ad5804.zip\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Shared date components and storefront `/account/orders` split layout\nget new default accessible button names; sales-rep filter date UX and\nchip formatting change but validation is delegated to the picker.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Replaces the Sales Rep customer-orders **custom date range** (two\n`VcDatePicker`s plus hand-rolled ordering/validation) with\n**`VcDateRangePicker`**, matching the account orders filter: **split**\nstart/end on desktop and **combined** “Date range” below `sm` via\n`useBreakpoints` and `BREAKPOINTS`.\n> \n> **Customer-orders** filter chips now show dates with\n**`formatDateLocale`** (same as the inputs) and set\n**`close-button-aria-label`** from a new `remove_filter` string;\n`invalid_range` locale keys are dropped in favor of the picker’s\nmessages.\n> \n> **ui-kit (additive):** optional **`clearButtonAriaLabel`** on\n`VcInput` / `VcDateInput` and **`clearButtonAriaLabel`** +\n**`calendarButtonAriaLabel`** on `VcDatePicker`; **`VcDateRangePicker`\nsplit** wires per-field names through new `clear_field` /\n`open_calendar_for` strings (13 locales). The **`@vc-frontend/core`\ncontract** documents `VcInput.clearButtonAriaLabel`. **`PORT_TO_MF.md`**\nnotes new non-facade imports (`formatDateLocale`, `tryParseDate`,\n`BREAKPOINTS`).\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\nc7ad58042a8421ce99368e95a76f8a6cbe7a57e2. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"f9508d35a846717b702529d242e0453c59a10399","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/f9508d35a846717b702529d242e0453c59a10399"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/702d1c1c7c72360aad8c3e22389ad653dc58df0e","verification":{"payload":"tree f9508d35a846717b702529d242e0453c59a10399\nparent 35a8890efc70e11d27b702574a6418e25973c2e8\nauthor Maiia Diachkovskaia <mayapavlovna@gmail.com> 1791358906 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791358906 +0300\n\nfeat(VCST-6001): adopt VcDateRangePicker in the sales-rep orders filter (#2519)\n\n## Description\n\nThe Sales Rep customer-orders filter hand-assembled its custom date\nrange from two single-date pickers, a separator and its own \"end before\nstart\" check. It now uses `VcDateRangePicker`, the same component as the\nstorefront''s `/account/orders` filter.\n\n### What changes for the user\n\n- **Desktop:** two labelled fields (Start date / End date) — the `split`\nlayout, with the picker''s `fieldset` / `group \"Date range\"` semantics,\n`aria-invalid`, `aria-haspopup=\"dialog\"` and an `aria-hidden` separator.\n- **Phone** (below `sm`, 640px): one combined field labelled \"Date\nrange\", as on the storefront.\n- **Range validity** (format, start ≤ end) is the picker''s own; the\nfilter''s hand-rolled order check and its `invalid_range` key are gone.\n- **Chip dates** use the same format as the inputs (`formatDateLocale`):\n`Start: 08/01/2026`, not `8/1/2026`.\n- **Contextual accessible names** instead of duplicates:\n- calendar buttons — \"Open calendar: Start date\" / \"Open calendar: End\ndate\"\n- clear buttons, wherever a split field is clearable — \"Clear: Start\ndate\" / \"Clear: End date\" (this filter clears through the calendar\nfooter instead, see below)\n  - chip close buttons — \"Remove filter “Start: 08/01/2026”\"\n\n### ui-kit — additive only\n\nAll new props are optional; without them every component renders exactly\nas before.\n\n- `VcInput`: `clearButtonAriaLabel` — accessible name of the clear\nbutton (falls back to \"Clear\").\n- `VcDateInput`: `clearButtonAriaLabel`, forwarded.\n- `VcDatePicker`: `clearButtonAriaLabel`, `calendarButtonAriaLabel`\n(falls back to \"Open calendar\").\n- `VcDateRangePicker` (`split`): passes both, built from each field''s\nlabel — `ui_kit.buttons.clear_field` /\n`ui_kit.accessibility.open_calendar_for`, new in all 13 locales. The\ncolon form (\"Clear: {field}\") never inflects the field name, so it holds\nfor any caller label; ja and zh keep their own word order, where the\nfield name is not inflected either.\n- `@vc-frontend/core` contract (`core-api/contract/index.d.ts`):\n`VcInput` gains `clearButtonAriaLabel` — VcInput is a facade export.\nAdded as the two lines `yarn build:core-types` generates for it, with\nthe patch bump it writes (`core-api/package.json` 0.1.1 → 0.1.2); the\nrest of that command''s output is drift already on `dev`\n(`validate:core-types` is red at the merge base too), so it is left out\nof this PR.\n\n> ⚠️ **Visible to storefront users:** the storefront `/account/orders`\ndate filter uses `VcDateRangePicker` in `split` layout, so its two \"Open\ncalendar\" / \"Clear\" buttons get the same contextual names. This is the\nfix VCST-5718 asks for.\n\n### Removed / changed in the sales-rep module (shipped in 2.57.0 and\n2.58.0)\n\nFor forks that styled or overrode these — nothing raises an error, they\nsimply stop matching:\n\n- `.sales-rep-orders-filters__date` — gone (it sat on each of the two\ndate pickers).\n- `.sales-rep-orders-filters__separator` — gone; the separator is now\nthe picker''s own, `aria-hidden`.\n- `.sales-rep-orders-filters__range` — moved from a flex-row wrapper\n`div` onto the `VcDateRangePicker` root (the `fieldset` in split, the\npopover root in combined); it now only sets the top margin.\n- `sales_rep.customer_orders.filters.invalid_range` — removed from all\n13 locale files; the picker''s own message replaces it.\n\n### Deliberate\n\n- **No clear button inside the fields.** The filter never had one on\n`dev`. With `clearable` on, both fields clip their value (content 102px\nin a 100px field — that is VCST-6002). Clearing the range goes through\nthe calendar footer (`show-footer`) instead.\n- The chip label keeps the old \"Start: / End:\" wording; only the date\nformat changed.\n\n### Follow-ups, not in this PR\n\n- The returns module assembles the same date filter by hand.\n- Storefront order chips still format dates with `d()`, not the input\nformat.\n- Quote style in es / it / pt: this module quotes with « », like its\nexisting strings; the global `locales/{es,it,pt}.json` use “ ”. Worth\nsettling one style per language.\n\n### Screenshots\n\n| | dev | this branch |\n|---|---|---|\n| Desktop filter | <img width=\"300\" alt=\"6001-desktop-before\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c4ee6c17-3e1a-4eb8-94c8-f1f229a9cd86\"\n/> | <img width=\"300\" alt=\"6001-desktop-after\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0f9401af-e5a3-47d1-88f1-b65e4df207cd\"\n/> |\n| Chips | <img width=\"480\" alt=\"6001-chips-before\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/99ca7b48-2b26-4155-9883-0c41f7c43d76\"\n/> | <img width=\"480\" alt=\"6001-chips-after\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6d53fedd-177c-4f28-88e4-74114121a417\"\n/> |\n| Mobile, 390px | <img width=\"260\" alt=\"6001-mobile-before\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a4c95cc8-9ed3-4386-a290-aa5281f02cff\"\n/> | <img width=\"260\" alt=\"6001-mobile-after\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d209dc51-9e68-4fc1-868e-2ba2642dbfe3\"\n/> |\n\nCalendar on the phone: <img width=\"260\" alt=\"6001-mobile-calendar\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/78d0ab73-6266-407b-a15e-e73fa7c545a5\"\n/>\n\n### Verification\n\neslint and `validate:types` clean, `check-locales` clean. Unit tests:\nfilter component, customer-orders page, `VcInput`, `VcDatePicker`, the\nrange picker''s per-field names (new\n`vc-date-range-picker.names.test.ts`); 1241 tests green across\n`client-app/modules/{sales-rep,federated}`,\n`ui-kit/components/molecules/{input,date-input}`,\n`ui-kit/components/organisms/{date-picker,date-range-picker}`,\n`ui-kit/utilities` and `shared/account`. Browser: desktop and a 390px\nmobile viewport against a mocked Sales Rep backend; desktop split,\nchips, the out-of-order error, footer Clear and Escape re-checked\nagainst the QA backend with a real Sales Rep account. PORT_TO_MF.md\nlists the new non-facade imports.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6001\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2519-c7ad-c7ad5804.zip\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Shared date components and storefront `/account/orders` split layout\nget new default accessible button names; sales-rep filter date UX and\nchip formatting change but validation is delegated to the picker.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Replaces the Sales Rep customer-orders **custom date range** (two\n`VcDatePicker`s plus hand-rolled ordering/validation) with\n**`VcDateRangePicker`**, matching the account orders filter: **split**\nstart/end on desktop and **combined** “Date range” below `sm` via\n`useBreakpoints` and `BREAKPOINTS`.\n> \n> **Customer-orders** filter chips now show dates with\n**`formatDateLocale`** (same as the inputs) and set\n**`close-button-aria-label`** from a new `remove_filter` string;\n`invalid_range` locale keys are dropped in favor of the picker’s\nmessages.\n> \n> **ui-kit (additive):** optional **`clearButtonAriaLabel`** on\n`VcInput` / `VcDateInput` and **`clearButtonAriaLabel`** +\n**`calendarButtonAriaLabel`** on `VcDatePicker`; **`VcDateRangePicker`\nsplit** wires per-field names through new `clear_field` /\n`open_calendar_for` strings (13 locales). The **`@vc-frontend/core`\ncontract** documents `VcInput.clearButtonAriaLabel`. **`PORT_TO_MF.md`**\nnotes new non-facade imports (`formatDateLocale`, `tryParseDate`,\n`BREAKPOINTS`).\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\nc7ad58042a8421ce99368e95a76f8a6cbe7a57e2. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxfe6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVGAQAHM5rtSFpQBLi833yOJZsLid\nWwklG34hDa24e4qT/3YbJfXrMHfMMfQzMKZ1HIl7yAoPwLR5309s2DyYy+79rfRr\nfcMiLaoUl1Xc7m79DX6gpQ6pCeVeAZraRFeY2juaKVt65e77EB9FcXkLkvjnlOFU\nsYskHfVAiUfS4D9YiiDpbskDtIE9+nm6uITZV+giAyXxmRjYZ2G64Sg2ZmdptXzQ\nBhjQTZXJdUYnb4wpLb+r1fT/krtBVvti7iMAmefdLLsRQ3Q4i3bZfchpWMb45hut\n2HHrgr0UAQLhaqFzoOTBUzUvvId/FAFGPQqcanj6dDinKRvRRkpY3ob7CvOkKuQF\n/SsuvPq61z0KgtuPQ8vfu7HAo1bS9zJaDFOZe/z+FUCFQzhjm8UJ55nLe6iEqA3o\n+QyvOIADbJeJTRdPTh105UCtduXOqGvGd7m8681Ya/28+XsWZJZyXQt1jFHJdGr3\ngbacZwpbCxQRh0CrHBMAVqtr+RoCwoicZutRZ0cNr6Q9AzaLkcGtU50uxKrBC+H9\n3RIpR9NgdRy5wTYyaFx0z8EPXtwrd8/2WccAvpbTtuxOpiM6Ros/xXNPRUOC+Lx3\n7E10/eQEaY66NspceCExuaWiqc9HA+RWzB3zpchSW3ib8b+7RG0qdA3mLkMjP6aC\nlUJOP5p7bhOEkQGlpY7q\n=QhfT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T07:41:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/702d1c1c7c72360aad8c3e22389ad653dc58df0e","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDcwMmQxYzFjN2M3MjM2MGFhZDhjM2UyMjM4OWFkNjUzZGM1OGRmMGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/35a8890efc70e11d27b702574a6418e25973c2e8","sha":"35a8890efc70e11d27b702574a6418e25973c2e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/35a8890efc70e11d27b702574a6418e25973c2e8"}],"sha":"702d1c1c7c72360aad8c3e22389ad653dc58df0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/702d1c1c7c72360aad8c3e22389ad653dc58df0e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16372194?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/goldenmaya","id":16372194,"login":"goldenmaya","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzcyMTk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/35a8890efc70e11d27b702574a6418e25973c2e8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T06:18:16Z","email":"mayapavlovna@gmail.com","name":"Maiia Diachkovskaia"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T06:18:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(VCST-6107): raise returns secondary text and dark table hover contrast to AA (#2532)\n\n## Description\n\nThe returns pages draw field labels and other secondary text in\n`text-neutral-400` (#a3a3a3), which is 2.52:1 on white and fails WCAG\n1.4.3.\n\n**Scope: the returns module only**, by product-owner decision.\n`text-neutral-400` is still used as text in about 36 other files\n(dashboard, addresses, quotes, purchase requests, loyalty, sales rep).\nThat app-wide fix needs its own ticket.\n\n### Returns: `neutral-400` / `neutral-500` → `neutral-600`\n- Every secondary-text use in `client-app/modules/returns` (32 class\ntokens in 6 files) is changed, including `cancel-return-modal.vue`,\nwhich was already on `neutral-500`.\n- `neutral-500` was not enough. On white it measures 4.02 in black-gold,\n4.17 in watermelon and 4.33 in purple-pink. On zebra rows\nblack-gold.dark drops to 3.87.\n- `neutral-600` passes in all 14 preset files, on both the plate\n(`additional-50`) and the zebra rows (`neutral-50`). The lowest value is\n5.19 (black-gold.dark, zebra).\n- The non-returnable rows in `select-return-items.vue` also move to 600.\nThey contain no disabled control: the quantity input is replaced by a\ndash and the reason is shown as text. So the 1.4.3 exemption for\ninactive components does not apply. The rows remain visibly different\nthrough the dash and the warning reason.\n\n### VcTable (ui-kit): dark row hover\n- The hover fill was `neutral-200` in every theme. Secondary text on it\nmeasured 3.40 in coffee.dark and watermelon.dark, and 4.12 in\nblack-gold.dark.\n- The fill now comes from one variable: `--row-hover-shade` →\n`--row-hover-bg-color: var(--vc-table-row-hover-bg-color,\nvar(--row-hover-shade))`. The dark layer\n(`assets/styles/dark/organisms/vc-table.scss`) overrides only the shade,\nsetting it to `neutral-100`.\n- `neutral-600` on the new fill measures at least 4.68 in every dark\npreset, and the hover still brightens.\n  - Light mode is unchanged (`neutral-200`, verified in the built CSS).\n- Sticky (`fixed`) cells had their own hard-coded `bg-neutral-200`\nhover. They now use the same variable, so a hovered row has one colour.\n- New public knob for forks: `--vc-table-row-hover-bg-color`.\n\n### Verification\n- Contrast was computed from `client-app/assets/presets/*.json` (all 14\nfiles) and recomputed independently by two review passes.\n- `vite build`: `html.dark .vc-table{--row-hover-shade: rgb(from\nvar(--color-neutral-100) …)}` and `.vc-table__row:hover\n.vc-table__cell--fixed{background-color:var(--row-hover-bg-color)}` are\npresent.\n- In the live app (QA backend, purple-pink store, orders table), a\nhovered row computes to `#e8e8e8` (`neutral-200`) in light and `#1e1c22`\n(`neutral-100`) in dark.\n- `yarn validate:types` is clean, and eslint on the changed files\nreports 0 errors.\n\n**Not walked:** the returns pages themselves. The returns module is\ndisabled on the QA store (the route returns 404), so the returns change\nrests on the preset math and the template diff.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6107\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2532-c725-c7253361.zip\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Low Risk**\n> Visual-only token and CSS variable changes for contrast; no auth,\ndata, or API behavior changes.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Raises **WCAG 1.4.3 (AA)** contrast for returns UI and dark-theme\ntable row hover.\n> \n> **Returns module:** Secondary copy (labels, hints, SKU lines,\nplaceholders, non-returnable row styling) moves from `text-neutral-400`\n/ `neutral-500` to **`text-neutral-600`** across six components/pages\n(list, details, edit, item selection, modals). App-wide `neutral-400`\ntext is unchanged outside returns.\n> \n> **VcTable:** Row hover no longer hard-codes `bg-neutral-200`. Hover\nfill is driven by **`--row-hover-shade`** → **`--row-hover-bg-color`**,\nwith an override hook **`--vc-table-row-hover-bg-color`**. Sticky/fixed\ncells use the same hover color. Dark theme\n(`dark/organisms/vc-table.scss`) sets **`--row-hover-shade`** to\n**`neutral-100`** so secondary text on hover meets AA; light mode stays\n**`neutral-200`**.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\nc7253361452020567f14480bbca18999287a75b9. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->","tree":{"sha":"98d54567b58dda997d6a97ba2c07837ff8a20c0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/98d54567b58dda997d6a97ba2c07837ff8a20c0f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/35a8890efc70e11d27b702574a6418e25973c2e8","verification":{"payload":"tree 98d54567b58dda997d6a97ba2c07837ff8a20c0f\nparent 8ce895b79046c19da4a76e848abe10e9a276d8cc\nauthor Maiia Diachkovskaia <mayapavlovna@gmail.com> 1791353896 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791353896 +0300\n\nfix(VCST-6107): raise returns secondary text and dark table hover contrast to AA (#2532)\n\n## Description\n\nThe returns pages draw field labels and other secondary text in\n`text-neutral-400` (#a3a3a3), which is 2.52:1 on white and fails WCAG\n1.4.3.\n\n**Scope: the returns module only**, by product-owner decision.\n`text-neutral-400` is still used as text in about 36 other files\n(dashboard, addresses, quotes, purchase requests, loyalty, sales rep).\nThat app-wide fix needs its own ticket.\n\n### Returns: `neutral-400` / `neutral-500` → `neutral-600`\n- Every secondary-text use in `client-app/modules/returns` (32 class\ntokens in 6 files) is changed, including `cancel-return-modal.vue`,\nwhich was already on `neutral-500`.\n- `neutral-500` was not enough. On white it measures 4.02 in black-gold,\n4.17 in watermelon and 4.33 in purple-pink. On zebra rows\nblack-gold.dark drops to 3.87.\n- `neutral-600` passes in all 14 preset files, on both the plate\n(`additional-50`) and the zebra rows (`neutral-50`). The lowest value is\n5.19 (black-gold.dark, zebra).\n- The non-returnable rows in `select-return-items.vue` also move to 600.\nThey contain no disabled control: the quantity input is replaced by a\ndash and the reason is shown as text. So the 1.4.3 exemption for\ninactive components does not apply. The rows remain visibly different\nthrough the dash and the warning reason.\n\n### VcTable (ui-kit): dark row hover\n- The hover fill was `neutral-200` in every theme. Secondary text on it\nmeasured 3.40 in coffee.dark and watermelon.dark, and 4.12 in\nblack-gold.dark.\n- The fill now comes from one variable: `--row-hover-shade` →\n`--row-hover-bg-color: var(--vc-table-row-hover-bg-color,\nvar(--row-hover-shade))`. The dark layer\n(`assets/styles/dark/organisms/vc-table.scss`) overrides only the shade,\nsetting it to `neutral-100`.\n- `neutral-600` on the new fill measures at least 4.68 in every dark\npreset, and the hover still brightens.\n  - Light mode is unchanged (`neutral-200`, verified in the built CSS).\n- Sticky (`fixed`) cells had their own hard-coded `bg-neutral-200`\nhover. They now use the same variable, so a hovered row has one colour.\n- New public knob for forks: `--vc-table-row-hover-bg-color`.\n\n### Verification\n- Contrast was computed from `client-app/assets/presets/*.json` (all 14\nfiles) and recomputed independently by two review passes.\n- `vite build`: `html.dark .vc-table{--row-hover-shade: rgb(from\nvar(--color-neutral-100) …)}` and `.vc-table__row:hover\n.vc-table__cell--fixed{background-color:var(--row-hover-bg-color)}` are\npresent.\n- In the live app (QA backend, purple-pink store, orders table), a\nhovered row computes to `#e8e8e8` (`neutral-200`) in light and `#1e1c22`\n(`neutral-100`) in dark.\n- `yarn validate:types` is clean, and eslint on the changed files\nreports 0 errors.\n\n**Not walked:** the returns pages themselves. The returns module is\ndisabled on the QA store (the route returns 404), so the returns change\nrests on the preset math and the template diff.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6107\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2532-c725-c7253361.zip\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Low Risk**\n> Visual-only token and CSS variable changes for contrast; no auth,\ndata, or API behavior changes.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Raises **WCAG 1.4.3 (AA)** contrast for returns UI and dark-theme\ntable row hover.\n> \n> **Returns module:** Secondary copy (labels, hints, SKU lines,\nplaceholders, non-returnable row styling) moves from `text-neutral-400`\n/ `neutral-500` to **`text-neutral-600`** across six components/pages\n(list, details, edit, item selection, modals). App-wide `neutral-400`\ntext is unchanged outside returns.\n> \n> **VcTable:** Row hover no longer hard-codes `bg-neutral-200`. Hover\nfill is driven by **`--row-hover-shade`** → **`--row-hover-bg-color`**,\nwith an override hook **`--vc-table-row-hover-bg-color`**. Sticky/fixed\ncells use the same hover color. Dark theme\n(`dark/organisms/vc-table.scss`) sets **`--row-hover-shade`** to\n**`neutral-100`** so secondary text on hover meets AA; light mode stays\n**`neutral-200`**.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\nc7253361452020567f14480bbca18999287a75b9. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxeQoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAX+EQACcUhAA+rVliKnRQLcqynCCz\n1STGpa2Cbm37nwztO600++HzV9xn9ehhL6GUG42egRtcpBXxZw6f8UgZK/dgJJP0\n8h8dQtgAsHfk2XZDD4EjGKyHPZjZczlUJAlNrenWuVhmGhjmEqo1Q8PTKprJjYDR\n4zsIbEj4EO0DzG8iKDRhXzFXntdOM0qFreegsDO71jAsiYtYkZxsBdgd5XCrdunD\nCoPBDyaoWLPDrXjm40cAAeulbWogKpNI7zN0A8GZreZNTQwxm+PDaNQtIQ2x9+c2\niMWXorkBO0ayxjHJNLGb76OYysdNBOakjoLOTBsktbMp2VqPkox23pHSybYD57Rx\nYWFBfwSLTV4RuuiXq++ComYzWuIZF1nxg8qa0qToGrDEcCHB1fMdcSPD5ibbTouS\nCs0hup1imJLx+KSt76DKoU3vMjVvZVCzzpNgYNGZGQjUnKgzJqT7ZO51kkbu4SRY\nE3YpKgE6nDVO/5FMgPOOYWNHf+NRn51y5+a7FjSC5jpeuyvWpljF1F5PIRVEcdxZ\nYOW4DwPLohuwlSm+DVK4Uqmso0lLkBGmVu9oc9smwCABV1uYkdb/8t8glCDVa+hw\nYH0BYYDz/9dybtLNMh4GgEUG/bqZ36GzLLb9gDnRNSZDI3dToO/SXB6I0Ef/mRuB\nQ/ZWuNsDPLSM8Uf/UtW4\n=ubIh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T06:18:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/35a8890efc70e11d27b702574a6418e25973c2e8","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDM1YTg4OTBlZmM3MGUxMWQyN2I3MDI1NzRhNjQxOGUyNTk3M2MyZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/8ce895b79046c19da4a76e848abe10e9a276d8cc","sha":"8ce895b79046c19da4a76e848abe10e9a276d8cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/8ce895b79046c19da4a76e848abe10e9a276d8cc"}],"sha":"35a8890efc70e11d27b702574a6418e25973c2e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/35a8890efc70e11d27b702574a6418e25973c2e8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54628043?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aleksandra-Mitricheva/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aleksandra-Mitricheva/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aleksandra-Mitricheva/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aleksandra-Mitricheva/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Aleksandra-Mitricheva","id":54628043,"login":"Aleksandra-Mitricheva","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0NjI4MDQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aleksandra-Mitricheva/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aleksandra-Mitricheva/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aleksandra-Mitricheva/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aleksandra-Mitricheva/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aleksandra-Mitricheva/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Aleksandra-Mitricheva","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/8ce895b79046c19da4a76e848abe10e9a276d8cc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T14:52:18Z","email":"54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Aleksandra-Mitricheva"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T14:52:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(VCST-6000): reject zero-byte files as satisfying a required File section (#2510)\n\n## Problem\n\nOn configurable products, a genuinely empty (0-byte) file **satisfies a\nREQUIRED File section** in the storefront: the chip renders `(0B)`, the\nsection header flips to the filename, and **\"Add to cart\" loses\n`disabled`** with nothing actually attached.\n\nThis is the **storefront half of VCST-6000**. The backend half\n([vc-module-x-cart#144](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-module-x-cart/pull/144))\nnow rejects the same state with `CONFIGURATION_SECTION_FILES_REQUIRED`,\nwhich made the remaining frontend gap the *visible* defect.\n\nMeasured live on vcptcore-qa against the fixed backend build (`XCart\n3.1037.0-pr-144`): the button stays enabled, the server refuses the line\nitem, and the buyer is shown **nothing** — no toast, no inline error,\nclean console, empty cart. A live button that silently does nothing.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`useConfigurableProduct.ts` → `validateValue` gated a required File\nsection on file **presence** only:\n\n```ts\nconst isValid = !section.isRequired || !!value?.files?.length;\n```\n\nA 0-byte file is present, so the gate passed.\n\nThis also left `validateValue` **inconsistent with itself** — the `text`\ncase one branch above already requires non-empty *content*:\n\n```ts\nconst isValid = !section.isRequired || !!value?.customText?.trim();\n```\n\nSo empty content did not satisfy a required Text section but did satisfy\na required File section. The backend fix rests on exactly the same\nargument, one layer down.\n\n## Change\n\n```diff\n       case CONFIGURABLE_SECTION_TYPES.file: {\n-        const isValid = !section.isRequired || !!value?.files?.length;\n+        const isValid = !section.isRequired || !!value?.files?.some((file) => file.size > 0);\n```\n\nOne line, plus a new test file. No other case, function or component\ntouched.\n\n| Case | Behaviour |\n|---|---|\n| Required section, only 0-byte file(s) | **invalid** (new) — button\nblocked, inline error shown |\n| Required section, one real file | valid |\n| Required section, 0-byte + real file | valid |\n| Optional section, 0-byte file | valid (unchanged) |\n| Required section, no files at all | invalid (unchanged) |\n\n### Two deliberate decisions\n\n**1. The existing `required_section` i18n key is reused**, not replaced\nwith a new message. A new key would require every locale file to be\nupdated; the backend reused its existing error code for the same reason,\nand the two halves stay symmetrical.\n\n**2. Scoped to required sections only.** `!section.isRequired ||` stays\nfirst, so an empty file in an *optional* section is still accepted —\nmatching the backend''s scope exactly.\n\n### Why gating on `size` is safe\n\n`CartConfigurationItemFileType.size` is a non-nullable `Long`, and no\nin-flight or placeholder file ever reaches `validateValue`:\n\n- `option-file.vue` emits only **after** `await uploadFiles()` resolves.\n- `attachedAndUploadedFiles` (`useFiles.ts`) explicitly excludes files\nin `new` / `uploading` / `error` status.\n- Locally picked files carry the browser''s native `File.size`;\n`toUploadingFile` / `toUploadedFile` only add\n`status`/`progress`/`id`/`url` and never overwrite it.\n- Already-attached files take `size` from the server''s own record.\n\nSo a legitimate non-empty upload cannot read as `size <= 0` at\nvalidation time.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew\n`client-app/shared/catalog/composables/useConfigurableProduct.fileSize.test.ts`\n(6 cases, no existing test or story modified). It asserts only the\npublic API — `validateSections()`, `validationErrors`,\n`isRequiredConfigurationComplete` — since `validateValue` is private.\n\nVerified **red before / green after**: pre-fix, exactly two cases failed\n— the bug itself and the add-to-cart linkage (`expected true to be\nfalse`) — with the other four already green; post-fix all 6 pass.\n\n**The add-to-cart linkage is asserted, not assumed.**\n`isRequiredConfigurationComplete` routes through `validateValue`, so the\nsingle change both blocks the button and surfaces the inline error; a\ndedicated case pins that it flips from `true` to `false`.\n\nThe controls are genuinely discriminating: the \"0-byte alongside a real\nfile\" case kills an `every()`-style misfix, and the optional-section\ncase kills one that ignores `isRequired`.\n\nGates: sibling `useConfigurableProduct.test.ts` 43/43 still green and\nunmodified · `vue-tsc --build --force` clean · eslint 0 errors ·\nprettier clean · `vite build` succeeded.\n\n## Notes for the reviewer\n\n- **DO NOT MERGE until human review.**\n- **Needs deploy verification** — unit-proven only. The live symptom\n(button state + the inline error actually rendering) should be\nre-checked on a deployed build. Pairs with vc-module-x-cart#144; the\nbackend half is already verified live.\n- Out of scope, flagged during verification and **not** addressed here:\noptional File sections also drop disallowed types and oversize files\n**silently** (no inline error) — the same silent-failure pattern on a\ndifferent path. Worth a ticket of its own.\n\nPart of VCST-6000.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nArtifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2510-2e9a-2e9a6793.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"86c501525c03c8a5027ec3b7067c95eb8a81de92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/86c501525c03c8a5027ec3b7067c95eb8a81de92"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/8ce895b79046c19da4a76e848abe10e9a276d8cc","verification":{"payload":"tree 86c501525c03c8a5027ec3b7067c95eb8a81de92\nparent 270de5a070268b3d30e807d007941beca682e755\nauthor Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com> 1791298338 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791298338 +0200\n\nfix(VCST-6000): reject zero-byte files as satisfying a required File section (#2510)\n\n## Problem\n\nOn configurable products, a genuinely empty (0-byte) file **satisfies a\nREQUIRED File section** in the storefront: the chip renders `(0B)`, the\nsection header flips to the filename, and **\"Add to cart\" loses\n`disabled`** with nothing actually attached.\n\nThis is the **storefront half of VCST-6000**. The backend half\n([vc-module-x-cart#144](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-module-x-cart/pull/144))\nnow rejects the same state with `CONFIGURATION_SECTION_FILES_REQUIRED`,\nwhich made the remaining frontend gap the *visible* defect.\n\nMeasured live on vcptcore-qa against the fixed backend build (`XCart\n3.1037.0-pr-144`): the button stays enabled, the server refuses the line\nitem, and the buyer is shown **nothing** — no toast, no inline error,\nclean console, empty cart. A live button that silently does nothing.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`useConfigurableProduct.ts` → `validateValue` gated a required File\nsection on file **presence** only:\n\n```ts\nconst isValid = !section.isRequired || !!value?.files?.length;\n```\n\nA 0-byte file is present, so the gate passed.\n\nThis also left `validateValue` **inconsistent with itself** — the `text`\ncase one branch above already requires non-empty *content*:\n\n```ts\nconst isValid = !section.isRequired || !!value?.customText?.trim();\n```\n\nSo empty content did not satisfy a required Text section but did satisfy\na required File section. The backend fix rests on exactly the same\nargument, one layer down.\n\n## Change\n\n```diff\n       case CONFIGURABLE_SECTION_TYPES.file: {\n-        const isValid = !section.isRequired || !!value?.files?.length;\n+        const isValid = !section.isRequired || !!value?.files?.some((file) => file.size > 0);\n```\n\nOne line, plus a new test file. No other case, function or component\ntouched.\n\n| Case | Behaviour |\n|---|---|\n| Required section, only 0-byte file(s) | **invalid** (new) — button\nblocked, inline error shown |\n| Required section, one real file | valid |\n| Required section, 0-byte + real file | valid |\n| Optional section, 0-byte file | valid (unchanged) |\n| Required section, no files at all | invalid (unchanged) |\n\n### Two deliberate decisions\n\n**1. The existing `required_section` i18n key is reused**, not replaced\nwith a new message. A new key would require every locale file to be\nupdated; the backend reused its existing error code for the same reason,\nand the two halves stay symmetrical.\n\n**2. Scoped to required sections only.** `!section.isRequired ||` stays\nfirst, so an empty file in an *optional* section is still accepted —\nmatching the backend''s scope exactly.\n\n### Why gating on `size` is safe\n\n`CartConfigurationItemFileType.size` is a non-nullable `Long`, and no\nin-flight or placeholder file ever reaches `validateValue`:\n\n- `option-file.vue` emits only **after** `await uploadFiles()` resolves.\n- `attachedAndUploadedFiles` (`useFiles.ts`) explicitly excludes files\nin `new` / `uploading` / `error` status.\n- Locally picked files carry the browser''s native `File.size`;\n`toUploadingFile` / `toUploadedFile` only add\n`status`/`progress`/`id`/`url` and never overwrite it.\n- Already-attached files take `size` from the server''s own record.\n\nSo a legitimate non-empty upload cannot read as `size <= 0` at\nvalidation time.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew\n`client-app/shared/catalog/composables/useConfigurableProduct.fileSize.test.ts`\n(6 cases, no existing test or story modified). It asserts only the\npublic API — `validateSections()`, `validationErrors`,\n`isRequiredConfigurationComplete` — since `validateValue` is private.\n\nVerified **red before / green after**: pre-fix, exactly two cases failed\n— the bug itself and the add-to-cart linkage (`expected true to be\nfalse`) — with the other four already green; post-fix all 6 pass.\n\n**The add-to-cart linkage is asserted, not assumed.**\n`isRequiredConfigurationComplete` routes through `validateValue`, so the\nsingle change both blocks the button and surfaces the inline error; a\ndedicated case pins that it flips from `true` to `false`.\n\nThe controls are genuinely discriminating: the \"0-byte alongside a real\nfile\" case kills an `every()`-style misfix, and the optional-section\ncase kills one that ignores `isRequired`.\n\nGates: sibling `useConfigurableProduct.test.ts` 43/43 still green and\nunmodified · `vue-tsc --build --force` clean · eslint 0 errors ·\nprettier clean · `vite build` succeeded.\n\n## Notes for the reviewer\n\n- **DO NOT MERGE until human review.**\n- **Needs deploy verification** — unit-proven only. The live symptom\n(button state + the inline error actually rendering) should be\nre-checked on a deployed build. Pairs with vc-module-x-cart#144; the\nbackend half is already verified live.\n- Out of scope, flagged during verification and **not** addressed here:\noptional File sections also drop disallowed types and oversize files\n**silently** (no inline error) — the same silent-failure pattern on a\ndifferent path. Worth a ticket of its own.\n\nPart of VCST-6000.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nArtifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2510-2e9a-2e9a6793.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxQsiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAU8MQABJOVHGcp4JWtKLt/UYo+jpX\nGVKFIeygP927KyKzA8E4cGnhLPfU8E92qC3xy09IJgmhWvmBl+tWNDSdAHqqw4GO\nxuKw3gxRW0+JJPLlj5UE0kdyRwAHzWLMu5VBHgUnf3TbUtOpuqRrXmzxTwR8yyDM\n3zt+IKio+7/FM3p6P9J4bghXH+iqno57Bmz3pZGGapkO+T/UmOl74O0xL76EqqYq\nkTkNHvBmWfxLLtRqbjQKHnn+rgtYcKrqMdg1muyIDaUuMXFsnAsRZttXW+rGnhSj\njAuQulRK/pV2b2sA0yJEdJHrapqnKC7h3LfBHIayuvHDbUbYPmuSN7woHdsqe2kx\nug1LcfQbAJ304iyejy8BUQ9TAvMB4f8PjIqVUCCJmi6sebGlWvjkVoa/1v67UfwX\n9u/YsXTy8lmABFEQOxkYwmDAFDAbv0s1Hi/MwJmeeiCY/HV3zMwL5Ak/U8vAS25e\nIY45yXMmNcm7K9N7lCCuFTbnhRgW68zFYZ2FEs7HNpeCUt2Z/mvgLnUHG5ftILar\nrWCp9B0/kuRVtVdPUFJCP+L6BQkmPpRsxyXCD7bKy68vCXCa1QIoBxfi9Wb9rjHL\nI91DyqGQ8rtbYIsDths3p0eEPg4DQtDcL+GUogD5Biw90reOC68r1F1e8NV6I2hi\nJ08KLisu4isCOPV86XR9\n=YiEw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T14:52:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/8ce895b79046c19da4a76e848abe10e9a276d8cc","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDhjZTg5NWI3OTA0NmMxOWRhNGE3NmU4NDhhYmUxMGU5YTI3NmQ4Y2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/270de5a070268b3d30e807d007941beca682e755","sha":"270de5a070268b3d30e807d007941beca682e755","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/270de5a070268b3d30e807d007941beca682e755"}],"sha":"8ce895b79046c19da4a76e848abe10e9a276d8cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/8ce895b79046c19da4a76e848abe10e9a276d8cc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/231671742?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kutasinaelena/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kutasinaelena/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kutasinaelena/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kutasinaelena/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/kutasinaelena","id":231671742,"login":"kutasinaelena","node_id":"U_kgDODc8Hvg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kutasinaelena/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kutasinaelena/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kutasinaelena/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kutasinaelena/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kutasinaelena/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kutasinaelena","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/270de5a070268b3d30e807d007941beca682e755/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T14:50:05Z","email":"kutasina.elena@gmail.com","name":"Elena Kutasina"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T14:50:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(VCST-6175): keep localized status chip label on zero-match results (#2541)\n\n## Description\nOn the Sales Rep customer orders page, an applied status filter chip\nswitched from its localized label to the raw English status term (e.g.\n`Abgesagt` → `Cancelled` under German) whenever the result list came\nback empty. The chip now keeps its localized label regardless of how\nmany orders match.\nRoot cause: the chip label was looked up only in the current response''s\nstatus facet, and a zero-match response carries no bucket for the\napplied status, so the lookup fell back to the raw term.\n\nNo new props / events / slots · no new GraphQL fields · no new settings\n· no new dependencies.\n\n## Breaking changes\n- Component contract (props / events / slots): None.\n- GraphQL operations the client sends (fields, variables): None.\n- Settings (`$cfg` keys, theme settings): None.\n- Runtime behaviour: with a status filter applied and zero matching\norders, the status chip showed the raw status term; it now shows the\nlocalized label already seen in an earlier response (the raw term\nremains the fallback only for a status never returned by the facet).\n\n## New dependencies\nNone.\n\n> **Note** — The page now remembers every status label returned by the\nstatus facet and resolves chip labels from that map; `statusOptions`\nitself is unchanged, so the filter drawer''s options and counts still\nreflect the current response. The map is never cleared: switching\nlanguage reloads the app, so labels cannot leak across cultures. Kept in\nthe page rather than the composable to avoid changing the composable''s\nreturned shape. Out of scope: the drawer''s status group still hides when\nthe facet is empty (separate behaviour). Reviewer focus: localized\nstatus labels on the Sales Rep orders filter chips.\n\n<details><summary>Auto-fix evidence (red → green)</summary>\n\n- Reproduction:\n`client-app/modules/sales-rep/pages/customer-orders.test.ts` — \"keeps\nthe localized status chip label when the result set comes back empty\":\nthe chip reads `Abgesagt`, then after an empty status facet it still\nreads `Abgesagt` (was `Cancelled`). Fails on the base commit, passes\nwith this fix.\n- Local checks:\n  - vue-tsc --build — pass\n- lint (changed files) — 0 errors (1 pre-existing warning, untouched\nline)\n- vitest (customer-orders + useSalesRepCustomerOrders specs) — 33/33\npass\n- build — not run (page-local script change, no shared/core/UI-kit code)\n\n**⚠ Needs visual verification.** Logic is unit-proven. The chip label\nbehaviour from VCST-6175 must be re-confirmed on a real deployment\n(German culture, status filter + zero-match search).\n</details>\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6175\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2541-828b-828bbbe1.zip\n> 🤖 Opened by `/vc-fix:qa-fix`. **Human review required before merge —\ndo not auto-merge.**\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Anatolii Vasilev <anatolii.vslvv@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"4747f4172241b19e1b960e716128b2113d8fbf24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/4747f4172241b19e1b960e716128b2113d8fbf24"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/270de5a070268b3d30e807d007941beca682e755","verification":{"payload":"tree 4747f4172241b19e1b960e716128b2113d8fbf24\nparent c2c7c68cfb9c52225f45989a69f881249bba6d2b\nauthor Elena Kutasina <kutasina.elena@gmail.com> 1791298205 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791298205 +0200\n\nfix(VCST-6175): keep localized status chip label on zero-match results (#2541)\n\n## Description\nOn the Sales Rep customer orders page, an applied status filter chip\nswitched from its localized label to the raw English status term (e.g.\n`Abgesagt` → `Cancelled` under German) whenever the result list came\nback empty. The chip now keeps its localized label regardless of how\nmany orders match.\nRoot cause: the chip label was looked up only in the current response''s\nstatus facet, and a zero-match response carries no bucket for the\napplied status, so the lookup fell back to the raw term.\n\nNo new props / events / slots · no new GraphQL fields · no new settings\n· no new dependencies.\n\n## Breaking changes\n- Component contract (props / events / slots): None.\n- GraphQL operations the client sends (fields, variables): None.\n- Settings (`$cfg` keys, theme settings): None.\n- Runtime behaviour: with a status filter applied and zero matching\norders, the status chip showed the raw status term; it now shows the\nlocalized label already seen in an earlier response (the raw term\nremains the fallback only for a status never returned by the facet).\n\n## New dependencies\nNone.\n\n> **Note** — The page now remembers every status label returned by the\nstatus facet and resolves chip labels from that map; `statusOptions`\nitself is unchanged, so the filter drawer''s options and counts still\nreflect the current response. The map is never cleared: switching\nlanguage reloads the app, so labels cannot leak across cultures. Kept in\nthe page rather than the composable to avoid changing the composable''s\nreturned shape. Out of scope: the drawer''s status group still hides when\nthe facet is empty (separate behaviour). Reviewer focus: localized\nstatus labels on the Sales Rep orders filter chips.\n\n<details><summary>Auto-fix evidence (red → green)</summary>\n\n- Reproduction:\n`client-app/modules/sales-rep/pages/customer-orders.test.ts` — \"keeps\nthe localized status chip label when the result set comes back empty\":\nthe chip reads `Abgesagt`, then after an empty status facet it still\nreads `Abgesagt` (was `Cancelled`). Fails on the base commit, passes\nwith this fix.\n- Local checks:\n  - vue-tsc --build — pass\n- lint (changed files) — 0 errors (1 pre-existing warning, untouched\nline)\n- vitest (customer-orders + useSalesRepCustomerOrders specs) — 33/33\npass\n- build — not run (page-local script change, no shared/core/UI-kit code)\n\n**⚠ Needs visual verification.** Logic is unit-proven. The chip label\nbehaviour from VCST-6175 must be re-confirmed on a real deployment\n(German culture, status filter + zero-match search).\n</details>\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6175\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2541-828b-828bbbe1.zip\n> 🤖 Opened by `/vc-fix:qa-fix`. **Human review required before merge —\ndo not auto-merge.**\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Anatolii Vasilev <anatolii.vslvv@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxQqdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1PAQADNh4BBCcUJUF21SvIBmSYSw\n86WrlmJ4ieFdQdEJ8G1U6g6ROfnqoiUhEIzsGqsjiE8kc/r13lTLdZEbONKFhCGI\nfC5PBPtvFe2eGyD6uaF70ggrbZHfQbATnVcmFrPYr0+Trk5HcKzHP3wRkSjulJh4\n4YTk85KDl34kD8qa4QnKLNvNp8GYHWCZ6L81P1+JiqJdIDLVRuUOAH5hlYAh81i1\nFCtNNUiouMqOh6mGDQ3uQs+cUCak3mX2JqMGTI8bL0r4FfYsBvZzbmFGN2/1TqVB\noM873kjcptsRm0D17CRjyxsLxWUCqeMfEdb4Q8qCRsEaLsAqBDdT3sBHJYi+HPw5\nPhpQ6UtuD1ZzvKNPBko+JF0puqlUwlKQv7F7XIeLgKpPIPK90hHCkC/lr0TjKxHn\nnj0WGo0TIuJTUDYzSsu4ykfdNYmaUZx9iVPJXKgrvOKYXjphiSy0AAWg1p9qnL4k\nGZbGVuW9M8M0Z+gRf0uymsAVnbXbSdoG8XICqzFr1PCU6/fXTRUeVtxBjBXde8gz\nBiuqAQox5agXctVk5m42DcGQnE5x0aan/Hi9KOCIxFKy+h8FUqR14tykV/VchjBp\n6zdx7Q2kzZIMoztJN/T9dzEeRTKt1gXElFgtDMuO/PLKb7kPfQEaTdhdDzUihB/V\neWcolN0x1EMAE8sAXrSB\n=i2SS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T14:50:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/270de5a070268b3d30e807d007941beca682e755","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDI3MGRlNWEwNzAyNjhiM2QzMGU4MDdkMDA3OTQxYmVjYTY4MmU3NTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/c2c7c68cfb9c52225f45989a69f881249bba6d2b","sha":"c2c7c68cfb9c52225f45989a69f881249bba6d2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/c2c7c68cfb9c52225f45989a69f881249bba6d2b"}],"sha":"270de5a070268b3d30e807d007941beca682e755","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/270de5a070268b3d30e807d007941beca682e755"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18286430?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ivan-kalachikov","id":18286430,"login":"ivan-kalachikov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Mjg2NDMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/c2c7c68cfb9c52225f45989a69f881249bba6d2b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T13:51:15Z","email":"ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com","name":"Ivan Kalachikov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T13:51:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VCST-5707): rework list sharing (#2476)\n\n## Description\n\nA Sales Rep can share one list with several customers at once. The\ncombined \"List settings\" dialog is split into **Rename** and **Share**,\nand the list-actions menu becomes **Rename / Share / Remove list**.\n\n**Draft until VCST-5925 lands.** The generated types here came from\n`vcptcore-dev`. Re-run codegen and `generate:backend-packages` against a\nbackend carrying the merged schema before this is merged.\n\n### Dialogs\n\n- **Rename** (`AddOrUpdateWishlistModal`) — name and description;\ncreates and renames. A new list starts private.\n- **Share** (`ShareWishlistModal`) — scope tabs, the sharing link, and\nthe selected scope''s own controls. Primary action reads **Share** for a\nscope with recipients, **Save** otherwise.\n- List details gains a Share button.\n- Each dialog sends only the fields it owns, so a rename cannot\noverwrite sharing and a share cannot overwrite the name.\n- Sharing is offered to the list''s owner only.\n\n### Scopes\n\n- `VcTabSwitch` tabs replace the select: Private, My organization,\nAnyone with link, Specific customers. The registry gained `icon` and\n`order`.\n- The selected scope''s controls are kept alive, so switching tabs\npreserves the draft. The cache dies with the dialog.\n- The sales-rep Customer scope plugs in through the existing registry.\n\n### Recipients\n\n- Reads use `sharingSetting.targets`; `sharedWithId` is gone. The module\nowning the scope resolves each target''s name, city and logo server-side.\n- Writes are deltas — `addSharedWithIds` / `removeSharedWithIds` — never\na replace-set.\n- Multi-select picker over one page of 100 served customers, two-line\noptions, client-side filter.\n- Recipients list: per-row remove, `Clear all` with undo, and a `Show\nall N` / `Show less` toggle past three rows.\n- Emptying the list does not stop sharing — Save stays disabled and the\nfield says so. Changing the scope is the way out.\n\n### Message\n\n- Saved with the share (`sharingSetting.message`), offered whether or\nnot anyone new is added, capped at 250 characters (the backend allows\n1024).\n- One `sendCustomerCommunication` per save reaches every newly added\norganization; a member of several receives it once.\n- The success toast counts the audience the server persisted.\n\n### Stopping a share\n\n- Changing the scope of a shared list asks for confirmation first.\n- It asks only where an audience is lost: not on a first share out of\nPrivate, not when recipients change inside one scope, and not when the\nscope being left has no recipients.\n- The confirmation renders inside the share dialog''s own tree rather\nthan on the modal stack.\n\n### Changed surface\n\n- `WishlistDropdownMenu`: new `shareable` prop, new `share` emit, and\n`edit` / `remove` now carry the trigger element so a modal opened from\nthe menu can return the focus to something still on screen.\n- `WishlistCard`: same three emits, each forwarding that element.\n- `SalesRepCommunicationInputType.organizationId` → `organizationIds`;\none send now covers the whole newly added audience.\n- Locale keys removed: `list_card.list_edit_button`,\n`add_or_update_wishlist_modal.sharing_scope_label`,\n`add_or_update_wishlist_modal.sharing_scope_placeholder`,\n`sales_rep.list_sharing.share_replace_hint`.\n`list_details.list_settings_button` and\n`add_or_update_wishlist_modal.edit_mode_title` became linked messages\npointing at the new `rename_list_button`.\n\n### Not in this PR\n\nSelect-all with its row counter, and picker paging — both belong to\nVCST-5923.\n\n### Notes for review\n\n- Design spec:\n`client-app/modules/sales-rep/specs/VCST-5707-lists-sharing/2026-09-14-lists-sharing-design.md`.\n- `core/api/graphql/types.ts` carries two fields unrelated to this\nticket from the dev environment (`isLockedForCurrentUser`, Loyalty''s\n`storeId`). They go on the regeneration above.\n- The core contract is regenerated and `@vc-frontend/core` goes 0.1.0 →\n**0.2.0**, the breaking level the README asks for on the 0.x line.\n`IWishlistSharingScopeControlsType.payload` changed shape and the scope\nelement''s props were renamed, but no export was removed — and the\nauto-bump only compares exported names, so it settled on a patch. That\nmatters: a plugin built against 0.1.x declares `requiredHostVersion`\n\"0.1.0\", which `^0.1.0` still satisfies on 0.1.1, so it would load and\nthen read props that no longer arrive. At 0.2.0 the manifest gate and\nthe shared-singleton range (raised to match in `federation.mjs`) both\nrefuse it with a reason. `vc-module-sales-rep`''s StorefrontApp is that\nplugin and needs a release of its own.\n- The contract also picks up what landed on dev since it was last built:\n`isLockedForCurrentUser` (VCST-5317) and the `VcTable` header slot scope\n(VCST-5472).\n- New test ids `wishlist-sharing-*`. The e2e flows in vc-testing-module\nthat went through the old combined dialog need updating.\n- \"Remove list\" follows the Acceptance''s Action-wheel screenshot and the\nFigma menu; the Acceptance text says \"Delete\". Its icons deliberately do\nnot: the Figma draws a pencil and a trash can, while\n`address-dropdown-menu` and `members-dropdown-menu` both use `edit` and\n`delete-2` and colour only the icon. Matching the Figma in one menu of\nthree is the worse outcome, so this one keeps its siblings'' pair and the\nFigma''s belongs to a pass over all three.\n- `viewItemList` now fires once per list id rather than on every\nreassignment of `list`. Saving from a dialog would otherwise send a\nsecond impression for the same items with no navigation in between; the\nsame change also stops it re-firing on an item removal or a refetch of\nthe open list.\n- The dialog leaves out the \"Notify via\" checkboxes the Figma carries,\nand its recipient rows show the customer''s address where the Figma shows\nan email — both settled with the requester. Every share goes out on\nemail and push, so the checkboxes would never be anything but ticked and\ndisabled, and there is no email search behind the picker.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5707\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2476-7d1a-7d1a4b3a.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: yuskithedeveloper <yuskianywhere@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"3350ba50ea407626c0ac3a778febc28b9b641e4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/3350ba50ea407626c0ac3a778febc28b9b641e4e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/c2c7c68cfb9c52225f45989a69f881249bba6d2b","verification":{"payload":"tree 3350ba50ea407626c0ac3a778febc28b9b641e4e\nparent 45334f968d9d785a75e9754e86bdac7e1e96e22e\nauthor Ivan Kalachikov <ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com> 1791294675 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791294675 +0100\n\nfeat(VCST-5707): rework list sharing (#2476)\n\n## Description\n\nA Sales Rep can share one list with several customers at once. The\ncombined \"List settings\" dialog is split into **Rename** and **Share**,\nand the list-actions menu becomes **Rename / Share / Remove list**.\n\n**Draft until VCST-5925 lands.** The generated types here came from\n`vcptcore-dev`. Re-run codegen and `generate:backend-packages` against a\nbackend carrying the merged schema before this is merged.\n\n### Dialogs\n\n- **Rename** (`AddOrUpdateWishlistModal`) — name and description;\ncreates and renames. A new list starts private.\n- **Share** (`ShareWishlistModal`) — scope tabs, the sharing link, and\nthe selected scope''s own controls. Primary action reads **Share** for a\nscope with recipients, **Save** otherwise.\n- List details gains a Share button.\n- Each dialog sends only the fields it owns, so a rename cannot\noverwrite sharing and a share cannot overwrite the name.\n- Sharing is offered to the list''s owner only.\n\n### Scopes\n\n- `VcTabSwitch` tabs replace the select: Private, My organization,\nAnyone with link, Specific customers. The registry gained `icon` and\n`order`.\n- The selected scope''s controls are kept alive, so switching tabs\npreserves the draft. The cache dies with the dialog.\n- The sales-rep Customer scope plugs in through the existing registry.\n\n### Recipients\n\n- Reads use `sharingSetting.targets`; `sharedWithId` is gone. The module\nowning the scope resolves each target''s name, city and logo server-side.\n- Writes are deltas — `addSharedWithIds` / `removeSharedWithIds` — never\na replace-set.\n- Multi-select picker over one page of 100 served customers, two-line\noptions, client-side filter.\n- Recipients list: per-row remove, `Clear all` with undo, and a `Show\nall N` / `Show less` toggle past three rows.\n- Emptying the list does not stop sharing — Save stays disabled and the\nfield says so. Changing the scope is the way out.\n\n### Message\n\n- Saved with the share (`sharingSetting.message`), offered whether or\nnot anyone new is added, capped at 250 characters (the backend allows\n1024).\n- One `sendCustomerCommunication` per save reaches every newly added\norganization; a member of several receives it once.\n- The success toast counts the audience the server persisted.\n\n### Stopping a share\n\n- Changing the scope of a shared list asks for confirmation first.\n- It asks only where an audience is lost: not on a first share out of\nPrivate, not when recipients change inside one scope, and not when the\nscope being left has no recipients.\n- The confirmation renders inside the share dialog''s own tree rather\nthan on the modal stack.\n\n### Changed surface\n\n- `WishlistDropdownMenu`: new `shareable` prop, new `share` emit, and\n`edit` / `remove` now carry the trigger element so a modal opened from\nthe menu can return the focus to something still on screen.\n- `WishlistCard`: same three emits, each forwarding that element.\n- `SalesRepCommunicationInputType.organizationId` → `organizationIds`;\none send now covers the whole newly added audience.\n- Locale keys removed: `list_card.list_edit_button`,\n`add_or_update_wishlist_modal.sharing_scope_label`,\n`add_or_update_wishlist_modal.sharing_scope_placeholder`,\n`sales_rep.list_sharing.share_replace_hint`.\n`list_details.list_settings_button` and\n`add_or_update_wishlist_modal.edit_mode_title` became linked messages\npointing at the new `rename_list_button`.\n\n### Not in this PR\n\nSelect-all with its row counter, and picker paging — both belong to\nVCST-5923.\n\n### Notes for review\n\n- Design spec:\n`client-app/modules/sales-rep/specs/VCST-5707-lists-sharing/2026-09-14-lists-sharing-design.md`.\n- `core/api/graphql/types.ts` carries two fields unrelated to this\nticket from the dev environment (`isLockedForCurrentUser`, Loyalty''s\n`storeId`). They go on the regeneration above.\n- The core contract is regenerated and `@vc-frontend/core` goes 0.1.0 →\n**0.2.0**, the breaking level the README asks for on the 0.x line.\n`IWishlistSharingScopeControlsType.payload` changed shape and the scope\nelement''s props were renamed, but no export was removed — and the\nauto-bump only compares exported names, so it settled on a patch. That\nmatters: a plugin built against 0.1.x declares `requiredHostVersion`\n\"0.1.0\", which `^0.1.0` still satisfies on 0.1.1, so it would load and\nthen read props that no longer arrive. At 0.2.0 the manifest gate and\nthe shared-singleton range (raised to match in `federation.mjs`) both\nrefuse it with a reason. `vc-module-sales-rep`''s StorefrontApp is that\nplugin and needs a release of its own.\n- The contract also picks up what landed on dev since it was last built:\n`isLockedForCurrentUser` (VCST-5317) and the `VcTable` header slot scope\n(VCST-5472).\n- New test ids `wishlist-sharing-*`. The e2e flows in vc-testing-module\nthat went through the old combined dialog need updating.\n- \"Remove list\" follows the Acceptance''s Action-wheel screenshot and the\nFigma menu; the Acceptance text says \"Delete\". Its icons deliberately do\nnot: the Figma draws a pencil and a trash can, while\n`address-dropdown-menu` and `members-dropdown-menu` both use `edit` and\n`delete-2` and colour only the icon. Matching the Figma in one menu of\nthree is the worse outcome, so this one keeps its siblings'' pair and the\nFigma''s belongs to a pass over all three.\n- `viewItemList` now fires once per list id rather than on every\nreassignment of `list`. Saving from a dialog would otherwise send a\nsecond impression for the same items with no navigation in between; the\nsame change also stops it re-firing on an item removal or a refetch of\nthe open list.\n- The dialog leaves out the \"Notify via\" checkboxes the Figma carries,\nand its recipient rows show the customer''s address where the Figma shows\nan email — both settled with the requester. Every share goes out on\nemail and push, so the checkboxes would never be anything but ticked and\ndisabled, and there is no email search behind the picker.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5707\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2476-7d1a-7d1a4b3a.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: yuskithedeveloper <yuskianywhere@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxPzTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYRMQAEycxtlH1/JTtzJk5GKbytaA\ndpsKszsel18G87daEoGTaQN69IoesuilEfKLq020aR5pue5tLvrKB9b6QeB0mOiJ\nOdnR3a6PYQ7klL2FPfD9WymSKuqodPSsgpWbam/oTIJXoeTUcJ6VKZrAtff3DYMo\nQwbmhYDD+Tz4Ekc1TqOREgVV8U/h/oLCDOEdPOHPECSD6mA4g+fq1Yh7V8BFBzsl\nvINuB/vDKDmeZD+2t+2Vc