9a69f881249bba6d2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/c2c7c68cfb9c52225f45989a69f881249bba6d2b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18286430?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ivan-kalachikov","id":18286430,"login":"ivan-kalachikov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Mjg2NDMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/45334f968d9d785a75e9754e86bdac7e1e96e22e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T13:19:40Z","email":"ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com","name":"Ivan Kalachikov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T13:19:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(VCST-6153, VCST-6180): keep sales-rep table values on one line (#2537)\n\n## Description\nIn the Sales Rep customer profile, VcTable''s `word-break: break-word`\nlet long text in one column squeeze the value columns until they split\nmid-value:\n- **Top sellers** (VCST-6153): a long product name split Revenue and\nrank (`$1,462.1` / `5`, `1` / `0`). Rank, Units and Revenue now get\n`white-space: nowrap` (`top-sellers__number`).\n- **My recent orders** (VCST-6180): a long order number split Total and\nDate (`$33.0` / `0`, `Aug 17,` / `2026`). Date, Items and Total now get\n`white-space: nowrap` (`sales-rep-orders__value`). The full customer\norders page (`customer-orders.vue`) gets the same treatment for Date and\nTotal.\n\nThe shared VcTable rule is unchanged.\n\nVerified in Chrome at 1300 px with long product names and order numbers\nswapped into the rendered cells: every value stays on one line, only the\nProduct and Order # columns wrap, and nothing overflows horizontally.\nTop sellers was also checked at 1030 px.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6153\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6180\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2537-07fe-07fe166f.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"af104d7cf34cdbf77e885902fc1e86fdc7d98578","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/af104d7cf34cdbf77e885902fc1e86fdc7d98578"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/45334f968d9d785a75e9754e86bdac7e1e96e22e","verification":{"payload":"tree af104d7cf34cdbf77e885902fc1e86fdc7d98578\nparent d450f5482102013c51de339843465e5d617ff204\nauthor Ivan Kalachikov <ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com> 1791292780 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791292780 +0100\n\nfix(VCST-6153, VCST-6180): keep sales-rep table values on one line (#2537)\n\n## Description\nIn the Sales Rep customer profile, VcTable''s `word-break: break-word`\nlet long text in one column squeeze the value columns until they split\nmid-value:\n- **Top sellers** (VCST-6153): a long product name split Revenue and\nrank (`$1,462.1` / `5`, `1` / `0`). Rank, Units and Revenue now get\n`white-space: nowrap` (`top-sellers__number`).\n- **My recent orders** (VCST-6180): a long order number split Total and\nDate (`$33.0` / `0`, `Aug 17,` / `2026`). Date, Items and Total now get\n`white-space: nowrap` (`sales-rep-orders__value`). The full customer\norders page (`customer-orders.vue`) gets the same treatment for Date and\nTotal.\n\nThe shared VcTable rule is unchanged.\n\nVerified in Chrome at 1300 px with long product names and order numbers\nswapped into the rendered cells: every value stays on one line, only the\nProduct and Order # columns wrap, and nothing overflows horizontally.\nTop sellers was also checked at 1030 px.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6153\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6180\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2537-07fe-07fe166f.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxPVsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyVwQADREaW1Ccg9NnKO9ZRZyMA4+\nR9TOUxrXtrGzAdQhmExR34svbUq2YOnp1H22noZw6La1TS3fvMYaWasWlsEhtVTo\nMBZUzBqSZQ6XBlY2LMktT6hGhOKrUbi9x7XXtPO04MQxHGEPjqhcXT4W3gg5CxQM\n/oW9wLZ4IJPI05nZO+rrqudpD8zRsD/YZpPS5w3fwru3nt6s13QCxGl8FQbLvCew\nYhOMptMkKNjNz0HA4y8G9Q/ljyd80gjluE1/kWTdl4qzRyMGR/WwIfD4DNNfREP9\n8SlrRCgAS87NzOM3u8mlt/FN+sUXxYWFj0glr8FPVv0OwgHES7WjQuFx6vgIa9zy\nPKSAE8NK2VVY+WCbYhNtVFo+teikxPP2kwkbZnrLOx0B+ACDnQOVPlA6bOtOj3ER\nnO9rSFCs6GKBFILlH71eHUBdL7mDc0CKcG/g4Y6/nAWe9ws1gQf8FBYbajYGUsLZ\n2N342lSQsYhxgIh7O5sWzwRoEXTtysbywOHyYSA5znRLRIU6xN88b3G5AXOIdJG9\n6LcPcztRPu9pUDZ2Np/06V/DYtjtIj7wzgVFQS6Tod+UAKdNDiutDoX5hs2LqAyc\nmDWNBO2LMkfERTfBrrdR1GH8gF7brR7zKfM6XzqinGG+yOcaXRmyQLe7KGbYslYF\nEYnHVwllbF6WUKuGIo1o\n=ipn7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T13:19:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/45334f968d9d785a75e9754e86bdac7e1e96e22e","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDQ1MzM0Zjk2OGQ5ZDc4NWE3NWU5NzU0ZTg2YmRhYzdlMWU5NmUyMmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/d450f5482102013c51de339843465e5d617ff204","sha":"d450f5482102013c51de339843465e5d617ff204","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/d450f5482102013c51de339843465e5d617ff204"}],"sha":"45334f968d9d785a75e9754e86bdac7e1e96e22e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/45334f968d9d785a75e9754e86bdac7e1e96e22e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56412054?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Lenajava1","id":56412054,"login":"Lenajava1","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2NDEyMDU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/d450f5482102013c51de339843465e5d617ff204/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T09:40:52Z","email":"56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Elena Mutykova"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T09:40:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(VCST-6176): render Returns icon as outline (alias receipt-refund to undo-2) (#2544)\n\n## Summary\n\nFixes [VCST-6176](https://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6176):\nthe Returns item in the account menu (desktop and mobile) and the\n\"Request return\" button showed the legacy solid 20×20 `receipt-refund`\nglyph, while the other menu items show outline (Lucide) icons.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`receipt-refund` (added with the Returns module) has no outline asset\nand no entry in `icon-aliases.ts`, so `resolveIcon()` used the\ntransitional outline→solid fallback.\n\n## Change\n\n- `ui-kit/utilities/icon-aliases.ts`: add `\"receipt-refund\": \"undo-2\"`.\n`undo-2` is the glyph the ticket reporter chose; `outline/undo-2.svg` is\nalready in the kit. One alias line covers all three call sites (desktop\nmenu, mobile menu, \"Request return\" button).\n- `ui-kit/utilities/icons.test.ts`: add `[\"receipt-refund\", true]` to\nthe existing `resolveIcon` `isOutline` table, next to the other alias\nchecks (per review).\n\n## Proof\n\n- With the alias line removed, the new table row fails (`expected false\nto be true`). With the fix, it passes.\n- `icons.test.ts` and `vc-icon.test.ts` pass (35/35).\n- `eslint` passes on the changed files.\n\n## Notes\n\n- The sales-rep module has the same fallback for `office-building` and\n`presentation-chart-bar`. Those are left out of scope.\n- **Needs deploy verification:** visually check the icon on vcst-qa\nafter deploy.\n- Do not auto-merge. This PR is waiting for human review.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n[VCST-6176]:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6176?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4de8bf26a756c33dad77df92649641430def5092","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/4de8bf26a756c33dad77df92649641430def5092"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/d450f5482102013c51de339843465e5d617ff204","verification":{"payload":"tree 4de8bf26a756c33dad77df92649641430def5092\nparent 8581c575b9491d8c788c1d4e2160adef8c93a8a9\nauthor Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com> 1791279652 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791279652 +0200\n\nfix(VCST-6176): render Returns icon as outline (alias receipt-refund to undo-2) (#2544)\n\n## Summary\n\nFixes [VCST-6176](https://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6176):\nthe Returns item in the account menu (desktop and mobile) and the\n\"Request return\" button showed the legacy solid 20×20 `receipt-refund`\nglyph, while the other menu items show outline (Lucide) icons.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`receipt-refund` (added with the Returns module) has no outline asset\nand no entry in `icon-aliases.ts`, so `resolveIcon()` used the\ntransitional outline→solid fallback.\n\n## Change\n\n- `ui-kit/utilities/icon-aliases.ts`: add `\"receipt-refund\": \"undo-2\"`.\n`undo-2` is the glyph the ticket reporter chose; `outline/undo-2.svg` is\nalready in the kit. One alias line covers all three call sites (desktop\nmenu, mobile menu, \"Request return\" button).\n- `ui-kit/utilities/icons.test.ts`: add `[\"receipt-refund\", true]` to\nthe existing `resolveIcon` `isOutline` table, next to the other alias\nchecks (per review).\n\n## Proof\n\n- With the alias line removed, the new table row fails (`expected false\nto be true`). With the fix, it passes.\n- `icons.test.ts` and `vc-icon.test.ts` pass (35/35).\n- `eslint` passes on the changed files.\n\n## Notes\n\n- The sales-rep module has the same fallback for `office-building` and\n`presentation-chart-bar`. Those are left out of scope.\n- **Needs deploy verification:** visually check the icon on vcst-qa\nafter deploy.\n- Do not auto-merge. This PR is waiting for human review.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n[VCST-6176]:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6176?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxMIkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKkEQAD7G9K7Jt63HC/u5oOBZqKGA\nf7y7N3U2VKAhFcElNLI/U3i8xBA99hWwXr3OJi2+Xxok5Spf4w8yTGcbbNxIDbX3\nzC3NPE8RxZ9bKBEpkiEgb3kS+2WHw/0IOlDYA76j/PqJj4/ImTvvXsJKTLfOMB+x\n4AEqm9y9UA6QUnmgQKo6V093qcMNZVFCF4EauT+e4dMyM/zEuiZuzsJxu6kXSOOJ\nM3i2DGDix4njQyIaMelASoiBF1RmryMbycJOxpC4SQpZddiRJyfijh9zRepqbjdi\nc5A6fevxMUvjlZpEp9Zsa/gN9f7JNM2J7cVasVIzUDQuyT390u4p6EW/odAtq9k/\n6xwfh9pN+rZNAWXfDstndVUHhzBxN9nVRSaErGXOfqlWmyHlro/t4O10KrY857xx\nNya+IOTLNhOazYS6+TAarK7OqRzKdu8yfqo+QuasAf0ZVs0+yOdck8Y/b0bFGzBT\nZ4O1EMBKEyliiMhB2Lx3DK0RjOey7dPwfcx4fDiYwRYvoofiJ0tROEEUEWGjRtZo\nrudC9ghCde39mC+O1YMy9Iez9pac6QqK1qqdJmBusqX9w95TnWjzA7qqU7pRgU7l\nVmsk3Re+pB6zqVWQq2wzp6W5i7IGF5I8c2LXLl6JbQLWDL+7mjmHPyTmmEIHgU32\nJEWHi1RoOQsSw3QCwHvF\n=9xCN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T09:40:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/d450f5482102013c51de339843465e5d617ff204","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKGQ0NTBmNTQ4MjEwMjAxM2M1MWRlMzM5ODQzNDY1ZTVkNjE3ZmYyMDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/8581c575b9491d8c788c1d4e2160adef8c93a8a9","sha":"8581c575b9491d8c788c1d4e2160adef8c93a8a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/8581c575b9491d8c788c1d4e2160adef8c93a8a9"}],"sha":"d450f5482102013c51de339843465e5d617ff204","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/d450f5482102013c51de339843465e5d617ff204"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16372194?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/goldenmaya","id":16372194,"login":"goldenmaya","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzcyMTk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/8581c575b9491d8c788c1d4e2160adef8c93a8a9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:35:49Z","email":"mayapavlovna@gmail.com","name":"Maiia Diachkovskaia"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:35:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(VCST-5945): keep the signed-in top header on one line at 1280 (#2534)\n\n## Description\n\nAt 1280px, for a signed-in multi-organization user with long names,\n\"Ship to: Select address\" wrapped inside the 40px top bar and ran into\n\"Call us\".\n\n**Root cause.** The organization and user names have `truncate\nxl:max-w-80`, but their wrapper was `xl:inline`. On inline boxes neither\n`truncate` nor `max-width` has any effect, so the names never truncated\nand kept their full width. The right column is `shrink-0` (added in\n#1866 so that a long ship-to address truncates instead of breaking the\nbar), so all of the squeeze fell on the ship-to placeholder. The\nplaceholder had no `nowrap`, so it wrapped. 1280 is the worst width\nbecause the names first appear at `xl`.\n\n**Fix (4 class changes):**\n- The names wrapper is now `gap-1 xl:flex`, so `truncate` and\n`max-width` finally apply. The full name is still available in `title`.\n- Between `xl` (1280) and `2xl` (1500) the names are capped at\n`max-w-32` when both organization and user are shown.\nSingle-organization users keep `xl:max-w-80`.\n- `.ship-to-selector__placeholder` gets `truncate`, matching\n`__selected`.\n- The right column keeps `shrink-0`, as on `dev`.\n\nAn intermediate version removed that `shrink-0`. Review caught that this\nreopens #1866: with a long selected address the page overflowed to\n1172px at 1024. That was confirmed in the live app and reverted.\n\n**Side effect for forks:** names longer than 320px now truncate at every\nwidth ≥1500. Before, that cap never took effect.\n\n### Ticket''s open questions\n- **Production-length names:** with \"Lone Star Outfitters / Elena\nMutykova\" and \"Purple Pink123 / Sasha Sasha\" the bar is clean on `dev`\nat every width. The bug needs long names like the QA fixtures\n(`AGENT-TEST-Org-BuildRight-20260310` / `AGENT-TEST-MultiOrgAlt FE`).\n- **Range on `dev` with those names:**\n  - 1280: 2-line wrap and a 70px overlap.\n  - 1366 and 1440: 2-line wrap that spills out of the bar.\n  - ≥1500: clean.\n- **QA badge over \"Dashboard\":** this is an environment artefact and is\nnot touched.\n\n### Verification\nLive app on the QA backend, signed-in multi-org user, in Playwright. All\nof the following were on at the same time: language, currency, ship-to,\nphone, dark-mode toggle.\n- 7 widths (1024, 1280, 1366, 1440, 1499, 1500, 1920) × 3 name sets ×\nwith and without a 107-character address (injected into the DOM) = 42\ncases.\n  - 0px overlap between any left and right descendant.\n  - No horizontal page overflow.\n  - No header element taller than 40px.\n- Worst case, 1280 with the QA names: \"Select ad…\" (69 of 90px) and\nnames at 128px.\n- Single-org, simulated in the DOM: a 41-character name stays\nuntruncated (291px) at 1280–1500, with no overlap or overflow.\n- The account dropdown still opens right-aligned under its button.\n- `yarn validate:types` is clean, and eslint on the changed files\nreports 0 errors.\n\n**Not walked:** a real single-org account, operator impersonation, and\nnon-English locales in the live app. The right column is `shrink-0` as\non `dev`, so link labels cannot wrap.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5945\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2534-e127-e1271b10.zip\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Low Risk**\n> CSS/layout-only changes in the header; no auth, API, or data-flow\nchanges. Long names may truncate earlier at ≥1500px when both org and\nuser labels show.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Fixes the signed-in **top header** wrapping and overlapping **“Call\nus”** around **1280px** when organization/user names and ship-to text\nare long.\n> \n> The account label wrapper switches from **`xl:inline` to `xl:flex`**\nso **`truncate`** and **`max-width`** apply to org/user names; multi-org\nusers get **`xl:max-w-32`** until **`2xl`**, while single-org keeps\n**`xl:max-w-80`**. The ship-to **“Select address”** placeholder now uses\n**`truncate`**, aligned with the selected-address styling, so it\nellipsizes instead of wrapping inside the 40px bar.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\ne1271b10b8788aa5958633a9bdd9d18a03daa0a9. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->","tree":{"sha":"2f23ec05e3b17b5ba92dea76b466f31058537554","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/2f23ec05e3b17b5ba92dea76b466f31058537554"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/8581c575b9491d8c788c1d4e2160adef8c93a8a9","verification":{"payload":"tree 2f23ec05e3b17b5ba92dea76b466f31058537554\nparent dbc3f53b7243011ee423310389e44936d6897b12\nauthor Maiia Diachkovskaia <mayapavlovna@gmail.com> 1791272149 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791272149 +0300\n\nfix(VCST-5945): keep the signed-in top header on one line at 1280 (#2534)\n\n## Description\n\nAt 1280px, for a signed-in multi-organization user with long names,\n\"Ship to: Select address\" wrapped inside the 40px top bar and ran into\n\"Call us\".\n\n**Root cause.** The organization and user names have `truncate\nxl:max-w-80`, but their wrapper was `xl:inline`. On inline boxes neither\n`truncate` nor `max-width` has any effect, so the names never truncated\nand kept their full width. The right column is `shrink-0` (added in\n#1866 so that a long ship-to address truncates instead of breaking the\nbar), so all of the squeeze fell on the ship-to placeholder. The\nplaceholder had no `nowrap`, so it wrapped. 1280 is the worst width\nbecause the names first appear at `xl`.\n\n**Fix (4 class changes):**\n- The names wrapper is now `gap-1 xl:flex`, so `truncate` and\n`max-width` finally apply. The full name is still available in `title`.\n- Between `xl` (1280) and `2xl` (1500) the names are capped at\n`max-w-32` when both organization and user are shown.\nSingle-organization users keep `xl:max-w-80`.\n- `.ship-to-selector__placeholder` gets `truncate`, matching\n`__selected`.\n- The right column keeps `shrink-0`, as on `dev`.\n\nAn intermediate version removed that `shrink-0`. Review caught that this\nreopens #1866: with a long selected address the page overflowed to\n1172px at 1024. That was confirmed in the live app and reverted.\n\n**Side effect for forks:** names longer than 320px now truncate at every\nwidth ≥1500. Before, that cap never took effect.\n\n### Ticket''s open questions\n- **Production-length names:** with \"Lone Star Outfitters / Elena\nMutykova\" and \"Purple Pink123 / Sasha Sasha\" the bar is clean on `dev`\nat every width. The bug needs long names like the QA fixtures\n(`AGENT-TEST-Org-BuildRight-20260310` / `AGENT-TEST-MultiOrgAlt FE`).\n- **Range on `dev` with those names:**\n  - 1280: 2-line wrap and a 70px overlap.\n  - 1366 and 1440: 2-line wrap that spills out of the bar.\n  - ≥1500: clean.\n- **QA badge over \"Dashboard\":** this is an environment artefact and is\nnot touched.\n\n### Verification\nLive app on the QA backend, signed-in multi-org user, in Playwright. All\nof the following were on at the same time: language, currency, ship-to,\nphone, dark-mode toggle.\n- 7 widths (1024, 1280, 1366, 1440, 1499, 1500, 1920) × 3 name sets ×\nwith and without a 107-character address (injected into the DOM) = 42\ncases.\n  - 0px overlap between any left and right descendant.\n  - No horizontal page overflow.\n  - No header element taller than 40px.\n- Worst case, 1280 with the QA names: \"Select ad…\" (69 of 90px) and\nnames at 128px.\n- Single-org, simulated in the DOM: a 41-character name stays\nuntruncated (291px) at 1280–1500, with no overlap or overflow.\n- The account dropdown still opens right-aligned under its button.\n- `yarn validate:types` is clean, and eslint on the changed files\nreports 0 errors.\n\n**Not walked:** a real single-org account, operator impersonation, and\nnon-English locales in the live app. The right column is `shrink-0` as\non `dev`, so link labels cannot wrap.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5945\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2534-e127-e1271b10.zip\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Low Risk**\n> CSS/layout-only changes in the header; no auth, API, or data-flow\nchanges. Long names may truncate earlier at ≥1500px when both org and\nuser labels show.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Fixes the signed-in **top header** wrapping and overlapping **“Call\nus”** around **1280px** when organization/user names and ship-to text\nare long.\n> \n> The account label wrapper switches from **`xl:inline` to `xl:flex`**\nso **`truncate`** and **`max-width`** apply to org/user names; multi-org\nusers get **`xl:max-w-32`** until **`2xl`**, while single-org keeps\n**`xl:max-w-80`**. The ship-to **“Select address”** placeholder now uses\n**`truncate`**, aligned with the selected-address styling, so it\nellipsizes instead of wrapping inside the 40px bar.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\ne1271b10b8788aa5958633a9bdd9d18a03daa0a9. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxKTVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVRkQADHGLCPMBA3F25D56L0+Nrl2\ne0OKG9ZlyEhrYMxTzrC4cAbBrIaaP6WZzksKBU3VTRwpdDMZTLSla9kaMgJ5Zgfw\nh3IVgwcEao746QIZZfTr3nBM95DKj5hcO0vP8pVx8UZxDEi3AyPPIKwBcXNrSkks\n3RS3c7OQ9IpAbT99IPrDsQcleeeVJGxSHSsH4XVe/rJ6yvJqYVD/W6KSQ8yP7X2S\n8xXdq6oqrBc95C5KjAssEqcB4y3Z4L1T0yFU8BNuw+XkatRMtTPNnH/dAv7ig1/g\nhthXdWAdvIXxqAK2sY8DSS/eI9z51r5Fy5xPcmqL+XAYqx/38uIiWzh3UNMEm6wH\nV0nWocQlsR9bHzxNzB9gn8OzkFAcfk2esjHMiohS0HvvvdBASX+JGLx6EfEzSfZJ\nhrqWzv7v4c25gh9Wfqff7BUlBTcTB3LbwBX3BIVxMsa1KivwozguSaSY8smGDcw/\nImGnXyG0cWi1ljuJ+tDU6Yqdhx0X9/B5ipkp3Jz2rcUgH9Drl9pXcAks5vulT+Rj\nFWqtmtanQJuh2PbjU3+X2aU22RIihP565uUaO3cqePMz9wsr92exaOezMsBqcaAf\nNMR0bmruYbeYLsyCr8Bf+UrYnuT7X4Ki6p6PIT6RXnsUcLyxDGoWO/5QdPrg0Vcy\nDDWd+GGWyqvwis7VQsGb\n=DkxO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T07:35:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/8581c575b9491d8c788c1d4e2160adef8c93a8a9","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDg1ODFjNTc1Yjk0OTFkOGM3ODhjMWQ0ZTIxNjBhZGVmOGM5M2E4YTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/dbc3f53b7243011ee423310389e44936d6897b12","sha":"dbc3f53b7243011ee423310389e44936d6897b12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/dbc3f53b7243011ee423310389e44936d6897b12"}],"sha":"8581c575b9491d8c788c1d4e2160adef8c93a8a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/8581c575b9491d8c788c1d4e2160adef8c93a8a9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56412054?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Lenajava1","id":56412054,"login":"Lenajava1","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2NDEyMDU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/dbc3f53b7243011ee423310389e44936d6897b12/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T16:52:16Z","email":"56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Elena Mutykova"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T16:52:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(VCST-6096): keep VcButton accessible name while loading (#2528)\n\n## Description\nWhile a `VcButton` is in its `loading` state, it now keeps its\naccessible name and is marked `aria-busy=\"true\"`. Before, screen readers\nannounced an unlabelled button: for example the \"Browse files\" button in\nthe Barcode scan modal, which stays loading while no camera stream\nplays.\nRoot cause: in loading state `.vc-button__content` was hidden with\n`visibility: hidden` (`invisible`), which also removes the slot text\nfrom the accessibility tree; the spinner that replaces it has no name.\n\nNo new props / events / slots · no new GraphQL fields · no new settings\n· no new dependencies.\n\n## Breaking changes\n- Component contract (props / events / slots): None.\n- GraphQL operations the client sends (fields, variables): None.\n- Settings (`$cfg` keys, theme settings): None.\n- Runtime behaviour: a loading `VcButton` used to expose an empty\naccessible name and no busy state; it now exposes its slot label (or\n`aria-label`/`title`, as before) and `aria-busy=\"true\"`. The hidden\ncontent now uses `opacity: 0` instead of `visibility: hidden`, so it\nstill takes the same space; rendered pixels are unchanged.\n\n## New dependencies\nNone.\n\n> **Note** — One change in the shared component fixes every caller,\ninstead of adding `aria-label` to each loading button. An sr-only\n\"Loading\" label on the spinner was the alternative; it was rejected\nbecause it would replace the button''s own name rather than keep it. The\nbutton stays `disabled` while loading, so the transparent content cannot\nbe clicked. Reviewer focus: the `VcButton` loading stories in Storybook.\n\n<details><summary>Auto-fix evidence (red → green)</summary>\n\n- Reproduction:\n`client-app/ui-kit/components/molecules/button/vc-button.test.ts` — a\nloading button has `aria-busy=\"true\"` and keeps its slot label. Fails on\nthe base commit, passes with this fix.\n- Rendered check in headless Chromium (a throwaway page that mounts\n`VcButton loading` with the slot \"Browse files\"; not committed):\n- base commit: accessibility tree name `\"\"`, axe `button-name`\nviolation: 1, content `visibility: hidden`;\n- with this fix: name `\"Browse files\"`, `aria-busy=\"true\"`, axe\n`button-name` violations: 0, content `opacity: 0`;\n- button box 130×46 px in both runs, and the before/after screenshots\nare pixel-identical.\n- Live on vcst-qa (2026-10-01, camera denied): the Browse files button\nin the Barcode scan modal has no `aria-label`, its content is\n`visibility: hidden`, and the dialog exposes Close, Cancel and one\nunnamed disabled button.\n- Local checks:\n  - vue-tsc --noEmit — pass\n  - lint — no new findings (existing warnings only)\n  - vitest (new + all ui-kit tests) — 887 passed\n  - build — pass\n\n**⚠ Needs visual verification.** The accessible name is unit- and\nrender-proven. The spinner overlay on loading buttons must be\nre-confirmed on a real deployment.\n</details>\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6096\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2528-8108-8108a070.zip\n> 🤖 Opened by `/vc-fix:qa-fix`. **Human review required before merge —\ndo not auto-merge.**\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Ivan Kalachikov <ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"7efc0fa13bfabb4d0a9a4bbb56e2fdd56f1805d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/7efc0fa13bfabb4d0a9a4bbb56e2fdd56f1805d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/dbc3f53b7243011ee423310389e44936d6897b12","verification":{"payload":"tree 7efc0fa13bfabb4d0a9a4bbb56e2fdd56f1805d8\nparent a8f4deb82d26fb7c9d9fcce5c703dc68843701f9\nauthor Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com> 1791219136 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791219136 +0100\n\nfix(VCST-6096): keep VcButton accessible name while loading (#2528)\n\n## Description\nWhile a `VcButton` is in its `loading` state, it now keeps its\naccessible name and is marked `aria-busy=\"true\"`. Before, screen readers\nannounced an unlabelled button: for example the \"Browse files\" button in\nthe Barcode scan modal, which stays loading while no camera stream\nplays.\nRoot cause: in loading state `.vc-button__content` was hidden with\n`visibility: hidden` (`invisible`), which also removes the slot text\nfrom the accessibility tree; the spinner that replaces it has no name.\n\nNo new props / events / slots · no new GraphQL fields · no new settings\n· no new dependencies.\n\n## Breaking changes\n- Component contract (props / events / slots): None.\n- GraphQL operations the client sends (fields, variables): None.\n- Settings (`$cfg` keys, theme settings): None.\n- Runtime behaviour: a loading `VcButton` used to expose an empty\naccessible name and no busy state; it now exposes its slot label (or\n`aria-label`/`title`, as before) and `aria-busy=\"true\"`. The hidden\ncontent now uses `opacity: 0` instead of `visibility: hidden`, so it\nstill takes the same space; rendered pixels are unchanged.\n\n## New dependencies\nNone.\n\n> **Note** — One change in the shared component fixes every caller,\ninstead of adding `aria-label` to each loading button. An sr-only\n\"Loading\" label on the spinner was the alternative; it was rejected\nbecause it would replace the button''s own name rather than keep it. The\nbutton stays `disabled` while loading, so the transparent content cannot\nbe clicked. Reviewer focus: the `VcButton` loading stories in Storybook.\n\n<details><summary>Auto-fix evidence (red → green)</summary>\n\n- Reproduction:\n`client-app/ui-kit/components/molecules/button/vc-button.test.ts` — a\nloading button has `aria-busy=\"true\"` and keeps its slot label. Fails on\nthe base commit, passes with this fix.\n- Rendered check in headless Chromium (a throwaway page that mounts\n`VcButton loading` with the slot \"Browse files\"; not committed):\n- base commit: accessibility tree name `\"\"`, axe `button-name`\nviolation: 1, content `visibility: hidden`;\n- with this fix: name `\"Browse files\"`, `aria-busy=\"true\"`, axe\n`button-name` violations: 0, content `opacity: 0`;\n- button box 130×46 px in both runs, and the before/after screenshots\nare pixel-identical.\n- Live on vcst-qa (2026-10-01, camera denied): the Browse files button\nin the Barcode scan modal has no `aria-label`, its content is\n`visibility: hidden`, and the dialog exposes Close, Cancel and one\nunnamed disabled button.\n- Local checks:\n  - vue-tsc --noEmit — pass\n  - lint — no new findings (existing warnings only)\n  - vitest (new + all ui-kit tests) — 887 passed\n  - build — pass\n\n**⚠ Needs visual verification.** The accessible name is unit- and\nrender-proven. The spinner overlay on loading buttons must be\nre-confirmed on a real deployment.\n</details>\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6096\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2528-8108-8108a070.zip\n> 🤖 Opened by `/vc-fix:qa-fix`. **Human review required before merge —\ndo not auto-merge.**\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Ivan Kalachikov <ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw9XACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAB3UQAAufWHG003XO7uwXFmvNWLke\nc40sKM9TKREiHiWyCnkQHnT083uHZgcHeORMmLVII801WbwmoCnJ1uGj4aMSmNAP\nDcwQ14vvlamtdF0GI2zCBNG5CfSEZWedMJicwiMDE3xrvFjpfGuTTJ1BrX7oVnoO\nsRyREiojbjXL2Zre69pAtgeVtI3XCHECpDIISHTK4550pYcXB7Rj9M5kq2WRLywg\nyoLnG5zPfuuRe8CshTKXOdcUGcxxysIlhDyraoQw6+Awgb5TfH0+80YmguKX3VBY\nU4cnlw5Kd/C+xi0x3PQTWBrbuH4Pq5R6B/+eiF4hmnw5uMDlY1GCs8jd0Egjye30\nBZMIrhgqfZzPRQ7fKq7