ow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/e565d851b7a9f978c3610f16bc3c89ec2e0752e0","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKGU1NjVkODUxYjdhOWY5NzhjMzYxMGYxNmJjM2M4OWVjMmUwNzUyZTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/e5fbcdf8206ddd05fffa4c0c6c2624afdb42065d","sha":"e5fbcdf8206ddd05fffa4c0c6c2624afdb42065d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/e5fbcdf8206ddd05fffa4c0c6c2624afdb42065d"}],"sha":"e565d851b7a9f978c3610f16bc3c89ec2e0752e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/e565d851b7a9f978c3610f16bc3c89ec2e0752e0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/126832118?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yuskithedeveloper","id":126832118,"login":"yuskithedeveloper","node_id":"U_kgDOB49N9g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/e5fbcdf8206ddd05fffa4c0c6c2624afdb42065d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T12:47:59Z","email":"126832118+yuskithedeveloper@users.noreply.github.com","name":"yuskithedeveloper"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T12:47:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VCST-2945): barcode search setup (#2501)\n\n## Description\n\nAdds the storefront half of **VCST-2945 — barcode scanner search\nsetup**. The existing barcode scanner (VCST-2622) now follows two store\nsettings owned by the Catalog module: whether the scanner button is\nshown at all, and how a scanned code is matched — the old **full-text\nsearch**, or an **exact match** on the fields the store configured (SKU,\nGTIN, MPN or short-text properties), which also finds variations and\nopens the product directly on a single hit.\n\nRequires the backend PRs:\n- https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-module-catalog/pull/909 — the\nsettings `Catalog.Search.BarcodeScannerEnabled` /\n`Catalog.Search.BarcodeSearchFields` and the admin blade that edits them\n- https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-module-x-catalog/pull/113 —\nexpands the `barcode:\"<value>\"` filter term into the configured fields\n\nOn an older backend both settings are absent: the scanner stays enabled\nand behaves exactly as today.\n\n## Behaviour\n\n- **Settings** (`shared/layout/composables/useBarcodeSearch.ts`, keys in\n`core/constants/modules.ts`): read from module `VirtoCommerce.Catalog`\nthrough `useModuleSettings`. `BarcodeScannerEnabled === false` hides the\nscanner in both search bars (missing ⇒ enabled). `BarcodeSearchFields`\nis the JSON array the blade saves; a non-empty array switches scans to\nexact mode, anything else (missing, `[]`, unparsable) keeps full text.\n\n- **Exact mode**: a scan navigates to the search page with\n**`?barcode=<value>`**; `category.vue` turns it into the filter term\n`barcode:\"<escaped value>\"` (the existing `escapeFilterSyntaxValue`, so\nQR payloads with quotes or colons stay one term) and leaves the keyword\nempty — the backend expands the term into the configured fields.\n**Full-text mode is unchanged**: the value is submitted as the search\nphrase (`?q=`).\n\n- **A scan is an identity lookup, not browsing**: a barcode request\nignores `?facets=` and the in-stock, purchased-before and branch\npreferences (the shopper is holding the item; the sample store''s\nvariation is out of stock and would otherwise be unfindable), so the\nsidebar, browsing controls and control chips stay hidden while a barcode\nis active — no control claims a filter that is not applied. Paging and\nsorting still work.\n\n- **A single hit opens the product** (`shouldOpenSingleBarcodeHit`, a\npure function with its own tests): the redirect is bound to the request\nthat produced the result — the code captured when the request was issued\nmust still be the current one, the request must not have been narrowed\nby facets/page/sort, exactly one product with total 1, and at most once\nper code — so a slower earlier response or a later narrowing of a\nmulti-hit page can never redirect. `router.replace`, so Back does not\nloop. A variation hit opens the variation''s own page (`/product/<id>`;\nvariations have no slug).\n\n- **Headings and empty state**: *Your search for barcode {barcode}\nreturned the following* / *No products found for barcode {barcode}*,\nwith the search-only empty view and a Reset that clears `barcode` (and\n`q`), so a miss is never a dead end.\n\n- **Generated filters**: the `filter` fragment now selects `isGenerated`\nand `useProducts.prepareFilters` drops generated filters — the backend\nreports the barcode expansion that way, like `is:product`. `barcode` is\nadditionally listed in `EXCLUDED_FILTER_NAMES` so an older backend that\nechoes it as a user filter still shows no chip. `types.ts` was patched\nby hand for the new field (codegen is not runnable against a\nsource-linked backend) and checked against the schema.\n\n- **Both bars, one handler**: `search-bar.vue` and\n`mobile-search-bar.vue` delegate to the composable; the mobile\noverlay/dropdown is hidden before the push through the same mechanism\nthe full-text path uses. Scans fire the `search` analytics event, are\ndeliberately **not** written to search history, and stay **global** (no\ncategory scope).\n\n- **Tests**: `useBarcodeSearch.test.ts` (17 — settings parsing, route\nbuilding, hide-before-push order, analytics, the redirect decision),\nscanner gating in `search-bar.test.ts` and the new\n`mobile-search-bar.test.ts`, escaping in `facets.test.ts`, the\ngenerated-filter drop in `useProducts.test.ts`. Full vitest run green\n(3123); eslint 0 errors in touched files; vue-tsc clean.\n\n- **i18n**: `pages.search.header_barcode` / `header_barcode_empty` in\nall 13 locales.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-2945\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2501-4e0e-4e0e12df.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Oleg Zhuk <zhukoo@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"421ba57472b1bc767f93d63638662ccfd15d7ff3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/421ba57472b1bc767f93d63638662ccfd15d7ff3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/e5fbcdf8206ddd05fffa4c0c6c2624afdb42065d","verification":{"payload":"tree 421ba57472b1bc767f93d63638662ccfd15d7ff3\nparent 203908b91082de9addd2fe50c957ffe0f15fc357\nauthor yuskithedeveloper <126832118+yuskithedeveloper@users.noreply.github.com> 1790858879 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790858879 -0600\n\nfeat(VCST-2945): barcode search setup (#2501)\n\n## Description\n\nAdds the storefront half of **VCST-2945 — barcode scanner search\nsetup**. The existing barcode scanner (VCST-2622) now follows two store\nsettings owned by the Catalog module: whether the scanner button is\nshown at all, and how a scanned code is matched — the old **full-text\nsearch**, or an **exact match** on the fields the store configured (SKU,\nGTIN, MPN or short-text properties), which also finds variations and\nopens the product directly on a single hit.\n\nRequires the backend PRs:\n- https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-module-catalog/pull/909 — the\nsettings `Catalog.Search.BarcodeScannerEnabled` /\n`Catalog.Search.BarcodeSearchFields` and the admin blade that edits them\n- https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-module-x-catalog/pull/113 —\nexpands the `barcode:\"<value>\"` filter term into the configured fields\n\nOn an older backend both settings are absent: the scanner stays enabled\nand behaves exactly as today.\n\n## Behaviour\n\n- **Settings** (`shared/layout/composables/useBarcodeSearch.ts`, keys in\n`core/constants/modules.ts`): read from module `VirtoCommerce.Catalog`\nthrough `useModuleSettings`. `BarcodeScannerEnabled === false` hides the\nscanner in both search bars (missing ⇒ enabled). `BarcodeSearchFields`\nis the JSON array the blade saves; a non-empty array switches scans to\nexact mode, anything else (missing, `[]`, unparsable) keeps full text.\n\n- **Exact mode**: a scan navigates to the search page with\n**`?barcode=<value>`**; `category.vue` turns it into the filter term\n`barcode:\"<escaped value>\"` (the existing `escapeFilterSyntaxValue`, so\nQR payloads with quotes or colons stay one term) and leaves the keyword\nempty — the backend expands the term into the configured fields.\n**Full-text mode is unchanged**: the value is submitted as the search\nphrase (`?q=`).\n\n- **A scan is an identity lookup, not browsing**: a barcode request\nignores `?facets=` and the in-stock, purchased-before and branch\npreferences (the shopper is holding the item; the sample store''s\nvariation is out of stock and would otherwise be unfindable), so the\nsidebar, browsing controls and control chips stay hidden while a barcode\nis active — no control claims a filter that is not applied. Paging and\nsorting still work.\n\n- **A single hit opens the product** (`shouldOpenSingleBarcodeHit`, a\npure function with its own tests): the redirect is bound to the request\nthat produced the result — the code captured when the request was issued\nmust still be the current one, the request must not have been narrowed\nby facets/page/sort, exactly one product with total 1, and at most once\nper code — so a slower earlier response or a later narrowing of a\nmulti-hit page can never redirect. `router.replace`, so Back does not\nloop. A variation hit opens the variation''s own page (`/product/<id>`;\nvariations have no slug).\n\n- **Headings and empty state**: *Your search for barcode {barcode}\nreturned the following* / *No products found for barcode {barcode}*,\nwith the search-only empty view and a Reset that clears `barcode` (and\n`q`), so a miss is never a dead end.\n\n- **Generated filters**: the `filter` fragment now selects `isGenerated`\nand `useProducts.prepareFilters` drops generated filters — the backend\nreports the barcode expansion that way, like `is:product`. `barcode` is\nadditionally listed in `EXCLUDED_FILTER_NAMES` so an older backend that\nechoes it as a user filter still shows no chip. `types.ts` was patched\nby hand for the new field (codegen is not runnable against a\nsource-linked backend) and checked against the schema.\n\n- **Both bars, one handler**: `search-bar.vue` and\n`mobile-search-bar.vue` delegate to the composable; the mobile\noverlay/dropdown is hidden before the push through the same mechanism\nthe full-text path uses. Scans fire the `search` analytics event, are\ndeliberately **not** written to search history, and stay **global** (no\ncategory scope).\n\n- **Tests**: `useBarcodeSearch.test.ts` (17 — settings parsing, route\nbuilding, hide-before-push order, analytics, the redirect decision),\nscanner gating in `search-bar.test.ts` and the new\n`mobile-search-bar.test.ts`, escaping in `facets.test.ts`, the\ngenerated-filter drop in `useProducts.test.ts`. Full vitest run green\n(3123); eslint 0 errors in touched files; vue-tsc clean.\n\n- **i18n**: `pages.search.header_barcode` / `header_barcode_empty` in\nall 13 locales.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-2945\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2501-4e0e-4e0e12df.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Oleg Zhuk <zhukoo@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvlZ/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwXIQAESLhzxk/y2FkDB2wbfQxh3/\nMkgW1KrM87ka6nahKL0dv7gRt3Z+BQe5xps3ypl78fsUx9GyLNL0HS+sbrqJLHM7\nnyh+Wpt7muKCxLULnCQ4sg+rpqT3sA/6/Py3Slc3G2dno75Cqk21jJGnzqys+Rkp\ncu39RZCRsdCn4Nv4wVhksM1FEcoPKd/TDwOjIF42pJCIR2v3w2mY/9kiUfApex8u\ng9nXqcwwOfUlR2HZ6OUx2PzZbPpA9pTOcYG7p/yelK5RAKGLkm5RqWhF4/9YI1mD\nB8NkvNYkmSp9IeCuceS17oLTNMcVY6/2qRfcluyRRI6h7Iw5l6HGyoSmPInGATdh\nWkwTy3PV3P66aIR+M0AclqJj53R287ll6AsjI0r/UmE9EleOOi1V7dL7bH0ij/ky\n3l0ArDnCZ9MTNSa93E/tlxvu39rGDY8U//z1xP956OD31eMqb6gIaueRer9FdsRt\nZuP2smJJXyT3j9iFSz4FP9QYfSV1TWWwqvFjvkovfUAGALQFDz9/gfW+jHW+u01X\nkgbFzE809fq9v/5rA26ckNT+W3ixHwAJUmiZOZ1lNyLK9l30+oIemUwJG9w+tpVL\nI65CO9uNA/OJWd9SwzmkqzWXHogrI5YyNA5nWuxtzgONd7sLwewWLOoolKJaKghs\nUVXgGoKJIDUiMz8xO7Pj\n=4YvC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-01T12:47:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/e5fbcdf8206ddd05fffa4c0c6c2624afdb42065d","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKGU1ZmJjZGY4MjA2ZGRkMDVmZmZhNGMwYzZjMjYyNGFmZGI0MjA2NWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/203908b91082de9addd2fe50c957ffe0f15fc357","sha":"203908b91082de9addd2fe50c957ffe0f15fc357","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/203908b91082de9addd2fe50c957ffe0f15fc357"}],"sha":"e5fbcdf8206ddd05fffa4c0c6c2624afdb42065d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/e5fbcdf8206ddd05fffa4c0c6c2624afdb42065d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49168917?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vas11yev1work","id":49168917,"login":"vas11yev1work","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5MTY4OTE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/203908b91082de9addd2fe50c957ffe0f15fc357/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T08:20:18Z","email":"49168917+vas11yev1work@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Anatolii Vasilev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T08:20:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(VCST-6005): keep sales-rep order total on one line in mobile cards (#2525)\n\n## Problem\n[VCST-6005](https://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6005): on\nthe sales-rep customer orders list at 375px, when a long order number\nwraps it squeezes the Total, which then breaks mid-number (`$247.0` /\n`0`) and reads as a different amount.\n\n## Fix\nIn the mobile card row, the total is now `shrink-0 whitespace-nowrap`,\nso the order number wraps instead. Added `gap-2` so the two don''t touch.\n\n## Check\nOpen My Customers → a customer with a long order number → Orders at\n375px. The Total should stay on one line.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n[VCST-6005]:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6005?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ\nArtifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2525-51fb-51fba2b4.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"adcb6ddf59dc545abf3d957224c9e44d0b5a9ac6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/adcb6ddf59dc545abf3d957224c9e44d0b5a9ac6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/203908b91082de9addd2fe50c957ffe0f15fc357","verification":{"payload":"tree adcb6ddf59dc545abf3d957224c9e44d0b5a9ac6\nparent 483b2712ad64695e8fa290e97c85dea8719a76ed\nauthor Anatolii Vasilev <49168917+vas11yev1work@users.noreply.github.com> 1790842818 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790842818 +0200\n\nfix(VCST-6005): keep sales-rep order total on one line in mobile cards (#2525)\n\n## Problem\n[VCST-6005](https://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6005): on\nthe sales-rep customer orders list at 375px, when a long order number\nwraps it squeezes the Total, which then breaks mid-number (`$247.0` /\n`0`) and reads as a different amount.\n\n## Fix\nIn the mobile card row, the total is now `shrink-0 whitespace-nowrap`,\nso the order number wraps instead. Added `gap-2` so the two don''t touch.\n\n## Check\nOpen My Customers → a customer with a long order number → Orders at\n375px. The Total should stay on one line.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n[VCST-6005]:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6005?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ\nArtifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2525-51fb-51fba2b4.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvhfCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFPsQAKUPvcrGL9AO9UP0RGbRDtWa\n95E4rtWOUqREAAJKB5swgBPgPakiO4Bs/ZPBjKNTjq+rzUYNhIIqxF+0d60Graie\nIDTJXCFIJG0ZcGcfssx1bt6T1Iv1zspF0kMy+4uXAYrZKB83ua2q77orFW3z6a3k\nOTrubbWHrJFpQGYhgbSpTUouJpnbnI5jzPkQOvudlBw/0oIds6BW9izVAz5PfPpe\n6Tny2bgn1GiAXfrhITwkB0/2WSmEFpAW0l6NFdwZfGGqSgpX+9+PaBkhJOOkAr3y\n9YJQpZT7bUj7UyN5acTucIPgnOJiEK9PvzotjjpYSBztjHZnQAd7Fs/bXWPqEJ8k\nklNqJaa/s6BTbr+g5CVAGSF2guFfZkDGQhRS2TjkP2D0R/Wy8dOBktlJgLMfKEsl\n45xg6JRxcx1kRXuLCpeRzXuy9O32ZVB1t1TOGhiS2y9YOpaFl22w52Y3TST