b.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/d5c6500729f36dd3bb13039b18cfd9cddf276c3e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/330693?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilkot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilkot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilkot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilkot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/basilkot","id":330693,"login":"basilkot","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMDY5Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilkot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilkot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilkot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilkot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilkot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilkot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/62d91663d101fe2e6c8010362bbfbaf626b733da/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T19:00:24Z","email":"basilkot@gmail.com","name":"Basil Kotov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T19:00:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VCST-5883): returns — decline reasons and buyer culture (#2500)\n\n## Description\n\nAdds the storefront half of **VCST-5883 — returns, step 2**. The return\npage shows the buyer why their return, or a line of it, was declined —\nthe reasons the decline email gives them — and the storefront sends the\nbuyer''s culture when it creates a return, so the return''s status emails\nand push messages are written in it.\n\nRequires the backend PR:\n- https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-module-return/pull/27 — the\napprove / decline flow, the buyer notifications and the `cultureName`\ninput on `createReturn`\n\nOn an older backend (Return 3.1002.0) `createReturn` refuses the unknown\n`cultureName` input, so no return can be created: deploy this together\nwith #27.\n\n## Behaviour\n\n- **Decline reasons** (`pages/return.vue`,\n`components/return-item-summary.vue`): the reason for the whole return\nand each line''s reason appear under \"Reason for decline\", only when the\nagent gave one. `GetReturn` now also selects the line''s `rejectReason`;\nthe return''s own was already selected.\n\n- **The buyer''s culture** (`composables/useReturnableItems.ts`):\n`createReturn` sends `cultureName`, the storefront''s current culture. A\nreturn created without one takes the order''s language.\n\n- **Page title** (`pages/return.vue`): the browser tab, the heading and\nthe breadcrumb read \"Return {number}\" through `usePageHead`; while the\nreturn loads they read \"Return\", as the order page does.\n\n- **Quantity field** (`components/return-quantity-input.vue`): a number\ntyped past the maximum is now corrected in the visible field as well.\nThe correction used to land in the same tick and hand the field back the\nvalue it had before the keystroke, so the field was never rewritten and\nkept showing, say, \"50 of 5 available\" while 5 was sent. The field is\nalso one size up (`sm`: 38 px with 16 px text), the size of the\nstorefront''s own quantity field; iOS zooms only into fields with text\nunder 16 px, so focusing it should no longer zoom the page.\n\n- **i18n**: `return_details.reject_reason` in all 13 locales.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5883\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2500-250d-250df5f0.zip\n\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> `createReturn` with `cultureName` breaks return creation on Return\n3.1002.0 until the paired backend is deployed; otherwise mostly UI and\nGraphQL field additions.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Storefront support for **VCST-5883** return step 2: buyers see decline\nreasons and create returns with their locale for status emails.\n> \n> **Decline reasons** — `GetReturn` now loads per-line `rejectReason`\n(return-level was already there). The return details page and\n`return-item-summary` show *Reason for decline* when the agent provided\none, with new `return_details.reject_reason` strings across locales.\n> \n> **Buyer culture** — Draft creation via `useReturnableItems` passes\n`cultureName` from storefront globals on `createReturn`, so\nnotifications match the buyer’s language instead of defaulting to the\norder’s.\n> \n> **Return details UX** — Tab title, H1, and breadcrumbs share a\ncomputed title through `usePageHead` (shows “Return” while loading).\n> \n> **Quantity input** — Over-max typing is clamped on `nextTick` so the\nvisible field updates (fixes stale “50” when max is 5); input size `xs`\n→ `sm` to reduce iOS zoom; regression test added.\n> \n> **Dependencies** — `VirtoCommerce.Return` bumped to **3.1003.0** (must\ndeploy with backend that accepts `cultureName`); `PageBuilderModule`\n**3.1029.0**.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n250df5f02d334f57af037f15764617f436740a58. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Elena Kutasina <kutasina.elena@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: yuskithedeveloper <yuskianywhere@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: yuskithedeveloper <126832118+yuskithedeveloper@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"17af02948f65fe87e635bd93232f33763cbd24ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/17af02948f65fe87e635bd93232f33763cbd24ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/62d91663d101fe2e6c8010362bbfbaf626b733da","verification":{"payload":"tree 17af02948f65fe87e635bd93232f33763cbd24ef\nparent a67c92a60c28fe6bc1ded95610ac394652f69921\nauthor Basil Kotov <basilkot@gmail.com> 1790794824 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790794824 -0600\n\nfeat(VCST-5883): returns — decline reasons and buyer culture (#2500)\n\n## Description\n\nAdds the storefront half of **VCST-5883 — returns, step 2**. The return\npage shows the buyer why their return, or a line of it, was declined —\nthe reasons the decline email gives them — and the storefront sends the\nbuyer''s culture when it creates a return, so the return''s status emails\nand push messages are written in it.\n\nRequires the backend PR:\n- https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-module-return/pull/27 — the\napprove / decline flow, the buyer notifications and the `cultureName`\ninput on `createReturn`\n\nOn an older backend (Return 3.1002.0) `createReturn` refuses the unknown\n`cultureName` input, so no return can be created: deploy this together\nwith #27.\n\n## Behaviour\n\n- **Decline reasons** (`pages/return.vue`,\n`components/return-item-summary.vue`): the reason for the whole return\nand each line''s reason appear under \"Reason for decline\", only when the\nagent gave one. `GetReturn` now also selects the line''s `rejectReason`;\nthe return''s own was already selected.\n\n- **The buyer''s culture** (`composables/useReturnableItems.ts`):\n`createReturn` sends `cultureName`, the storefront''s current culture. A\nreturn created without one takes the order''s language.\n\n- **Page title** (`pages/return.vue`): the browser tab, the heading and\nthe breadcrumb read \"Return {number}\" through `usePageHead`; while the\nreturn loads they read \"Return\", as the order page does.\n\n- **Quantity field** (`components/return-quantity-input.vue`): a number\ntyped past the maximum is now corrected in the visible field as well.\nThe correction used to land in the same tick and hand the field back the\nvalue it had before the keystroke, so the field was never rewritten and\nkept showing, say, \"50 of 5 available\" while 5 was sent. The field is\nalso one size up (`sm`: 38 px with 16 px text), the size of the\nstorefront''s own quantity field; iOS zooms only into fields with text\nunder 16 px, so focusing it should no longer zoom the page.\n\n- **i18n**: `return_details.reject_reason` in all 13 locales.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5883\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2500-250d-250df5f0.zip\n\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> `createReturn` with `cultureName` breaks return creation on Return\n3.1002.0 until the paired backend is deployed; otherwise mostly UI and\nGraphQL field additions.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Storefront support for **VCST-5883** return step 2: buyers see decline\nreasons and create returns with their locale for status emails.\n> \n> **Decline reasons** — `GetReturn` now loads per-line `rejectReason`\n(return-level was already there). The return details page and\n`return-item-summary` show *Reason for decline* when the agent provided\none, with new `return_details.reject_reason` strings across locales.\n> \n> **Buyer culture** — Draft creation via `useReturnableItems` passes\n`cultureName` from storefront globals on `createReturn`, so\nnotifications match the buyer’s language instead of defaulting to the\norder’s.\n> \n> **Return details UX** — Tab title, H1, and breadcrumbs share a\ncomputed title through `usePageHead` (shows “Return” while loading).\n> \n> **Quantity input** — Over-max typing is clamped on `nextTick` so the\nvisible field updates (fixes stale “50” when max is 5); input size `xs`\n→ `sm` to reduce iOS zoom; regression test added.\n> \n> **Dependencies** — `VirtoCommerce.Return` bumped to **3.1003.0** (must\ndeploy with backend that accepts `cultureName`); `PageBuilderModule`\n**3.1029.0**.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n250df5f02d334f57af037f15764617f436740a58. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Elena Kutasina <kutasina.elena@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: yuskithedeveloper <yuskianywhere@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: yuskithedeveloper <126832118+yuskithedeveloper@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvVxICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApIMQACg/aJ1bBLFY6w5b5lhbDBcz\nPR+GIlCcMxFHDbT4ATGnMleL92kNEdfiRlCXlnRHE2Kc7imcNj5VdRkAdcr335Bc\nUyDOBecdZK1GrRI2qU0ukiZkEBPSxpt7hMnSEOozxc/5kLGPxm5d/hBg7B5u7fi5\n72gfw3vZFGnZcTaQOlW1yx51XCX9ZOuGaG+BgpsvYA8r6buBRVtYJdeoKJcBown3\nP2LguHa5Moeb7n8FPD+i1fyles+b1sGTMfPXPxNZZm93nmE4GsIzWiYTpeAp4Wzz\narW64R1iztcCwaVPIKWRUyJkdbsK9w07sUYV5eV61r4XPd2T9t+wzRU5SN84bVg1\nZi/GPgAThijAip5RFVydpYgkUsV2Y9CVUCcQjRRGpl6ZwSFX02BBFb50h6yE493i\nes+a+MBJ4k/3XTskcJStpeikC8SUrp23gyku+aLyS8kXOGgESRDorEUBWQPM1m63\nddo7vsUkwPDrEL6skwySCdEhXVcuN2+dINLQ89fSlHbaI0XbutuB6fQqpVXhePgI\n97r+pBOgQXwTqWhNxTMjO6Xu2B+fv4SmA2PKJkIm8a2B++NXIBPROG99A/vhKOpu\nVNPokLSKixK2eSFItS73xF6t7Ca/NKEC9WCuX/nku0wZWv0hN3ZSQjWNoNux2G8V\nGiDPhGH6bWgx272LtmmR\n=K5y8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T19:00:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-