ps://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56412054?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Lenajava1","id":56412054,"login":"Lenajava1","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2NDEyMDU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/fd8497cdc97a9aa6c80cbd2c5c07450ae26e8a46/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T14:57:47Z","email":"56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Elena Mutykova"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T14:57:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(VCST-5840): mark language option flags as decorative (#2513)\n\n## VCST-5840: language selector flags announce the wrong language\n\nJira: https://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5840\n\n**DO NOT MERGE until human review.**\n\n### Problem\nEvery option in the header language selector renders its flag with\n`alt=\"{current language}\"`, so on an en-US storefront every flag says\n\"English (United States)\". A screen reader announces the German option\nas \"English (United States) Deutsch\". Each option''s accessible name\ncontradicts itself (WCAG 4.1.2).\n\nConfirmed on vcst-qa: all 16 option flags carry `alt=\"English (United\nStates)\"`.\n\n### Fix\nThe flag is decorative, because the adjacent text already names the\nlanguage. The option image now has `alt=\"\"` (WCAG 1.1.1). This is one\ntemplate attribute in `language-selector.vue`. Prettier collapsed the\nelement onto one line.\n\nThe trigger button''s flag is unchanged. It shows the current language,\nso its alt is not contradictory.\n\n### Proof\n- New `language-selector.test.ts` mounts the real component with the\nreal `VcImage` and asserts the rendered `<img alt>`. It is **RED** on\n`dev` (`\"English (United States)\"`) and **GREEN** with the fix.\n- eslint: 0 errors on the folder. `vue-tsc --build`: clean.\n- No existing tests or stories were changed.\n\n### Deploy check\nAfter deploy, open the language selector and confirm each option''s flag\nhas an empty `alt`. The options should read as just their language name\nin the accessibility tree.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nArtifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2513-5dd6-5dd6d29c.zip\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8512b649734cdf8fbea5238bc3583e1cf20fe9e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/8512b649734cdf8fbea5238bc3583e1cf20fe9e6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/fd8497cdc97a9aa6c80cbd2c5c07450ae26e8a46","verification":{"payload":"tree 8512b649734cdf8fbea5238bc3583e1cf20fe9e6\nparent f3adb7e63b25959a6745f77372ecbf7d418bad93\nauthor Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com> 1790348267 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790348267 +0200\n\nfix(VCST-5840): mark language option flags as decorative (#2513)\n\n## VCST-5840: language selector flags announce the wrong language\n\nJira: https://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5840\n\n**DO NOT MERGE until human review.**\n\n### Problem\nEvery option in the header language selector renders its flag with\n`alt=\"{current language}\"`, so on an en-US storefront every flag says\n\"English (United States)\". A screen reader announces the German option\nas \"English (United States) Deutsch\". Each option''s accessible name\ncontradicts itself (WCAG 4.1.2).\n\nConfirmed on vcst-qa: all 16 option flags carry `alt=\"English (United\nStates)\"`.\n\n### Fix\nThe flag is decorative, because the adjacent text already names the\nlanguage. The option image now has `alt=\"\"` (WCAG 1.1.1). This is one\ntemplate attribute in `language-selector.vue`. Prettier collapsed the\nelement onto one line.\n\nThe trigger button''s flag is unchanged. It shows the current language,\nso its alt is not contradictory.\n\n### Proof\n- New `language-selector.test.ts` mounts the real component with the\nreal `VcImage` and asserts the rendered `<img alt>`. It is **RED** on\n`dev` (`\"English (United States)\"`) and **GREEN** with the fix.\n- eslint: 0 errors on the folder. `vue-tsc --build`: clean.\n- No existing tests or stories were changed.\n\n### Deploy check\nAfter deploy, open the language selector and confirm each option''s flag\nhas an empty `alt`. The options should read as just their language name\nin the accessibility tree.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nArtifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.59.0-pr-2513-5dd6-5dd6d29c.zip\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtovrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbKYQAGb/a9G2yXtEvRe1YB8rUVcV\nCjqHx1Xgfu1LVOVuq7VPYm7Mo0N3rqp5dj/s/KslozFhnm4hud/XVb4yUFsK7EDX\nLiTE7lS8FZ4PBix5XFCvsDZ0j8pqacsBgtgmOoAnugW9AC/EzRvv31Y6bBITOXua\nYDzdScMT5vl/fUkGjWa9X9gWXKWQYhk/ibj7OvpfyYLqZy9/X4aXxD5q2IzgwqvB\nTmm1hyP1gI3+OdIQfI8pRPKPQDp5qiPsX5xhaU+L+81JF3qp9SdesSgm7o3F1n8t\nhe5QsW5RTHJk5SQdzIdETpHPf8h9une8LAbkMdpZU+X8JdMCHVm18VpczO129k3s\nN1mdDRpXVqpjzkOMdRiD+dXRSDdUvksTA8n0ZI+wCz33FDb1v1Q4+KW1gFOuVPap\nBR6ITdtvE7CnVyumtFNlhjvupvjgMarFH6RKIxjKQ6NBGdVL7FIGSSeUT