tps://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56412054?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Lenajava1","id":56412054,"login":"Lenajava1","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2NDEyMDU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/cbae929708771d3deb58d7191cccf8fce81da9ea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T11:31:27Z","email":"56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Elena Mutykova"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T11:31:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(VCST-6046): pluralize product-card variations button label (#2497)\n\n## Summary\nThe catalog product-card \"variations\" button used a fixed `\"{0}\nvariations\"` i18n template, so a product with exactly one variation\nrendered **\"1 variations\"**. The expanded panel it opens is correctly\npluralized (\"1 available variation\"), so the page contradicted itself.\n\n## Fix\n- Initial commit gave the English message vue-i18n plural forms and\nupdated 5 call sites to pass the count as the plural argument.\n- **Ivan Kalachikov''s follow-up commit extends this to all 13 locales**\n— `ru`/`pl` get the four plural forms their grammar needs, the rest a\nzero form so the button matches the panel when nothing is purchasable.\nIt also switches to the named `{count}` shape (matching the sibling\n`available_variations` key), moves the counting rule into a shared\n`shared/catalog/utilities/variations` module used by all five\ncomponents, and strengthens the tests to read both the button and the\npanel heading out of the DOM (mutation-tested — see his review comments\non the original PR).\n- Branch merged with `dev` to stay current.\n\n## Proof\nRendered-DOM (jsdom) vitest, red->green, mutation-tested (3 independent\nmutations of the source all caught). Typecheck, eslint, `check-locales`\nclean; existing tests/stories untouched.\n\n## Notes\n- No visual/layout risk expected, but worth a quick live glance\npost-deploy across catalog grid/list, related, recently-browsed,\nwishlist rows, and compare-table.\n- Supersedes #2493, which was opened from a fork and could not run this\nrepo''s PR-gated CI (all checks reported SKIPPED there). Same full commit\nhistory (including Ivan''s review-driven commit and his APPROVED review),\npushed directly to this repo so CI can actually run.\n\nCloses VCST-6046: https://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6046\n\n**DO NOT MERGE until human review.**\n\nGenerated with Claude Code (https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nArtifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2497-5711-5711176e.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Ivan Kalachikov <ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"85a180efbe8b0aa522866832980b3da71eaf6f13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/85a180efbe8b0aa522866832980b3da71eaf6f13"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/cbae929708771d3deb58d7191cccf8fce81da9ea","verification":{"payload":"tree 85a180efbe8b0aa522866832980b3da71eaf6f13\nparent 80c66aece52c25b8cbe2e70250388298c348f393\nauthor Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com> 1790076687 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790076687 +0100\n\nfix(VCST-6046): pluralize product-card variations button label (#2497)\n\n## Summary\nThe catalog product-card \"variations\" button used a fixed `\"{0}\nvariations\"` i18n template, so a product with exactly one variation\nrendered **\"1 variations\"**. The expanded panel it opens is correctly\npluralized (\"1 available variation\"), so the page contradicted itself.\n\n## Fix\n- Initial commit gave the English message vue-i18n plural forms and\nupdated 5 call sites to pass the count as the plural argument.\n- **Ivan Kalachikov''s follow-up commit extends this to all 13 locales**\n— `ru`/`pl` get the four plural forms their grammar needs, the rest a\nzero form so the button matches the panel when nothing is purchasable.\nIt also switches to the named `{count}` shape (matching the sibling\n`available_variations` key), moves the counting rule into a shared\n`shared/catalog/utilities/variations` module used by all five\ncomponents, and strengthens the tests to read both the button and the\npanel heading out of the DOM (mutation-tested — see his review comments\non the original PR).\n- Branch merged with `dev` to stay current.\n\n## Proof\nRendered-DOM (jsdom) vitest, red->green, mutation-tested (3 independent\nmutations of the source all caught). Typecheck, eslint, `check-locales`\nclean; existing tests/stories untouched.\n\n## Notes\n- No visual/layout risk expected, but worth a quick live glance\npost-deploy across catalog grid/list, related, recently-browsed,\nwishlist rows, and compare-table.\n- Supersedes #2493, which was opened from a fork and could not run this\nrepo''s PR-gated CI (all checks reported SKIPPED there). Same full commit\nhistory (including Ivan''s review-driven commit and his APPROVED review),\npushed directly to this repo so CI can actually run.\n\nCloses VCST-6046: https://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6046\n\n**DO NOT MERGE until human review.**\n\nGenerated with Claude Code (https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nArtifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2497-5711-5711176e.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Ivan Kalachikov <ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsmcPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnyYQAHu+9kRTyOajcg8t/K0hj+0L\nZ3G/naFu2RrHxJ1kHLM3eWHFGJZIa5OiOUowz9C9xLpl8BmYppiBK45JssBn3kuX\nS2YBdng4/3nDWYt1slq8jbUTtAx6CMaSu5xXd4iftcljCq8Kpc9Rxku1C+gF5Hm+\nP5vGGQvF0o//4kaXw6GpExMJiOHPpgDTygWwJzdpua6m2SAg+cTBjgdqYg0xSJbX\nfgN47QZ09V05Go9kcQD5bzMTU/4NF6lVnCck2wFLERlbBOYlihCFbeGnhvZs4dNZ\n8WIqUUQ7R87UTNg9fJW2aeG9hr1fGn7h3eGKG3ZcHSNsZ2x8BfOa4zyF1i3MuINF\nys0z6OQvjCtvPu1o6OXorSS5uyWfk3hlClDsJEhVesuHI2ZbJ28nsCGTvPTj0wa2\np9P/nLnpxSgRgUB1SAtvQbdSMMpjw+tBoY2/ODa5vF6b7oSa/Aij9gtrkDhGD7kw\nrrajrybXPYnV3U+3Xp+SkmTpRoin4UF3pmB1Ido+J5tEf1KUMIWIJoN8+ju2FIxI\nzyU/JGbvaMDDK9pMxw7cLr9unbkP+P652Oz/MY9DG9wsckJO2Cv+01f3nIodp1xu\nQi1D9Tgw0LPfFIUet3/fN6cn/sjYX6SBmXahEo3UZhdWL2gQ66Gwp0ylN8vLslKg\nlS3fzimltdZh8CoKXCnJ\n=jGDV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T11:31:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/cbae929708771d3deb58d7191cccf8fce81da9ea","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKGNiYWU5Mjk3MDg3NzFkM2RlYjU4ZDcxOTFjY2NmOGZjZTgxZGE5ZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/80c66aece52c25b8cbe2e70250388298c348f393","sha":"80c66aece52c25b8cbe2e70250388298c348f393","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/80c66aece52c25b8cbe2e70250388298c348f393"}],"sha":"cbae929708771d3deb58d7191cccf8fce81da9ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/cbae929708771d3deb58d7191cccf8fce81da9ea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49168917?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vas11yev1work","id":49168917,"login":"vas11yev1work","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5MTY4OTE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/80c66aece52c25b8cbe2e70250388298c348f393/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T11:28:51Z","email":"49168917+vas11yev1work@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Anatolii Vasilev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T11:28:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(VCST-6029): keep long compare values inside their cell (#2495)\n\n[VCST-6029](https://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6029)\n\nA long unbroken property value (e.g. a 32-char SKU) overflowed its\ncompare-table cell and was painted over the neighbouring column — at\n390px the two values were drawn on top of each other, with nothing\nscrollable to disambiguate them.\n\n`overflow-wrap: break-word` does not reduce a box''s min-content width,\nso the value''s intrinsic width won over the cell''s `max-width`. Swapped\nit for `overflow-wrap: anywhere` on `.compare-table__row-value`, which\ndoes shrink min-content width, so the value wraps inside its own column.\n\nCSS only, one rule; applies to every value cell, not just SKU.\n\n**Test:** `/compare` with a product whose SKU is a 32-char hex code\n(e.g. CHAMPAGNE COOLER STAINLESS STEEL MAT 20CM) — check the SKU row at\n1920px and at 390px. Layout defect, so not covered by vitest.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n[VCST-6029]:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6029?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ\nArtifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2495-c828-c828ee92.zip\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"713120ecc2e243766995b38fde81b4cdb4555ba4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/713120ecc2e243766995b38fde81b4cdb4555ba4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/80c66aece52c25b8cbe2e70250388298c348f393","verification":{"payload":"tree 713120ecc2e243766995b38fde81b4cdb4555ba4\nparent a2d75898f171f1aa322b7a8fdfa9331f32ee9562\nauthor Anatolii Vasilev <49168917+vas11yev1work@users.noreply.github.com> 1790076531 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790076531 +0200\n\nfix(VCST-6029): keep long compare values inside their cell (#2495)\n\n[VCST-6029](https://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6029)\n\nA long unbroken property value (e.g. a 32-char SKU) overflowed its\ncompare-table cell and was painted over the neighbouring column — at\n390px the two values were drawn on top of each other, with nothing\nscrollable to disambiguate them.\n\n`overflow-wrap: break-word` does not reduce a box''s min-content width,\nso the value''s intrinsic width won over the cell''s `max-width`. Swapped\nit for `overflow-wrap: anywhere` on `.compare-table__row-value`, which\ndoes shrink min-content width, so the value wraps inside its own column.\n\nCSS only, one rule; applies to every value cell, not just SKU.\n\n**Test:** `/compare` with a product whose SKU is a 32-char hex code\n(e.g. CHAMPAGNE COOLER STAINLESS STEEL MAT 20CM) — check the SKU row at\n1920px and at 390px. Layout defect, so not covered by vitest.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n[VCST-6029]:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-6029?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ\nArtifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2495-c828-c828ee92.zip\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsmZzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkf4QAGKXubd6qQvhaoTcCGvMymxC\nyVYIGAAlfRrXdHp7qcal4NTJ7J9PB9zsyygyfSaEnljlJda/T598etW3/RumOzG1\nS0JUTM2yAcG0VjJVoONnm6pCiYi0nRZi86zZ1D1TxSBkUPnwm/rydPBtZx2mYJNN\n+7bGuA4HCIs9vEZTeFbwsfgcivH4EPkjDZJfos2rSc7grT4lQWbusQgW7/Y8kWew\nDuasQH9kibv7togfamewULojyiKaGd43f4fbkkXbBkFCD7JsZ/pHhMetHHg4TAlr\npW9RgD5E4DSOYj2Y/TcP5r8pdMXFZOctiGrPlzKFQdalkTr0c7B3bolbvfPfLPFs\ns/i5/7hf2A82eFqb/DrwDnjwK7saelIDhehnlB80R1Dg1dSr7biHv9C/DL8UtrN4\nwQgiRevNKDyUrAZ6IZtvowRNfiHWFdzIGqb6uF+3R5Y1VDlXsjUxH1VT0Pmo2C43\nMql6lWCnCVXZZ71WwOmn87oOplUchsDEZaZZN7uALncnD/9NtiakfnWczfIaLqJg\nMb2TSKWS09yDCAFM0sCPusb6N5i1M4T8B8firgAdQmr0fhwerhMzzYkJOjMuF/XN\nESP2Pw2fRXNQ0YxFW31MIijs1N4kV3laJI79aiCQeswAoqlmevzLtIhftye8G00k\nGHxTBgdDfUw1HJJuCZVu\n=p2R1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T11:28:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/80c66aece52c25b8cbe2e70250388298c348f393","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDgwYzY2YWVjZTUyYzI1YjhjYmUyZTcwMjUwMzg4Mjk4YzM0OGYzOTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/a2d75898f171f1aa322b7a8fdfa9331f32ee9562","sha":"a2d75898f171f1aa322b7a8fdfa9331f32ee9562","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/a2d75898f171f1aa322b7a8fdfa9331f32ee9562"}],"sha":"80c66aece52c25b8cbe2e70250388298c348f393","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/80c66aece52c25b8cbe2e70250388298c348f393"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18286430?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ivan-kalachikov","id":18286430,"login":"ivan-kalachikov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Mjg2NDMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/a2d75898f171f1aa322b7a8fdfa9331f32ee9562/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T11:28:38Z","email":"ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com","name":"Ivan Kalachikov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T11:28:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(VCST-5681): account sidebar renders raw i18n keys for module links (#2496)\n\n## Description\n\nThe account sidebar intermittently rendered raw i18n keys\n(`Quotes.navigation.route_name`, `Loyalty.navigation.route_name`,\n`Sales_rep.navigation.link`, …) instead of labels, on any locale, and\nnever recovered on that page load.\n\n**Root cause.** `getTranslatedMenuLink` translated the menu tree *in\nplace*. Module locale bundles (`quotes`, `loyalty`, `push-messages`,\n`back-in-stock`, `purchase-requests`, `sales-rep`, `skyflow`) are\n`import()`-ed and merged asynchronously after the sidebar has already\nrendered, so on that first pass `t(key)` returns the key. Because the\nlink objects were mutated rather than replaced, their identity never\nchanged — so when the bundle landed and the computed re-ran with the\ncorrect labels, Vue saw unchanged props on the child components and\nskipped the re-render. The schema healed; the DOM did not.\n\nThe same mutation also wrote the resolved label back over the i18n key,\nleaving nothing to re-translate on a runtime locale switch — which is\nthe \"wider set leaks after the in-page EN→DE switch\" symptom in the\nticket.\n\n**Fix.** Translate into a deep copy and leave the input untouched, so\nevery node in the returned tree is a new object and the raw keys survive\nfor the next locale. `children` are deliberately excluded from the clone\n— the recursion already copies them, so cloning them here would copy\neach subtree twice.\n\nThe defensive `clone`/`cloneDeep` calls at the three call sites only\nexisted to contain the mutation and are dropped. One of them was leaky:\nlodash `clone` is shallow, so `schema.children` stayed the caller''s\narray and the `sort()` below it reordered the shared menu schema in\nplace. The guarantee now lives in the helper instead of in each caller,\nwhich is what `registerAccountSection` — part of the `core-api`\ncontract, so the section object can belong to an out-of-repo plugin —\nneeds.\n\n**Note on the ticket''s premise:** the German keys are *not* missing —\nall six module `de.json` files carry them. The proposed \"key in\n`en.json` but absent from a sibling locale\" CI guard would not have\ncaught this.\n\n### Verification\n\nRan locally against `vcst-qa` with a 6 s delay injected into the module\nlocale loader to force the race (removed before commit):\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| cold load, `en-US` | 8 raw keys, still raw at 16 s+ | raw during the\nforced delay, all resolved once the bundle lands |\n| in-page EN→DE switch | English labels leak | all 18 links German, 0\nraw keys |\n\nAlso verified on a normal (undelayed) load: 0 raw keys at any point.\n\nNew regression tests mount the link objects through a child component,\nso they fail on the prop-identity freeze rather than only on the data.\nEach was confirmed to fail with the fix reverted:\n- `useNavigations.locale-merge.test.ts` — a late bundle reaches the DOM;\nlabels re-translate on a locale switch; the shared menu schema and a\nregistered account section both keep their raw keys.\n- `menu/index.test.ts` — `getTranslatedMenuLink` leaves its input\nuntouched, and the returned `route` object is not shared with it.\n\n`vue-tsc --build --force` clean, eslint clean, `vitest` 3130/3132. The\ntwo failures are `Test timed out in 5000ms` on the first test of\n`useNavigations.test.ts` and `useLanguages.test.ts` — the cold `await\nimport()` in each file, under load. Neither file''s subject is touched\nhere (`useLanguages.test.ts` is not in this PR at all), and both pass\nrun on their own: 21/21 and 36/36.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5681\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2496-afe9-afe9b2e4.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d63531f83079eb7bada4ac632f08e6b6ac45d365","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/d63531f83079eb7bada4ac632f08e6b6ac45d365"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/a2d75898f171f1aa322b7a8fdfa9331f32ee9562","verification":{"payload":"tree d63531f83079eb7bada4ac632f08e6b6ac45d365\nparent 755279c4771e3f10bf5267b43a16d0f7dd0d6c43\nauthor Ivan Kalachikov <ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com> 1790076518 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790076518 +0100\n\nfix(VCST-5681): account sidebar renders raw i18n keys for module links (#2496)\n\n## Description\n\nThe account sidebar intermittently rendered raw i18n keys\n(`Quotes.navigation.route_name`, `Loyalty.navigation.route_name`,\n`Sales_rep.navigation.link`, …) instead of labels, on any locale, and\nnever recovered on that page load.\n\n**Root cause.** `getTranslatedMenuLink` translated the menu tree *in\nplace*. Module locale bundles (`quotes`, `loyalty`, `push-messages`,\n`back-in-stock`, `purchase-requests`, `sales-rep`, `skyflow`) are\n`import()`-ed and merged asynchronously after the sidebar has already\nrendered, so on that first pass `t(key)` returns the key. Because the\nlink objects were mutated rather than replaced, their identity never\nchanged — so when the bundle landed and the computed re-ran with the\ncorrect labels, Vue saw unchanged props on the child components and\nskipped the re-render. The schema healed; the DOM did not.\n\nThe same mutation also wrote the resolved label back over the i18n key,\nleaving nothing to re-translate on a runtime locale switch — which is\nthe \"wider set leaks after the in-page EN→DE switch\" symptom in the\nticket.\n\n**Fix.** Translate into a deep copy and leave the input untouched, so\nevery node in the returned tree is a new object and the raw keys survive\nfor the next locale. `children` are deliberately excluded from the clone\n— the recursion already copies them, so cloning them here would copy\neach subtree twice.\n\nThe defensive `clone`/`cloneDeep` calls at the three call sites only\nexisted to contain the mutation and are dropped. One of them was leaky:\nlodash `clone` is shallow, so `schema.children` stayed the caller''s\narray and the `sort()` below it reordered the shared menu schema in\nplace. The guarantee now lives in the helper instead of in each caller,\nwhich is what `registerAccountSection` — part of the `core-api`\ncontract, so the section object can belong to an out-of-repo plugin —\nneeds.\n\n**Note on the ticket''s premise:** the German keys are *not* missing —\nall six module `de.json` files carry them. The proposed \"key in\n`en.json` but absent from a sibling locale\" CI guard would not have\ncaught this.\n\n### Verification\n\nRan locally against `vcst-qa` with a 6 s delay injected into the module\nlocale loader to force the race (removed before commit):\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| cold load, `en-US` | 8 raw keys, still raw at 16 s+ | raw during the\nforced delay, all resolved once the bundle lands |\n| in-page EN→DE switch | English labels leak | all 18 links German, 0\nraw keys |\n\nAlso verified on a normal (undelayed) load: 0 raw keys at any point.\n\nNew regression tests mount the link objects through a child component,\nso they fail on the prop-identity freeze rather than only on the data.\nEach was confirmed to fail with the fix reverted:\n- `useNavigations.locale-merge.test.ts` — a late bundle reaches the DOM;\nlabels re-translate on a locale switch; the shared menu schema and a\nregistered account section both keep their raw keys.\n- `menu/index.test.ts` — `getTranslatedMenuLink` leaves its input\nuntouched, and the returned `route` object is not shared with it.\n\n`vue-tsc --build --force` clean, eslint clean, `vitest` 3130/3132. The\ntwo failures are `Test timed out in 5000ms` on the first test of\n`useNavigations.test.ts` and `useLanguages.test.ts` — the cold `await\nimport()` in each file, under load. Neither file''s subject is touched\nhere (`useLanguages.test.ts` is not in this PR at all), and both pass\nrun on their own: 21/21 and 36/36.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5681\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2496-afe9-afe9b2e4.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsmZmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbh8QAJcBKMyZI1MH9C2A48l07etA\nZNFTITQ/GYErynSUXJgcHRsBbx1erma38xAm7V0tn3fSeePWJIgwuBWKLvB/2Evw\n6WPehHtTxFfcBgj5zOVNHmEAs1dAvkojf2E1PxM/m93sqyYs+RJbxxuVVGFI8GrO\n4DL+6cpJ597/nMlmUyXxcsMvYxkkXVUNx21GLtlJsIicf5dRnSzletvPsmZcF+oM\n+yFNQ48Cri0D7brR//JaHz4PwpQsGzVkn9IlA/69qd5aPDkShaLhZngzDCCJvBtu\nyBrTpah1VLL1aEAt0/jVmMkdeHO1to+1IDDrh6uZNGx2fgEdVSn4245yc1zv+GXJ\nDsu3kC8Yg7gx7Ikwi5WCvatISSWyz5T2IyJXFS9gQw+ycbSFK3Qh2crX5sD0GK/Q\n3nQsuO8Q4MHRz0taiy2SnNdi48bA3KrLs2PTmRYARgnwWLjSKgXpkWYa9Ottz9yc\neKABeWdp4pnawjUzmCaRc/NAyBBdWRRpToi3YoBhtMCNgxLa9HvrzBfQ9qIWqW7Y\nLwjnoDjB+NvEnUa72KZW+MaJ9RZxL9X9W/K/xu70FNBnO7Sewd5hbqntn1/xEsbM\nr+nGi6mfVc1v7ZldyQgehb8t+QhPr4i6iSj2QBUQ7Q7JvM9atxADqmHeY+CPzDA+\nVWM7J9fpm5vdNoxUjYQo\n=3fHy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T11:28:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/a2d75898f171f1aa322b7a8fdfa9331f32ee9562","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKGEyZDc1ODk4ZjE3MWYxYWEzMjJiN2E4ZmRmYTkzMzFmMzJlZTk1NjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/755279c4771e3f10bf5267b43a16d0f7dd0d6c43","sha":"755279c4771e3f10bf5267b43a16d0f7dd0d6c43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/755279c4771e3f10bf5267b43a16d0f7dd0d6c43"}],"sha":"a2d75898f171f1aa322b7a8fdfa9331f32ee9562","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/a2d75898f171f1aa322b7a8fdfa9331f32ee9562"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16372194?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/goldenmaya","id":16372194,"login":"goldenmaya","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzcyMTk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/755279c4771e3f10bf5267b43a16d0f7dd0d6c43/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T08:17:58Z","email":"mayapavlovna@gmail.com","name":"Maiia Diachkovskaia"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T08:17:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(VCST-5869): make popover dialogs announce, dismiss and restore focus (#2486)\n\n## Description\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\n<!-- Put link to your task in Jira here -->\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5869\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2486-00d2-00d2433a.zip\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Touches shared `VcPopover`, `VcSelect`, and focus/keyboard behavior\nacross many consumers; regressions could affect nested popovers, forms\n(Enter on selects), and focus after apply/reload.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Fixes **VCST-5869** by giving filter drawers a real non-modal dialog\nexperience: named panels, keyboard dismiss, and predictable focus.\n> \n> **`VcPopover`** gains an opt-in **`role=\"dialog\"`**\ncontract—`aria-label`, panel focus on open, Escape to close (one nested\nlevel at a time), focus return to the trigger (including after\ndisable/re-enable while loading), and **`aria-haspopup`** aligned with\npanel role. Escape handling moves from **keyup** to **keydown**;\ndisabling force-closes the panel so it cannot stay “open” in ARIA state.\n> \n> **Order filter UIs** (account desktop filters and sales-rep orders\nfilters) wire **`role=\"dialog\"`** + **`aria-label`** on the popover and\nset **`VcDialog :auto-focus=\"false\"`** so initial focus stays with the\npopover, not remounting dialog chrome.\n> \n> **`VcSelect`** and calendar popover wiring are adjusted so nested\ndropdowns/calendars **consume Escape only while open**, return focus to\ntheir triggers, and support ArrowDown/Enter keyboard entry—so Escape\nstill closes the outer filter drawer when inner layers are shut.\n> \n> Adds broad unit tests plus a Storybook **Dialog** story documenting\nthe contract.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n00d2433a909ec38a8fd9d77b0802b7575316011d. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"59ad03e5548321be5dfff72c59542652ac77b0fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/59ad03e5548321be5dfff72c59542652ac77b0fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/755279c4771e3f10bf5267b43a16d0f7dd0d6c43","verification":{"payload":"tree 59ad03e5548321be5dfff72c59542652ac77b0fe\nparent 510763312f93e979bbd0c33aa6459e7800e5c622\nauthor Maiia Diachkovskaia <mayapavlovna@gmail.com> 1790065078 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790065078 +0300\n\nfix(VCST-5869): make popover dialogs announce, dismiss and restore focus (#2486)\n\n## Description\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\n<!-- Put link to your task in Jira here -->\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5869\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2486-00d2-00d2433a.zip\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Touches shared `VcPopover`, `VcSelect`, and focus/keyboard behavior\nacross many consumers; regressions could affect nested popovers, forms\n(Enter on selects), and focus after apply/reload.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Fixes **VCST-5869** by giving filter drawers a real non-modal dialog\nexperience: named panels, keyboard dismiss, and predictable focus.\n> \n> **`VcPopover`** gains an opt-in **`role=\"dialog\"`**\ncontract—`aria-label`, panel focus on open, Escape to close (one nested\nlevel at a time), focus return to the trigger (including after\ndisable/re-enable while loading), and **`aria-haspopup`** aligned with\npanel role. Escape handling moves from **keyup** to **keydown**;\ndisabling force-closes the panel so it cannot stay “open” in ARIA state.\n> \n> **Order filter UIs** (account desktop filters and sales-rep orders\nfilters) wire **`role=\"dialog\"`** + **`aria-label`** on the popover and\nset **`VcDialog :auto-focus=\"false\"`** so initial focus stays with the\npopover, not remounting dialog chrome.\n> \n> **`VcSelect`** and calendar popover wiring are adjusted so nested\ndropdowns/calendars **consume Escape only while open**, return focus to\ntheir triggers, and support ArrowDown/Enter keyboard entry—so Escape\nstill closes the outer filter drawer when inner layers are shut.\n> \n> Adds broad unit tests plus a Storybook **Dialog** story documenting\nthe contract.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n00d2433a909ec38a8fd9d77b0802b7575316011d. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsjm2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiCcQAFiFhJ5rqYbdzdUV5+/NBMus\nAwtQR9PMPQynDc1yMOx8n4s+dLM6tYI68YtChvvn282A1V0sIHlyo6WAoylZDjXZ\nY6GLoHusVICLoSBuCn/knALweIWjlpleBjTCsWUXwHgQcpi+ATBVRzsPWZMldt3j\nl/XXXXkY3gjz6F3+U3FNshrZ6yCr/IDepT0gUZ5e9j5JrOeXXLA3Yt8Y/ILXFE5v\nyivPRcQtDAg4gFagyFaB87pUXZdIaFXuB92kxm6W55KOclVCJgPdXO/ZUW25BRSj\nGpFkdSggAZHqPSgQsIwJJ4yrMQ+k3T9IZ2mJDKBMs00a8+pbo1lhrxHFa6ZLUQFG\nML5WSq9Wo7rha0w9o2QrOBC3xeFZ+KEnqnm6OSq+Yvm1ZgmYckpY6h58+5//YbGi\nCMSpSArPUr+SOzYRVGd2obn1537IOMZ/hk4crarSuIYwZtoDjy+CsNvtup/ZzP3m\npTjrR1NP9/Py0R2yL3SNP2nWj5hk/hrv0ecbuyaoWLDkRlCSChOkkLxOe3+a2xo9\nrQbQMfo9+hllxzlGsIPxgzz71c7jMi10DE94c2/d4j9w23z0WPlF1nXUb12VxStn\nru33RPDtuUPpgbFK7O6ykzhhwC2cCTaLM1D+Zaf6SPYCB0iw5FzkzNGog5Bwx6f3\nrVft7lEcg97/g7InuWvZ\n=qldu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T08:17:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/755279c4771e3f10bf5267b43a16d0f7dd0d6c43","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDc1NTI3OWM0NzcxZTNmMTBiZjUyNjdiNDNhMTZkMGY3ZGQwZDZjNDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/510763312f93e979bbd0c33aa6459e7800e5c622","sha":"510763312f93e979bbd0c33aa6459e7800e5c622","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/510763312f93e979bbd0c33aa6459e7800e5c622"}],"sha":"755279c4771e3f10bf5267b43a16d0f7dd0d6c43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/755279c4771e3f10bf5267b43a16d0f7dd0d6c43"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16372194?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/goldenmaya","id":16372194,"login":"goldenmaya","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzcyMTk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/510763312f93e979bbd0c33aa6459e7800e5c622/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T02:56:05Z","email":"mayapavlovna@gmail.com","name":"Maiia Diachkovskaia"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T02:56:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(VCST-5870): breadcrumb a11y and the dead Sales Rep hub crumb (#2491)\n\n## Description\n\nVCST-5870 reported that the breadcrumb separators are announced by\nscreen readers.\nThe conclusion held; the mechanism named in the report did not.\n\n`aria-hidden=\"true\"` was already on `span.vc-breadcrumbs__slash` — since\n`b16357861`\n(PR #2200), and present at `261432a07b`, the merge commit of #2444 the\nreport was taken\nfrom. There is one breadcrumb component, so the report''s per-route table\n(present on\n`/catalog` and the PDP, absent on the sales-rep routes) cannot hold\neither.\n\nWhat did reach the accessibility tree is the wrapping element:\n`aria-hidden` covers an\nelement and its subtree but not its parent, so every separator''s `<li>`\nstayed in the list\nas a blank entry, and the sales-rep trail read as a 7-item list of which\n4 are crumbs.\n\n### Changes\n\n- `aria-hidden` moved from the slash `<span>` to its `<li>`.\n- `user-select: none` added to the slash, as\n`preview/vc-breadcrumbs.html` declares.\n- The slash is recoloured from `neutral-400` to `neutral-500`, the same\ntone as the crumb\ntext. This is a deliberate divergence from the same spec, which declares\n`color: var(--color-neutral-400)`, and still needs a design sign-off.\nAgainst the page\nbackground, on the two presets this repo measures: red light and coffee\nlight go\n2.42:1 → 4.54:1, red dark 3.67:1 → 6.99:1, coffee dark 3.39:1 → 4.56:1.\nThe glyph is\ndecorative and `aria-hidden`, so WCAG 1.4.3 does not require the change.\n- A crumb without a route renders as plain text instead of carrying\n  `vc-breadcrumbs__link`, so it no longer looks clickable.\n- The \"Sales Rep hub\" crumb now links to the Sales Rep dashboard on all\nthree hub pages.\nIt was painted in the link colour but carried no route: not focusable,\nand a click did\n  nothing.\n\n### For forks\n\nA routeless non-last crumb no longer renders an element carrying\n`.vc-breadcrumbs__link`;\nits text now sits directly in the `<li>`, matching the current-page\ncrumb. A fork styling\nthat class will no longer reach those crumbs.\n\n### Verification\n\n`yarn lint`, `yarn validate:types` and `yarn build-only` clean; 1329\nunit tests pass across\n`ui-kit` and `modules/sales-rep`. The new breadcrumb tests were\nmutation-tested with 7\nmutations — including moving `aria-hidden` back to the `<span>` and\nrenaming the slash\nclass — all caught.\n\nNot measured: that hidden items leave the accessibility tree is\ndocumented `aria-hidden`\nbehaviour, not a measurement of mine. The browser tooling available here\nderives its tree\nfrom the DOM and ignores the attribute — confirmed with a control by\nsetting `aria-hidden`\non the \"Home\" crumb and seeing it still reported.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5870\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2491-a69d-a69ddec8.zip\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Low Risk**\n> Localized UI-kit breadcrumb markup/styling and Sales Rep breadcrumb\nroutes; no auth or data-path changes.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Fixes **VCST-5870** by changing how `VcBreadcrumbs` exposes separators\nand routeless crumbs to assistive tech. Separator slashes now sit in\n**`aria-hidden` `<li>` items** (not only on the inner span), so screen\nreaders no longer hear blank list entries between real crumbs. **Middle\ncrumbs without a `route`** render as plain text in the list item instead\nof using the link styling, so they are not mistaken for clickable links.\n> \n> On Sales Rep **customer profile, orders, and order details**, the hub\ncrumb now **`route`s to `DASHBOARD_ROUTE_NAME`** instead of looking like\na link with no navigation. Unit tests cover the hub link and the\nbreadcrumb DOM/a11y shape; Storybook adds a **WithRouteGaps** example\nfor mixed linked and text-only crumbs. Separator styling adds\n**`select-none`** and shifts slash color to **`neutral-500`**.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\na69ddec8df30fd8983933fc00478640fed49d6e9. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->","tree":{"sha":"8dc89f908bcfe0d41b88edd9386124d093ec8b2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/8dc89f908bcfe0d41b88edd9386124d093ec8b2e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/510763312f93e979bbd0c33aa6459e7800e5c622","verification":{"payload":"tree 8dc89f908bcfe0d41b88edd9386124d093ec8b2e\nparent 9b59baefc0ed687d83e1fd82cc709ebb837e4eb6\nauthor Maiia Diachkovskaia <mayapavlovna@gmail.com> 1790045765 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790045765 +0300\n\nfix(VCST-5870): breadcrumb a11y and the dead Sales Rep hub crumb (#2491)\n\n## Description\n\nVCST-5870 reported that the breadcrumb separators are announced by\nscreen readers.\nThe conclusion held; the mechanism named in the report did not.\n\n`aria-hidden=\"true\"` was already on `span.vc-breadcrumbs__slash` — since\n`b16357861`\n(PR #2200), and present at `261432a07b`, the merge commit of #2444 the\nreport was taken\nfrom. There is one breadcrumb component, so the report''s per-route table\n(present on\n`/catalog` and the PDP, absent on the sales-rep routes) cannot hold\neither.\n\nWhat did reach the accessibility tree is the wrapping element:\n`aria-hidden` covers an\nelement and its subtree but not its parent, so every separator''s `<li>`\nstayed in the list\nas a blank entry, and the sales-rep trail read as a 7-item list of which\n4 are crumbs.\n\n### Changes\n\n- `aria-hidden` moved from the slash `<span>` to its `<li>`.\n- `user-select: none` added to the slash, as\n`preview/vc-breadcrumbs.html` declares.\n- The slash is recoloured from `neutral-400` to `neutral-500`, the same\ntone as the crumb\ntext. This is a deliberate divergence from the same spec, which declares\n`color: var(--color-neutral-400)`, and still needs a design sign-off.\nAgainst the page\nbackground, on the two presets this repo measures: red light and coffee\nlight go\n2.42:1 → 4.54:1, red dark 3.67:1 → 6.99:1, coffee dark 3.39:1 → 4.56:1.\nThe glyph is\ndecorative and `aria-hidden`, so WCAG 1.4.3 does not require the change.\n- A crumb without a route renders as plain text instead of carrying\n  `vc-breadcrumbs__link`, so it no longer looks clickable.\n- The \"Sales Rep hub\" crumb now links to the Sales Rep dashboard on all\nthree hub pages.\nIt was painted in the link colour but carried no route: not focusable,\nand a click did\n  nothing.\n\n### For forks\n\nA routeless non-last crumb no longer renders an element carrying\n`.vc-breadcrumbs__link`;\nits text now sits directly in the `<li>`, matching the current-page\ncrumb. A fork styling\nthat class will no longer reach those crumbs.\n\n### Verification\n\n`yarn lint`, `yarn validate:types` and `yarn build-only` clean; 1329\nunit tests pass across\n`ui-kit` and `modules/sales-rep`. The new breadcrumb tests were\nmutation-tested with 7\nmutations — including moving `aria-hidden` back to the `<span>` and\nrenaming the slash\nclass — all caught.\n\nNot measured: that hidden items leave the accessibility tree is\ndocumented `aria-hidden`\nbehaviour, not a measurement of mine. The browser tooling available here\nderives its tree\nfrom the DOM and ignores the attribute — confirmed with a control by\nsetting `aria-hidden`\non the \"Home\" crumb and seeing it still reported.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5870\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2491-a69d-a69ddec8.zip\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Low Risk**\n> Localized UI-kit breadcrumb markup/styling and Sales Rep breadcrumb\nroutes; no auth or data-path changes.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Fixes **VCST-5870** by changing how `VcBreadcrumbs` exposes separators\nand routeless crumbs to assistive tech. Separator slashes now sit in\n**`aria-hidden` `<li>` items** (not only on the inner span), so screen\nreaders no longer hear blank list entries between real crumbs. **Middle\ncrumbs without a `route`** render as plain text in the list item instead\nof using the link styling, so they are not mistaken for clickable links.\n> \n> On Sales Rep **customer profile, orders, and order details**, the hub\ncrumb now **`route`s to `DASHBOARD_ROUTE_NAME`** instead of looking like\na link with no navigation. Unit tests cover the hub link and the\nbreadcrumb DOM/a11y shape; Storybook adds a **WithRouteGaps** example\nfor mixed linked and text-only crumbs. Separator styling adds\n**`select-none`** and shifts slash color to **`neutral-500`**.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\na69ddec8df30fd8983933fc00478640fed49d6e9. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqse5FCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3bMQAAp0JMSe4nKevDzEFpBbvyl0\nZayWxxWCxADn181uVaUqS9ogHCqpG3mg51S1aBqU0pwDqt5mlmQBtlXmSzhm90l4\nXGmipJqcLBKkfT/ENYgMguQ2q1H5wrbU2TXdFasqpPIMWlsfsr+cTUZLTnvkInZm\nXIUY6pF48EmN6VdRubQchNKbkdZj8cA6Qbul1wap+f4WsJsFUxOn3vs/R8r0Y2jW\nZueSPelx/w9wUhydesKan1gEoLrireOxcjA7HFUz3HylQPJXVpobaBMvfk+lt3V9\nmM9C2/qIi2Vb3dRG4EydUi1Q4OyxNgNZNrqbxJMnf62iGE/UAaYTE2tKV3CqLUR9\n1aXVBUK5pLwEvhF7ZbFgBp3LyE/0p2aC+yt+1noeXVL7oGG8Ty0JF7y4PcLkXzXv\nE4ZQc9xMAyJxURK4Sn0FpMWeqf5yIn0JESK6ji2pYePTsbAaFGnx1UjR2SshejdJ\noMWrOzCIdgt31Kuf33u6GRTTJOK95gRrgL20EI86VRb765w6fPpqd7HfIQ/eyofL\n/E2GJj/xx4/dOJGU2JsGGewfZWWpv06uH5JSS7E1KxwQn9eQcdwieKMY8iEK0vHI\n6raebldJiBOFmxvUV+Iu29k5fWjJVKKtvsV5uLJTP90izpfpCXVJvKpEWT/fbx6x\nSzjLVY1x+9HqvcvDSg2e\n=ahfp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T02:56:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/510763312f93e979bbd0c33aa6459e7800e5c622","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDUxMDc2MzMxMmY5M2U5NzliYmQwYzMzYWE2NDU5ZTc4MDBlNWM2MjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/9b59baefc0ed687d83e1fd82cc709ebb837e4eb6","sha":"9b59baefc0ed687d83e1fd82cc709ebb837e4eb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/9b59baefc0ed687d83e1fd82cc709ebb837e4eb6"}],"sha":"510763312f93e979bbd0c33aa6459e7800e5c622","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/510763312f93e979bbd0c33aa6459e7800e5c622"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6213124?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToxaKZ/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToxaKZ/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToxaKZ/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToxaKZ/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ToxaKZ","id":6213124,"login":"ToxaKZ","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyMTMxMjQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToxaKZ/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToxaKZ/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToxaKZ/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToxaKZ/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToxaKZ/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ToxaKZ","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/9b59baefc0ed687d83e1fd82cc709ebb837e4eb6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T08:48:55Z","email":"Anton.Zorya@gmail.com","name":"Anton Zorya"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T08:48:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VCST-4933): support Shared Components in Page Builder preview (#2410)\n\n## Description\n\nAdds the Storefront preview support required by Page Builder Shared\nComponents.\n\nThe published Storefront does not resolve or fetch Shared Components at\nruntime. The Page Builder module expands `componentRef` placements\nbefore Pages indexing, so public Storefront routes continue to receive\nordinary Page Builder blocks.\n\nThis PR implements the authoring-preview side:\n\n- reactive VPPageBuilder content replacement;\n- a strict Designer/Storefront preview protocol;\n- one visual boundary around every multi-section Shared Component\nplacement;\n- hover, selection, and scroll synchronization between Designer and\npreview;\n- reliable iframe reconnect behavior;\n- trusted endpoint-origin validation.\n\n### Companion PageBuilder module PR\n\nhttps://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-module-pagebuilder/pull/159\n\n### Reactive Page Builder content\n\n`vp-page-builder.vue` reparses incoming content whenever the Pages\ndocument changes. It updates the rendered page for cache/network\nreplacements, validates the expected Page Builder shape, clears stale\ncontent when the new payload is empty or malformed, and preserves\nordinary block rendering.\n\n### Preview protocol and security\n\nThe preview `postMessage` contract is centralized and validated.\n\nMessages are accepted only when:\n\n- the source is the current parent Designer window;\n- the origin matches the configured Designer origin;\n- the payload has the expected `source`;\n- the message type and fields conform to the protocol.\n\nAsynchronous handling is serialized so an older locale or navigation\nupdate cannot overwrite newer preview state.\n\nThe `ep` query parameter accepts only valid HTTP(S) URLs and is reduced\nto its clean origin. Malformed values and `javascript:`/`file:`\nendpoints are rejected.\n\n### Shared Component placement overlay\n\nDesigner sends a resolved template together with placement metadata:\n\n```ts\n{\n  placementId,\n  componentRef,\n  startIndex,\n  count,\n  label\n}\n```\n\nThe preview:\n\n1. creates stable anchors around rendered Page Builder sections;\n2. maps each boundary to its first section and following section/end\nanchor;\n3. draws one boundary around all sections belonging to the placement;\n4. recalculates geometry after content, layout, or viewport changes;\n5. sends placement-level hover and selection events back to Designer;\n6. scrolls to the complete placement when Designer selects it.\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant D as Page Builder Designer\n    participant I as Storefront preview iframe\n    participant O as Shared Component overlay\n\n    I->>D: preview loaded and supported blocks\n    D->>I: resolved template and placement boundaries\n    I->>O: render anchors and boundaries\n    O->>D: hover/select placementId\n    D->>I: select/hover placementId\n    I->>O: highlight or scroll to placement\n```\n\nOverlay elements are authoring-only and are not part of business\ncontent.\n\n### Iframe lifecycle\n\nA newly loaded or replaced iframe must complete its own `preview-loaded`\nhandshake before queued messages are sent. Ready state from an old\niframe is not reused.\n\nThis prevents updates from being posted before the new iframe has\ninstalled its listener.\n\n### Published-page behavior\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    PB[\"Page Builder raw content\"] -->|\"resolve componentRef\"| PI[\"Pages index\"]\n    PI -->|\"ordinary expanded blocks\"| SF[\"Storefront VPPageBuilder\"]\n```\n\nThere is no production-time Storefront request to the Shared Components\nAPI. A component update becomes visible after the PageBuilder\npropagation job causes Pages to reindex affected published documents.\n\n\n### Verification\n\nCovered scenarios include VPPageBuilder content replacement, malformed\ncontent clearing, protocol validation, message ordering, iframe\nreconnect, boundary normalization, overlay\nrendering/resize/hover/click/selection/scrolling, and endpoint\nvalidation.\n\n## References\n\n### QA-test:\n\nAssume the Page Builder module and this Storefront build are already\ninstalled and configured.\n\n#### 1. Ordinary content regression\n\n1. Open a Page Builder page containing only ordinary sections.\n2. Verify Designer preview loads and renders every block.\n3. Add, edit, remove, reorder, hover, and select ordinary sections.\n4. Verify preview updates and bidirectional selection still work.\n5. Publish and verify the normal public Storefront route renders\ncorrectly.\n\n#### 2. Shared Component preview boundary\n\n1. Open a page containing a Shared Component with at least three visible\nsections.\n2. Verify all sections render in preview.\n3. Verify one boundary surrounds the complete component rather than each\nindividual section.\n4. Resize the preview and change content height; verify the boundary\nrealigns.\n5. Place the same component twice and verify two independent boundaries.\n\n#### 3. Selection and navigation synchronization\n\n1. Hover the component in Designer and verify its preview boundary\nhighlights.\n2. Hover/click the boundary and verify Designer receives placement\nhover/selection.\n3. Select an off-screen component in Designer and verify preview scrolls\nto the beginning of the full placement.\n4. Verify ordinary sections retain section-level selection and\nscrolling.\n\n#### 4. Live component editing\n\n1. Open **Edit original** for a Shared Component.\n2. Edit individual sections/blocks, including an image.\n3. Add, remove, and reorder component sections.\n4. Save and verify preview redraws the updated component and correct\nboundary.\n5. Detach one placement and verify its boundary disappears while its\nindependent blocks remain visible.\n\n#### 5. Iframe lifecycle\n\n1. Open Designer and wait for preview.\n2. Reload or recreate the preview iframe.\n3. Immediately perform several page edits.\n4. Verify messages are applied only after the new iframe announces\nreadiness.\n5. Verify no edit is lost and old iframe state is not reused.\n6. Navigate quickly between pages/components and verify the newest state\nwins.\n\n#### 6. Published Storefront integration\n\n1. Publish a page containing a Shared Component and wait for Pages\nindexing.\n2. Open the regular public Storefront URL, not `/designer-preview`.\n3. Verify the component renders as ordinary blocks.\n4. Verify no preview boundary, blocker, anchors, or Designer messaging\nappears.\n5. Edit the component original, wait for propagation/reindexing, and\nreload the public page.\n6. Verify the updated component appears without republishing the page.\n7. Verify ordinary page content remains unchanged.\n\n#### 7. Security validation\n\n1. Open Designer through the expected platform URL and verify preview\nconnects.\n2. Verify malformed, `javascript:`, and `file:` `ep` values do not\nestablish a trusted Designer origin.\n3. Verify a valid HTTP(S) endpoint is normalized to its origin.\n4. Verify messages from an unexpected origin or window are ignored.\n\n### Jira-link:\n\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-4933\n\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2410-4cf5-4cf5c3a6.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Basil Kotov <basilkot@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Anatolii Vasilev <49168917+vas11yev1work@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"8a2eea043505a534c424aeb2b6b21fb37d56917f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/8a2eea043505a534c424aeb2b6b21fb37d56917f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/9b59baefc0ed687d83e1fd82cc709ebb837e4eb6","verification":{"payload":"tree 8a2eea043505a534c424aeb2b6b21fb37d56917f\nparent b9a74dd7fb471927f698246087f0a367d28cfe3a\nauthor Anton Zorya <Anton.Zorya@gmail.com> 1789980535 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789980535 +0500\n\nfeat(VCST-4933): support Shared Components in Page Builder preview (#2410)\n\n## Description\n\nAdds the Storefront preview support required by Page Builder Shared\nComponents.\n\nThe published Storefront does not resolve or fetch Shared Components at\nruntime. The Page Builder module expands `componentRef` placements\nbefore Pages indexing, so public Storefront routes continue to receive\nordinary Page Builder blocks.\n\nThis PR implements the authoring-preview side:\n\n- reactive VPPageBuilder content replacement;\n- a strict Designer/Storefront preview protocol;\n- one visual boundary around every multi-section Shared Component\nplacement;\n- hover, selection, and scroll synchronization between Designer and\npreview;\n- reliable iframe reconnect behavior;\n- trusted endpoint-origin validation.\n\n### Companion PageBuilder module PR\n\nhttps://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-module-pagebuilder/pull/159\n\n### Reactive Page Builder content\n\n`vp-page-builder.vue` reparses incoming content whenever the Pages\ndocument changes. It updates the rendered page for cache/network\nreplacements, validates the expected Page Builder shape, clears stale\ncontent when the new payload is empty or malformed, and preserves\nordinary block rendering.\n\n### Preview protocol and security\n\nThe preview `postMessage` contract is centralized and validated.\n\nMessages are accepted only when:\n\n- the source is the current parent Designer window;\n- the origin matches the configured Designer origin;\n- the payload has the expected `source`;\n- the message type and fields conform to the protocol.\n\nAsynchronous handling is serialized so an older locale or navigation\nupdate cannot overwrite newer preview state.\n\nThe `ep` query parameter accepts only valid HTTP(S) URLs and is reduced\nto its clean origin. Malformed values and `javascript:`/`file:`\nendpoints are rejected.\n\n### Shared Component placement overlay\n\nDesigner sends a resolved template together with placement metadata:\n\n```ts\n{\n  placementId,\n  componentRef,\n  startIndex,\n  count,\n  label\n}\n```\n\nThe preview:\n\n1. creates stable anchors around rendered Page Builder sections;\n2. maps each boundary to its first section and following section/end\nanchor;\n3. draws one boundary around all sections belonging to the placement;\n4. recalculates geometry after content, layout, or viewport changes;\n5. sends placement-level hover and selection events back to Designer;\n6. scrolls to the complete placement when Designer selects it.\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant D as Page Builder Designer\n    participant I as Storefront preview iframe\n    participant O as Shared Component overlay\n\n    I->>D: preview loaded and supported blocks\n    D->>I: resolved template and placement boundaries\n    I->>O: render anchors and boundaries\n    O->>D: hover/select placementId\n    D->>I: select/hover placementId\n    I->>O: highlight or scroll to placement\n```\n\nOverlay elements are authoring-only and are not part of business\ncontent.\n\n### Iframe lifecycle\n\nA newly loaded or replaced iframe must complete its own `preview-loaded`\nhandshake before queued messages are sent. Ready state from an old\niframe is not reused.\n\nThis prevents updates from being posted before the new iframe has\ninstalled its listener.\n\n### Published-page behavior\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    PB[\"Page Builder raw content\"] -->|\"resolve componentRef\"| PI[\"Pages index\"]\n    PI -->|\"ordinary expanded blocks\"| SF[\"Storefront VPPageBuilder\"]\n```\n\nThere is no production-time Storefront request to the Shared Components\nAPI. A component update becomes visible after the PageBuilder\npropagation job causes Pages to reindex affected published documents.\n\n\n### Verification\n\nCovered scenarios include VPPageBuilder content replacement, malformed\ncontent clearing, protocol validation, message ordering, iframe\nreconnect, boundary normalization, overlay\nrendering/resize/hover/click/selection/scrolling, and endpoint\nvalidation.\n\n## References\n\n### QA-test:\n\nAssume the Page Builder module and this Storefront build are already\ninstalled and configured.\n\n#### 1. Ordinary content regression\n\n1. Open a Page Builder page containing only ordinary sections.\n2. Verify Designer preview loads and renders every block.\n3. Add, edit, remove, reorder, hover, and select ordinary sections.\n4. Verify preview updates and bidirectional selection still work.\n5. Publish and verify the normal public Storefront route renders\ncorrectly.\n\n#### 2. Shared Component preview boundary\n\n1. Open a page containing a Shared Component with at least three visible\nsections.\n2. Verify all sections render in preview.\n3. Verify one boundary surrounds the complete component rather than each\nindividual section.\n4. Resize the preview and change content height; verify the boundary\nrealigns.\n5. Place the same component twice and verify two independent boundaries.\n\n#### 3. Selection and navigation synchronization\n\n1. Hover the component in Designer and verify its preview boundary\nhighlights.\n2. Hover/click the boundary and verify Designer receives placement\nhover/selection.\n3. Select an off-screen component in Designer and verify preview scrolls\nto the beginning of the full placement.\n4. Verify ordinary sections retain section-level selection and\nscrolling.\n\n#### 4. Live component editing\n\n1. Open **Edit original** for a Shared Component.\n2. Edit individual sections/blocks, including an image.\n3. Add, remove, and reorder component sections.\n4. Save and verify preview redraws the updated component and correct\nboundary.\n5. Detach one placement and verify its boundary disappears while its\nindependent blocks remain visible.\n\n#### 5. Iframe lifecycle\n\n1. Open Designer and wait for preview.\n2. Reload or recreate the preview iframe.\n3. Immediately perform several page edits.\n4. Verify messages are applied only after the new iframe announces\nreadiness.\n5. Verify no edit is lost and old iframe state is not reused.\n6. Navigate quickly between pages/components and verify the newest state\nwins.\n\n#### 6. Published Storefront integration\n\n1. Publish a page containing a Shared Component and wait for Pages\nindexing.\n2. Open the regular public Storefront URL, not `/designer-preview`.\n3. Verify the component renders as ordinary blocks.\n4. Verify no preview boundary, blocker, anchors, or Designer messaging\nappears.\n5. Edit the component original, wait for propagation/reindexing, and\nreload the public page.\n6. Verify the updated component appears without republishing the page.\n7. Verify ordinary page content remains unchanged.\n\n#### 7. Security validation\n\n1. Open Designer through the expected platform URL and verify preview\nconnects.\n2. Verify malformed, `javascript:`, and `file:` `ep` values do not\nestablish a trusted Designer origin.\n3. Verify a valid HTTP(S) endpoint is normalized to its origin.\n4. Verify messages from an unexpected origin or window are ignored.\n\n### Jira-link:\n\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-4933\n\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2410-4cf5-4cf5c3a6.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Basil Kotov <basilkot@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Anatolii Vasilev <49168917+vas11yev1work@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsO93CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAm4QQAA0FreXofOb/9hOFV7mSjdCN\nBQ2+nw8tZcsHU4kIeoL+1uVAtK4oxZT50Nd3VAi7ndJXXoYHLhmax+ZhNF2ePnEt\n0HLB00of5Y8r6HlEb/dLJwWSIj7R8q/UF9hQLUc/iLSBn69k0lIY4GYf3hrx1UwH\ngoFPionv/0P+rPOD1TyDRr3C8t4opIzhXPLu5Dth07bST6YtOye3NLD4m1Tv+yPC\nNZyjItzQgV82639WkdZXGOsCm2YRj/UzNzbB+ZvrSePp9DVQMOcKcgn4rhcJ1EU2\nJZXyOikr8sCkkmlQkSl7IC/Q5zjHjwt4ecP1/vpRaFXSbRvd7GzwvTv2i1p3L8ku\nqIFMTPlDymqS3fxJFb/nWV7cMcnZbohEVM3l0cK5ls8ilY5CeKAawrdQ2eFex6u3\nSK2JHnNNpXcDmrJIC3632/t0hCuTx9hQVpMi2ktR5NIpNH84+lkuwOupZkATalbG\nZz72p+SrIaKYVJbii9hNnwfm5PGUGeIoFlUMSP4+hvQp+UML65gJsBwEB8GL9+Ig\nJ172WNNCvrjOcu94+8ZWSs04GgH9XE00fjj5/i8w8vRmpU6X3fRuMBaYYD3GpsVp\n4tHld094isK9HJBxPsf8sxJpgvJT9+bK7Vh7vjbGgoM8f8XJ4ep1ONEk/qTma4sL\nz9hY1uEvdhc3T2XzqcgE\n=2Q1/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T08:48:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/9b59baefc0ed687d83e1fd82cc709ebb837e4eb6","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDliNTliYWVmYzBlZDY4N2Q4M2UxZmQ4MmNjNzA5ZWJiODM3ZTRlYjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/b9a74dd7fb471927f698246087f0a367d28cfe3a","sha":"b9a74dd7fb471927f698246087f0a367d28cfe3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/b9a74dd7fb471927f698246087f0a367d28cfe3a"}],"sha":"9b59baefc0ed687d83e1fd82cc709ebb837e4eb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/9b59baefc0ed687d83e1fd82cc709ebb837e4eb6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18286430?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ivan-kalachikov","id":18286430,"login":"ivan-kalachikov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Mjg2NDMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/b9a74dd7fb471927f698246087f0a367d28cfe3a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T07:33:14Z","email":"ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com","name":"Ivan Kalachikov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T07:33:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(a11y): make clickable table rows reachable by keyboard (#2492)\n\n## Description\n\nSonar''s quality gate on `dev` fails on exactly two conditions, and both\ncome from the same three bugs:\n\n| Condition | Threshold | Actual |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `new_bugs` | 0 | **3** |\n| `new_reliability_rating` | A | **B** |\n\nAll three are `Web:MouseEventWithoutKeyboardEquivalentCheck` — a `<tr>`\nwith an `@click` handler, no `tabindex` and no key handler. These are\nthe only three clickable `<tr>` elements in the codebase:\n\n- `client-app/modules/quotes/pages/quotes.vue` — open a quote\n- `client-app/modules/purchase-requests/pages/purchase-requests.vue` —\nopen a purchase request\n- `client-app/shared/checkout/components/select-address-modal.vue` —\npick an address\n\nNot false positives: the rows genuinely could not be reached or fired\nwithout a mouse. The mobile variant of each table already ships a real\n`<button>` (or a `role=\"button\"` div) for the same action, so only the\ndesktop table was unreachable.\n\nEach row now gets `tabindex=\"0\"` and Enter/Space handlers calling the\nsame action as the click. That is the pattern `VcTable` already\nimplements for its own built-in clickable rows (`rowTabindex` /\n`onRowKeydown`), so these three hand-rolled `#desktop-body` /\n`#desktop-item` slots now behave like the kit''s. No ui-kit files are\ntouched, and the global `*:focus-visible` rule in `preflight.scss`\nsupplies the focus ring with no new CSS.\n\n`role=\"button\"` is deliberately **not** set. It would take the rows out\nof the table''s accessibility tree, and Sonar''s `PreferTagOverRoleCheck`\nreports a static `role=\"button\"` on a non-button tag — which would have\nadded three new `Web:S6819` major violations, another condition the gate\ncounts at threshold 0.\n\nEach row also gets a regression test covering click, Enter, Space and\nthe `tabindex` attribute. Removing the fix turns 6 of the 8 new keyboard\nassertions red, so the tests hold the behaviour rather than just\ndescribing it.\n\n### Out of scope\n\nThe remaining 131 Sonar issues on `dev` are all MINOR/INFO code smells\nand gate nothing; they are untouched here. Two adjacent observations\nworth their own ticket:\n\n- `quotes.vue` and `purchase-requests.vue` pass `@item-click` to\n`VcTable`, which emits `rowClick` — the listener is dead.\n- The mobile slot in both pages fires the same action from `@click` and\n`@keyup.enter`; on a native `<button>` Enter already produces a click,\nso it navigates twice.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `vitest run --dir client-app` — 183 files, 2970 tests, all green\n- `vue-tsc --build --force` — clean\n- `eslint` and `prettier --check` on the six touched files — clean\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\n\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2492-aca6-aca6e8fc.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dc7cee63f99c7e5ef37fe0ff8aeb6285cc80db0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/dc7cee63f99c7e5ef37fe0ff8aeb6285cc80db0d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/b9a74dd7fb471927f698246087f0a367d28cfe3a","verification":{"payload":"tree dc7cee63f99c7e5ef37fe0ff8aeb6285cc80db0d\nparent 324deb7ac45da0b9a96b1b7a30b0c611e4b42ace\nauthor Ivan Kalachikov <ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com> 1789975994 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789975994 +0100\n\nfix(a11y): make clickable table rows reachable by keyboard (#2492)\n\n## Description\n\nSonar''s quality gate on `dev` fails on exactly two conditions, and both\ncome from the same three bugs:\n\n| Condition | Threshold | Actual |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `new_bugs` | 0 | **3** |\n| `new_reliability_rating` | A | **B** |\n\nAll three are `Web:MouseEventWithoutKeyboardEquivalentCheck` — a `<tr>`\nwith an `@click` handler, no `tabindex` and no key handler. These are\nthe only three clickable `<tr>` elements in the codebase:\n\n- `client-app/modules/quotes/pages/quotes.vue` — open a quote\n- `client-app/modules/purchase-requests/pages/purchase-requests.vue` —\nopen a purchase request\n- `client-app/shared/checkout/components/select-address-modal.vue` —\npick an address\n\nNot false positives: the rows genuinely could not be reached or fired\nwithout a mouse. The mobile variant of each table already ships a real\n`<button>` (or a `role=\"button\"` div) for the same action, so only the\ndesktop table was unreachable.\n\nEach row now gets `tabindex=\"0\"` and Enter/Space handlers calling the\nsame action as the click. That is the pattern `VcTable` already\nimplements for its own built-in clickable rows (`rowTabindex` /\n`onRowKeydown`), so these three hand-rolled `#desktop-body` /\n`#desktop-item` slots now behave like the kit''s. No ui-kit files are\ntouched, and the global `*:focus-visible` rule in `preflight.scss`\nsupplies the focus ring with no new CSS.\n\n`role=\"button\"` is deliberately **not** set. It would take the rows out\nof the table''s accessibility tree, and Sonar''s `PreferTagOverRoleCheck`\nreports a static `role=\"button\"` on a non-button tag — which would have\nadded three new `Web:S6819` major violations, another condition the gate\ncounts at threshold 0.\n\nEach row also gets a regression test covering click, Enter, Space and\nthe `tabindex` attribute. Removing the fix turns 6 of the 8 new keyboard\nassertions red, so the tests hold the behaviour rather than just\ndescribing it.\n\n### Out of scope\n\nThe remaining 131 Sonar issues on `dev` are all MINOR/INFO code smells\nand gate nothing; they are untouched here. Two adjacent observations\nworth their own ticket:\n\n- `quotes.vue` and `purchase-requests.vue` pass `@item-click` to\n`VcTable`, which emits `rowClick` — the listener is dead.\n- The mobile slot in both pages fires the same action from `@click` and\n`@keyup.enter`; on a native `<button>` Enter already produces a click,\nso it navigates twice.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `vitest run --dir client-app` — 183 files, 2970 tests, all green\n- `vue-tsc --build --force` — clean\n- `eslint` and `prettier --check` on the six touched files — clean\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\n\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2492-aca6-aca6e8fc.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsN26CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtjYQAIz01raT5+zPdS3chRqTVutz\nSFMz2MqPFhKklkRH7QRPknLjp6HCAj/2gBe6vbiw8K4ggK+M66c7k+oAhJ7wr3Ee\nB2LDHrnxGElQYG1UCtc9h5hVO8KkpcEqi7GMTSmpcyWDbwmOn/Lc4IV9t3tPtt4b\nd0EoLgFcnX8/vOAEjA7Sji7UST5XBznPWswUgJQnF6i+nRk420EbwotJaHxQ4AQA\nv4JQ/qfouW8ROTIIcYb42v4gmfa380GaUZSQXggDuI2ImiAy8BhqfBj8qVrZYr6Y\n3tuvJtLVLyWN3fQ0mshr3w7Gr8qP/9cmTmisnOCrMmkZGQbgkrpHGUxAnawBsZV/\nhv/5N21pXG7zPH3sEmw78IUAml8m58UbhB0NIZp15BjF6o4l+IyMbm72NjNyvAoP\nb6fUOUT+f0Gb+lIqr1LL4UaJqw6GO9Pm1MBk7dr8SvQ8Wk8k5hDPT+ODVmIc1eoj\nIEgChQaRbUtxo0tno+l/NteEbskF0gA6Q+ts/Nw4Pzs285Rbw9m2fUkuGMVj/5kl\nezu5fP19hRft+WKNMihye4YePEWTSg5f1MDpltLdTRqF54mcF0C7Qp+dJ7WXqbL/\nlRB1Br+Wf91Ro315QYh2rJ0kfbqBZjl1N2tDj9TaAqSF0x7Iib/g97Xs05VFGBmv\ntfzS1UXQJQ6N3KkqHIBX\n=EFja\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-21T07:33:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/b9a74dd7fb471927f698246087f0a367d28cfe3a","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKGI5YTc0ZGQ3ZmI0NzE5MjdmNjk4MjQ2MDg3ZjBhMzY3ZDI4Y2ZlM2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/324deb7ac45da0b9a96b1b7a30b0c611e4b42ace","sha":"324deb7ac45da0b9a96b1b7a30b0c611e4b42ace","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/324deb7ac45da0b9a96b1b7a30b0c611e4b42ace"}],"sha":"b9a74dd7fb471927f698246087f0a367d28cfe3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/b9a74dd7fb471927f698246087f0a367d28cfe3a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46611511?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/muller39","id":46611511,"login":"muller39","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NjExNTEx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/324deb7ac45da0b9a96b1b7a30b0c611e4b42ace/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T07:22:42Z","email":"46611511+muller39@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Kurilin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T07:22:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(VCST-5773): pin GitHub Actions to SHAs and gate freshly published npm releases (#2462)\n\n## Description\n\n**Why:** 22 open Semgrep alerts on CI config. 20 are first-party\nVirtoCommerce actions pinned to `@master` — any push to those repos''\ndefault branch runs in our pipelines unreviewed. 2 are missing\nminimum-release-age gates for npm/yarn, so a freshly published (possibly\ncompromised) package version installs immediately.\n\n**Pinned 20 action refs to commit SHA**, across `theme-ci.yml`,\n`deploy-cloud.yml`, `theme-release-hotfix.yml`, `storybook-ci.yml`:\n\n| Repo | Refs | Comment | Note |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `VirtoCommerce/vc-github-actions` | 17 | `# master` | Latest tag\n(`v3.0.1`) is from 2020; master is 1555 commits ahead. Some referenced\nsub-actions (e.g. `get-deploy-param`) don''t exist at that tag, so\npinning to it would have broken CI — pinned to current master HEAD\ninstead. |\n| `VirtoCommerce/jira-upload-build-info` | 2 | `# master` | Fork of\n`HighwayThree/jira-upload-build-info`, no tags. |\n| `VirtoCommerce/jira-upload-deployment-info` | 1 | `# master` | Fork of\n`HighwayThree/jira-upload-deployment-info`, no tags. |\n\nNone of the three repos tag releases in active use, so Dependabot''s\n`github-actions` group (weekly, already configured with a 7-day\n`cooldown`) can''t reliably track updates by comparing tags for any of\nthem. Bumping these 20 refs to a newer commit stays a manual, periodic\ntask.\n\n**Install-age gates** (the other 2 alerts), 7 days to match the\nDependabot `cooldown` in `.github/dependabot.yml`:\n- `.npmrc`: `min-release-age=7`\n- `.yarnrc.yml`: `npmMinimalAgeGate: 10080` (minutes) — requires Yarn\n≥4.10, so `packageManager` was bumped `4.7.0` → `4.18.0` via `corepack\nuse yarn@4.18.0`, which also regenerated the pinned integrity hash in\n`package.json` and migrated `.yarnrc.yml`/`yarn.lock`.\n\n## Verified\n\n- `yarn install` and `yarn build` clean on Yarn 4.18.0 with the age gate\nenabled\n- All 20 pinned SHAs resolve (`gh api .../commits/<sha>`); for\n`vc-github-actions`, all 11 referenced sub-action folders exist at the\npinned commit\n- All 4 edited workflow files parse as valid YAML\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5773\n### Artifact URL:\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"678e0ef3e99e97129cd4582a4ac141ea08d37496","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/678e0ef3e99e97129cd4582a4ac141ea08d37496"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/324deb7ac45da0b9a96b1b7a30b0c611e4b42ace","verification":{"payload":"tree 678e0ef3e99e97129cd4582a4ac141ea08d37496\nparent 6cc0bb825e1ad71d405cf38e5b25355842560e26\nauthor Alexander Kurilin <46611511+muller39@users.noreply.github.com> 1789716162 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789716162 +0200\n\nfix(VCST-5773): pin GitHub Actions to SHAs and gate freshly published npm releases (#2462)\n\n## Description\n\n**Why:** 22 open Semgrep alerts on CI config. 20 are first-party\nVirtoCommerce actions pinned to `@master` — any push to those repos''\ndefault branch runs in our pipelines unreviewed. 2 are missing\nminimum-release-age gates for npm/yarn, so a freshly published (possibly\ncompromised) package version installs immediately.\n\n**Pinned 20 action refs to commit SHA**, across `theme-ci.yml`,\n`deploy-cloud.yml`, `theme-release-hotfix.yml`, `storybook-ci.yml`:\n\n| Repo | Refs | Comment | Note |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `VirtoCommerce/vc-github-actions` | 17 | `# master` | Latest tag\n(`v3.0.1`) is from 2020; master is 1555 commits ahead. Some referenced\nsub-actions (e.g. `get-deploy-param`) don''t exist at that tag, so\npinning to it would have broken CI — pinned to current master HEAD\ninstead. |\n| `VirtoCommerce/jira-upload-build-info` | 2 | `# master` | Fork of\n`HighwayThree/jira-upload-build-info`, no tags. |\n| `VirtoCommerce/jira-upload-deployment-info` | 1 | `# master` | Fork of\n`HighwayThree/jira-upload-deployment-info`, no tags. |\n\nNone of the three repos tag releases in active use, so Dependabot''s\n`github-actions` group (weekly, already configured with a 7-day\n`cooldown`) can''t reliably track updates by comparing tags for any of\nthem. Bumping these 20 refs to a newer commit stays a manual, periodic\ntask.\n\n**Install-age gates** (the other 2 alerts), 7 days to match the\nDependabot `cooldown` in `.github/dependabot.yml`:\n- `.npmrc`: `min-release-age=7`\n- `.yarnrc.yml`: `npmMinimalAgeGate: 10080` (minutes) — requires Yarn\n≥4.10, so `packageManager` was bumped `4.7.0` → `4.18.0` via `corepack\nuse yarn@4.18.0`, which also regenerated the pinned integrity hash in\n`package.json` and migrated `.yarnrc.yml`/`yarn.lock`.\n\n## Verified\n\n- `yarn install` and `yarn build` clean on Yarn 4.18.0 with the age gate\nenabled\n- All 20 pinned SHAs resolve (`gh api .../commits/<sha>`); for\n`vc-github-actions`, all 11 referenced sub-action folders exist at the\npinned commit\n- All 4 edited workflow files parse as valid YAML\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5773\n### Artifact URL:\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrObCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPboQAC1wTMsUeaDKb/Bmd3+HyQnZ\ngCIhTjPQ8tfrXDnvEGwgf+zG1Zpe9dDSic+emrGfNetIugxsfJAyaLMw8qQ6Kire\nBtcJraUmB3f+OYDrQ1SB6YEaNw5X9NpsqWFtDI3H+ZwvoOQMJ+VRzv7O/kaolZzt\naeIotFiGA+FDUfR9j8ln7mOijqKFTjizcxpcoTshP8GhtpYOnnwQ8JRX+wdr1V7w\n9sd+QdYa9AjnYW9hiRSvGIu6sHma5AOPmzULIdXQokNOTJmLsDZf51M37dpwejO8\n1xafxx5AinTv3fzqVy/p895qP0lQG7I1I99RBC3qKuXdm3qVp3L+rg/Bhhcsaz9x\nVSyFaPkUKs1CNoVASts4uSkrCow8LBmNe1VoJbzTqMu8zCgK2wy2FDCmaYD1TRH7\nvfYiiFav67fvhXF/a/nJnv7mdaC1EOx2V5dorfGSDd2pZQiuAvzVTrb1xTZ53irh\neXHupe9Wa/S0hYWQz+S/Pr2atvx99AZy4Vn+5/KvX3B+/m14rI14PvcN8pg8Xwk4\nTBXRsamjfM4nrMnrTd2TtI+e6GPVXtrHPzB1c6lNoY8+wx9NZ+cHkUBKUUaTb56T\nQSGsvahWLZRl3WFjsRuQz94G2vcyemJM9s7Z0qiDkj+OZ03xXn4nw/m1zByzfIoi\ncooBPkDRLMAJZfvwLcdd\n=xkKL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T07:22:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/324deb7ac45da0b9a96b1b7a30b0c611e4b42ace","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDMyNGRlYjdhYzQ1ZGEwYjlhOTZiMWI3YTMwYjBjNjExZTRiNDJhY2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/6cc0bb825e1ad71d405cf38e5b25355842560e26","sha":"6cc0bb825e1ad71d405cf38e5b25355842560e26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/6cc0bb825e1ad71d405cf38e5b25355842560e26"}],"sha":"324deb7ac45da0b9a96b1b7a30b0c611e4b42ace","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/324deb7ac45da0b9a96b1b7a30b0c611e4b42ace"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46611511?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/muller39","id":46611511,"login":"muller39","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NjExNTEx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/6cc0bb825e1ad71d405cf38e5b25355842560e26/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T07:22:33Z","email":"46611511+muller39@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Kurilin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T07:22:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(VCST-5772): clear scanner noise — 3 false positives and 8 dev-script findings (#2461)\n\n## Description\n- Fixes the `vc-postmessage-no-origin-check` Semgrep rule: the\ndeep-expression operator never reached into a nested `if`-condition, so\nthe real origin guards in `builder-preview.plugin.ts` and\n`fcm-service-worker-v1.12.js` slipped past it (false positives\n[#217](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/security/code-scanning/217),\n[#221](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/security/code-scanning/221),\n[#222](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/security/code-scanning/222)).\n- Closes the 8 CodeQL findings in `scripts/` (build-only dev tooling,\nnever reaches a browser):\n- TLS bypasses\n([#145](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/security/code-scanning/145),\n[#146](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/security/code-scanning/146))\nare already gated to localhost/dev-only — annotated with CodeQL\nsuppression comments.\n- Log injection\n([#148](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/security/code-scanning/148)-[#152](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/security/code-scanning/152))\n— response/error data is now stripped of control characters before it\nreaches `console.log`/`console.error`.\n- Write-to-file\n([#147](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/security/code-scanning/147))\n— the resolved locale file path is validated to stay inside the locale\nfolder before the translated content is written back.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5772\nArtifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2461-ea8a-ea8a8f4d.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"287a4cdbfb5cac67139666e48ad3db72ce157db6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/287a4cdbfb5cac67139666e48ad3db72ce157db6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/6cc0bb825e1ad71d405cf38e5b25355842560e26","verification":{"payload":"tree 287a4cdbfb5cac67139666e48ad3db72ce157db6\nparent ea075776282e02c491357c594f1b3104743deaed\nauthor Alexander Kurilin <46611511+muller39@users.noreply.github.com> 1789716153 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789716153 +0200\n\nfix(VCST-5772): clear scanner noise — 3 false positives and 8 dev-script findings (#2461)\n\n## Description\n- Fixes the `vc-postmessage-no-origin-check` Semgrep rule: the\ndeep-expression operator never reached into a nested `if`-condition, so\nthe real origin guards in `builder-preview.plugin.ts` and\n`fcm-service-worker-v1.12.js` slipped past it (false positives\n[#217](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/security/code-scanning/217),\n[#221](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/security/code-scanning/221),\n[#222](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/security/code-scanning/222)).\n- Closes the 8 CodeQL findings in `scripts/` (build-only dev tooling,\nnever reaches a browser):\n- TLS bypasses\n([#145](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/security/code-scanning/145),\n[#146](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/security/code-scanning/146))\nare already gated to localhost/dev-only — annotated with CodeQL\nsuppression comments.\n- Log injection\n([#148](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/security/code-scanning/148)-[#152](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/security/code-scanning/152))\n— response/error data is now stripped of control characters before it\nreaches `console.log`/`console.error`.\n- Write-to-file\n([#147](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/security/code-scanning/147))\n— the resolved locale file path is validated to stay inside the locale\nfolder before the translated content is written back.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5772\nArtifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2461-ea8a-ea8a8f4d.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-