,"node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDZjYzBiYjgyNWUxYWQ3MWQ0MDVjZjM4ZTViMjUzNTU4NDI1NjBlMjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/ea075776282e02c491357c594f1b3104743deaed","sha":"ea075776282e02c491357c594f1b3104743deaed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/ea075776282e02c491357c594f1b3104743deaed"}],"sha":"6cc0bb825e1ad71d405cf38e5b25355842560e26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/6cc0bb825e1ad71d405cf38e5b25355842560e26"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46611511?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/muller39","id":46611511,"login":"muller39","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NjExNTEx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/ea075776282e02c491357c594f1b3104743deaed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T07:22:20Z","email":"46611511+muller39@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Kurilin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T07:22:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(VCST-5771): harden three untrusted-input sinks in client-app (#2460)\n\n## Description\n\nCloses\n[VCST-5771](https://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5771).\nCodeQL and Semgrep flagged 5 alerts across 3 places where untrusted\ninput reaches a navigation or query sink. One commit per sink so any\nsingle flow can be reverted independently.\n\n- **Return-URL redirect** (`core/utilities/common/index.ts` —\n`getReturnUrlValue`): only accept genuine same-origin relative paths\nbefore assigning `location.href`, instead of a hostname comparison\nscanners don''t recognize as a sanitizer. Normalizes backslashes and\nASCII tab/newline first, mirroring the browser''s own URL parsing, so a\nvalue like `/\\t/evil.com` can''t collapse into a protocol-relative\n`//evil.com` after the check already said \"safe\". Closes #143 (open\nredirect) and #144 (XSS). This also hardens the OIDC external sign-in\nredirect in `useIdentityProvider.ts`, which shares the same source\nfunction.\n- **Order navigation** (`useOrderNavigation.ts`): add `\"noopener\"` to\nthe `_blank` `window.open` call, closing #139 (missing noopener /\nreverse tabnabbing). The `router.resolve()`-based `location.href` branch\n(#140) is left as-is and should be dismissed in code scanning — that URL\ncomes from an internal route name/id, not user input.\n- **Organization search** (`useUserOrganizations.ts`): the search phrase\nescaped `\"` but not `\\`, so a trailing backslash broke out of the quoted\nfilter-syntax string sent to the Contact/Member query. Closes #142.\nExtracted the escaping into `escapeFilterSyntaxValue()` in\n`core/utilities/search/facets.ts` and reused it from the two\nfacet-filter call sites that already implemented the identical rule —\nthree independent copies of the same escaping logic is how this bug\nhappened in the first place.\n\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5771\n\n[VCST-5771]:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5771?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ\nArtifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2460-d04a-d04ac964.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"01b7e576ef1980212d7b6a77a65871cfba418037","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/01b7e576ef1980212d7b6a77a65871cfba418037"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/ea075776282e02c491357c594f1b3104743deaed","verification":{"payload":"tree 01b7e576ef1980212d7b6a77a65871cfba418037\nparent 85505ec6f7c29efb06f5cc9e25185dfa27f31ea4\nauthor Alexander Kurilin <46611511+muller39@users.noreply.github.com> 1789716140 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789716140 +0200\n\nfix(VCST-5771): harden three untrusted-input sinks in client-app (#2460)\n\n## Description\n\nCloses\n[VCST-5771](https://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5771).\nCodeQL and Semgrep flagged 5 alerts across 3 places where untrusted\ninput reaches a navigation or query sink. One commit per sink so any\nsingle flow can be reverted independently.\n\n- **Return-URL redirect** (`core/utilities/common/index.ts` —\n`getReturnUrlValue`): only accept genuine same-origin relative paths\nbefore assigning `location.href`, instead of a hostname comparison\nscanners don''t recognize as a sanitizer. Normalizes backslashes and\nASCII tab/newline first, mirroring the browser''s own URL parsing, so a\nvalue like `/\\t/evil.com` can''t collapse into a protocol-relative\n`//evil.com` after the check already said \"safe\". Closes #143 (open\nredirect) and #144 (XSS). This also hardens the OIDC external sign-in\nredirect in `useIdentityProvider.ts`, which shares the same source\nfunction.\n- **Order navigation** (`useOrderNavigation.ts`): add `\"noopener\"` to\nthe `_blank` `window.open` call, closing #139 (missing noopener /\nreverse tabnabbing). The `router.resolve()`-based `location.href` branch\n(#140) is left as-is and should be dismissed in code scanning — that URL\ncomes from an internal route name/id, not user input.\n- **Organization search** (`useUserOrganizations.ts`): the search phrase\nescaped `\"` but not `\\`, so a trailing backslash broke out of the quoted\nfilter-syntax string sent to the Contact/Member query. Closes #142.\nExtracted the escaping into `escapeFilterSyntaxValue()` in\n`core/utilities/search/facets.ts` and reused it from the two\nfacet-filter call sites that already implemented the identical rule —\nthree independent copies of the same escaping logic is how this bug\nhappened in the first place.\n\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5771\n\n[VCST-5771]:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5771?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ\nArtifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2460-d04a-d04ac964.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrOatCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2tMQAJbEwokKdf9p4LLrVOHtcYiq\nPfTj453ZaClp1ZP8z9ihUTovCV1sFDNQT0ImwyAK2YPCSERgDZB5VODaIbJ5BDFa\nhDB6AMOL7egC+/rbRgw74+Fh4US+pbIh8HJ2woPOU64qtQHtB+64qmeljRmwOs+Z\n+G0MqXegRHCVaXRt3oBrjsniszL6eiQEvhfBjRB8gduCSXFSL6tw4YNgW61unpPS\nKomXBydR31Mn8sHHph/McBlrrIGSu4PlCUCBoJ+4Fjk0VNBwc4sOToO+Ul/ouP5q\nucDo2U+MDeV5Dvq2iGE28FzCyWIf/sHW4vmWP3RWLbfiSPmkhuxceS7iTDEzGtmG\nxqXnTR+NpJOWP6L9DvBvoujDEoyJJ5CSzNgMCQyBc2VwsFwM76PeIsYcqM9StM+A\nNrRt6sPuO22MVcmnyocax/tr+YxNHyosEpEHegISubYSVq1cxwJFNQJ+L2A4WaBO\n9QDcu2zwZRKtm26CnsDOditam9WmWvKNQeitiqV4RhctxYqkkM8gyyNJRrrPLmiu\nTXDu4D5fRhjakiIMQX1Qs5wFShVK0xzUKzGwBJnFTatCU6gMLDHmdiqkFibCv37x\n39aAmzDyTSAFRCEnKui9aLX+Hj7UW2Myft/ahWGDdqZ+x7tIfX4IdQ2eW2m561qV\nSQA3iKiAHbT9tudjwI4+\n=vEPy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T07:22:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/ea075776282e02c491357c594f1b3104743deaed","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKGVhMDc1Nzc2MjgyZTAyYzQ5MTM1N2M1OTRmMWIzMTA0NzQzZGVhZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/85505ec6f7c29efb06f5cc9e25185dfa27f31ea4","sha":"85505ec6f7c29efb06f5cc9e25185dfa27f31ea4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/85505ec6f7c29efb06f5cc9e25185dfa27f31ea4"}],"sha":"ea075776282e02c491357c594f1b3104743deaed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/ea075776282e02c491357c594f1b3104743deaed"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16372194?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/goldenmaya","id":16372194,"login":"goldenmaya","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzcyMTk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/85505ec6f7c29efb06f5cc9e25185dfa27f31ea4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T07:08:32Z","email":"mayapavlovna@gmail.com","name":"Maiia Diachkovskaia"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T07:08:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(VCST-5912): fix false invalid state and wrong values on the quantity spinbutton (#2484)\n\n## Description\n\nThe quantity spinbutton announced a false state before the user touched\nit: an untouched `0` was reported as invalid, and the value read out was\n`min` rather than the `0` on screen.\n\n**Root cause.** `min` is the *stepping floor*, not the range the control\naccepts — with `allowZero` (the default) `0` stays reachable below it.\nPublishing `min` as the input''s own bound made an untouched `0` a\ngenuine constraint violation, and Chrome clamps a spinbutton''s announced\nvalue into `[valuemin, valuemax]`, so the screen said `0` while a screen\nreader said `3`.\n\nVerified on the same Storybook story before and after:\n\n```\nbefore   invalid=true  value=3  valuemin=3  valuemax=10  valuetext=0\nafter                  value=0  valuemin=0  valuemax=10  valuetext=0\n```\n\n**What changed**\n\n- `VcQuantityStepper` now separates the two meanings:\n`stepMin`/`stepMax` feed the stepping helpers, `boundMin` is what the\ninput and `aria-valuemin` publish. Stepping behaviour is unchanged — 1→3\nand 2→0 across the gap still hold, and there are now tests for both.\n- `max` is published raw. Omitting it means unbounded and nothing is\nannounced, instead of advertising `9007199254740991`.\n- `aria-valuenow` / `aria-valuemax` use `null` rather than `\"\"` when\nabsent — an empty ARIA value is not the same as no value.\n- `VcInput` exposes `aria-invalid` from its `error` prop, with a\nconsumer override through `aria[\"aria-invalid\"]`.\n\n**Two decisions worth flagging to reviewers**\n\n*Why `:max=\"max\"` and not `:max=\"stepMax\"`.* `stepMax` is `props.max ??\nNumber.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER`, an internal fallback needed only because the\nstepping helpers read `max === 0` as \"unbounded\". Publishing it would\nrestore the ticket''s own complaint — an absurd upper bound read out to\nthe user. That `max === 0` ambiguity is real but pre-existing and now\ntracked separately.\n\n*Why `aria-invalid` on `VcInput` is in this PR and not in the a11y\nfollow-ups.* It is not an addition — it replaces a signal this fix\nremoves. The native `rangeUnderflow` used to mark the whole band below\n`min` as invalid, including values that genuinely are (2 with a minimum\nof 3). Moving the bound to `0` removes that signal for the legitimate\ncase too, so `aria-invalid` plus `aria-describedby` put it back, now\nwith a message that explains it:\n\n```\n2 with min 3   min=\"0\"  rangeUnderflow=false  aria-invalid=\"true\"  aria-describedby → message\n```\n\nThe same treatment for `VcTextarea`, `VcCheckbox` and `VcDatePicker` is\ndeliberately *not* here — nothing in this PR breaks without it.\n\n**Follow-ups filed**\n\n- [VCST-5990](https://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5990) —\nwith `allowZero: false` (cart and quote line items) a value below the\nfloor is a truthful constraint violation that nothing explains.\nDifferent failure from this ticket: every attribute is correct, the\nmessage is missing.\n- [VCST-5991](https://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5991) —\n`max={0}` means \"unbounded\" to the stepping helpers and \"ceiling is\nzero\" to the DOM. Measured: the control announces a ceiling of `0`,\nreports overflow, and still steps 5→6. Unreachable from the shipped app,\na trap for forks.\n- [VCST-5993](https://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5993),\n[VCST-5994](https://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5994) —\n`VcTextarea` accessible name, and the error state on the remaining\ncontrols.\n\n**Verification**\n\nStorybook AX tree before/after (above); unit coverage for the stepper\nbounds, `QuantityControl` in stepper mode against the mission-modal row,\nand `VcInput`''s `aria-invalid`; each new behaviour mutation-tested.\n`yarn lint` clean — 7 warnings, identical at the merge base.\n`validate:types`, `build-only` and the full suite green.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\n<!-- Put link to your task in Jira here -->\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5912\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2484-ae2f-ae2f564d.zip\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Touches shared UI primitives (`VcInput`, `VcQuantityStepper`) used\nacross cart and product flows; behavior is accessibility-focused but\nchanges published min/max and invalid signaling.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Fixes **VCST-5912**: quantity spinbuttons no longer announce a false\ninvalid state or the wrong value when `allowZero` shows `0` below a\nproduct minimum.\n> \n> **`VcQuantityStepper`** splits the stepping floor (`stepMin` /\ninternal `stepMax`) from what the native input and ARIA expose\n(`boundMin` is `0` when `allowZero`, otherwise the floor). Omitted `max`\nstays unbounded in the DOM instead of advertising\n`Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER`; `aria-valuenow` / `aria-valuemax` use `null`\nwhen there is nothing to announce. Increment/decrement behavior across\nthe gap below `min` is unchanged and now covered by tests.\n> \n> **`VcInput`** maps the visual `error` prop to **`aria-invalid`**, with\nsensible handling of consumer overrides via `aria[\"aria-invalid\"]`, so\nvalidation errors (e.g. quantity between 0 and minimum) are exposed to\nassistive tech together with `aria-describedby`.\n> \n> Adds unit tests for stepper bounds, `QuantityControl` in stepper mode,\nand `VcInput` `aria-invalid`, plus a Storybook **`AllowZeroBelowMin`**\nexample.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\nae2f564d6f12c406715f571817e0ca6c02afbeb8. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n\n[VCST-5990]:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5990?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ","tree":{"sha":"5b81163c83852513e2bd00f659968212eff078ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/5b81163c83852513e2bd00f659968212eff078ec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/85505ec6f7c29efb06f5cc9e25185dfa27f31ea4","verification":{"payload":"tree 5b81163c83852513e2bd00f659968212eff078ec\nparent 41d8351f2ecc830d7a5cea7c9b57b1657335401d\nauthor Maiia Diachkovskaia <mayapavlovna@gmail.com> 1789715312 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789715312 +0300\n\nfix(VCST-5912): fix false invalid state and wrong values on the quantity spinbutton (#2484)\n\n## Description\n\nThe quantity spinbutton announced a false state before the user touched\nit: an untouched `0` was reported as invalid, and the value read out was\n`min` rather than the `0` on screen.\n\n**Root cause.** `min` is the *stepping floor*, not the range the control\naccepts — with `allowZero` (the default) `0` stays reachable below it.\nPublishing `min` as the input''s own bound made an untouched `0` a\ngenuine constraint violation, and Chrome clamps a spinbutton''s announced\nvalue into `[valuemin, valuemax]`, so the screen said `0` while a screen\nreader said `3`.\n\nVerified on the same Storybook story before and after:\n\n```\nbefore   invalid=true  value=3  valuemin=3  valuemax=10  valuetext=0\nafter                  value=0  valuemin=0  valuemax=10  valuetext=0\n```\n\n**What changed**\n\n- `VcQuantityStepper` now separates the two meanings:\n`stepMin`/`stepMax` feed the stepping helpers, `boundMin` is what the\ninput and `aria-valuemin` publish. Stepping behaviour is unchanged — 1→3\nand 2→0 across the gap still hold, and there are now tests for both.\n- `max` is published raw. Omitting it means unbounded and nothing is\nannounced, instead of advertising `9007199254740991`.\n- `aria-valuenow` / `aria-valuemax` use `null` rather than `\"\"` when\nabsent — an empty ARIA value is not the same as no value.\n- `VcInput` exposes `aria-invalid` from its `error` prop, with a\nconsumer override through `aria[\"aria-invalid\"]`.\n\n**Two decisions worth flagging to reviewers**\n\n*Why `:max=\"max\"` and not `:max=\"stepMax\"`.* `stepMax` is `props.max ??\nNumber.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER`, an internal fallback needed only because the\nstepping helpers read `max === 0` as \"unbounded\". Publishing it would\nrestore the ticket''s own complaint — an absurd upper bound read out to\nthe user. That `max === 0` ambiguity is real but pre-existing and now\ntracked separately.\n\n*Why `aria-invalid` on `VcInput` is in this PR and not in the a11y\nfollow-ups.* It is not an addition — it replaces a signal this fix\nremoves. The native `rangeUnderflow` used to mark the whole band below\n`min` as invalid, including values that genuinely are (2 with a minimum\nof 3). Moving the bound to `0` removes that signal for the legitimate\ncase too, so `aria-invalid` plus `aria-describedby` put it back, now\nwith a message that explains it:\n\n```\n2 with min 3   min=\"0\"  rangeUnderflow=false  aria-invalid=\"true\"  aria-describedby → message\n```\n\nThe same treatment for `VcTextarea`, `VcCheckbox` and `VcDatePicker` is\ndeliberately *not* here — nothing in this PR breaks without it.\n\n**Follow-ups filed**\n\n- [VCST-5990](https://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5990) —\nwith `allowZero: false` (cart and quote line items) a value below the\nfloor is a truthful constraint violation that nothing explains.\nDifferent failure from this ticket: every attribute is correct, the\nmessage is missing.\n- [VCST-5991](https://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5991) —\n`max={0}` means \"unbounded\" to the stepping helpers and \"ceiling is\nzero\" to the DOM. Measured: the control announces a ceiling of `0`,\nreports overflow, and still steps 5→6. Unreachable from the shipped app,\na trap for forks.\n- [VCST-5993](https://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5993),\n[VCST-5994](https://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5994) —\n`VcTextarea` accessible name, and the error state on the remaining\ncontrols.\n\n**Verification**\n\nStorybook AX tree before/after (above); unit coverage for the stepper\nbounds, `QuantityControl` in stepper mode against the mission-modal row,\nand `VcInput`''s `aria-invalid`; each new behaviour mutation-tested.\n`yarn lint` clean — 7 warnings, identical at the merge base.\n`validate:types`, `build-only` and the full suite green.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\n<!-- Put link to your task in Jira here -->\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5912\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2484-ae2f-ae2f564d.zip\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Touches shared UI primitives (`VcInput`, `VcQuantityStepper`) used\nacross cart and product flows; behavior is accessibility-focused but\nchanges published min/max and invalid signaling.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Fixes **VCST-5912**: quantity spinbuttons no longer announce a false\ninvalid state or the wrong value when `allowZero` shows `0` below a\nproduct minimum.\n> \n> **`VcQuantityStepper`** splits the stepping floor (`stepMin` /\ninternal `stepMax`) from what the native input and ARIA expose\n(`boundMin` is `0` when `allowZero`, otherwise the floor). Omitted `max`\nstays unbounded in the DOM instead of advertising\n`Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER`; `aria-valuenow` / `aria-valuemax` use `null`\nwhen there is nothing to announce. Increment/decrement behavior across\nthe gap below `min` is unchanged and now covered by tests.\n> \n> **`VcInput`** maps the visual `error` prop to **`aria-invalid`**, with\nsensible handling of consumer overrides via `aria[\"aria-invalid\"]`, so\nvalidation errors (e.g. quantity between 0 and minimum) are exposed to\nassistive tech together with `aria-describedby`.\n> \n> Adds unit tests for stepper bounds, `QuantityControl` in stepper mode,\nand `VcInput` `aria-invalid`, plus a Storybook **`AllowZeroBelowMin`**\nexample.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\nae2f564d6f12c406715f571817e0ca6c02afbeb8. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n\n[VCST-5990]:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5990?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrONwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAv8oQAJls//gknzrqxRrBd993kSSL\n3WX/K+NBNtj9oVssRRzqwGsnHwl5rpciyRyNnpcOCYrN1LGMrI6E0tnwujUETgYI\niuXjrxO/oJp0lHQvWAd483M+joJHXYGAK05v91YhaQ0EMCICAi0C9gvCmaUUrthF\nBjYPI2Ye4nSr68gdQYt7Tq7PNCHiREkXlUwYdjsm3k8Lhs2YJdf01UZ4A0dQZjKS\n55DyzD8PaZHLo2mNBIZPis9xSnOfmPYSmJvBtygzc/uOfcETgMw+jnup2aOL/qSV\nrNIj7743QCCLcRwyJO8qJru2xU25a5JDirRKdH2Btyo4NzxOxad4Tu4PcAECcrSi\nmgCgg//9OfB9uGJJkU629KV9jpfXT+qN6goq+Gd+mQzBlR3SfeMJVcNofftHH0dr\nKiPJEgQH/FW8kMHGyV3qw0tXOOI4uwpGMqMNb8pr7dKndqT+iU/WZbO4I4fqGxb/\nWU+9wyRn9rt4D+FXl7SNTUCznSl3PezjQCO2XbrninTOHX76uUa4urGAEuYlGKlA\ngqMGXjzt4AvrXeTmCe8fotCiVh7Rp6aZP0w3wDss9njBZlYmwD55wbGfnUPuYRD5\nPso09BNtByaN+ieacRXwkYnyxsMM665vvbqpUhGsmQaEtPy5htYW0L3WLGyBdGpr\n+zCxY1IklUJc+/V5StLI\n=Gi2V\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T07:08:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/85505ec6f7c29efb06f5cc9e25185dfa27f31ea4","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDg1NTA1ZWM2ZjdjMjllZmIwNmY1Y2M5ZTI1MTg1ZGZhMjdmMzFlYTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/41d8351f2ecc830d7a5cea7c9b57b1657335401d","sha":"41d8351f2ecc830d7a5cea7c9b57b1657335401d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/41d8351f2ecc830d7a5cea7c9b57b1657335401d"}],"sha":"85505ec6f7c29efb06f5cc9e25185dfa27f31ea4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/85505ec6f7c29efb06f5cc9e25185dfa27f31ea4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20122385?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ksavosteev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ksavosteev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ksavosteev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ksavosteev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ksavosteev","id":20122385,"login":"ksavosteev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMTIyMzg1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ksavosteev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ksavosteev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ksavosteev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ksavosteev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ksavosteev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ksavosteev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/41d8351f2ecc830d7a5cea7c9b57b1657335401d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T16:08:06Z","email":"Konstantin.Savosteev@virtoway.com","name":"Konstantin Savosteev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T16:08:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VCST-5024): add storeId to loyalty points queries (#2475)\n\n## Description\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5024\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2475-31ff-31ff8d30.zip\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Changes loyalty balance and history API contracts (required storeId)\nand depends on Loyalty module 3.1008.0; wrong or missing globals.storeId\nwould break those queries at runtime.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> **Adds required `storeId` to loyalty balance and points history\nGraphQL queries**, matching the updated Loyalty API and the existing\nmission-progress pattern.\n> \n> `GetLoyaltyBalance` and `GetLoyaltyPointsHistory` now declare\n`$storeId: String!` and pass it to the API. The client helpers read\n`storeId` from `globals` so callers (`useLoyaltyBalance`,\n`useLoyaltyPointsHistory`) stay unchanged. `getLoyaltyPointsHistory`\naccepts `Partial<QueryLoyaltyPointsHistoryArgs>` since `storeId` is\nsupplied internally. Generated GraphQL types in core and the loyalty\nmodule are updated accordingly.\n> \n> **VirtoCommerce.Loyalty** is bumped from `3.1006.0` to `3.1008.0` in\n`backend-packages.json` for the backend schema that requires\nstore-scoped loyalty data.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n31ff8d301eea2d32911ae9b8ad33653548fc353d. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"8d0fa3f02cfc1f8f6130b887da56addaa8787d90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/8d0fa3f02cfc1f8f6130b887da56addaa8787d90"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/41d8351f2ecc830d7a5cea7c9b57b1657335401d","verification":{"payload":"tree 8d0fa3f02cfc1f8f6130b887da56addaa8787d90\nparent 683016d7359e64d82d52b03d19f9e693614cb6ea\nauthor Konstantin Savosteev <Konstantin.Savosteev@virtoway.com> 1789661286 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789661286 +0200\n\nfeat(VCST-5024): add storeId to loyalty points queries (#2475)\n\n## Description\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5024\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2475-31ff-31ff8d30.zip\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Changes loyalty balance and history API contracts (required storeId)\nand depends on Loyalty module 3.1008.0; wrong or missing globals.storeId\nwould break those queries at runtime.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> **Adds required `storeId` to loyalty balance and points history\nGraphQL queries**, matching the updated Loyalty API and the existing\nmission-progress pattern.\n> \n> `GetLoyaltyBalance` and `GetLoyaltyPointsHistory` now declare\n`$storeId: String!` and pass it to the API. The client helpers read\n`storeId` from `globals` so callers (`useLoyaltyBalance`,\n`useLoyaltyPointsHistory`) stay unchanged. `getLoyaltyPointsHistory`\naccepts `Partial<QueryLoyaltyPointsHistoryArgs>` since `storeId` is\nsupplied internally. Generated GraphQL types in core and the loyalty\nmodule are updated accordingly.\n> \n> **VirtoCommerce.Loyalty** is bumped from `3.1006.0` to `3.1008.0` in\n`backend-packages.json` for the backend schema that requires\nstore-scoped loyalty data.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n31ff8d301eea2d32911ae9b8ad33653548fc353d. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrBBmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwu0QAHy/0QuAVe1J8k5igrf8l1ym\neATwUMc2psC/TdX89EyCD3+jXKKkPfiPlKF4Oo2wN8oBKmxOF2Dqor88puGBvLO5\nH6CK5qdhaPQqLR3oK7F/In+80kcsBXyln3/bsftoo8FOBRAyrZD4Bmj/KDSph4N5\nUGWyd9NxurvjOxJeNwAxUCZehFecrwxU4JyaFyIg88kuS+w+TXS4ZQaNeo8KWtEh\nwqd2HXRk503qdZ3AAR9SXFBMtyyaW5bl8PbEbQYwYs2dax7aFjevqdk6djTATx+G\nEvjkodNB/M3OiT4o5KgCmtUOwMqFjloLhCJh9Yllu03mT9S8zuc8pIW8S/lS5MZf\nJhrCGjTT1a1sr8F+MygQjMSD6jvx5c5ghzgrWxoDyibIPoyIEtf8yIt470o6bU3j\nX2yNf5lN/1DcMyZW7miFTxmOeO++9Q+UxfxbUQsMA8AkXyNCeL/8QbSK3uM6Tayv\nw1btttCBVAt81xgNcBf/P5wXk5A5RnvEp/f4K0MI8T2BzCHTfW7UXh3OBNc9R+FE\nNtIkJMuNYcCWE3ncSR6KMD6u23Gnyyh1BZSkoqTIEdpWzhC1o2PlscsUHU3CZshl\nPvcVOrEZe31t0F98JLH2ZeB9cR+1hhY4C8bAi8YxL7vjpVFjnoiYEA8efLkHAw59\npVVZvDLvFH2tZAf7mdJG\n=WClB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T16:08:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/41d8351f2ecc830d7a5cea7c9b57b1657335401d","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDQxZDgzNTFmMmVjYzgzMGQ3YTVjZWE3YzliNTdiMTY1NzMzNTQwMWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/683016d7359e64d82d52b03d19f9e693614cb6ea","sha":"683016d7359e64d82d52b03d19f9e693614cb6ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/683016d7359e64d82d52b03d19f9e693614cb6ea"}],"sha":"41d8351f2ecc830d7a5cea7c9b57b1657335401d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/41d8351f2ecc830d7a5cea7c9b57b1657335401d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16372194?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/goldenmaya","id":16372194,"login":"goldenmaya","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzcyMTk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/683016d7359e64d82d52b03d19f9e693614cb6ea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T11:14:23Z","email":"mayapavlovna@gmail.com","name":"Maiia Diachkovskaia"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T11:14:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VCST-5097): implement vc-date-range-picker component (#2402)\n\n## Description\n\nAdds the date-range stack to the UI kit and moves the account orders\nfilter onto it.\n\n**New public components**\n\n- `VcRangeCalendar` — two-endpoint calendar grid on reka''s\n`RangeCalendarRoot`.\n- `VcDateRangeInput` — one field with two typed segments, a shared\ndetails row and one clear button.\n- `VcDateRangePicker` — the shell, in two layouts: `combined` (one\nfield, one range calendar) and\n`split` (two separately labelled `VcDatePicker`s, each with its own\ncalendar).\n- New composables `useDateRangeField`, `useCalendarPopover`,\n`useShellFocusEvents`, plus date and\n  focus utilities.\n\n**Shared components this PR also changes.** These ride along and reach\nfurther than the date stack:\n\n- `VcInput` — new `seamless` and `hideDetails` props, so a parent shell\ncan own the chrome and the\ndetails row. `aria-describedby` is now merged rather than overwritten,\nso a forwarded value is no\nlonger dropped. Horizontal padding moved behind `--vc-input-padding-x`.\n- `VcSelect` and `VcInput` — the clear-icon size literal moved into\n`getInputClearIconSize()` in\n  `ui-kit/utilities/css.ts`. Same values, one source.\n- `VcCalendar` / `use-calendar-base` — advisory `softMin`/`softMax`,\nHome/End/PageUp/PageDown per\nAPG, a `clear` emit, a `preventDeselect` prop, and two contrast fixes:\nthe selected day moves from\n`primary-500` to `primary-700`, the focus ring from `0.35` to `0.8`\nalpha. Both were under the 3:1\nof WCAG 1.4.11 in some presets; the new pair clears AA in all 14\npreset/mode combinations, worst\n  case 5.02 : 1.\n- `VcDateInput` — `seamless`, `hideDetails` and an `update:errorText`\nemit, so a shell can render the\n  validation message itself.\n\n**Orders filter**\n\n`DateFilterSelect` now renders a single `VcDateRangePicker`. Desktop\npasses `layout=\"split\"`.\nMobile stays on `combined` — that is the designer''s mock — and the group\ncarries a visible label, so\nthe field is not left unlabelled. Validity is seeded from the range\norder and re-emitted on mount, so\nApply is not left latched after the filter popover remounts.\n\n**Notes for forks**\n\n- The range-order message moved from\n`shared.account.orders_filter.invalid_range` to\n`ui_kit.date_range_input.invalid_range`: it belongs to the ui-kit\ncomponent now, not the orders\n  page. A fork overriding the old key has to re-point it.\n- New override keys: `--vc-calendar-selected-bg` / `-text` and\n`--vc-range-calendar-selected-bg` /\n`-text` for the selected day, `--vc-input-padding-x` for input padding.\n- `preventDeselect` defaults to `true` on `VcCalendar` and\n`VcDatePicker`, so re-clicking the\nselected day no longer clears it. An optional field that passes neither\n`clearable` nor\n`showFooter` should set `preventDeselect: false` to keep a pointer route\nto clearing.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\n<!-- Put link to your task in Jira here -->\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5097\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2402-2425-2425c9a1.zip\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Touches shared calendar/input primitives and filter validity wiring\nused by orders Apply; behavior changes (e.g. default preventDeselect,\nrange-order i18n key) can affect forks and edge cases around Escape/reka\nsync in range calendars.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Introduces a **date-range UI stack** (`VcRangeCalendar`,\n`VcDateRangeInput`, and the `VcDateRangePicker` shell with **combined**\nvs **split** layouts) and wires the account **orders date filter** to a\nsingle `VcDateRangePicker` instead of two separate `VcDatePicker`s.\nDesktop filters use `layout=\"split\"`; validity is seeded from range\norder and re-emitted on mount/remount so Apply does not stay disabled.\n> \n> **Calendar and input building blocks** gain shared behavior:\n`use-calendar-base` adds advisory `softMin`/`softMax`, APG keyboard\nnavigation, placeholder clamping, and focus entry; `VcCalendar` adds\n`preventDeselect`, a footer **`clear`** emit, soft-bound styling/a11y,\nand **selected-day contrast** (`primary-700` + theme tokens). Dark mode\nadds range-calendar **hover-preview** colors so preview text stays\nreadable.\n> \n> **Composable shells** get `seamless` / `hideDetails` on `VcDateInput`\n(and contract types), plus `update:errorText` and exposed clear/reset\nhelpers for parent-owned chrome. `@vc-frontend/core` bumps to **0.1.1**\nwith `organization.isLockedForCurrentUser` on user types.\n> \n> Large Vitest coverage accompanies `DateFilterSelect`, calendars, range\ninput, and input-details single-line clamping.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n2425c9a176c5490f1c0b1f35abd8ccd897448294. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"cf8adf99b781c40b6a5f5bcadbb3f68d434c9131","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/cf8adf99b781c40b6a5f5bcadbb3f68d434c9131"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/683016d7359e64d82d52b03d19f9e693614cb6ea","verification":{"payload":"tree cf8adf99b781c40b6a5f5bcadbb3f68d434c9131\nparent 450f76fad69f357fe0c656512f6adf27430b6c64\nauthor Maiia Diachkovskaia <mayapavlovna@gmail.com> 1789643663 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789643663 +0300\n\nfeat(VCST-5097): implement vc-date-range-picker component (#2402)\n\n## Description\n\nAdds the date-range stack to the UI kit and moves the account orders\nfilter onto it.\n\n**New public components**\n\n- `VcRangeCalendar` — two-endpoint calendar grid on reka''s\n`RangeCalendarRoot`.\n- `VcDateRangeInput` — one field with two typed segments, a shared\ndetails row and one clear button.\n- `VcDateRangePicker` — the shell, in two layouts: `combined` (one\nfield, one range calendar) and\n`split` (two separately labelled `VcDatePicker`s, each with its own\ncalendar).\n- New composables `useDateRangeField`, `useCalendarPopover`,\n`useShellFocusEvents`, plus date and\n  focus utilities.\n\n**Shared components this PR also changes.** These ride along and reach\nfurther than the date stack:\n\n- `VcInput` — new `seamless` and `hideDetails` props, so a parent shell\ncan own the chrome and the\ndetails row. `aria-describedby` is now merged rather than overwritten,\nso a forwarded value is no\nlonger dropped. Horizontal padding moved behind `--vc-input-padding-x`.\n- `VcSelect` and `VcInput` — the clear-icon size literal moved into\n`getInputClearIconSize()` in\n  `ui-kit/utilities/css.ts`. Same values, one source.\n- `VcCalendar` / `use-calendar-base` — advisory `softMin`/`softMax`,\nHome/End/PageUp/PageDown per\nAPG, a `clear` emit, a `preventDeselect` prop, and two contrast fixes:\nthe selected day moves from\n`primary-500` to `primary-700`, the focus ring from `0.35` to `0.8`\nalpha. Both were under the 3:1\nof WCAG 1.4.11 in some presets; the new pair clears AA in all 14\npreset/mode combinations, worst\n  case 5.02 : 1.\n- `VcDateInput` — `seamless`, `hideDetails` and an `update:errorText`\nemit, so a shell can render the\n  validation message itself.\n\n**Orders filter**\n\n`DateFilterSelect` now renders a single `VcDateRangePicker`. Desktop\npasses `layout=\"split\"`.\nMobile stays on `combined` — that is the designer''s mock — and the group\ncarries a visible label, so\nthe field is not left unlabelled. Validity is seeded from the range\norder and re-emitted on mount, so\nApply is not left latched after the filter popover remounts.\n\n**Notes for forks**\n\n- The range-order message moved from\n`shared.account.orders_filter.invalid_range` to\n`ui_kit.date_range_input.invalid_range`: it belongs to the ui-kit\ncomponent now, not the orders\n  page. A fork overriding the old key has to re-point it.\n- New override keys: `--vc-calendar-selected-bg` / `-text` and\n`--vc-range-calendar-selected-bg` /\n`-text` for the selected day, `--vc-input-padding-x` for input padding.\n- `preventDeselect` defaults to `true` on `VcCalendar` and\n`VcDatePicker`, so re-clicking the\nselected day no longer clears it. An optional field that passes neither\n`clearable` nor\n`showFooter` should set `preventDeselect: false` to keep a pointer route\nto clearing.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\n<!-- Put link to your task in Jira here -->\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5097\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2402-2425-2425c9a1.zip\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Touches shared calendar/input primitives and filter validity wiring\nused by orders Apply; behavior changes (e.g. default preventDeselect,\nrange-order i18n key) can affect forks and edge cases around Escape/reka\nsync in range calendars.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Introduces a **date-range UI stack** (`VcRangeCalendar`,\n`VcDateRangeInput`, and the `VcDateRangePicker` shell with **combined**\nvs **split** layouts) and wires the account **orders date filter** to a\nsingle `VcDateRangePicker` instead of two separate `VcDatePicker`s.\nDesktop filters use `layout=\"split\"`; validity is seeded from range\norder and re-emitted on mount/remount so Apply does not stay disabled.\n> \n> **Calendar and input building blocks** gain shared behavior:\n`use-calendar-base` adds advisory `softMin`/`softMax`, APG keyboard\nnavigation, placeholder clamping, and focus entry; `VcCalendar` adds\n`preventDeselect`, a footer **`clear`** emit, soft-bound styling/a11y,\nand **selected-day contrast** (`primary-700` + theme tokens). Dark mode\nadds range-calendar **hover-preview** colors so preview text stays\nreadable.\n> \n> **Composable shells** get `seamless` / `hideDetails` on `VcDateInput`\n(and contract types), plus `update:errorText` and exposed clear/reset\nhelpers for parent-owned chrome. `@vc-frontend/core` bumps to **0.1.1**\nwith `organization.isLockedForCurrentUser` on user types.\n> \n> Large Vitest coverage accompanies `DateFilterSelect`, calendars, range\ninput, and input-details single-line clamping.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n2425c9a176c5490f1c0b1f35abd8ccd897448294. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqq8uPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbxIQABOYui6MOXnPet24YyJmvzld\n3kNPyTr4ykN6Xm0aHSgiqCLhALcH01QJpEDjmEA8XxAGWZPm9uEdRusMLShwr/Dg\ntGdaztuY43TxSX07m7AGxpXMPVhU44a0SJ/URg9TnJDXtP0isH+VNr4Ep4U+P2yl\nSvLZsbiBiTvTeddiT/J+l8X9A9FY5pqHVIjApgYXv2m3JIJo6q+Puydir1k+qwjd\nqdQOg/hAufQOWt/ZisSzRdbHsqddXncj6HKzpfHIVetaeTYi5sPLAc1wd7OEA0/l\nMNzMA6uS/YnsvEFUDYjvbqvWFPMqTkEnU+r3Reu/jm7x6DVvuq+MNIDBgpzZaWJ5\nwrnaoDkO