693614cb6ea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49168917?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vas11yev1work","id":49168917,"login":"vas11yev1work","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5MTY4OTE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/450f76fad69f357fe0c656512f6adf27430b6c64/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T07:31:56Z","email":"49168917+vas11yev1work@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Anatolii Vasilev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T07:31:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VCST-4386): skyflow module (#2440)\n\n## Description\n\nAdds Skyflow as a payment method: a PCI-compliant tokenized card form\n(iframe via the `skyflow-js` SDK) at checkout/order-payment/cart, plus\nan account page to view and delete saved cards.\n\nThe whole feature ships as a self-contained module in\n`client-app/modules/skyflow` — its own GraphQL queries/mutations,\ncomposables, CVV validation, and locale files for all 13 supported\nlanguages — following `modules/README.md`''s rule that core must be able\nto work with any module deleted.\n\n### How it plugs into core\n\n- **Extension points, not hardcoded checks.** All three payment surfaces\n(`checkout/payment.vue`, `account/order-payment.vue`, and the cart-stage\n`payment.vue`) render Skyflow through `<ExtensionPointList>` against\ngeneric `paymentPage` / `orderPaymentPage` / `cartPayment` categories.\n`cartPayment` is new — added so the cart-stage payment step no longer\nneeds a direct import of the module (previously the only one of the\nthree that did). The module registers itself into all three from\n`modules/skyflow/index.ts`; core never references Skyflow by name.\n- **Reliable feature flag.** Gating uses `useModuleSettings`, which\nreads from `getPageContext` (the query the app can''t boot without),\nrather than the module-version list populated by a call that''s allowed\nto fail silently on boot. The other 7 modules already use this pattern —\nSkyflow follows it instead of introducing a second, less reliable source\nof \"is this module installed\".\n- **Lazy-loaded SDK.** `payment-processing-skyflow.vue` is only pulled\nin behind `defineAsyncComponent`, so the ~80 KB gzip `skyflow-js` bundle\nstays out of the eager graph shared by checkout/account routes.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-4386\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2440-d131-d1310391.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2be2c00ac2486b33b0a788b3582dae30f7c8012f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/2be2c00ac2486b33b0a788b3582dae30f7c8012f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/450f76fad69f357fe0c656512f6adf27430b6c64","verification":{"payload":"tree 2be2c00ac2486b33b0a788b3582dae30f7c8012f\nparent 308ff1d700f9bcfae6234ae356bb12740ee467f6\nauthor Anatolii Vasilev <49168917+vas11yev1work@users.noreply.github.com> 1789630316 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789630316 +0200\n\nfeat(VCST-4386): skyflow module (#2440)\n\n## Description\n\nAdds Skyflow as a payment method: a PCI-compliant tokenized card form\n(iframe via the `skyflow-js` SDK) at checkout/order-payment/cart, plus\nan account page to view and delete saved cards.\n\nThe whole feature ships as a self-contained module in\n`client-app/modules/skyflow` — its own GraphQL queries/mutations,\ncomposables, CVV validation, and locale files for all 13 supported\nlanguages — following `modules/README.md`''s rule that core must be able\nto work with any module deleted.\n\n### How it plugs into core\n\n- **Extension points, not hardcoded checks.** All three payment surfaces\n(`checkout/payment.vue`, `account/order-payment.vue`, and the cart-stage\n`payment.vue`) render Skyflow through `<ExtensionPointList>` against\ngeneric `paymentPage` / `orderPaymentPage` / `cartPayment` categories.\n`cartPayment` is new — added so the cart-stage payment step no longer\nneeds a direct import of the module (previously the only one of the\nthree that did). The module registers itself into all three from\n`modules/skyflow/index.ts`; core never references Skyflow by name.\n- **Reliable feature flag.** Gating uses `useModuleSettings`, which\nreads from `getPageContext` (the query the app can''t boot without),\nrather than the module-version list populated by a call that''s allowed\nto fail silently on boot. The other 7 modules already use this pattern —\nSkyflow follows it instead of introducing a second, less reliable source\nof \"is this module installed\".\n- **Lazy-loaded SDK.** `payment-processing-skyflow.vue` is only pulled\nin behind `defineAsyncComponent`, so the ~80 KB gzip `skyflow-js` bundle\nstays out of the eager graph shared by checkout/account routes.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-4386\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2440-d131-d1310391.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cla