efe8d4fa78dfaa532a8ff919d9bb03b1a1471cf"}],"sha":"916b986b88bd863b5afcb14158645b75e5478521","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/916b986b88bd863b5afcb14158645b75e5478521"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16372194?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/goldenmaya","id":16372194,"login":"goldenmaya","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzcyMTk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/3efe8d4fa78dfaa532a8ff919d9bb03b1a1471cf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T11:13:19Z","email":"mayapavlovna@gmail.com","name":"Maiia Diachkovskaia"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T11:13:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VCST-5472): expose selection scope and headAttrs on VcTable #header slot (#2459)\n\n## Problem\n\n`#header` replaces the built-in header row entirely — selection cell\nincluded — but the\n  slot got no scope. A custom header therefore could not:\n\n- render the leading selection cell, so every column shifted by one\nwhile body rows kept\n    theirs, silently and with no error;\n- drive select-all, or read whether the page is fully / partially\nselected;\n- reproduce `vc-table__head--sticky`, the sole carrier of the header''s\nsticky positioning,\nso `sticky-header` and `max-height` had no effect on a custom header.\n\nThe last one was live in our own docs: `SlotsApiCustomHeader` hardcoded\n  `class=\"vc-table__head\"` and its sticky controls did nothing.\n\n  ## What this adds\n\n  `#header` now receives a scope:\n\n  | Field | |\n  |---|---|\n  | `showSelectionColumn` | whether a selection cell must be rendered |\n  | `selectionMode` | `\"single\"` \\| `\"multiple\"` \\| `undefined` |\n  | `isAllSelected` / `isSomeSelected` | select-all checkbox state |\n  | `canSelectAll` | `false` when no row on the page is selectable |\n  | `toggleSelectAll` | no-op outside `multiple` |\n| `selectionColumnAttrs` | `v-bind` onto a `<th>` — matching width +\nsticky behaviour |\n| `headAttrs` | `v-bind` onto the `<thead>` — carries the sticky\nmodifier |\n\nPlus a DEV-only console warning when a custom header renders one cell\nfewer than the body,\n  which is the misalignment case above.\n\nBoth attrs bags expose `class` as a **string**, not an array. A bare\n`v-bind=\"attrs\"`\ncompiles to `normalizeProps(guardReactiveProps(attrs))`;\n`guardReactiveProps` does not clone\na plain object, so `normalizeProps` rewrites `class` in place on the\ncomputed''s cached\nvalue. With a sibling attribute Vue routes through `mergeProps` and\nclones instead — which\nis why the built-in call sites never showed it while the documented\nusage was broken.\n\n  ## Breaking change — needs a decision before merge\n\n  `--vc-table-selected-bg` → `--vc-table-selected-bg-color`.\n\nThe old name shipped in 2.53.0–2.56.0. A fork overriding it in\n`_custom.scss` gets no merge\nconflict, no build error and no lint failure — the selected-row\nhighlight just reverts to\nthe default in all 7 presets and both themes. `ui-kit/DEPRECATION.md`\nrequires keeping the\nold name working through a deprecation period for renamed\nprops/slots/events; CSS custom\n  properties are not literally named there.\n\nOptions: ship an alias (`var(--vc-table-selected-bg, …)` as the fallback\ntail), or accept\n  the rename and call it out in the changelog.\n\n  ## Verification\n\n  - `yarn test:unit` 2101/2101; the table file 108 → 156 tests.\n- `yarn validate:types` clean; `yarn lint` 0 errors, warning set\nunchanged vs `dev`.\n- New tests mutation-checked: deleting the `maxHeight` disjunct, or the\nbuilt-in `sr-only`\n    label, fails exactly and only its own test.\n- Storybook, both new/updated stories: sticky header pins on scroll on a\nconsumer-authored\n`<thead>`; 27 hit-test points across the header band show no body\nbleed-through in light\nor dark; `single` mode renders the `sr-only` label and keeps 3 `th` / 3\n`td`.\n\n  ## Notes\n\n- Additive against `dev`: the slot had no scope there, so all three new\ntypes are new-on-new\nand no fork can depend on them. The only non-additive change is the\ntoken rename above.\n- `SlotsApiCustomHeader` was swept to `v-bind=\"headAttrs\"` so the file\nstops teaching the\nhardcoded class; rendering is byte-identical with that story''s own args.\n- `SELECTION_COLUMN_WIDTH` stays the plain `3rem` it is on `dev` — an\nearlier revision\nturned it into a public `--vc-table-selection-cell-width` token; dropped\nas unrequested\n    API.\n\n**Known, not fixed here:** VcTable never prunes `selection` when\n`selectionMode` changes,\nso `multiple` → `single` leaves every key selected and renders several\nchecked radios.\nPre-existing on `dev`; fixing it means emitting `update:selection` in\nresponse to a prop\nchange, which is a public-behaviour change out of scope for this PR.\nWorked around in the\n  story; worth its own ticket.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\n<!-- Put link to your task in Jira here -->\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5472\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2459-2f36-2f363489.zip\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Touches public VcTable slot API, selection key semantics, and CSS\ncustom properties that forks may override; behavior changes are mostly\nadditive with alias compatibility for the old token.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> **VcTable `#header` now exposes a scoped API** so custom headers can\nmirror the built-in row: selection column attrs, select-all\nstate/`toggleSelectAll`, and `headAttrs` for sticky header behavior.\nStories and docs were updated to bind `headAttrs` on `<thead>` instead\nof hardcoding classes.\n> \n> **DEV-only guards** warn when a custom header is missing `<thead>`,\ndrops the selection cell while selection is on, or is one header cell\nshort of the body (including after column changes or mobile→desktop\nflip). **Selection behavior** is tightened: id-less rows use\n`__row_<index>` keys, `toggleSelectAll` is gated to multiple mode and\nskips no-op commits, and single-mode header cells get an accessible\nlabel.\n> \n> **Theming:** selected-row background moves to\n`--vc-table-selected-bg-color` with `--vc-table-selected-bg` kept in the\nfallback chain; dark theme only overrides `--selected-bg-alpha`.\n**DEPRECATION.md** documents the CSS-variable deprecation pattern and\nchecklist.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n2f3634894b81d52eb0f9160f040529b5c236175f. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"d15662f356cb8db80ef80c44a8a37129720a9759","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/d15662f356cb8db80ef80c44a8a37129720a9759"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/3efe8d4fa78dfaa532a8ff919d9bb03b1a1471cf","verification":{"payload":"tree d15662f356cb8db80ef80c44a8a37129720a9759\nparent d2a86a47f97715eda33c26debb684c5c724ea1b6\nauthor Maiia Diachkovskaia <mayapavlovna@gmail.com> 1789384399 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789384399 +0300\n\nfeat(VCST-5472): expose selection scope and headAttrs on VcTable #header slot (#2459)\n\n## Problem\n\n`#header` replaces the built-in header row entirely — selection cell\nincluded — but the\n  slot got no scope. A custom header therefore could not:\n\n- render the leading selection cell, so every column shifted by one\nwhile body rows kept\n    theirs, silently and with no error;\n- drive select-all, or read whether the page is fully / partially\nselected;\n- reproduce `vc-table__head--sticky`, the sole carrier of the header''s\nsticky positioning,\nso `sticky-header` and `max-height` had no effect on a custom header.\n\nThe last one was live in our own docs: `SlotsApiCustomHeader` hardcoded\n  `class=\"vc-table__head\"` and its sticky controls did nothing.\n\n  ## What this adds\n\n  `#header` now receives a scope:\n\n  | Field | |\n  |---|---|\n  | `showSelectionColumn` | whether a selection cell must be rendered |\n  | `selectionMode` | `\"single\"` \\| `\"multiple\"` \\| `undefined` |\n  | `isAllSelected` / `isSomeSelected` | select-all checkbox state |\n  | `canSelectAll` | `false` when no row on the page is selectable |\n  | `toggleSelectAll` | no-op outside `multiple` |\n| `selectionColumnAttrs` | `v-bind` onto a `<th>` — matching width +\nsticky behaviour |\n| `headAttrs` | `v-bind` onto the `<thead>` — carries the sticky\nmodifier |\n\nPlus a DEV-only console warning when a custom header renders one cell\nfewer than the body,\n  which is the misalignment case above.\n\nBoth attrs bags expose `class` as a **string**, not an array. A bare\n`v-bind=\"attrs\"`\ncompiles to `normalizeProps(guardReactiveProps(attrs))`;\n`guardReactiveProps` does not clone\na plain object, so `normalizeProps` rewrites `class` in place on the\ncomputed''s cached\nvalue. With a sibling attribute Vue routes through `mergeProps` and\nclones instead — which\nis why the built-in call sites never showed it while the documented\nusage was broken.\n\n  ## Breaking change — needs a decision before merge\n\n  `--vc-table-selected-bg` → `--vc-table-selected-bg-color`.\n\nThe old name shipped in 2.53.0–2.56.0. A fork overriding it in\n`_custom.scss` gets no merge\nconflict, no build error and no lint failure — the selected-row\nhighlight just reverts to\nthe default in all 7 presets and both themes. `ui-kit/DEPRECATION.md`\nrequires keeping the\nold name working through a deprecation period for renamed\nprops/slots/events; CSS custom\n  properties are not literally named there.\n\nOptions: ship an alias (`var(--vc-table-selected-bg, …)` as the fallback\ntail), or accept\n  the rename and call it out in the changelog.\n\n  ## Verification\n\n  - `yarn test:unit` 2101/2101; the table file 108 → 156 tests.\n- `yarn validate:types` clean; `yarn lint` 0 errors, warning set\nunchanged vs `dev`.\n- New tests mutation-checked: deleting the `maxHeight` disjunct, or the\nbuilt-in `sr-only`\n    label, fails exactly and only its own test.\n- Storybook, both new/updated stories: sticky header pins on scroll on a\nconsumer-authored\n`<thead>`; 27 hit-test points across the header band show no body\nbleed-through in light\nor dark; `single` mode renders the `sr-only` label and keeps 3 `th` / 3\n`td`.\n\n  ## Notes\n\n- Additive against `dev`: the slot had no scope there, so all three new\ntypes are new-on-new\nand no fork can depend on them. The only non-additive change is the\ntoken rename above.\n- `SlotsApiCustomHeader` was swept to `v-bind=\"headAttrs\"` so the file\nstops teaching the\nhardcoded class; rendering is byte-identical with that story''s own args.\n- `SELECTION_COLUMN_WIDTH` stays the plain `3rem` it is on `dev` — an\nearlier revision\nturned it into a public `--vc-table-selection-cell-width` token; dropped\nas unrequested\n    API.\n\n**Known, not fixed here:** VcTable never prunes `selection` when\n`selectionMode` changes,\nso `multiple` → `single` leaves every key selected and renders several\nchecked radios.\nPre-existing on `dev`; fixing it means emitting `update:selection` in\nresponse to a prop\nchange, which is a public-behaviour change out of scope for this PR.\nWorked around in the\n  story; worth its own ticket.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\n<!-- Put link to your task in Jira here -->\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5472\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2459-2f36-2f363489.zip\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Touches public VcTable slot API, selection key semantics, and CSS\ncustom properties that forks may override; behavior changes are mostly\nadditive with alias compatibility for the old token.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> **VcTable `#header` now exposes a scoped API** so custom headers can\nmirror the built-in row: selection column attrs, select-all\nstate/`toggleSelectAll`, and `headAttrs` for sticky header behavior.\nStories and docs were updated to bind `headAttrs` on `<thead>` instead\nof hardcoding classes.\n> \n> **DEV-only guards** warn when a custom header is missing `<thead>`,\ndrops the selection cell while selection is on, or is one header cell\nshort of the body (including after column changes or mobile→desktop\nflip). **Selection behavior** is tightened: id-less rows use\n`__row_<index>` keys, `toggleSelectAll` is gated to multiple mode and\nskips no-op commits, and single-mode header cells get an accessible\nlabel.\n> \n> **Theming:** selected-row background moves to\n`--vc-table-selected-bg-color` with `--vc-table-selected-bg` kept in the\nfallback chain; dark theme only overrides `--selected-bg-alpha`.\n**DEPRECATION.md** documents the CSS-variable deprecation pattern and\nchecklist.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n2f3634894b81d52eb0f9160f040529b5c236175f. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqp9bPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtG0QABE5vJWSluWSheyXzgw0Ny1Y\nmNKHpbVHHrqyydXpRGhXQXQ4Cr4u5g/KIUM0KEQmYEFx2p9SsURRVNwelQsu5vXU\n6Ft5nz8MPK5P0ICS5fujXD7YA/TpiTRyfF9kkzJ2H30LKPC0qNcgynvXRZskd3dZ\nhU5uxNQHc1iiMgXjI9OC8b6ilmYF9ZSQa6XX1Kdw22VGB/8STk4NQauMfliQ9G35\nE3gjum+sslZhSwDQGtHIPfn+eatoI7Qy+ALyh0QH7cfVQroxjYMzN8Dxq620rczG\nf5XUgV8PE663dFRbH2g0PjYw7m5oCuL2i9mxx2ZlST9Bo79xVJ9X172LH/li5Wde\n5XHZ2se7GoaT7aWVpJP7e2a62NIV/FfUU8yUABe2bK4KGFBeelA4gaOPmLiQfVrc\ncROpYdgm7ugSjUuQeRY3pHncFi766GIsLAVu2BF8PHWFSFhDhIVQ52EMqJWETa32\nGZV3QAi52hjeEe7rLWxNXEbQc+4vlodu62Alfd5IN5bRY5phiq2lXNkpujwdvDjG\ncp3WyRChdXvPAIZRivpnaSepcfs/51lO6EYuQZ32aCA+MnclC7fzvupT84x3yvCv\nbbJ/W9wuxHXAZeuEc1sukUtXa4RxqUGSQvL29BKdQpKN3JlWN/+Ru7AqB03YK6CM\nI6tHZ7c3ZtRyvviap3nW\n=DC/Q\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T11:13:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/3efe8d4fa78dfaa532a8ff919d9bb03b1a1471cf","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDNlZmU4ZDRmYTc4ZGZhYTUzMmE4ZmY5MTlkOWJiMDNiMWExNDcxY2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/d2a86a47f97715eda33c26debb684c5c724ea1b6","sha":"d2a86a47f97715eda33c26debb684c5c724ea1b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/d2a86a47f97715eda33c26debb684c5c724ea1b6"}],"sha":"3efe8d4fa78dfaa532a8ff919d9bb03b1a1471cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/3efe8d4fa78dfaa532a8ff919d9bb03b1a1471cf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/279651339?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks","id":279651339,"login":"DmitryGrishinVirtoworks","node_id":"U_kgDOEKskCw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/d2a86a47f97715eda33c26debb684c5c724ea1b6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T08:19:21Z","email":"Dmitry.Grishin@virtoworks.com","name":"DmitryGrishinVirtoworks"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T08:19:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"VCST-5317: Hide locked organizations from the header org switcher (#2483)\n\n## Description\n\nBumps `VirtoCommerce.Customer` and\n`VirtoCommerce.ProfileExperienceApiModule` in `backend-packages.json` to\nthe released versions that include the VCST-5317 fixes\n(`isLockedForCurrentUser` field, all-organizations-locked sign-in\nfallback), so CI installs a backend that actually has them instead of\nthe older pinned versions.\n\nThis carries forward everything already done for VCST-5317 (desktop +\nmobile org switcher disabled state, stale-cache refresh on menu reopen)\n— see the individual commits.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5317\n### Artifact URL:\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"31b980ce087e23cda24dc08eb0ca6316de52425a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/31b980ce087e23cda24dc08eb0ca6316de52425a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/d2a86a47f97715eda33c26debb684c5c724ea1b6","verification":{"payload":"tree 31b980ce087e23cda24dc08eb0ca6316de52425a\nparent b220e38725f31df754002885065c927b902bd364\nauthor DmitryGrishinVirtoworks <Dmitry.Grishin@virtoworks.com> 1789114761 +0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789114761 +0400\n\nVCST-5317: Hide locked organizations from the header org switcher (#2483)\n\n## Description\n\nBumps `VirtoCommerce.Customer` and\n`VirtoCommerce.ProfileExperienceApiModule` in `backend-packages.json` to\nthe released versions that include the VCST-5317 fixes\n(`isLockedForCurrentUser` field, all-organizations-locked sign-in\nfallback), so CI installs a backend that actually has them instead of\nthe older pinned versions.\n\nThis carries forward everything already done for VCST-5317 (desktop +\nmobile org switcher disabled state, stale-cache refresh on menu reopen)\n— see the individual commits.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5317\n### Artifact URL:\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo7mJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACXQQAFUEBxM16/eJS0jivZh03cHJ\nF+vSs9HHKJsjKU32btORMdGnnhGHv53kApgdnOOSPRPFsVVY8bswIM+fsrCnD0US\ncCafGo3GmmA5q96ZZUbgf9MhhNqMJXmm2r1OH+qP5ILt3TDY9qoFIj4BGDIw6BUs\nUGoJkLyzg08XRV5pRI6XEqZR7gvfmFyuEDmb+IejRuNsMZ5I5XU5DbPTAa88UdH/\n74pHWICip69kd5pFL29g0MIVzyLZNE4CkFibMt1s/nGvSJSevljwzrcVnWBuOUHC\nuNbElJB9cw7r3CzBpui/jqu93ckVtYwSnaSpexRUwdgKzJgMH9W1pJX+dS0VL8OP\nohyBqSNJxDTxP3saeDxxUR2ckz8b3x9W5ehUbV+rJZvt5zmK0h00eTheBHi7yg8g\nsc7n/NhzMTrEteu5+BGVJouiH6zB1JqGl3Kujz1f+BnEqvgPeHinBaWsIVBtthqG\nL3zPOG1LtvosbfCm5DtfOjgeaansaNh4sV6Jn6MYYsFtdd/ICO7xd8XNGkBAa1I6\n8NYMFGHc7/E13kT5oLxoklA5Cpq2o8UkdkZOEakwdcEmIjSmWj6DqqNHUtq2Nh9V\nvswwnyG8M8yTYJV9tKq2TV5dNjcC/vLk5QTeo6hqvuNt9G9vUBMrkuJeuT+v5eOq\n+QV8Z8cDyqU/Ohzr8IEL\n=3MhP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T08:19:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/d2a86a47f97715eda33c26debb684c5c724ea1b6","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKGQyYTg2YTQ3Zjk3NzE1ZWRhMzNjMjZkZWJiNjg0YzVjNzI0ZWExYjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/b220e38725f31df754002885065c927b902bd364","sha":"b220e38725f31df754002885065c927b902bd364","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/b220e38725f31df754002885065c927b902bd364"}],"sha":"d2a86a47f97715eda33c26debb684c5c724ea1b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/d2a86a47f97715eda33c26debb684c5c724ea1b6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/279651339?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks","id":279651339,"login":"DmitryGrishinVirtoworks","node_id":"U_kgDOEKskCw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/b220e38725f31df754002885065c927b902bd364/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T07:26:28Z","email":"Dmitry.Grishin@virtoworks.com","name":"DmitryGrishinVirtoworks"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T07:26:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"VCST-5317: Hide locked organizations from the header org switcher (#2469)\n\n## Description\n\nThe header organization switcher now shows every organization the user\nbelongs to. Ones where the membership is currently locked are rendered\ndisabled (lock icon + tooltip) instead of being hidden.\n\n`organizationFields` fragment requests the new `isLockedForCurrentUser`\nfield.\n\n**Follow-ups from QA (VCST-5317 reopened):**\n- The mobile switcher (`multi-organisation-menu.vue`) got the same\ntreatment (disabled row, lock icon, tooltip, click guard) — it was\nmissed in the original change, see VCST-5931.\n- Both the desktop and mobile switcher now refresh the organizations\nlist on every menu open, since `useUserOrganizations` caches it for the\nwhole session — a lock applied while the menu was closed used to leave a\nstale, clickable row.\n\n## Depends on\n\nvc-module-profile-experience-api#145 - the GraphQL field this relies on.\nRequires `yarn generate:graphql-types` against a backend that already\nserves it.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2469-c3dd-c3dd795c.zip\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.57.0-pr-2469-a94a-a94a6c1a.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a0648c205b8008b879b1da187bd1404f0ff39f3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/a0648c205b8008b879b1da187bd1404f0ff39f3c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/b220e38725f31df754002885065c927b902bd364","verification":{"payload":"tree a0648c205b8008b879b1da187bd1404f0ff39f3c\nparent b341fcf7b2a4be7a4a6e54984129a43222d0adfb\nauthor DmitryGrishinVirtoworks <Dmitry.Grishin@virtoworks.com> 1789111588 +0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789111588 +0400\n\nVCST-5317: Hide locked organizations from the header org switcher (#2469)\n\n## Description\n\nThe header organization switcher now shows every organization the user\nbelongs to. Ones where the membership is currently locked are rendered\ndisabled (lock icon + tooltip) instead of being hidden.\n\n`organizationFields` fragment requests the new `isLockedForCurrentUser`\nfield.\n\n**Follow-ups from QA (VCST-5317 reopened):**\n- The mobile switcher (`multi-organisation-menu.vue`) got the same\ntreatment (disabled row, lock icon, tooltip, click guard) — it was\nmissed in the original change, see VCST-5931.\n- Both the desktop and mobile switcher now refresh the organizations\nlist on every menu open, since `useUserOrganizations` caches it for the\nwhole session — a lock applied while the menu was closed used to leave a\nstale, clickable row.\n\n## Depends on\n\nvc-module-profile-experience-api#145 - the GraphQL field this relies on.\nRequires `yarn generate:graphql-types` against a backend that already\nserves it.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2469-c3dd-c3dd795c.zip\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.57.0-pr-2469-a94a-a94a6c1a.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo60kCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAn0kQAKkIJw+SGJOVcUg2zyhfaF1/\nVwV9xIHlo9HtfuF5YR2SrKNq4f3+VgfhSRLi4Ud4A0syEIWVu/oZ0JCu3aTCRudi\nq86ut73OM39fJ0Ly5goypfFCHYmXe7PRA+gSsBGpIRkltigN6djnlyGo5je6nheS\n++L7+Bn1HRrs4g4dCOBxKBWKrwNuImA+/vbV0v4AaL51t00GKwgtBunxWi0eltfi\n54l+pmVtXRbuR1wBK2PGQkEn7bNvjdLy4n4YBN+O+A6IaicqYAZSs1U+MsExLB1z\nNHlZ5rH92EoSW3ze8UYZnNMagiR0QqghUDRcR1Luq1lx3bkXfdQ+z0rsu014eepd\nTDzeSWQyQN76btzT9ul4B0LIlk5xNKA2gz3ncRhyEBrSv+XTn1eJZ0udvsBN3mP/\nXxW2Cgk+GtslVP7leIbXn2w5JOSn7LDAHqDY7MAgeS5Lf5BI7rOJUfUyCfXR0wD+\nD3oTAc44ofyHOx3BagJotSU330sOnMOA2zl3BohUj0oLeG2XkEDR+kUz5aEK4sY+\nPc0DTV1hsq6cRu44J8luyl/C4k5Ro+EpRCSNcKKoHGijP999btsioWw9gfOm53rX\nj0CoSBXH9QBctTyPQOW5RQHQ6Yl2rSWYzHzDxVnyIaBVsFqdLV3mCDeceDuys6J1\navIYkn1MOyuYmoJSewJC\n=sNIt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T07:26:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/b220e38725f31df754002885065c927b902bd364","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKGIyMjBlMzg3MjVmMzFkZjc1NDAwMjg4NTA2NWM5MjdiOTAyYmQzNjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/b341fcf7b2a4be7a4a6e54984129a43222d0adfb","sha":"b341fcf7b2a4be7a4a6e54984129a43222d0adfb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/b341fcf7b2a4be7a4a6e54984129a43222d0adfb"}],"sha":"b220e38725f31df754002885065c927b902bd364","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/b220e38725f31df754002885065c927b902bd364"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16372194?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/goldenmaya","id":16372194,"login":"goldenmaya","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzcyMTk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/b341fcf7b2a4be7a4a6e54984129a43222d0adfb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T03:55:52Z","email":"mayapavlovna@gmail.com","name":"Maiia Diachkovskaia"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T03:55:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VCST-5653): improve focus ring a11y (#2468)\n\n## Description\nUnifies every focus indicator in the app behind one token set and one\nmixin, and\n  makes the ring **keyboard-only**.\n\n  ### Focus is no longer shown on click\n\nThe global rule moved from `:focus` to `:focus-visible`. A mouse click\nno longer\n  draws a ring; Tab navigation does. Agreed with design.\n\nOne deliberate exception, courtesy of the browser: `:focus-visible`\nstays on\n**editable** text fields even when clicked, so typing targets still\nring. Readonly\n  inputs do not.\n\n  ### New API\n\n  | token | default | preset key |\n  |---|---|---|\n| `--vc-focus-ring-color` | `accent-500` (`accent-600` under\n`html.dark`) | `color_vc_focus_ring` |\n  | `--vc-focus-ring-width` | `2px` | — |\n  | `--vc-focus-ring-offset` | `2px` | — |\n\nStructure lives in a mixin, `client-app/ui-kit/styles/_focus-ring.scss`:\n`@include focus-ring;`, or `@include focus-ring($inset: true)` where an\noutset ring\nwould be clipped (menu-item, scrollbar, product-image carousel button).\n12 call\n  sites; a structural change to the ring is now a one-file edit.\n\n  ### Accessibility\n\nTargets WCAG 1.4.11 (non-text contrast, 3:1) and 2.4.7 (focus visible).\n\nMeasured in-browser across `red` and `coffee`, light and dark: **114/114\nfocusable\nelements carry a ring, 0 contrast failures.** Worst case per theme —\nlight 3.72,\n  red dark 8.40, coffee dark 3.83.\n\nBefore this change four different mechanisms coexisted (`--focus-color`,\n`--outline-color`, `--focus-ring`, Tailwind `ring-*` utilities) plus a\nhardcoded\n`box-shadow` in the Skyflow payment form; several controls had no\nindicator at all.\n\n**Known gap:** `coffee` light measures 2.97 on the three surfaces that\nshare\n  `#3d2b24` (header top, footer top, mobile menu). Tracked separately.\n\n  ### Breaking for forks\n\nThese custom properties are **removed** — a fork that reads or overrides\nthem\n  silently gets nothing:\n\n- `--outline-color` — was set on `body`, `vc-button`, `vc-chip` and two\ndark partials\n  - `--focus-color` — 8 scopes\n  - `--vc-radio-button-focus-color`\n  - `--focus-ring` — `vc-calendar`\n\nReplace with `--vc-focus-ring-color` / `-width` / `-offset`, or override\ncentrally\n  via the `color_vc_focus_ring` preset key.\n\nAlso removed: 12 Tailwind `ring-*` focus utilities, and 8 dark override\npartials\n  that existed only to restate a focus colour.\n\n  ### Also in this PR\n\n- **VcButton gains a pressed state** — every variant darkens one step\nfurther than\nhover, with a `transition-colors` under `prefers-reduced-motion:\nno-preference`.\nMeasured over 192 variant × colour × theme combinations: press is\nvisible from\nboth rest and hover everywhere, nothing brightens in dark mode, and no\ncell drops\n    below AA because of it.\n- `storybook:styles` now runs `sass` before `tailwindcss`. The Storybook\npreflight\nis `.scss` in name only — it was built straight through PostCSS, so it\ncould not\nshare the mixin, and a Sass line comment in it silently deleted the\nfocus rule.\n\n<img width=\"1100\" height=\"582\" alt=\"coffee-dark\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e3696ea6-98a0-4190-b185-851f3fa30edc\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1100\" height=\"582\" alt=\"coffee-light\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f2a55411-7cd6-4cd7-bd26-fa1d71bffdd3\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1100\" height=\"582\" alt=\"red-dark\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dae3ed83-422b-44f3-88b8-e0b571972c3b\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1100\" height=\"582\" alt=\"red-light\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f988da54-0fd0-4fdd-9567-ced7e6170d45\"\n/>\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\n<!-- Put link to your task in Jira here -->\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5653\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2468-8e45-8e45ee74.zip\n\n\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Wide-reaching visual and accessibility behavior across the UI kit,\nglobal base styles, and payment iframe styling, with a breaking change\nto legacy focus CSS variables that forks may override.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> **Unifies focus styling** behind `--vc-focus-ring-color`,\n`--vc-focus-ring-width`, and `--vc-focus-ring-offset` (preset override\n`color_vc_focus_ring`), applied through a shared `@include focus-ring`\nmixin. Global preflight now rings **only on `:focus-visible`** (keyboard\nnavigation), replacing scattered `--outline-color` / `--focus-color` /\nTailwind `ring-*` rules and deleting dark-mode partials that only bumped\nthose overrides.\n> \n> **Component updates** wire the mixin where needed (inputs,\ncheckbox/radio indicators, menu-item/scrollbar/product-image carousel\nwith inset rings, payment iframe wrappers, keyboard-sort layout blocks).\n**Skyflow/Datatrans** read ring tokens via new **`readCssVar`**\n(replacing `useCssVar`) so iframe styles don’t get frozen when switching\nlight/dark themes.\n> \n> **Also:** **VcButton** (and dark button overrides) gain distinct\n**`:active` pressed** fills plus optional `transition-colors`; Storybook\npreflight runs **Sass before Tailwind** so the mixin compiles.\n**Breaking for forks:** removed `--outline-color`, `--focus-color`,\n`--vc-radio-button-focus-color`, and `--focus-ring` — use the new tokens\ninstead.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n8e45ee740847f9188247075f1940511495a7723b. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"f1e81e5dbaaef5761f4d697af64b70b62565f6c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/f1e81e5dbaaef5761f4d697af64b70b62565f6c8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/b341fcf7b2a4be7a4a6e54984129a43222d0adfb","verification":{"payload":"tree f1e81e5dbaaef5761f4d697af64b70b62565f6c8\nparent 976b29294d3d6c429f99152296535d5616a9a65c\nauthor Maiia Diachkovskaia <mayapavlovna@gmail.com> 1789098952 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789098952 +0300\n\nfeat(VCST-5653): improve focus ring a11y (#2468)\n\n## Description\nUnifies every focus indicator in the app behind one token set and one\nmixin, and\n  makes the ring **keyboard-only**.\n\n  ### Focus is no longer shown on click\n\nThe global rule moved from `:focus` to `:focus-visible`. A mouse click\nno longer\n  draws a ring; Tab navigation does. Agreed with design.\n\nOne deliberate exception, courtesy of the browser: `:focus-visible`\nstays on\n**editable** text fields even when clicked, so typing targets still\nring. Readonly\n  inputs do not.\n\n  ### New API\n\n  | token | default | preset key |\n  |---|---|---|\n| `--vc-focus-ring-color` | `accent-500` (`accent-600` under\n`html.dark`) | `color_vc_focus_ring` |\n  | `--vc-focus-ring-width` | `2px` | — |\n  | `--vc-focus-ring-offset` | `2px` | — |\n\nStructure lives in a mixin, `client-app/ui-kit/styles/_focus-ring.scss`:\n`@include focus-ring;`, or `@include focus-ring($inset: true)` where an\noutset ring\nwould be clipped (menu-item, scrollbar, product-image carousel button).\n12 call\n  sites; a structural change to the ring is now a one-file edit.\n\n  ### Accessibility\n\nTargets WCAG 1.4.11 (non-text contrast, 3:1) and 2.4.7 (focus visible).\n\nMeasured in-browser across `red` and `coffee`, light and dark: **114/114\nfocusable\nelements carry a ring, 0 contrast failures.** Worst case per theme —\nlight 3.72,\n  red dark 8.40, coffee dark 3.83.\n\nBefore this change four different mechanisms coexisted (`--focus-color`,\n`--outline-color`, `--focus-ring`, Tailwind `ring-*` utilities) plus a\nhardcoded\n`box-shadow` in the Skyflow payment form; several controls had no\nindicator at all.\n\n**Known gap:** `coffee` light measures 2.97 on the three surfaces that\nshare\n  `#3d2b24` (header top, footer top, mobile menu). Tracked separately.\n\n  ### Breaking for forks\n\nThese custom properties are **removed** — a fork that reads or overrides\nthem\n  silently gets nothing:\n\n- `--outline-color` — was set on `body`, `vc-button`, `vc-chip` and two\ndark partials\n  - `--focus-color` — 8 scopes\n  - `--vc-radio-button-focus-color`\n  - `--focus-ring` — `vc-calendar`\n\nReplace with `--vc-focus-ring-color` / `-width` / `-offset`, or override\ncentrally\n  via the `color_vc_focus_ring` preset key.\n\nAlso removed: 12 Tailwind `ring-*` focus utilities, and 8 dark override\npartials\n  that existed only to restate a focus colour.\n\n  ### Also in this PR\n\n- **VcButton gains a pressed state** — every variant darkens one step\nfurther than\nhover, with a `transition-colors` under `prefers-reduced-motion:\nno-preference`.\nMeasured over 192 variant × colour × theme combinations: press is\nvisible from\nboth rest and hover everywhere, nothing brightens in dark mode, and no\ncell drops\n    below AA because of it.\n- `storybook:styles` now runs `sass` before `tailwindcss`. The Storybook\npreflight\nis `.scss` in name only — it was built straight through PostCSS, so it\ncould not\nshare the mixin, and a Sass line comment in it silently deleted the\nfocus rule.\n\n<img width=\"1100\" height=\"582\" alt=\"coffee-dark\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e3696ea6-98a0-4190-b185-851f3fa30edc\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1100\" height=\"582\" alt=\"coffee-light\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f2a55411-7cd6-4cd7-bd26-fa1d71bffdd3\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1100\" height=\"582\" alt=\"red-dark\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dae3ed83-422b-44f3-88b8-e0b571972c3b\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1100\" height=\"582\" alt=\"red-light\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f988da54-0fd0-4fdd-9567-ced7e6170d45\"\n/>\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\n<!-- Put link to your task in Jira here -->\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5653\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2468-8e45-8e45ee74.zip\n\n\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Wide-reaching visual and accessibility behavior across the UI kit,\nglobal base styles, and payment iframe styling, with a breaking change\nto legacy focus CSS variables that forks may override.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> **Unifies focus styling** behind `--vc-focus-ring-color`,\n`--vc-focus-ring-width`, and `--vc-focus-ring-offset` (preset override\n`color_vc_focus_ring`), applied through a shared `@include focus-ring`\nmixin. Global preflight now rings **only on `:focus-visible`** (keyboard\nnavigation), replacing scattered `--outline-color` / `--focus-color` /\nTailwind `ring-*` rules and deleting dark-mode partials that only bumped\nthose overrides.\n> \n> **Component updates** wire the mixin where needed (inputs,\ncheckbox/radio indicators, menu-item/scrollbar/product-image carousel\nwith inset rings, payment iframe wrappers, keyboard-sort layout blocks).\n**Skyflow/Datatrans** read ring tokens via new **`readCssVar`**\n(replacing `useCssVar`) so iframe styles don’t get frozen when switching\nlight/dark themes.\n> \n> **Also:** **VcButton** (and dark button overrides) gain distinct\n**`:active` pressed** fills plus optional `transition-colors`; Storybook\npreflight runs **Sass before Tailwind** so the mixin compiles.\n**Breaking for forks:** removed `--outline-color`, `--focus-color`,\n`--vc-radio-button-focus-color`, and `--focus-ring` — use the new tokens\ninstead.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n8e45ee740847f9188247075f1940511495a7723b. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo3vICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAY7AQADCDNnyXVobD4Ha7JMDymhYe\nzSrgCUKAjfHI9yUnPl/CSzgLlGHfHc3fIwhZHUdaERfM5Z7xAIwf+eOMXYc/cUVD\nmVs0NKNoZFcIQYdQOowAC4EpiDzY7vaRQc7rSjsGK0Ju+ZB+J32fYtobZbNWaKLb\nb2vPV4Px/Dm2VuDUQbLwModLfp5O0NeVcdVcYNU0UNCgC4RtD+qJ97hBvgkGWFfM\nEtg+coGLomUm9aBJqGqm6IZXLMMBYYqOzP+STkyfpr2k7py9OMsRFg89L723DSR9\n+u/oRMI2PZt513UrdXrn2gPE2lAiNJEoRczjgFjLQJ+vu/TKhRw3DjWypyyPuYOL\nfo7N30FB6F8yzj+V9ZuZoF7kQimEE9Od5uSq6NifezYrLSRDBYd8FPEV/Ri9lhHt\nALhJXbjS6Pzp3a7yKl+oSNN8P0Vhak+tXy5E3Pu00ZDuC59vReqwz57VJaS2xMmi\ny9YIsp0D9vzGgNHA+Gd/4ZwYWf+GWrnL3lNaw78a7KESof5ViZvMKZEn8tijr4j/\nOHeA+b8W5FCJbPx96BWHugnk93vqqtIJm/0k7vt3vIv2xUcjOISzq38RiOlph8gO\nyQ6SFHtz3Z8lzJT/uXeQOMAGnKQxrppSJd/ksz0la5xpf8KzGddPRmW25lgoms3w\nxK1RL7u2sNAbD4bPf3T+\n=rFRb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T03:55:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/b341fcf7b2a4be7a4a6e54984129a43222d0adfb","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKGIzNDFmY2Y3YjJhNGJlN2E0YTZlNTQ5ODQxMjlhNDMyMjJkMGFkZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/976b29294d3d6c429f99152296535d5616a9a65c","sha":"976b29294d3d6c429f99152296535d5616a9a65c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/976b29294d3d6c429f99152296535d5616a9a65c"}],"sha":"b341fcf7b2a4be7a4a6e54984129a43222d0adfb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/b341fcf7b2a4be7a4a6e54984129a43222d0adfb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18286430?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ivan-kalachikov","id":18286430,"login":"ivan-kalachikov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Mjg2NDMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/976b29294d3d6c429f99152296535d5616a9a65c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T12:34:35Z","email":"ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com","name":"Ivan Kalachikov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T12:34:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VCST-5159): extend the core facade so sales-rep can ship as a plugin (#2427)\n\n## What this is for\n\nThe `sales-rep` module should ship as a separate Module Federation\nplugin, from its own repo. To do that it needs everything it uses from\nthe host to come through `@vc-frontend/core` — the facade — instead of\n`@/...` paths.\n\nThis PR widens the facade to cover what the module actually imports, and\nfixes the one case that did not fit.\n\nAfter this, **every host import in `modules/sales-rep` resolves to the\nfacade** — runtime imports through the root export, and its specs'' mount\nhelpers through a new `@vc-frontend/core/testing` subpath.\n\n---\n\n## The one case that did not fit: the mobile nav badge\n\nThe \"My customers\" link in the mobile menu shows a count badge.\n\nTo render it, the plugin''s component had to import `MobileMenuLink` from\nthe host''s `_internal/` folder. That is a private folder — once a plugin\ndepends on it, the host can no longer restyle its own menu without\nbreaking the plugin. And the plugin now lives in a different repo with\nits own release cycle.\n\nSo an extension entry can now contribute **data** instead of markup:\n\n```ts\n// before — the plugin renders the menu link itself\nregister(\"mobileMenu\", MY_CUSTOMERS_NAV_LINK_ID, {\n  component: defineAsyncComponent(() => import(\"./components/link-my-customers-mobile.vue\")),\n});\n\n// after — the host renders its own link, the plugin supplies the number\nregister(\"mobileMenu\", MY_CUSTOMERS_NAV_LINK_ID, {\n  use: useSharedSalesRepCustomersCount,\n});\n```\n\n`link-my-customers-mobile.vue` is deleted. The desktop link stays a\ncomponent on purpose — it carries real logic (keeping the link active on\nthe sibling customer-profile route) and never imported anything\ninternal.\n\n### Why `use()` is a function and not a value\n\nThe count comes from a GraphQL query, so it has a lifecycle: start it,\nstop it, refresh it. A plain value cannot express that.\n\n`ExtensionPoint` calls `use()` **in its own setup**, inside a scope it\nstops when the entry unmounts. That is the only place Vue lets you\nregister cleanup. `useSharedSalesRepCustomersCount` wraps the composable\nin `createSharedComposable` (the repo''s existing idiom — `useCart`,\n`usePayment`, `useUserQuote`): one query for however many surfaces show\nthe badge, disposed when the last unmounts, rebuilt fresh on the next\nmount.\n\nAn earlier revision of this PR passed a getter through `props` instead.\nIt ran during render, where lifecycle hooks silently do not register,\nand it memoised the query for the whole session — so the badge kept\nshowing a number from earlier while the desktop link showed the current\none. `data-freshness.test.ts` asserts exactly the behaviour that was\nlost.\n\n### Contributing is not allowed where the host has no fallback\n\n`ExtensionPoint` renders the plugin''s component **or** the host''s\nfallback slot. A component-less entry only works where that fallback\nexists — and in 6 of 9 categories it does not: those call sites are\nself-closing, so such an entry would render nothing at all, with no\nerror.\n\nA category opts in by declaring a contributed shape:\n\n```ts\ntype ExtensionEntryType<Props, Contributed, Condition> =\n  [Contributed] extends [never]\n    ? ReplaceEntryType<Props, Condition>                            // component required\n    : ReplaceEntryType<Props, Condition> | DecorateEntryType<...>;  // either mode\n```\n\nLeave `Contributed` at `never` and the decorate branch does not exist,\nso registering one there is a **compile error**, not a silent no-op.\nToday only `mobileMenu` opts in.\n\n`ExtensionPointList` now delegates to `ExtensionPoint` per entry, so\nboth renderers agree on what a component-less entry means.\n\n---\n\n## The rest of the facade\n\nGrouped by export shape — the tiering rule is now written down in\n`client-app/core-api/README.md`, so the next request answers itself.\n\n| Tier | Shape | What went in |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1. Capability | composable / function | `registerCacheTypePolicies`,\n`useWishlistSharingScopes`, `Logger`, `useUser`, `useNavigations`,\n`useModal`, `useNotifications`, `useBreadcrumbs`, `usePageHead`,\n`getProductRoute`, `EXTENSION_NAMES`, menu types, the sharing-scope\ncontrols type |\n| 2. Host-rendered chrome | nothing — an extension entry | the sales-rep\nmobile nav link |\n| 3. Frozen component | a `.vue` component | `OrderStatus` |\n\nPlus a new subpath export alongside the existing `/federation` and\n`/tailwind-preset`: **`/testing`**, for the mount helpers a plugin''s\nspecs need.\n\n**`registerCacheTypePolicies`** lets a plugin normalise its own GraphQL\ntypes without importing the Apollo cache. It warns in development when a\ntypename is already in the cache — policies do not apply retroactively,\nand registering late otherwise fails silently. Its first consumer is on\nthis branch: the layout policies from #2400 register through it, so\n`modules/sales-rep` no longer touches the cache instance.\n\n**ui-kit** — all **21** `Vc*` components the module''s templates use are\nexported, up from 7. The host registers them globally, but a remote only\nresolves that when it renders inside the host''s app instance, and a\nplugin''s own dev server has none.\n\n**`@vc-frontend/core/testing`** ships `createWrapperFactory` /\n`createShallowWrapperFactory` as *real source*, unlike the root export:\nthat one is types-only because the host injects the implementation at\nruntime, and a plugin''s specs run with no host to inject anything.\n`@vue/test-utils` is passed in rather than imported, so the module never\nreaches for the consumer''s copy. The host''s own `@/core/utilities/tests`\nre-exports it, so the four in-repo specs are untouched.\n\nThe Apollo cache is deliberately *not* exported.\n`data-freshness.test.ts` needs *an* Apollo cache, not the host''s\ninstance — the host''s type policies are cart/checkout-specific, and the\nones that spec exercises come from the module''s own\n`layout/cache-policies.ts`.\n\n**`OrderStatus`** is exported as-is because its status → colour mapping\ncomes from per-store `orders_statuses` settings; a plugin-side chip\nwould drift. Its four props are contract from here on.\n\n---\n\n## Versioning: the contract goes to 0.1.0\n\nIt was heading for 1.2.0. It is not ready to promise stability to a\nthird-party plugin author, so it moves to a pre-1.0 line instead.\n\nNothing breaks by doing so: **no `core-v*` release has ever been\npublished**, so `0.1.0` is the first version anyone can actually\ninstall.\n\nUnder `^0.x` the **minor** is what a caret range refuses, so the levels\nshift down one: additive is a **patch**, breaking is a **minor**. The\nversioning automation now picks its levels from the release line it is\non; the 1.x mapping is untouched and takes over at 1.0.0.\n\n`core-v0.1.0` still has to be published by the *Core Facade Release*\nworkflow before a plugin can install against it.\n\nA plugin pins the facade by tarball URL, so anything added to the\npackage later re-pins every plugin. That is why the two remaining gaps —\nui-kit coverage and the specs'' mount helpers — are closed here rather\nthan deferred to the move.\n\n---\n\n---\n\n## Defects found and fixed while reviewing this branch\n\nEach one below is a real defect in this PR''s own additions, with a test\nthat fails without the fix.\n\n### `@vc-frontend/core/testing` did not work for the only consumer it\nexists for\n\n`testing.mjs` imports `lodash-es` at runtime. It was a peer only, and\n`create-plugin` drew its\n`devDependencies` from `CONTRACT_TYPE_PEERS` — where `lodash-es` never\nappeared. So the first spec in\na scaffolded plugin importing the mount helpers died on `Cannot find\nmodule`. `vue-i18n` survived by\nhappening to be MF-shared.\n\nSame root cause, wider blast radius: `peerDependencies` declared **2 of\nthe 14** packages the\npublished files import. The real list lived in build-time JS objects no\npackage manager reads, so a\nconsumer installing the tarball by hand — a supported path,\n`PORT_TO_MF.md` §4 — was missing five type\npeers, and `skipLibCheck: true` in the scaffold''s own tsconfig kept it\nsilent: only the individual\nmembers degraded to `any`, never the top-level exports, so\n`mergeMenuSchema(42)` and\n`mergeMenuSchema(null)` compiled clean on the very call `PORT_TO_MF`\nsays to keep.\n\nThe declaration is now **derived, not maintained**. `build-types.mjs`\nscans every file in `files` —\nnot just the rolled contract, which is why `testing.mjs` went unchecked\n— for `from`, `require()` and\nthe `import(\"x\")` form the `.d.mts` files use, and fails with the exact\nobject to paste when\n`package.json` disagrees. Required vs optional follows reachability;\n`create-plugin` merges the\nfacade''s own `peerDependencies` so there is no second list left to\ndrift.\n\n### Five holes in `registerCacheTypePolicies`, the new plugin-facing\ncache seam\n\n- **Ownership was per typename, but Apollo merges `fields` per field\nname.** So the first plugin to\nregister any `Query.fields.*` owned all of `Query`, and every later\nplugin''s policy for a *different*\nroot field was refused wholesale — a refusal protecting nothing, since\nApollo merges the two\nadditively. Claims are keyed per field now, with a deliberately\n**asymmetric** collision rule:\n`keyFields` re-keys the whole entity, so a type-level claim collides\nwith the typename *and* every\nfield under it. Without that asymmetry the host''s `Product: { fields: {\nproperties } }` —\nfields-only, like most host policies — would leave `Product` formally\nunclaimed and a plugin could\n  redefine how the host identifies it. A spec pins that case.\n- **The late-registration warning could not see the two shapes that\nmatter.** A root-type policy never\nproduces a `Query:` key — its fields live under `ROOT_QUERY` — so a late\n`Query.fields.x.keyArgs`,\nthe commonest hazard there is, orphaned everything already stored under\nthe old field key and warned\nabout nothing. A typename stored inline (no `id`) was invisible for the\nsame reason.\n- **Re-registering your own claim reported a collision with yourself**,\nwhich is what HMR and a second\n`init()` both look like, sending the reader hunting for a plugin that\ndoes not exist.\n- **`priority` had no ceiling, so the docblock''s central promise was\nfalse.** `by.priority >= priority`\nis the whole gate and `priority` came from the caller, so `{ owner: \"x\",\npriority: 101 }` took the\nhost''s `CouponType: { keyFields: [\"code\"] }` over with zero refusals and\nzero warnings, and the cache\nreally re-keyed by `id`. A caller''s value is clamped below\n`HOST_PRIORITY` now. The host seeds its own\nclaims straight into the ownership map, never through the public\nfunction, so the cap costs it nothing\nand plugin-vs-plugin escalation is untouched. A non-finite priority is\nsanitized in the same step:\n  every `>= NaN` comparison is false, so `NaN` refused nothing at all.\n- **`owner` defaulted to `\"unknown\"`, which turned the same-owner\nexemption into a hole.** Two plugins\nthat both omitted it were indistinguishable, so neither blocked the\nother and the loser got no signal —\nin production none at all, since `Logger` is a no-op there. `owner` is\nrequired now, so every refusal\nnames someone. No `core-v*` contract is published, so tightening the\nsignature costs no consumer;\nafter the first release it would not be free, and the contract gate\ncompares export *names*, so it\n  would not have flagged it.\n\nAnd the docs stop overclaiming: `cache.ts` promised a plugin \"cannot\nquietly take over a typename the\nhost normalizes\", but the ownership map is seeded from the policies the\nhost *declares*, which is not\nthe set it stores — anything Apollo normalizes by its default `id` rule\nis unclaimed. Stated as a known\ngap now rather than a guarantee.\n\n### The typing CI step was checking zero files\n\n`vitest --typecheck` spawns `tsc --noEmit` from the repo root without\n`-p` unless `typecheck.tsconfig`\nis set, so it inherited the root `{\"files\": []}` config: every\n`.test-d.ts` reported \"no errors\"\nregardless of content — a planted `TS2322` and an unused\n`@ts-expect-error` both stayed green. Which\nmatters here, because `useExtensionRegistry.test-d.ts` is where this\nPR''s central type guard lives, so\nanyone verifying that claim by running the type test got a false pass.\n(The Build step''s\n`vue-tsc --build` *was* catching them — the step named after typing was\nnot.)\n\nPointing it at a project surfaced 26 pre-existing errors across the repo\nand red-lit CI for things\nthis PR is not about, so it now uses a dedicated\n`tsconfig.typecheck.json` scoped to `**/*.test-d.ts`.\nTypeScript still pulls in what those files import. `yarn test:typing\n--run` exits 0 clean and 1 on a\nplanted error — checked both, exit code included.\n\n### Smaller, each with a test that fails without it\n\n- **A released contract line only moves forward.** `escapesCaretRange`\nasked \"is the current version\noutside `^base`\", which is also true *below* the baseline — so `1.2.0 →\n1.1.0` with an export removed\nreturned \"major already bumped\" and would have minted a release whose\ncontract has fewer exports than\nthe earlier version number. A regression is refused outright now, gated\non `released` so the\ndeliberate 1.2.0 → 0.1.0 reset this PR performs stays legal. The bump\nguard also stops printing\n  \"passed\" when it compared the contract with itself.\n- **Both dependency-cruiser boundary rules are blind to `import type`.**\n`tsPreCompilationDeps` is off,\nso type-only edges never enter its graph — proven with probes: three\nvalue imports caught, the same\nthree as `import type` produce zero violations. That is exactly the\ncoupling that breaks when\n`modules/sales-rep` moves to its own repo. Turning the flag on is not a\ndrop-in (`true` → 19 errors,\n`\"specify\"` → 15), so the bans are restated in `eslint.config.js`, which\nsees `import type`. **Honest\nlimit:** CI runs `yarn build` → `validate:types` +\n`validate:dependencies`, not eslint, so the\ntype-only half holds in the IDE and `yarn lint`, not the pipeline.\nRecorded in the config; closing it\nproperly is a separate decision (scope the `tsPreCompilationDeps` work,\nor add lint to `validate`).\n- **Replacing a contribution under the same name kept the old one\nrunning** and never started the new\none — the child was keyed on `name`, and it reads `use` once in setup.\nNot reachable today (nothing\ncalls `unregister` but specs, and both triggers the reviews assumed hit\nthe duplicate guard instead),\nbut the registry README teaches the unregister-then-register pattern, so\nit is a trap for the first\nplugin author to update a contribution. Keyed on the contribution''s\nidentity now.\n- **A released line''s \"already bumped\" reason named the wrong level.**\n`breaking` comes from\n`policyFor(baseVersion)`, so promoting `0.9.0 → 1.0.0` with an export\nremoved reported `\"minor already\nbumped\"` when the human moved the major. The decision was right, the\nwording was not; it reads the\nbump that HAPPENED off `semver.diff` now. The `require-` path still\nnames the level a human is *asked*\n  for, which is the baseline''s.\n- **Two paths lost the `_internal` ban entirely.** The sales-rep block\nwaives `NO_RAW_APOLLO_QUERY` for\nits specs and `useSalesRepHubQuery.ts`, but the two boundary blocks\nbelow skip all of `sales-rep/**`,\nso those files matched no `no-restricted-syntax` block at all — value\n*and* type imports of a host\n`_internal/` component went uncaught, and dependency-cruiser sees\nneither type-only edge. A trailing\nblock restates just that ban for them, raw-Apollo waiver intact. A spec\ntravels with the module when\nit is extracted, so a host component mounted in one breaks the\nextraction exactly as a source import\n  would.\n- **`EXTENSION_NAMES.mobileMenu.myCustomers`** — the registry README''s\ncanonical example — is\n`undefined` at runtime while type-checking as `string`, so copying that\nline registers under the\nliteral string `\"undefined\"`. `EXTENSION_NAMES` is typed as its own\ndeclared names now, making that a\n  compile error.\n- The README told authors a late registration runs `use()` **outside** a\ncomponent context where\n`inject()` does not resolve — the opposite of what the code does and of\nthis PR''s own passing spec.\nBelieving it means avoiding every injection-dependent composable, i.e.\nall of Apollo, which is the\n  entire reason `use()` is a function.\n- `@vc-frontend/core/tailwind-preset` shipped with no `types` condition,\nso a TypeScript\n`tailwind.config.ts` failed with TS7016. `window.modulesCacheDebug` was\ndeclared always-present\nwhile only development assigns it. `default-menu.test.ts`''s \"renders no\ncount\" asserted\n`toContain(\"my customers:\")`, which `\"my customers:3\"` also satisfies —\nthe test could not fail.\n- **The tier table authorised one `.vue` export and the facade ships 22\n`Vc*` plus `uiKit`.** They are\nthere for a real reason (a plugin''s own dev server has no host app\ninstance, so nothing resolves a\nglobally-registered component), but a reviewer had no written basis to\nrefuse the 23rd. Now a tier of\nits own with one admission rule, and the unenforced half is stated: the\ngate compares exported\n*names*, so a renamed ui-kit prop ships as a patch and every plugin\npinned to the range keeps\nresolving it. A prop-level diff would make that promise real; until then\na ui-kit prop rename is a\nmanual breaking bump. (Correcting this PR''s own earlier claim: the\nfacade went from **3** `Vc*` at\nthe merge base to 22, and from 10 public names to 53 — not \"up from 7\".)\n\n### Sonar\n\nThe failing quality gate was one `javascript:S2871` BUG on\n`readdirSync(dir).sort()` — a false\npositive (S2871 exists for numeric arrays; the default comparator on\nstrings already *is* UTF-16 code\nunits, identical to the file''s own helper), fixed anyway since a bare\n`.sort()` reads as a latent\nnumeric-sort bug. The MAJOR `S6661` \"use object spread\" on\n`extension-point.vue` is **stale**: there is\nno `Object.assign` in any revision of that file on this branch, none in\nits compiled output, and the\nissue carries `\"line\": null` with a creation date eight days before the\nfile was rewritten. The\nremaining seven smells introduced by these fixes are cleared, and the\n`String.raw` ones turned out to\nsit on a real defect: `new RegExp(`\\b${name}\\b`)` interpolated\nidentifiers raw, and the\nambient-globals collector accepts `$` in identifiers — which is a regex\n*end anchor*, so `\\b$VcTheme\\b`\ncould never match and such a declaration was skipped with no diagnostic.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `yarn test:typing --run` (what CI runs) — **2188 tests / 143 files**,\nno type errors, exit 0\n- `yarn vitest run --dir client-app` — **2150 tests / 140 files**, exit\n0\n- `yarn build` — exit 0\n- `vue-tsc --build --force` — 0 errors\n- `yarn validate:dependencies` — 0 errors\n- `yarn validate:core-types` — contract matches the facade; peer\ndeclaration covers 10 required + 4\n  subpath-only packages\n- `eslint` — 0 errors on the changed files\n- Merged `dev` twice. The first merge (6 commits) mattered because `dev`\nhad independently rewritten\nthree files this branch touches, including `data-freshness.test.ts` —\nthe spec this PR offers as its\n  freshness guarantee — changing its GraphQL fixture shapes.\nThe second (4 commits, up to #2439) conflicted for real, in\n`modules/sales-rep`, and both conflicts\nwere resolved in this branch''s favour where the two disagree on purpose:\n- dev calls `registerLayoutTypePolicies(cache)`; this branch renamed\nthat export and routes it\nthrough `registerCacheTypePolicies`, so the module no longer imports the\ncache instance;\n- dev registers the mobile My customers link as a component — the very\ncomponent this PR deletes —\nso `registerContribution` stays and dev''s permission-gated documents\nblock sits ahead of it;\n- dev''s new documents route mounts via `ROUTES.COMPANY.NAME`, like its\nsiblings here.\n- Regenerated the GraphQL types from `vcptcore-dev`. Core types only;\nthe eight module schemas came\nback byte-identical. This picks up the document-library surface #2439\nadded to `Query`, which the\ncore snapshot had not caught up with, and drops `CartType.loyaltyPoints`\n— an environment\ndifference, not a schema change. Nothing reads that field, and the\nfacade contract is unaffected:\n  the `loyaltyPoints` it inlines belongs to `Product`.\n\n---\n\n## Notes for the reviewer\n\n- `yarn validate:core-types` is stale on `dev` itself — it does not run\nin `yarn validate` during the pilot — so regenerating here also pulls in\nthe `sharedList` category from #2405 that `dev`''s committed contract\npredates.\n- `isRegistered()` answers \"has a component\", not \"is registered\" — a\ndecorate entry returns false. That reading is what hid the\ndropped-contribution bug. The name is left alone here (renaming it is\nchurn this PR does not need) and noted where it is defined.\n- `headerMenu` and `accountMenu` have fallback markup but their slots\nare unscoped, so contributed data would be discarded, and both leave\n`Contributed` at `never` — the compile gate keeps them closed until\nthose slots are scoped. `mobileMenu`''s two call sites are both scoped\nhere: `default-menu.vue` is where today''s badge renders, since the My\ncustomers link is an account-section child; `main-menu.vue` opens\ndecorate mode for top-level mobile items, which nothing uses yet.\n- `modules/push-messages` still imports two `_internal/` components. The\nsame fix applies to it, out of scope here — and both files are the\ndocumented exemption in the new eslint rule as well as in\ndependency-cruiser.\n- Two things about the badge that look like defects and are not, so they\nneed not be re-raised. The badge is not stale across mount/unmount:\nstaleness is bounded to the account-shell visit, because\n`account-shell.vue` renders the desktop rail `max-md:hidden` — mounted,\nnot unmounted — which is the trade-off that makes the two surfaces\nagree. And `data-freshness.test.ts` does catch the regression it guards:\nreintroducing the session-lifetime memo, or switching to `cache-first`,\nturns it red.\n- One real behaviour delta in that area, stated rather than fixed: a\nfailed count fetch hides the badge for the rest of the account-shell\nvisit with no retry. Pre-PR each surface had its own query, so reopening\nthe mobile menu re-issued it. The designed failure mode is a hidden\nbadge and the consistency win is the point, but it is a behaviour delta\nworth knowing.\n- `sortablejs` is deliberately **not** in `MF_SHARED_RANGES`: a leaf DOM\nlibrary with no cross-copy state, so a duplicate costs bundle size, not\ncorrectness. The HOWTO documents that rule, plus the exception that does\nforce sharing — a library whose state crosses the boundary via\n`provide`/`inject`. `vee-validate` is the near-miss.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5159\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2427-8344-8344665b.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"107416848b3e5dc36b24b7eb27a3895dd3252ba2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/107416848b3e5dc36b24b7eb27a3895dd3252ba2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/976b29294d3d6c429f99152296535d5616a9a65c","verification":{"payload":"tree 107416848b3e5dc36b24b7eb27a3895dd3252ba2\nparent 844fdf29045007dd959e0b8ac798522ba30f3256\nauthor Ivan Kalachikov <ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com> 1789043675 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789043675 +0100\n\nfeat(VCST-5159): extend the core facade so sales-rep can ship as a plugin (#2427)\n\n## What this is for\n\nThe `sales-rep` module should ship as a separate Module Federation\nplugin, from its own repo. To do that it needs everything it uses from\nthe host to come through `@vc-frontend/core` — the facade — instead of\n`@/...` paths.\n\nThis PR widens the facade to cover what the module actually imports, and\nfixes the one case that did not fit.\n\nAfter this, **every host import in `modules/sales-rep` resolves to the\nfacade** — runtime imports through the root export, and its specs'' mount\nhelpers through a new `@vc-frontend/core/testing` subpath.\n\n---\n\n## The one case that did not fit: the mobile nav badge\n\nThe \"My customers\" link in the mobile menu shows a count badge.\n\nTo render it, the plugin''s component had to import `MobileMenuLink` from\nthe host''s `_internal/` folder. That is a private folder — once a plugin\ndepends on it, the host can no longer restyle its own menu without\nbreaking the plugin. And the plugin now lives in a different repo with\nits own release cycle.\n\nSo an extension entry can now contribute **data** instead of markup:\n\n```ts\n// before — the plugin renders the menu link itself\nregister(\"mobileMenu\", MY_CUSTOMERS_NAV_LINK_ID, {\n  component: defineAsyncComponent(() => import(\"./components/link-my-customers-mobile.vue\")),\n});\n\n// after — the host renders its own link, the plugin supplies the number\nregister(\"mobileMenu\", MY_CUSTOMERS_NAV_LINK_ID, {\n  use: useSharedSalesRepCustomersCount,\n});\n```\n\n`link-my-customers-mobile.vue` is deleted. The desktop link stays a\ncomponent on purpose — it carries real logic (keeping the link active on\nthe sibling customer-profile route) and never imported anything\ninternal.\n\n### Why `use()` is a function and not a value\n\nThe count comes from a GraphQL query, so it has a lifecycle: start it,\nstop it, refresh it. A plain value cannot express that.\n\n`ExtensionPoint` calls `use()` **in its own setup**, inside a scope it\nstops when the entry unmounts. That is the only place Vue lets you\nregister cleanup. `useSharedSalesRepCustomersCount` wraps the composable\nin `createSharedComposable` (the repo''s existing idiom — `useCart`,\n`usePayment`, `useUserQuote`): one query for however many surfaces show\nthe badge, disposed when the last unmounts, rebuilt fresh on the next\nmount.\n\nAn earlier revision of this PR passed a getter through `props` instead.\nIt ran during render, where lifecycle hooks silently do not register,\nand it memoised the query for the whole session — so the badge kept\nshowing a number from earlier while the desktop link showed the current\none. `data-freshness.test.ts` asserts exactly the behaviour that was\nlost.\n\n### Contributing is not allowed where the host has no fallback\n\n`ExtensionPoint` renders the plugin''s component **or** the host''s\nfallback slot. A component-less entry only works where that fallback\nexists — and in 6 of 9 categories it does not: those call sites are\nself-closing, so such an entry would render nothing at all, with no\nerror.\n\nA category opts in by declaring a contributed shape:\n\n```ts\ntype ExtensionEntryType<Props, Contributed, Condition> =\n  [Contributed] extends [never]\n    ? ReplaceEntryType<Props, Condition>                            // component required\n    : ReplaceEntryType<Props, Condition> | DecorateEntryType<...>;  // either mode\n```\n\nLeave `Contributed` at `never` and the decorate branch does not exist,\nso registering one there is a **compile error**, not a silent no-op.\nToday only `mobileMenu` opts in.\n\n`ExtensionPointList` now delegates to `ExtensionPoint` per entry, so\nboth renderers agree on what a component-less entry means.\n\n---\n\n## The rest of the facade\n\nGrouped by export shape — the tiering rule is now written down in\n`client-app/core-api/README.md`, so the next request answers itself.\n\n| Tier | Shape | What went in |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1. Capability | composable / function | `registerCacheTypePolicies`,\n`useWishlistSharingScopes`, `Logger`, `useUser`, `useNavigations`,\n`useModal`, `useNotifications`, `useBreadcrumbs`, `usePageHead`,\n`getProductRoute`, `EXTENSION_NAMES`, menu types, the sharing-scope\ncontrols type |\n| 2. Host-rendered chrome | nothing — an extension entry | the sales-rep\nmobile nav link |\n| 3. Frozen component | a `.vue` component | `OrderStatus` |\n\nPlus a new subpath export alongside the existing `/federation` and\n`/tailwind-preset`: **`/testing`**, for the mount helpers a plugin''s\nspecs need.\n\n**`registerCacheTypePolicies`** lets a plugin normalise its own GraphQL\ntypes without importing the Apollo cache. It warns in development when a\ntypename is already in the cache — policies do not apply retroactively,\nand registering late otherwise fails silently. Its first consumer is on\nthis branch: the layout policies from #2400 register through it, so\n`modules/sales-rep` no longer touches the cache instance.\n\n**ui-kit** — all **21** `Vc*` components the module''s templates use are\nexported, up from 7. The host registers them globally, but a remote only\nresolves that when it renders inside the host''s app instance, and a\nplugin''s own dev server has none.\n\n**`@vc-frontend/core/testing`** ships `createWrapperFactory` /\n`createShallowWrapperFactory` as *real source*, unlike the root export:\nthat one is types-only because the host injects the implementation at\nruntime, and a plugin''s specs run with no host to inject anything.\n`@vue/test-utils` is passed in rather than imported, so the module never\nreaches for the consumer''s copy. The host''s own `@/core/utilities/tests`\nre-exports it, so the four in-repo specs are untouched.\n\nThe Apollo cache is deliberately *not* exported.\n`data-freshness.test.ts` needs *an* Apollo cache, not the host''s\ninstance — the host''s type policies are cart/checkout-specific, and the\nones that spec exercises come from the module''s own\n`layout/cache-policies.ts`.\n\n**`OrderStatus`** is exported as-is because its status → colour mapping\ncomes from per-store `orders_statuses` settings; a plugin-side chip\nwould drift. Its four props are contract from here on.\n\n---\n\n## Versioning: the contract goes to 0.1.0\n\nIt was heading for 1.2.0. It is not ready to promise stability to a\nthird-party plugin author, so it moves to a pre-1.0 line instead.\n\nNothing breaks by doing so: **no `core-v*` release has ever been\npublished**, so `0.1.0` is the first version anyone can actually\ninstall.\n\nUnder `^0.x` the **minor** is what a caret range refuses, so the levels\nshift down one: additive is a **patch**, breaking is a **minor**. The\nversioning automation now picks its levels from the release line it is\non; the 1.x mapping is untouched and takes over at 1.0.0.\n\n`core-v0.1.0` still has to be published by the *Core Facade Release*\nworkflow before a plugin can install against it.\n\nA plugin pins the facade by tarball URL, so anything added to the\npackage later re-pins every plugin. That is why the two remaining gaps —\nui-kit coverage and the specs'' mount helpers — are closed here rather\nthan deferred to the move.\n\n---\n\n---\n\n## Defects found and fixed while reviewing this branch\n\nEach one below is a real defect in this PR''s own additions, with a test\nthat fails without the fix.\n\n### `@vc-frontend/core/testing` did not work for the only consumer it\nexists for\n\n`testing.mjs` imports `lodash-es` at runtime. It was a peer only, and\n`create-plugin` drew its\n`devDependencies` from `CONTRACT_TYPE_PEERS` — where `lodash-es` never\nappeared. So the first spec in\na scaffolded plugin importing the mount helpers died on `Cannot find\nmodule`. `vue-i18n` survived by\nhappening to be MF-shared.\n\nSame root cause, wider blast radius: `peerDependencies` declared **2 of\nthe 14** packages the\npublished files import. The real list lived in build-time JS objects no\npackage manager reads, so a\nconsumer installing the tarball by hand — a supported path,\n`PORT_TO_MF.md` §4 — was missing five type\npeers, and `skipLibCheck: true` in the scaffold''s own tsconfig kept it\nsilent: only the individual\nmembers degraded to `any`, never the top-level exports, so\n`mergeMenuSchema(42)` and\n`mergeMenuSchema(null)` compiled clean on the very call `PORT_TO_MF`\nsays to keep.\n\nThe declaration is now **derived, not maintained**. `build-types.mjs`\nscans every file in `files` —\nnot just the rolled contract, which is why `testing.mjs` went unchecked\n— for `from`, `require()` and\nthe `import(\"x\")` form the `.d.mts` files use, and fails with the exact\nobject to paste when\n`package.json` disagrees. Required vs optional follows reachability;\n`create-plugin` merges the\nfacade''s own `peerDependencies` so there is no second list left to\ndrift.\n\n### Five holes in `registerCacheTypePolicies`, the new plugin-facing\ncache seam\n\n- **Ownership was per typename, but Apollo merges `fields` per field\nname.** So the first plugin to\nregister any `Query.fields.*` owned all of `Query`, and every later\nplugin''s policy for a *different*\nroot field was refused wholesale — a refusal protecting nothing, since\nApollo merges the two\nadditively. Claims are keyed per field now, with a deliberately\n**asymmetric** collision rule:\n`keyFields` re-keys the whole entity, so a type-level claim collides\nwith the typename *and* every\nfield under it. Without that asymmetry the host''s `Product: { fields: {\nproperties } }` —\nfields-only, like most host policies — would leave `Product` formally\nunclaimed and a plugin could\n  redefine how the host identifies it. A spec pins that case.\n- **The late-registration warning could not see the two shapes that\nmatter.** A root-type policy never\nproduces a `Query:` key — its fields live under `ROOT_QUERY` — so a late\n`Query.fields.x.keyArgs`,\nthe commonest hazard there is, orphaned everything already stored under\nthe old field key and warned\nabout nothing. A typename stored inline (no `id`) was invisible for the\nsame reason.\n- **Re-registering your own claim reported a collision with yourself**,\nwhich is what HMR and a second\n`init()` both look like, sending the reader hunting for a plugin that\ndoes not exist.\n- **`priority` had no ceiling, so the docblock''s central promise was\nfalse.** `by.priority >= priority`\nis the whole gate and `priority` came from the caller, so `{ owner: \"x\",\npriority: 101 }` took the\nhost''s `CouponType: { keyFields: [\"code\"] }` over with zero refusals and\nzero warnings, and the cache\nreally re-keyed by `id`. A caller''s value is clamped below\n`HOST_PRIORITY` now. The host seeds its own\nclaims straight into the ownership map, never through the public\nfunction, so the cap costs it nothing\nand plugin-vs-plugin escalation is untouched. A non-finite priority is\nsanitized in the same step:\n  every `>= NaN` comparison is false, so `NaN` refused nothing at all.\n- **`owner` defaulted to `\"unknown\"`, which turned the same-owner\nexemption into a hole.** Two plugins\nthat both omitted it were indistinguishable, so neither blocked the\nother and the loser got no signal —\nin production none at all, since `Logger` is a no-op there. `owner` is\nrequired now, so every refusal\nnames someone. No `core-v*` contract is published, so tightening the\nsignature costs no consumer;\nafter the first release it would not be free, and the contract gate\ncompares export *names*, so it\n  would not have flagged it.\n\nAnd the docs stop overclaiming: `cache.ts` promised a plugin \"cannot\nquietly take over a typename the\nhost normalizes\", but the ownership map is seeded from the policies the\nhost *declares*, which is not\nthe set it stores — anything Apollo normalizes by its default `id` rule\nis unclaimed. Stated as a known\ngap now rather than a guarantee.\n\n### The typing CI step was checking zero files\n\n`vitest --typecheck` spawns `tsc --noEmit` from the repo root without\n`-p` unless `typecheck.tsconfig`\nis set, so it inherited the root `{\"files\": []}` config: every\n`.test-d.ts` reported \"no errors\"\nregardless of content — a planted `TS2322` and an unused\n`@ts-expect-error` both stayed green. Which\nmatters here, because `useExtensionRegistry.test-d.ts` is where this\nPR''s central type guard lives, so\nanyone verifying that claim by running the type test got a false pass.\n(The Build step''s\n`vue-tsc --build` *was* catching them — the step named after typing was\nnot.)\n\nPointing it at a project surfaced 26 pre-existing errors across the repo\nand red-lit CI for things\nthis PR is not about, so it now uses a dedicated\n`tsconfig.typecheck.json` scoped to `**/*.test-d.ts`.\nTypeScript still pulls in what those files import. `yarn test:typing\n--run` exits 0 clean and 1 on a\nplanted error — checked both, exit code included.\n\n### Smaller, each with a test that fails without it\n\n- **A released contract line only moves forward.** `escapesCaretRange`\nasked \"is the current version\noutside `^base`\", which is also true *below* the baseline — so `1.2.0 →\n1.1.0` with an export removed\nreturned \"major already bumped\" and would have minted a release whose\ncontract has fewer exports than\nthe earlier version number. A regression is refused outright now, gated\non `released` so the\ndeliberate 1.2.0 → 0.1.0 reset this PR performs stays legal. The bump\nguard also stops printing\n  \"passed\" when it compared the contract with itself.\n- **Both dependency-cruiser boundary rules are blind to `import type`.**\n`tsPreCompilationDeps` is off,\nso type-only edges never enter its graph — proven with probes: three\nvalue imports caught, the same\nthree as `import type` produce zero violations. That is exactly the\ncoupling that breaks when\n`modules/sales-rep` moves to its own repo. Turning the flag on is not a\ndrop-in (`true` → 19 errors,\n`\"specify\"` → 15), so the bans are restated in `eslint.config.js`, which\nsees `import type`. **Honest\nlimit:** CI runs `yarn build` → `validate:types` +\n`validate:dependencies`, not eslint, so the\ntype-only half holds in the IDE and `yarn lint`, not the pipeline.\nRecorded in the config; closing it\nproperly is a separate decision (scope the `tsPreCompilationDeps` work,\nor add lint to `validate`).\n- **Replacing a contribution under the same name kept the old one\nrunning** and never started the new\none — the child was keyed on `name`, and it reads `use` once in setup.\nNot reachable today (nothing\ncalls `unregister` but specs, and both triggers the reviews assumed hit\nthe duplicate guard instead),\nbut the registry README teaches the unregister-then-register pattern, so\nit is a trap for the first\nplugin author to update a contribution. Keyed on the contribution''s\nidentity now.\n- **A released line''s \"already bumped\" reason named the wrong level.**\n`breaking` comes from\n`policyFor(baseVersion)`, so promoting `0.9.0 → 1.0.0` with an export\nremoved reported `\"minor already\nbumped\"` when the human moved the major. The decision was right, the\nwording was not; it reads the\nbump that HAPPENED off `semver.diff` now. The `require-` path still\nnames the level a human is *asked*\n  for, which is the baseline''s.\n- **Two paths lost the `_internal` ban entirely.** The sales-rep block\nwaives `NO_RAW_APOLLO_QUERY` for\nits specs and `useSalesRepHubQuery.ts`, but the two boundary blocks\nbelow skip all of `sales-rep/**`,\nso those files matched no `no-restricted-syntax` block at all — value\n*and* type imports of a host\n`_internal/` component went uncaught, and dependency-cruiser sees\nneither type-only edge. A trailing\nblock restates just that ban for them, raw-Apollo waiver intact. A spec\ntravels with the module when\nit is extracted, so a host component mounted in one breaks the\nextraction exactly as a source import\n  would.\n- **`EXTENSION_NAMES.mobileMenu.myCustomers`** — the registry README''s\ncanonical example — is\n`undefined` at runtime while type-checking as `string`, so copying that\nline registers under the\nliteral string `\"undefined\"`. `EXTENSION_NAMES` is typed as its own\ndeclared names now, making that a\n  compile error.\n- The README told authors a late registration runs `use()` **outside** a\ncomponent context where\n`inject()` does not resolve — the opposite of what the code does and of\nthis PR''s own passing spec.\nBelieving it means avoiding every injection-dependent composable, i.e.\nall of Apollo, which is the\n  entire reason `use()` is a function.\n- `@vc-frontend/core/tailwind-preset` shipped with no `types` condition,\nso a TypeScript\n`tailwind.config.ts` failed with TS7016. `window.modulesCacheDebug` was\ndeclared always-present\nwhile only development assigns it. `default-menu.test.ts`''s \"renders no\ncount\" asserted\n`toContain(\"my customers:\")`, which `\"my customers:3\"` also satisfies —\nthe test could not fail.\n- **The tier table authorised one `.vue` export and the facade ships 22\n`Vc*` plus `uiKit`.** They are\nthere for a real reason (a plugin''s own dev server has no host app\ninstance, so nothing resolves a\nglobally-registered component), but a reviewer had no written basis to\nrefuse the 23rd. Now a tier of\nits own with one admission rule, and the unenforced half is stated: the\ngate compares exported\n*names*, so a renamed ui-kit prop ships as a patch and every plugin\npinned to the range keeps\nresolving it. A prop-level diff would make that promise real; until then\na ui-kit prop rename is a\nmanual breaking bump. (Correcting this PR''s own earlier claim: the\nfacade went from **3** `Vc*` at\nthe merge base to 22, and from 10 public names to 53 — not \"up from 7\".)\n\n### Sonar\n\nThe failing quality gate was one `javascript:S2871` BUG on\n`readdirSync(dir).sort()` — a false\npositive (S2871 exists for numeric arrays; the default comparator on\nstrings already *is* UTF-16 code\nunits, identical to the file''s own helper), fixed anyway since a bare\n`.sort()` reads as a latent\nnumeric-sort bug. The MAJOR `S6661` \"use object spread\" on\n`extension-point.vue` is **stale**: there is\nno `Object.assign` in any revision of that file on this branch, none in\nits compiled output, and the\nissue carries `\"line\": null` with a creation date eight days before the\nfile was rewritten. The\nremaining seven smells introduced by these fixes are cleared, and the\n`String.raw` ones turned out to\nsit on a real defect: `new RegExp(`\\b${name}\\b`)` interpolated\nidentifiers raw, and the\nambient-globals collector accepts `$` in identifiers — which is a regex\n*end anchor*, so `\\b$VcTheme\\b`\ncould never match and such a declaration was skipped with no diagnostic.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `yarn test:typing --run` (what CI runs) — **2188 tests / 143 files**,\nno type errors, exit 0\n- `yarn vitest run --dir client-app` — **2150 tests / 140 files**, exit\n0\n- `yarn build` — exit 0\n- `vue-tsc --build --force` — 0 errors\n- `yarn validate:dependencies` — 0 errors\n- `yarn validate:core-types` — contract matches the facade; peer\ndeclaration covers 10 required + 4\n  subpath-only packages\n- `eslint` — 0 errors on the changed files\n- Merged `dev` twice. The first merge (6 commits) mattered because `dev`\nhad independently rewritten\nthree files this branch touches, including `data-freshness.test.ts` —\nthe spec this PR offers as its\n  freshness guarantee — changing its GraphQL fixture shapes.\nThe second (4 commits, up to #2439) conflicted for real, in\n`modules/sales-rep`, and both conflicts\nwere resolved in this branch''s favour where the two disagree on purpose:\n- dev calls `registerLayoutTypePolicies(cache)`; this branch renamed\nthat export and routes it\nthrough `registerCacheTypePolicies`, so the module no longer imports the\ncache instance;\n- dev registers the mobile My customers link as a component — the very\ncomponent this PR deletes —\nso `registerContribution` stays and dev''s permission-gated documents\nblock sits ahead of it;\n- dev''s new documents route mounts via `ROUTES.COMPANY.NAME`, like its\nsiblings here.\n- Regenerated the GraphQL types from `vcptcore-dev`. Core types only;\nthe eight module schemas came\nback byte-identical. This picks up the document-library surface #2439\nadded to `Query`, which the\ncore snapshot had not caught up with, and drops `CartType.loyaltyPoints`\n— an environment\ndifference, not a schema change. Nothing reads that field, and the\nfacade contract is unaffected:\n  the `loyaltyPoints` it inlines belongs to `Product`.\n\n---\n\n## Notes for the reviewer\n\n- `yarn validate:core-types` is stale on `dev` itself — it does not run\nin `yarn validate` during the pilot — so regenerating here also pulls in\nthe `sharedList` category from #2405 that `dev`''s committed contract\npredates.\n- `isRegistered()` answers \"has a component\", not \"is registered\" — a\ndecorate entry returns false. That reading is what hid the\ndropped-contribution bug. The name is left alone here (renaming it is\nchurn this PR does not need) and noted where it is defined.\n- `headerMenu` and `accountMenu` have fallback markup but their slots\nare unscoped, so contributed data would be discarded, and both leave\n`Contributed` at `never` — the compile gate keeps them closed until\nthose slots are scoped. `mobileMenu`''s two call sites are both scoped\nhere: `default-menu.vue` is where today''s badge renders, since the My\ncustomers link is an account-section child; `main-menu.vue` opens\ndecorate mode for top-level mobile items, which nothing uses yet.\n- `modules/push-messages` still imports two `_internal/` components. The\nsame fix applies to it, out of scope here — and both files are the\ndocumented exemption in the new eslint rule as well as in\ndependency-cruiser.\n- Two things about the badge that look like defects and are not, so they\nneed not be re-raised. The badge is not stale across mount/unmount:\nstaleness is bounded to the account-shell visit, because\n`account-shell.vue` renders the desktop rail `max-md:hidden` — mounted,\nnot unmounted — which is the trade-off that makes the two surfaces\nagree. And `data-freshness.test.ts` does catch the regression it guards:\nreintroducing the session-lifetime memo, or switching to `cache-first`,\nturns it red.\n- One real behaviour delta in that area, stated rather than fixed: a\nfailed count fetch hides the badge for the rest of the account-shell\nvisit with no retry. Pre-PR each surface had its own query, so reopening\nthe mobile menu re-issued it. The designed failure mode is a hidden\nbadge and the consistency win is the point, but it is a behaviour delta\nworth knowing.\n- `sortablejs` is deliberately **not** in `MF_SHARED_RANGES`: a leaf DOM\nlibrary with no cross-copy state, so a duplicate costs bundle size, not\ncorrectness. The HOWTO documents that rule, plus the exception that does\nforce sharing — a library whose state crosses the boundary via\n`provide`/`inject`. `vee-validate` is the near-miss.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5159\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2427-8344-8344665b.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoqPbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAj5QQACELAnPOZexxTUa5RvCi0oOu\ny9Zy9YAfKP20auCSRRrg4sn/P+KucnSb8sXqNtg1OkD+j8CuPnR2eG0e2ruzjEHM\npFIivUKAELTHm6s268Nq+1AyQQJ/hksECv5V40KqU6lW81h/3q3oF8gEcyb1vLBz\nXPv/6FbGHfSuWNg3Kg5HO2qBQc8+3wiq0GOTkVeaJ+cBHT7oBogEjAC3XWjt1Llh\n4LgFzi38MEqKyOz2v2OlzaL92ZoydLPhbXjGn8AwjGlMeWo3WZgGne37U6dMzRgy\nBYsf5pzMUAzmB/n3EXk9RxZNFYQtSHHBP2sBKnGSEXhoWH+4kwgods3SOuqSonbZ\nMaI6xb0KpAot13/wB7V8MLfbEU7s9WzNmmUQCTFtZULvzAG5pqJlvTqknct3UL3i\nYQfhiVcfQeZ1Lc6a6f937XMIL7UovTFmG4yf9WpfrmBLN9S24NS1/K0eebUD9IQq\nDm/bQQjHr6l85I8JZfh+5l+PHSLMNp4YProy/DR6HjWyVOXFbXTnTTy1zBlRyAva\nxRnGweMS5u8iuMgEJmq0PrdLsmv1EPBAhTb5HoSae6O0my3du5XMRgA91axVrbqC\nV2l3BRdKqLg46Hx6BgisgOu2q3bXMYRMfEO0noRgFUDRQib038HmYju1VQ15T4G9\ns8h1yP7Xggo5D3emuyEX\n=wj/h\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-10T12:34:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/976b29294d3d6c429f99152296535d5616a9a65c","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDk3NmIyOTI5NGQzZDZjNDI5Zjk5MTUyMjk2NTM1ZDU2MTZhOWE2NWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/844fdf29045007dd959e0b8ac798522ba30f3256","sha":"844fdf29045007dd959e0b8ac798522ba30f3256","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/844fdf29045007dd959e0b8ac798522ba30f3256"}],"sha":"976b29294d3d6c429f99152296535d5616a9a65c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/976b29294d3d6c429f99152296535d5616a9a65c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56412054?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Lenajava1","id":56412054,"login":"Lenajava1","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2NDEyMDU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lenajava1","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/844fdf29045007dd959e0b8ac798522ba30f3256/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T11:23:23Z","email":"56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Elena Mutykova"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T11:23:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(VCST-5916): label mission-granted rows in points history (#2473)\n\n## Problem\n\nOn the **Points history** page (`/account/points-history`) the\n**Operation** column is empty for every points row granted by a loyalty\nmission. Order-driven rows show their order number correctly. Measured\non a QA environment: 69 of 167 ledger rows on one account, all mission\ngrants. No console error, no failing request — it fails silently.\n\nThere are two sequential causes. `VirtoCommerce/vc-module-loyalty#16`\nfixes the first (the xAPI resolver returned `object: null` for mission\nrows; it now returns `object.type === \"Mission\"`). **This PR fixes the\nsecond:** `getOperation()` had no branch for that type and fell through\nto `return log.object?.type`, which renders the raw, unlocalized token.\n\n## Change\n\n- `constants.ts` — add `MISSION_OBJECT_TYPE = \"Mission\"` beside the\nexisting `REGISTRATION_OBJECT_TYPE`.\n- `points-history.vue` — one branch in `getOperation()` returning\n`t(\"loyalty.points-history.mission\")`, mirroring the existing\nregistration branch. The `log.object?.type` fall-through is left as the\nfinal fallback.\n- **All 13 locale files** — add a `mission` key under\n`loyalty.points-history`, matching the repo''s convention that every\nlocale carries a translated value (as `registration` already does).\n\n`getOperation()` backs both the `#desktop-body` and `#mobile-item`\nslots, so one branch covers desktop and mobile.\n\nTranslations were aligned to the mission noun each locale **already\nuses** in the same file under `pages.account.missions.*`, rather than\ntransliterating — e.g. `de` \"Aufgabenbelohnung\" (that file already says\n\"Aufgabenziel\"), `fi` \"Tehtäväpalkkio\", `no` \"Oppdragsbelønning\", `sv`\n\"Uppdragsbelöning\".\n\n## Before\n\n<img width=\"1143\" height=\"621\"\nalt=\"layer1-points-history-operation-blank\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5f8f1dd0-d0c4-40fa-836d-2e5c07cfa2ce\"\n/>\n\n## After\n\n<img width=\"1218\" height=\"830\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d24e3295-a20a-4c99-8086-3487ac7a10e9\"\n/>\n\n\n## Tests\n\nAdds `client-app/modules/loyalty/pages/points-history.test.ts` (net-new;\nno existing test or story modified). It mounts the real page via the\nrepo''s `createWrapperFactory`, following the sibling\n`my-customers.test.ts` pattern, and stubs `VcTable` so one spec\nexercises both the desktop row and the mobile card.\n\nBecause the shared test `createI18n` is built with `messages: {}`, `t()`\nreturns the key path — the repo''s existing assertion convention. So the\nmount test alone cannot prove the translations exist; a second block\nreads all 13 locale JSON files **off disk** and asserts a non-empty\n`loyalty.points-history.mission` in each, which is what makes the locale\nhalf of this change falsifiable.\n\nConfirmed RED before the fix (3 failed / 2 passed — the 2 passing being\ndeliberate no-regression guards for the order/registration rows and the\nnull-`object` fall-through), GREEN after: scoped spec 5/5, `vue-tsc\n--build --force` exit 0, eslint clean, prettier clean, and the `Check\nLocales` CI script exit 0.\n\nProduction `build` and the full unit suite were deliberately not run:\nthe diff is one helper branch, one exported constant and 13 JSON leaf\nkeys, with no shared/core/UI-kit code touched, and `vue-tsc --build\n--force` already compiled the whole graph.\n\n## Merge order matters\n\nThese two PRs should land close together, and ideally this one first or\nsimultaneously. If `vc-module-loyalty#16` deploys **before** this PR,\nthe resolver starts returning `\"Mission\"` while the storefront still has\nno branch for it, so the column renders the literal token `Mission` in\nall 13 locales. That is an improvement on a blank cell but is not the\nfinished state — it is expected transitional behaviour, not a defect.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis makes the row state that the points came from a mission. It does\n**not** identify *which* mission — that needs a new field on the xAPI\nobject type and is tracked separately as **VCST-5917**.\n\n**DO NOT MERGE until human review.**\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01LUq39vVvCm1ATQnPJyCxvw\n\nArtifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2473-87a7-87a7e7a4.zip\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3badff51186de627ba1ac8fd906aa4f1ded68a0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/3badff51186de627ba1ac8fd906aa4f1ded68a0a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/844fdf29045007dd959e0b8ac798522ba30f3256","verification":{"payload":"tree 3badff51186de627ba1ac8fd906aa4f1ded68a0a\nparent 347eb10a27215f9a3a235bf556ecff7a6f28a946\nauthor Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com> 1789039403 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789039403 +0100\n\nfix(VCST-5916): label mission-granted rows in points history (#2473)\n\n## Problem\n\nOn the **Points history** page (`/account/points-history`) the\n**Operation** column is empty for every points row granted by a loyalty\nmission. Order-driven rows show their order number correctly. Measured\non a QA environment: 69 of 167 ledger rows on one account, all mission\ngrants. No console error, no failing request — it fails silently.\n\nThere are two sequential causes. `VirtoCommerce/vc-module-loyalty#16`\nfixes the first (the xAPI resolver returned `object: null` for mission\nrows; it now returns `object.type === \"Mission\"`). **This PR fixes the\nsecond:** `getOperation()` had no branch for that type and fell through\nto `return log.object?.type`, which renders the raw, unlocalized token.\n\n## Change\n\n- `constants.ts` — add `MISSION_OBJECT_TYPE = \"Mission\"` beside the\nexisting `REGISTRATION_OBJECT_TYPE`.\n- `points-history.vue` — one branch in `getOperation()` returning\n`t(\"loyalty.points-history.mission\")`, mirroring the existing\nregistration branch. The `log.object?.type` fall-through is left as the\nfinal fallback.\n- **All 13 locale files** — add a `mission` key under\n`loyalty.points-history`, matching the repo''s convention that every\nlocale carries a translated value (as `registration` already does).\n\n`getOperation()` backs both the `#desktop-body` and `#mobile-item`\nslots, so one branch covers desktop and mobile.\n\nTranslations were aligned to the mission noun each locale **already\nuses** in the same file under `pages.account.missions.*`, rather than\ntransliterating — e.g. `de` \"Aufgabenbelohnung\" (that file already says\n\"Aufgabenziel\"), `fi` \"Tehtäväpalkkio\", `no` \"Oppdragsbelønning\", `sv`\n\"Uppdragsbelöning\".\n\n## Before\n\n<img width=\"1143\" height=\"621\"\nalt=\"layer1-points-history-operation-blank\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5f8f1dd0-d0c4-40fa-836d-2e5c07cfa2ce\"\n/>\n\n## After\n\n<img width=\"1218\" height=\"830\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d24e3295-a20a-4c99-8086-3487ac7a10e9\"\n/>\n\n\n## Tests\n\nAdds `client-app/modules/loyalty/pages/points-history.test.ts` (net-new;\nno existing test or story modified). It mounts the real page via the\nrepo''s `createWrapperFactory`, following the sibling\n`my-customers.test.ts` pattern, and stubs `VcTable` so one spec\nexercises both the desktop row and the mobile card.\n\nBecause the shared test `createI18n` is built with `messages: {}`, `t()`\nreturns the key path — the repo''s existing assertion convention. So the\nmount test alone cannot prove the translations exist; a second block\nreads all 13 locale JSON files **off disk** and asserts a non-empty\n`loyalty.points-history.mission` in each, which is what makes the locale\nhalf of this change falsifiable.\n\nConfirmed RED before the fix (3 failed / 2 passed — the 2 passing being\ndeliberate no-regression guards for the order/registration rows and the\nnull-`object` fall-through), GREEN after: scoped spec 5/5, `vue-tsc\n--build --force` exit 0, eslint clean, prettier clean, and the `Check\nLocales` CI script exit 0.\n\nProduction `build` and the full unit suite were deliberately not run:\nthe diff is one helper branch, one exported constant and 13 JSON leaf\nkeys, with no shared/core/UI-kit code touched, and `vue-tsc --build\n--force` already compiled the whole graph.\n\n## Merge order matters\n\nThese two PRs should land close together, and ideally this one first or\nsimultaneously. If `vc-module-loyalty#16` deploys **before** this PR,\nthe resolver starts returning `\"Mission\"` while the storefront still has\nno branch for it, so the column renders the literal token `Mission` in\nall 13 locales. That is an improvement on a blank cell but is not the\nfinished state — it is expected transitional behaviour, not a defect.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis makes the row state that the points came from a mission. It does\n**not** identify *which* mission — that needs a new field on the xAPI\nobject type and is tracked separately as **VCST-5917**.\n\n**DO NOT MERGE until human review.**\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01LUq39vVvCm1ATQnPJyCxvw\n\nArtifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2473-87a7-87a7e7a4.zip\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqopMrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQiIQAIFzxcMLnu3XCebhQXAPeSkD\nNyc6W1HWmhxCwK8Xo7b6TaBI9+m/ESUAzCtBdK93JtQGJbgQ29Zg/g47h9mb04o3\n9EMV1upIkJlgMBkeAQoChQ+N4B3cIyxhr5LsyyX+vIy2Fm/VTMC2qutxN3A5Xt+Z\nWHhnQWqFyaa0SxrBfSXgu7GyhWj5f6ZDBpKmoD5TjetooNlaOIzqcabpRV6+99Vq\nWMgu3+EAfW0djU9nFUaMniLl0afMVpCTvmYiShHwmS5aA+JnfWyHDUX2NGyJs4T6\nITkoCUMDJKVySX+xl+iNyfWOJ/Z5714LHRoyE4dyxkzbWu37XneYogI1RVDc9Vr6\nTOj2bwTLQKSpCIwDlUluXxPrFgSY6mKFxsN3uzx/A+S9Lj5k5p6HP798xO28BwyA\nSXY13ApUxTEYStDJ8m7E2ubCvJ8J65waupkCrqlP9LoNGSyAWxAvKsm0+mALmbk3\nh5SY8ms3HRIPCxUT0cQfSrSWPLCoR1mHQUB0YPqZqxjMszJsUdPo1NUCezh7v+1Y\nRnoE0bN4JEY6w5eDdfxeJ/H8rKelCvI5ksJGu8xXtiYqIXf43HrpdMs1Jj8NoBW5\nPc8uOGjAW76gd3Iw1VVoArXXJQO+HdUOiNNMW+OJYtvf4KH28Y6iwvTtjv0X3cxO\nCbZUib1YB84yFsxqeysN\n=Xphx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-10T11:23:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/844fdf29045007dd959e0b8ac798522ba30f3256","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDg0NGZkZjI5MDQ1MDA3ZGQ5NTllMGI4YWM3OTg1MjJiYTMwZjMyNTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/347eb10a27215f9a3a235bf556ecff7a6f28a946","sha":"347eb10a27215f9a3a235bf556ecff7a6f28a946","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/347eb10a27215f9a3a235bf556ecff7a6f28a946"}],"sha":"844fdf29045007dd959e0b8ac798522ba30f3256","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/844fdf29045007dd959e0b8ac798522ba30f3256"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16372194?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/goldenmaya","id":16372194,"login":"goldenmaya","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzcyMTk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/347eb10a27215f9a3a235bf556ecff7a6f28a946/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T06:40:10Z","email":"mayapavlovna@gmail.com","name":"Maiia Diachkovskaia"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T06:40:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VCST-5891): icon sizing & sentence-case in vc-button (#2470)\n\n## Description\n<img width=\"597\" height=\"283\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-08 at 10 26 01\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ef9b0aa2-b03a-4487-92cf-b35d023e2e92\"\n/>\n<img width=\"586\" height=\"287\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-08 at 10 25 49\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fc4d57db-7142-4a68-bc76-49fcd7d9f1cf\"\n/>\n<img width=\"595\" height=\"289\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-08 at 10 25 41\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f8529688-8e1a-44f7-845c-e25baa4e8c10\"\n/>\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\n<!-- Put link to your task in Jira here -->\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5652\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5891\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2470-728c-728cf8f6.zip\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Visual breaking change for all sm–lg buttons app-wide; behavior is\nunchanged but labels will no longer render in uppercase unless\noverridden via CSS variable.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Updates **`VcButton`** typography for **sm**, **md**, and **lg** sizes\nto match sentence-case styling: drops forced **uppercase**,\n**font-black**, and letter-spacing, bumps text scale (e.g. md from\n`text-sm` to `text-base`), and uses **font-bold** instead.\n> \n> Casing is now driven by `text-transform:\nvar(--vc-button-text-transform, none)` so themes can opt back into\nuppercase without changing the component.\n> \n> Storybook updates swap demo icons from `save-v2` to `save`, use\n**bookmark** in the **IconVariant** story (with a note that\noutline/solid look the same), and add an **AllSizes** story that shows\ntext-only, prepend/append icon, and icon-only buttons across all sizes.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n728cf8f6bdaf6c638d0c77dd5757ce718f664dd5. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"0109ec3e4ee8f84f70e1922b26587650ac078ad3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/0109ec3e4ee8f84f70e1922b26587650ac078ad3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/347eb10a27215f9a3a235bf556ecff7a6f28a946","verification":{"payload":"tree 0109ec3e4ee8f84f70e1922b26587650ac078ad3\nparent bd427b46084682cc304922c3730c1f7d380e797c\nauthor Maiia Diachkovskaia <mayapavlovna@gmail.com> 1789022410 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789022410 +0300\n\nfeat(VCST-5891): icon sizing & sentence-case in vc-button (#2470)\n\n## Description\n<img width=\"597\" height=\"283\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-08 at 10 26 01\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ef9b0aa2-b03a-4487-92cf-b35d023e2e92\"\n/>\n<img width=\"586\" height=\"287\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-08 at 10 25 49\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fc4d57db-7142-4a68-bc76-49fcd7d9f1cf\"\n/>\n<img width=\"595\" height=\"289\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-09-08 at 10 25 41\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f8529688-8e1a-44f7-845c-e25baa4e8c10\"\n/>\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\n<!-- Put link to your task in Jira here -->\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5652\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5891\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2470-728c-728cf8f6.zip\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Visual breaking change for all sm–lg buttons app-wide; behavior is\nunchanged but labels will no longer render in uppercase unless\noverridden via CSS variable.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Updates **`VcButton`** typography for **sm**, **md**, and **lg** sizes\nto match sentence-case styling: drops forced **uppercase**,\n**font-black**, and letter-spacing, bumps text scale (e.g. md from\n`text-sm` to `text-base`), and uses **font-bold** instead.\n> \n> Casing is now driven by `text-transform:\nvar(--vc-button-text-transform, none)` so themes can opt back into\nuppercase without changing the component.\n> \n> Storybook updates swap demo icons from `save-v2` to `save`, use\n**bookmark** in the **IconVariant** story (with a note that\noutline/solid look the same), and add an **AllSizes** story that shows\ntext-only, prepend/append icon, and icon-only buttons across all sizes.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n728cf8f6bdaf6c638d0c77dd5757ce718f664dd5. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqolDKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAJ4QAAV9xrTqHKT1OIBtAoWlr5s5\nuUeLxaQWR1hnKgKhViq7zeKeV0BtQF3GW1G+gQsznrzjX1AhHMhoaTKljsjXcvX1\nFohGlQJgenm08tec68ig3DcjoqunmU9axj20j9k+kBRpItm5qQ/IHFbbxQ6uNMGE\nyI48Seg1Jw4JUm1g0bWOcLcAaRilWYyzIr2fOhTyE7+sjDK+0sS01tzLJgJ01LNt\neqkzLBv3EcTOY4DteqUFOYeTxiKGMMMnLGtcICenU2/bWeftdndc6guVEwuaZyab\nfAZK5Tw7yjO2rUeTZ0L+1b4mAbwV03dlP3qJzj+oZIha9OSmG9AghybZiQzg1G4a\nNAIT3BdKS6/bwi0a6WZt0fDumqTTVu6GtJWRneSA0vdkjefzMusAxA6S2afT/vyl\nzpE8NUFZ25ZzkYRbUsWn0dYiiUXLc3LWX9jRte8t8rIiEQAlvX9qnz6TZC+fP/Gy\nqH9itVTUUdQiOcIlHwwkngtpTx455jMGFZWXwdmV34lbMA9jBAypqAZXlRXG46t/\n+R0Getfy1xG4j5FMp1idkM4am+QnLnZQ2tnmTo1xRK8LKDJ49ENr+pihOK1A2dd8\ncMoNmivyeP4iyhaZja4JKaIej3wr+0d4TT+6Mgi6/hVHAn42PzLUhwfvalZNXNeH\nTcHnY5iN9Hcco0WRJf3X\n=SyK4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-10T06:40:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/347eb10a27215f9a3a235bf556ecff7a6f28a946","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDM0N2ViMTBhMjcyMTVmOWEzYTIzNWJmNTU2ZWNmZjdhNmYyOGE5NDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/bd427b46084682cc304922c3730c1f7d380e797c","sha":"bd427b46084682cc304922c3730c1f7d380e797c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/bd427b46084682cc304922c3730c1f7d380e797c"}],"sha":"347eb10a27215f9a3a235bf556ecff7a6f28a946","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/347eb10a27215f9a3a235bf556ecff7a6f28a946"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18286430?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ivan-kalachikov","id":18286430,"login":"ivan-kalachikov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Mjg2NDMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/bd427b46084682cc304922c3730c1f7d380e797c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T15:23:03Z","email":"ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com","name":"Ivan Kalachikov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T15:23:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VCST-5159): discover federated plugins from the platform (#2445)\n\n## Description\n\nThe federated loader could only read remotes from a build-time env map,\nso shipping a plugin meant\nrebuilding the storefront. The platform now advertises installed plugins\nper host app (vc-platform\n#3019) and xAPI projects them onto the store (x-api 3.1016.0, x-frontend\n3.1005.0), so discovery\nbecomes a runtime concern: installing a module is enough.\n\n### Discovery\n\n- A dedicated `GetStorePlugins` query (`store.plugins(appId:\n\"vc-frontend\")`), issued only by a host\nbuilt as a federation host, gated by `APP_MODULES_FEDERATION_ENABLED`,\nand skipped when\n`APP_MODULES_FEDERATION_REMOTES` is set — that list wins in the loader\nanyway. It goes out\nalongside the other boot queries, so it adds no serial round trip; a\nfailure degrades to \"no\n  plugins\" and is budgeted at 2s.\n- It carries `SUPPRESS_ERROR_NOTIFICATIONS_CONTEXT`: nothing on screen\nbelongs to it, and on a\nbackend that does not know the field the global handler would broadcast\na generic error toast to\n  every open tab for a feature the visitor cannot see.\n- It is deliberately **not** part of `InitializeApplication`.\n`store.plugins` needs x-api 3.1016.0\nand a single unknown field fails the whole GraphQL document, which would\ntake `settings.modules`\nwith it: `apply-gates-link` would then strip every `@gate(module:)`\nfield (branding silently\nreverts to defaults), the promotion-coupons route would 404, and\n`notifyOutdatedModules` — the one\ndiagnostic that names the real cause — would never fire. The document is\nstatic, so that would\n  happen with `APP_MODULES_FEDERATION_ENABLED` off as well.\n\n### Entry, expose key, permission, stylesheets\n\n- Platform descriptors point at `remoteEntry.js`; the contract gate\nneeds the MF manifest beside it,\nso the last path segment is rewritten to `mf-manifest.json` and\ncache-busted with the platform''s\nown `?v={hash}`. A plugin shipping no manifest stays unverifiable and is\nskipped. A platform entry\nmust be same-origin and http(s) *after* the rewrite — `blob:` shares\nthis origin and has an opaque\npath, which would make the rewrite a no-op and leave MF script-loading\nthe entry as code.\n- The expose key comes from the descriptor (`./Module` is the platform\ndefault) instead of being\n  hardcoded to the scaffold''s `./plugin`.\n- Permission is evaluated host-side before any fetch: the platform\nserves one cached list to every\ncaller and does not filter per user. No permission check available +\ndeclared permission ⇒ skipped.\nThis is a UX and latency filter, not an authorization boundary — the\nbundle is fetched by an\ninjected `<script>` with no credentials, so each plugin''s data access\nmust be authorized on its own.\n- `contentFiles` of type `style` are injected once each, after the\nplugin has loaded and before its\n`init()` runs: a timeout does not cancel `init()`, so withholding the\nsheets would leave a live\npage unstyled. A content file of any other kind — or of no declared kind\n— is logged, not dropped\n  in silence. Not wrapped in a cascade layer; see VCST-5760.\n- The env map wins when set, so a plugin author''s local remote is never\nreplaced by what the backend\n  serves.\n\n### Loader hardening\n\n- Remote names are validated (`/^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*$/`, both\ndiscovery paths). MF resolves a\n`loadRemote` id by **prefix**, so with remotes `a` and `a/plugin` the\nrequest meant for the second\nmatches the first and is served out of *its* bundle — one plugin''s code\nnever runs while both are\n  reported loaded. Exact-name dedup cannot see that, here or in MF.\n- Duplicate remote names: first wins, the rest are skipped loudly. A\nname is claimed only after the\ndescriptor passes validation, so a plugin about to be skipped cannot\nblock a working one.\n- A non-`script` `entry.type`, a non-string field anywhere in the\nprojection, and a non-array plugin\nlist each cost one plugin instead of throwing out of the batch. A\ndescriptor with neither `id` nor\nremote name is reported by its position, so nothing is dropped without a\ntrace.\n- `init()` is called **on** the module, so `{ services, init() {\nthis.services } }` — the natural\nshape of the platform''s default `./Module` expose — keeps its receiver.\nA module exposing no\n  `init()` counts as loaded with a warning: its module scope did run.\n- Per-phase budgets: manifest 2s, load 3s, init 3s, discovery 2s, under\na 12s boot backstop. Three\nof those are **reductions** from `dev` (manifest 3s, load 5s, backstop\n20s): the invariant only\nasks that the backstop clear discovery + manifest + 2×load, so the\ntighter numbers keep the same\n2s of headroom for the unbudgeted loader-chunk fetch while cutting\nworst-case blank screen from\n20s to 12s. The cost is that a plugin whose `init()` legitimately runs\nlonger than 3s now reports\n`failed`; 5s would need a 16s backstop. The loader chunk''s own fetch\nstays unbudgeted — bounding\n  it is what the backstop is for.\n- Route guard: for the whole load-and-init phase `addRoute` and\n`removeRoute` refuse a claim on a\nname the host already owns. Both `addRoute` overloads are covered,\ndispatched the way vue-router\ndispatches them (by predicate, not argument count), plus every named\nentry in `children`, since\nvue-router treats those as root adds. `removeRoute` is wrapped in the\nsame window because\nremove-then-add would otherwise leave the name free by the time the add\nis checked. One guard\ncovers the whole phase, and the loader starts only after every host\nplugin has installed, so a\n  host call is never refused in a plugin''s place.\n- No `{ force: true }` on `registerRemotes`: re-registering a known name\nis already a no-op in MF\n2.8.0, while `force` calls `removeRemote` first, so a second boot would\nre-run the plugin''s module\n  scope and call `init()` twice.\n- The manifest **response** is re-checked for origin, per discovery\nsource — same-origin for a\nplatform entry, https (or loopback http) for an env one — because\n`fetch` follows redirects.\n\n### Local dev and scaffolding\n\n- `^/modules/.*/plugins/vc-frontend/` is proxied to `APP_BACKEND_URL` in\ndev and preview, so the\ndiscovery path is exercisable without a deployed host. Scoped to the\nplugin folder, not all of\n  `/modules`.\n- `create:plugin` now writes `public/plugin.json` (Vite copies it into\n`dist/`). Without a descriptor\nthe platform assumes its own defaults — remote name = the .NET module\nid, expose `./Module` — and\nthe host would `loadRemote` a key the generated plugin does not export.\n\n### Deferred, with tickets\n\n- **VCST-5761** — let a plugin declare its routes in `plugin.json`, so\nthe host can register\n  placeholders and stop gating `app.mount()` on this loader.\n- **VCST-5762** — extension-registry precedence; needs a facade\nsignature change and a contract rebuild.\n- **VCST-5760** — plugin CSS containment through one host-declared\ncascade layer order. Wrapping only\nthe plugin''s sheet was tried and reverted: unlayered beats layered, so\nthe plugin would lose to all\n  host CSS. Measured regression surface and the rejected alternatives:\n\n`client-app/modules/federated/specs/2026-08-21-plugin-css-cascade-layers.md`.\n- Artifact integrity, the per-plugin kill switch, route authorization\nand the ingress CSP stay in\n`TODO.md`. The `?v={hash}` cache-buster reaches the manifest URL, not\nthe `remoteEntry.js` it\npoints at; the clean fix is a `Cache-Control` on the platform''s static\nfile middleware.\n\n### Docs\n\n- `README.md` — the security model no longer advertises a build-time\nremote list as an enforced\nproperty. It now states what is enforced (same-origin platform entries,\nhttps-or-loopback env\nentries, both re-checked after redirects) and what is not (no origin\nallowlist for env remotes; a\nsame-origin manifest may still declare chunk URLs elsewhere), plus the\nbudgets and the route\n  guard''s limits.\n- `HOWTO.md` — leads with the backend-module path and explains the\n`plugin.json` the scaffolder\nemits (the scaffold exposes `./plugin`, the platform defaults to\n`./Module`).\n- `TODO.md` — artifact integrity closed as deliberately not done, with\nthe reasons\n(hostile code arrives on the first fetch anyway; MF injects\n`remoteEntry.js` as a `<script>`, so\nthe executed bytes are never ours to hash, and `entry.hash` is a\ncache-buster, not an SRI digest).\n- `specs/2026-07-06-discovery-hosting-decision.md` — the discovery half\nis marked superseded.\n\n### Generated files\n\n`dev` is merged, and both generated GraphQL type files are regenerated\nagainst **vcptcore-dev**:\n`CustomerCartStatisticsPeriod.lastCartDate`, which `dev` removed in\n#2437, is gone, and\n`modules/sales-rep/api/graphql/types.ts` is byte-identical to `dev`''s.\nvcst-qa cannot generate the\nsales-rep module — its schema lacks the document queries added in #2439.\nThree environment deltas\nremain: `CartType.loyaltyPoints` is absent on that environment (no\ndocument selects it, and the other\nhits are untouched module files plus `Product.loyaltyPoints` in the\ncontract); one field description\ncarries older wording; and vcptcore-dev **adds**\n`SalesRepDocument{,Category,Connection,Edge}`,\n`Query.salesRepDocument{,Categories,s}` and their `*Args` — 86 of the 90\nadded lines, absent from\n`dev`, and reversed again by regenerating on vcst-qa.\n\nThe core contract was already stale on `dev` — the `sharedList`\nextension point and its\nwishlist-sharing types were added without a rebuild, and\n`validate:core-types` runs in no workflow —\nso it is rebuilt here. The build''s own automation bumps `CORE_VERSION`\n1.2.0 → 1.3.0 for the changed\ncontract; plugins built against `^1.2.0` keep running.\n\n### Verified\n\n- 2447 tests in 159 files; `vue-tsc --build --force` clean; eslint on\nthe touched files: 0 errors,\n23 warnings (10 `sonarjs/no-redundant-optional` on `IPlatformPlugin`,\nwhich mirrors codegen''s\n`Maybe<T>` on purpose, and a `sonarjs/null-dereference` false positive).\n`validate:core-types` is\nred on a local checkout, but the only differing line is the property\norder of `VcButton`''s\ninferred defaults, byte-identical at the merge base — a vue-tsc\nartefact, not this PR.\n  `boot-order.test.ts` executes the real `app-runner` against mocked\ncollaborators and pins the order the calls actually happen in: theme\ncontext and user before the\nloader, the router installed only after it, the plugin-list query issued\nbefore the page context is\nawaited, nothing issued when the flag is off or the env override is set,\nand the loader started\n  after the host''s route-mutating plugin.\n- Live against vcst-qa: `store.plugins(appId: \"vc-frontend\")` answers\nthrough the new query and\nreturns `[]` — no module there ships a storefront plugin yet. The dev\nproxy was verified end to\nend: a request to\n`/modules/$(VirtoCommerce.SalesRep)/plugins/vc-frontend/mf-manifest.json`\nreaches\nthe platform (HTTP 404, empty body), while\n`/modules/$(X)/Content/logo.png` and any other path\nstill get Vite''s SPA fallback — which is the old failure mode, since\nthat HTML is what the contract\n  gate used to try to parse as JSON.\n- Not exercised: a real platform-served plugin load. That needs a module\non the target environment\n  shipping `plugins/vc-frontend/`; no environment has one.\n\n### Known repo-state issues found alongside, not fixed here\n\n`validate:core-types` runs in no PR workflow while a comment claims it\ndoes, the breaking-change\ndetector diffs export names only, `federation.mjs` ships in the\nversioned tarball but is outside the\nchange detection, and the production logger noops every level including\n`error`.\n\n## References\n### QA-test:\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5159\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2445-d7c2-d7c2c9c6.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dd88d5f92be3f76721f2d74d7699a85a44e4aed8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/dd88d5f92be3f76721f2d74d7699a85a44e4aed8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/bd427b46084682cc304922c3730c1f7d380e797c","verification":{"payload":"tree dd88d5f92be3f76721f2d74d7699a85a44e4aed8\nparent 78d02b0e1b11bcfac29c5d40620d4b6789fe1fd4\nauthor Ivan Kalachikov <ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com> 1788967383 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788967383 +0100\n\nfeat(VCST-5159): discover federated plugins from the platform (#2445)\n\n## Description\n\nThe federated loader could only read remotes from a build-time env map,\nso shipping a plugin meant\nrebuilding the storefront. The platform now advertises installed plugins\nper host app (vc-platform\n#3019) and xAPI projects them onto the store (x-api 3.1016.0, x-frontend\n3.1005.0), so discovery\nbecomes a runtime concern: installing a module is enough.\n\n### Discovery\n\n- A dedicated `GetStorePlugins` query (`store.plugins(appId:\n\"vc-frontend\")`), issued only by a host\nbuilt as a federation host, gated by `APP_MODULES_FEDERATION_ENABLED`,\nand skipped when\n`APP_MODULES_FEDERATION_REMOTES` is set — that list wins in the loader\nanyway. It goes out\nalongside the other boot queries, so it adds no serial round trip; a\nfailure degrades to \"no\n  plugins\" and is budgeted at 2s.\n- It carries `SUPPRESS_ERROR_NOTIFICATIONS_CONTEXT`: nothing on screen\nbelongs to it, and on a\nbackend that does not know the field the global handler would broadcast\na generic error toast to\n  every open tab for a feature the visitor cannot see.\n- It is deliberately **not** part of `InitializeApplication`.\n`store.plugins` needs x-api 3.1016.0\nand a single unknown field fails the whole GraphQL document, which would\ntake `settings.modules`\nwith it: `apply-gates-link` would then strip every `@gate(module:)`\nfield (branding silently\nreverts to defaults), the promotion-coupons route would 404, and\n`notifyOutdatedModules` — the one\ndiagnostic that names the real cause — would never fire. The document is\nstatic, so that would\n  happen with `APP_MODULES_FEDERATION_ENABLED` off as well.\n\n### Entry, expose key, permission, stylesheets\n\n- Platform descriptors point at `remoteEntry.js`; the contract gate\nneeds the MF manifest beside it,\nso the last path segment is rewritten to `mf-manifest.json` and\ncache-busted with the platform''s\nown `?v={hash}`. A plugin shipping no manifest stays unverifiable and is\nskipped. A platform entry\nmust be same-origin and http(s) *after* the rewrite — `blob:` shares\nthis origin and has an opaque\npath, which would make the rewrite a no-op and leave MF script-loading\nthe entry as code.\n- The expose key comes from the descriptor (`./Module` is the platform\ndefault) instead of being\n  hardcoded to the scaffold''s `./plugin`.\n- Permission is evaluated host-side before any fetch: the platform\nserves one cached list to every\ncaller and does not filter per user. No permission check available +\ndeclared permission ⇒ skipped.\nThis is a UX and latency filter, not an authorization boundary — the\nbundle is fetched by an\ninjected `<script>` with no credentials, so each plugin''s data access\nmust be authorized on its own.\n- `contentFiles` of type `style` are injected once each, after the\nplugin has loaded and before its\n`init()` runs: a timeout does not cancel `init()`, so withholding the\nsheets would leave a live\npage unstyled. A content file of any other kind — or of no declared kind\n— is logged, not dropped\n  in silence. Not wrapped in a cascade layer; see VCST-5760.\n- The env map wins when set, so a plugin author''s local remote is never\nreplaced by what the backend\n  serves.\n\n### Loader hardening\n\n- Remote names are validated (`/^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*$/`, both\ndiscovery paths). MF resolves a\n`loadRemote` id by **prefix**, so with remotes `a` and `a/plugin` the\nrequest meant for the second\nmatches the first and is served out of *its* bundle — one plugin''s code\nnever runs while both are\n  reported loaded. Exact-name dedup cannot see that, here or in MF.\n- Duplicate remote names: first wins, the rest are skipped loudly. A\nname is claimed only after the\ndescriptor passes validation, so a plugin about to be skipped cannot\nblock a working one.\n- A non-`script` `entry.type`, a non-string field anywhere in the\nprojection, and a non-array plugin\nlist each cost one plugin instead of throwing out of the batch. A\ndescriptor with neither `id` nor\nremote name is reported by its position, so nothing is dropped without a\ntrace.\n- `init()` is called **on** the module, so `{ services, init() {\nthis.services } }` — the natural\nshape of the platform''s default `./Module` expose — keeps its receiver.\nA module exposing no\n  `init()` counts as loaded with a warning: its module scope did run.\n- Per-phase budgets: manifest 2s, load 3s, init 3s, discovery 2s, under\na 12s boot backstop. Three\nof those are **reductions** from `dev` (manifest 3s, load 5s, backstop\n20s): the invariant only\nasks that the backstop clear discovery + manifest + 2×load, so the\ntighter numbers keep the same\n2s of headroom for the unbudgeted loader-chunk fetch while cutting\nworst-case blank screen from\n20s to 12s. The cost is that a plugin whose `init()` legitimately runs\nlonger than 3s now reports\n`failed`; 5s would need a 16s backstop. The loader chunk''s own fetch\nstays unbudgeted — bounding\n  it is what the backstop is for.\n- Route guard: for the whole load-and-init phase `addRoute` and\n`removeRoute` refuse a claim on a\nname the host already owns. Both `addRoute` overloads are covered,\ndispatched the way vue-router\ndispatches them (by predicate, not argument count), plus every named\nentry in `children`, since\nvue-router treats those as root adds. `removeRoute` is wrapped in the\nsame window because\nremove-then-add would otherwise leave the name free by the time the add\nis checked. One guard\ncovers the whole phase, and the loader starts only after every host\nplugin has installed, so a\n  host call is never refused in a plugin''s place.\n- No `{ force: true }` on `registerRemotes`: re-registering a known name\nis already a no-op in MF\n2.8.0, while `force` calls `removeRemote` first, so a second boot would\nre-run the plugin''s module\n  scope and call `init()` twice.\n- The manifest **response** is re-checked for origin, per discovery\nsource — same-origin for a\nplatform entry, https (or loopback http) for an env one — because\n`fetch` follows redirects.\n\n### Local dev and scaffolding\n\n- `^/modules/.*/plugins/vc-frontend/` is proxied to `APP_BACKEND_URL` in\ndev and preview, so the\ndiscovery path is exercisable without a deployed host. Scoped to the\nplugin folder, not all of\n  `/modules`.\n- `create:plugin` now writes `public/plugin.json` (Vite copies it into\n`dist/`). Without a descriptor\nthe platform assumes its own defaults — remote name = the .NET module\nid, expose `./Module` — and\nthe host would `loadRemote` a key the generated plugin does not export.\n\n### Deferred, with tickets\n\n- **VCST-5761** — let a plugin declare its routes in `plugin.json`, so\nthe host can register\n  placeholders and stop gating `app.mount()` on this loader.\n- **VCST-5762** — extension-registry precedence; needs a facade\nsignature change and a contract rebuild.\n- **VCST-5760** — plugin CSS containment through one host-declared\ncascade layer order. Wrapping only\nthe plugin''s sheet was tried and reverted: unlayered beats layered, so\nthe plugin would lose to all\n  host CSS. Measured regression surface and the rejected alternatives:\n\n`client-app/modules/federated/specs/2026-08-21-plugin-css-cascade-layers.md`.\n- Artifact integrity, the per-plugin kill switch, route authorization\nand the ingress CSP stay in\n`TODO.md`. The `?v={hash}` cache-buster reaches the manifest URL, not\nthe `remoteEntry.js` it\npoints at; the clean fix is a `Cache-Control` on the platform''s static\nfile middleware.\n\n### Docs\n\n- `README.md` — the security model no longer advertises a build-time\nremote list as an enforced\nproperty. It now states what is enforced (same-origin platform entries,\nhttps-or-loopback env\nentries, both re-checked after redirects) and what is not (no origin\nallowlist for env remotes; a\nsame-origin manifest may still declare chunk URLs elsewhere), plus the\nbudgets and the route\n  guard''s limits.\n- `HOWTO.md` — leads with the backend-module path and explains the\n`plugin.json` the scaffolder\nemits (the scaffold exposes `./plugin`, the platform defaults to\n`./Module`).\n- `TODO.md` — artifact integrity closed as deliberately not done, with\nthe reasons\n(hostile code arrives on the first fetch anyway; MF injects\n`remoteEntry.js` as a `<script>`, so\nthe executed bytes are never ours to hash, and `entry.hash` is a\ncache-buster, not an SRI digest).\n- `specs/2026-07-06-discovery-hosting-decision.md` — the discovery half\nis marked superseded.\n\n### Generated files\n\n`dev` is merged, and both generated GraphQL type files are regenerated\nagainst **vcptcore-dev**:\n`CustomerCartStatisticsPeriod.lastCartDate`, which `dev` removed in\n#2437, is gone, and\n`modules/sales-rep/api/graphql/types.ts` is byte-identical to `dev`''s.\nvcst-qa cannot generate the\nsales-rep module — its schema lacks the document queries added in #2439.\nThree environment deltas\nremain: `CartType.loyaltyPoints` is absent on that environment (no\ndocument selects it, and the other\nhits are untouched module files plus `Product.loyaltyPoints` in the\ncontract); one field description\ncarries older wording; and vcptcore-dev **adds**\n`SalesRepDocument{,Category,Connection,Edge}`,\n`Query.salesRepDocument{,Categories,s}` and their `*Args` — 86 of the 90\nadded lines, absent from\n`dev`, and reversed again by regenerating on vcst-qa.\n\nThe core contract was already stale on `dev` — the `sharedList`\nextension point and its\nwishlist-sharing types were added without a rebuild, and\n`validate:core-types` runs in no workflow —\nso it is rebuilt here. The build''s own automation bumps `CORE_VERSION`\n1.2.0 → 1.3.0 for the changed\ncontract; plugins built against `^1.2.0` keep running.\n\n### Verified\n\n- 2447 tests in 159 files; `vue-tsc --build --force` clean; eslint on\nthe touched files: 0 errors,\n23 warnings (10 `sonarjs/no-redundant-optional` on `IPlatformPlugin`,\nwhich mirrors codegen''s\n`Maybe<T>` on purpose, and a `sonarjs/null-dereference` false positive).\n`validate:core-types` is\nred on a local checkout, but the only differing line is the property\norder of `VcButton`''s\ninferred defaults, byte-identical at the merge base — a vue-tsc\nartefact, not this PR.\n  `boot-order.test.ts` executes the real `app-runner` against mocked\ncollaborators and pins the order the calls actually happen in: theme\ncontext and user before the\nloader, the router installed only after it, the plugin-list query issued\nbefore the page context is\nawaited, nothing issued when the flag is off or the env override is set,\nand the loader started\n  after the host''s route-mutating plugin.\n- Live against vcst-qa: `store.plugins(appId: \"vc-frontend\")` answers\nthrough the new query and\nreturns `[]` — no module there ships a storefront plugin yet. The dev\nproxy was verified end to\nend: a request to\n`/modules/$(VirtoCommerce.SalesRep)/plugins/vc-frontend/mf-manifest.json`\nreaches\nthe platform (HTTP 404, empty body), while\n`/modules/$(X)/Content/logo.png` and any other path\nstill get Vite''s SPA fallback — which is the old failure mode, since\nthat HTML is what the contract\n  gate used to try to parse as JSON.\n- Not exercised: a real platform-served plugin load. That needs a module\non the target environment\n  shipping `plugins/vc-frontend/`; no environment has one.\n\n### Known repo-state issues found alongside, not fixed here\n\n`validate:core-types` runs in no PR workflow while a comment claims it\ndoes, the breaking-change\ndetector diffs export names only, `federation.mjs` ships in the\nversioned tarball but is outside the\nchange detection, and the production logger noops every level including\n`error`.\n\n## References\n### QA-test:\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5159\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.58.0-pr-2445-d7c2-d7c2c9c6.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoXnXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJagQAHJJEkCfd+QHfqfpdo2Ji3c/\nZ/P/rMF26Tk7xGwtjDz5yg40fXdg4xqi22UI2nCIQvua4151BJ15KJ3fQ3TqO2jC\neDEYMSwAb78ixp4nJDKiDUXLNB+gUbNwstduVdmSxuGSglN7oprDWtSANIAUQ66l\nRKJQuPZ