ts":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/17ad3e6f66a6fb4a5cf9514e47e905ed9df4b615","sha":"17ad3e6f66a6fb4a5cf9514e47e905ed9df4b615","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/17ad3e6f66a6fb4a5cf9514e47e905ed9df4b615"}],"sha":"36f99c1a86f250db41cc8febd71e5ac8abe4e0dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/36f99c1a86f250db41cc8febd71e5ac8abe4e0dc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49168917?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vas11yev1work","id":49168917,"login":"vas11yev1work","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5MTY4OTE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vas11yev1work","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/17ad3e6f66a6fb4a5cf9514e47e905ed9df4b615/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T10:58:56Z","email":"49168917+vas11yev1work@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Anatolii Vasilev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T10:58:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VCST-5735): Compare products (#2452)\n\n## Description\n\nRedesigns the Compare products page (VCST-5735) from a single flat\nproduct list into a category-grouped comparison table.\n\n**What''s new:**\n- **Category tabs** — products are grouped into per-category tabs\ninstead of one mixed list, so rows no longer fill up with dashes from\ncomparing unrelated product types.\n- **Transposed comparison table** (`CompareTable`) — products as\ncolumns, attributes as rows, with a sticky header that collapses into a\ncompact product-card strip on scroll.\n- **\"All / Differences\" toggle** — hides rows that are identical across\nevery product in view; differing rows are marked.\n- **Row pinning** — any row can be pinned to stay visible above the\nfold, including under the Differences filter.\n- **Add to cart directly from the table** for plain (non-configurable)\nproducts, without leaving the page.\n- Tooltips on domain-specific fields (price per unit, MOQ, ...),\nmobile-specific layout, auto-hidden empty rows, boolean-as-icon\nrendering.\n\n**Under the hood:**\n- `useCompareProducts` (list/storage state) and `useCompareProductsPage`\n(row/tab derivation) were rewritten around a single\n`ICompareProductEntry[]` localStorage shape, replacing the old split\n\"regular ids\" + \"configured products\" storage.\n- New composables: `useCompareAddToCart`, `useCompareTableRowPins`.\n- `product-card-compare.vue` was removed; its logic is now split between\n`CompareTable`''s compact/full product header and the row-building logic\nin `useCompareProductsPage`.\n- Test coverage added for all of the above (composables, utilities, and\nthe page itself).\n\n### Before\n<img width=\"1624\" height=\"996\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d8162196-af77-46c8-9740-3f010bd0c60f\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1624\" height=\"996\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/eb6684d7-0141-48d6-9706-777a49e03ce8\"\n/>\n\n### After\n<img width=\"1624\" height=\"996\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f2e58626-5f27-436c-9b67-fb0169bef13e\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1624\" height=\"996\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3fc79149-f342-4fe5-8340-122ac4bfa629\"\n/>\n\n## Breaking changes for forks\n\n**`@/core/constants`**\n\n| Removed | Replacement |\n|---|---|\n| `PRODUCT_COMPARE_LIST_IDS_LOCAL_STORAGE` |\n`COMPARE_PRODUCTS_LOCAL_STORAGE` — single key backing the new unified\n`ICompareProductEntry[]` storage shape |\n| `CONFIG_PRODUCTS_TO_COMPARE_LOCAL_STORAGE` |\n`COMPARE_PRODUCTS_LOCAL_STORAGE` (same) |\n\n**`@/shared/catalog`, `@/shared/catalog/components`**\n\n| Removed | Replacement |\n|---|---|\n| `ProductCardCompare` (`product-card-compare.vue`) | No single\nreplacement — split between `CompareTable`''s compact/full product header\nand the row-building logic in `useCompareProductsPage` |\n\n**`@/shared/compare`**\n\n| Removed | Replacement |\n|---|---|\n| `IConfigProductToCompare` (type) | `ICompareProductEntry` — `{\nproductId, categoryKey, localId?, configurationSectionInput?,\nproperties? }` |\n\n**`useCompareProducts()`**\n\n| Removed | Replacement |\n|---|---|\n| `productsIds` | `products` (`ICompareProductEntry[]`) — the old split\nbetween plain ids and configured products is gone; it''s one list now |\n| `configProductsToCompare` | `products` (same) |\n\n**`useCompareProductsPage()`**\n\n| Removed | Replacement |\n|---|---|\n| `hasProducts` | Derive from `useCompareProducts().products.length ===\n0` (how the page''s own empty state works now) |\n| `productsCount` | `selectedCategoryCount` — **not a direct\nequivalent**: scoped to the currently selected category tab, not a total\nacross everything (categories are new in this PR) |\n| `productsToShow` | `selectedCategoryProducts` (also scoped per\ncategory) |\n| `properties` | `tableRows` |\n| `propertiesDiffs` | Folded into `tableRows`: each row is `{ key,\nlabel, kind, values, differs, ... }` |\n| `showOnlyDifferences` | No longer exposed here — the All/Differences\ntoggle is now internal state inside `CompareTable` |\n| `handleRemoveFromCompareList` | Call\n`useCompareProducts().removeFromCompareList` directly |\n| `getConfigurationId` | No longer needed — every `ICompareProductEntry`\ncarries its own `localId` directly instead of deriving one by index |\n| `selectItemEvent` | Unchanged — the one member that survives by name |\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5735\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.57.0-pr-2452-8430-84305194.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Maiia Diachkovskaia <mayapavlovna@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"2c7d08883f2c832ff4e35779e390774318fd4ac9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/2c7d08883f2c832ff4e35779e390774318fd4ac9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/17ad3e6f66a6fb4a5cf9514e47e905ed9df4b615","verification":{"payload":"tree 2c7d08883f2c832ff4e35779e390774318fd4ac9\nparent 261432a07b89c9f725d19cef2195ead4dff57e6d\nauthor Anatolii Vasilev <49168917+vas11yev1work@users.noreply.github.com> 1788778736 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788778736 +0200\n\nfeat(VCST-5735): Compare products (#2452)\n\n## Description\n\nRedesigns the Compare products page (VCST-5735) from a single flat\nproduct list into a category-grouped comparison table.\n\n**What''s new:**\n- **Category tabs** — products are grouped into per-category tabs\ninstead of one mixed list, so rows no longer fill up with dashes from\ncomparing unrelated product types.\n- **Transposed comparison table** (`CompareTable`) — products as\ncolumns, attributes as rows, with a sticky header that collapses into a\ncompact product-card strip on scroll.\n- **\"All / Differences\" toggle** — hides rows that are identical across\nevery product in view; differing rows are marked.\n- **Row pinning** — any row can be pinned to stay visible above the\nfold, including under the Differences filter.\n- **Add to cart directly from the table** for plain (non-configurable)\nproducts, without leaving the page.\n- Tooltips on domain-specific fields (price per unit, MOQ, ...),\nmobile-specific layout, auto-hidden empty rows, boolean-as-icon\nrendering.\n\n**Under the hood:**\n- `useCompareProducts` (list/storage state) and `useCompareProductsPage`\n(row/tab derivation) were rewritten around a single\n`ICompareProductEntry[]` localStorage shape, replacing the old split\n\"regular ids\" + \"configured products\" storage.\n- New composables: `useCompareAddToCart`, `useCompareTableRowPins`.\n- `product-card-compare.vue` was removed; its logic is now split between\n`CompareTable`''s compact/full product header and the row-building logic\nin `useCompareProductsPage`.\n- Test coverage added for all of the above (composables, utilities, and\nthe page itself).\n\n### Before\n<img width=\"1624\" height=\"996\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d8162196-af77-46c8-9740-3f010bd0c60f\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1624\" height=\"996\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/eb6684d7-0141-48d6-9706-777a49e03ce8\"\n/>\n\n### After\n<img width=\"1624\" height=\"996\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f2e58626-5f27-436c-9b67-fb0169bef13e\"\n/>\n<img width=\"1624\" height=\"996\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3fc79149-f342-4fe5-8340-122ac4bfa629\"\n/>\n\n## Breaking changes for forks\n\n**`@/core/constants`**\n\n| Removed | Replacement |\n|---|---|\n| `PRODUCT_COMPARE_LIST_IDS_LOCAL_STORAGE` |\n`COMPARE_PRODUCTS_LOCAL_STORAGE` — single key backing the new unified\n`ICompareProductEntry[]` storage shape |\n| `CONFIG_PRODUCTS_TO_COMPARE_LOCAL_STORAGE` |\n`COMPARE_PRODUCTS_LOCAL_STORAGE` (same) |\n\n**`@/shared/catalog`, `@/shared/catalog/components`**\n\n| Removed | Replacement |\n|---|---|\n| `ProductCardCompare` (`product-card-compare.vue`) | No single\nreplacement — split between `CompareTable`''s compact/full product header\nand the row-building logic in `useCompareProductsPage` |\n\n**`@/shared/compare`**\n\n| Removed | Replacement |\n|---|---|\n| `IConfigProductToCompare` (type) | `ICompareProductEntry` — `{\nproductId, categoryKey, localId?, configurationSectionInput?,\nproperties? }` |\n\n**`useCompareProducts()`**\n\n| Removed | Replacement |\n|---|---|\n| `productsIds` | `products` (`ICompareProductEntry[]`) — the old split\nbetween plain ids and configured products is gone; it''s one list now |\n| `configProductsToCompare` | `products` (same) |\n\n**`useCompareProductsPage()`**\n\n| Removed | Replacement |\n|---|---|\n| `hasProducts` | Derive from `useCompareProducts().products.length ===\n0` (how the page''s own empty state works now) |\n| `productsCount` | `selectedCategoryCount` — **not a direct\nequivalent**: scoped to the currently selected category tab, not a total\nacross everything (categories are new in this PR) |\n| `productsToShow` | `selectedCategoryProducts` (also scoped per\ncategory) |\n| `properties` | `tableRows` |\n| `propertiesDiffs` | Folded into `tableRows`: each row is `{ key,\nlabel, kind, values, differs, ... }` |\n| `showOnlyDifferences` | No longer exposed here — the All/Differences\ntoggle is now internal state inside `CompareTable` |\n| `handleRemoveFromCompareList` | Call\n`useCompareProducts().removeFromCompareList` directly |\n| `getConfigurationId` | No longer needed — every `ICompareProductEntry`\ncarries its own `localId` directly instead of deriving one by index |\n| `selectItemEvent` | Unchanged — the one member that survives by name |\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5735\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.57.0-pr-2452-8430-84305194.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Maiia Diachkovskaia <mayapavlovna@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnpjwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANX4QALGxmQoJiCsCEUgqd04baUq5\nQjQJtTPYthJZ/4FauJb/4Py/fguaPTt2+RkvJpXeQoCCJDqkocssb9DR9P0xoLHn\no1xqE+2VCVgaiL+vdQm+hVfShWZHEHxJ896WO4cot46uKLFKL4DRUss+OJcBxdxe\nu57oUVJtIAtZcVDeWz8OapSqTH3ACTrg2vUHoFwmHhySU+xFgE3vnA4kinDd+YK5\nT1M9hP+iU9Mmq2SZpP1issLIhrnu53qnbXXvX+Ika9aNmI/iHn351M7qkGN5JOrS\n3MaMMbRhIlHuKJOvj2V7U9Vrtt9khLJMa3wVv8yNZ3fal0Ex5L3nWtU2ud7UkCf7\nKgNvi0/3o6Acck7ZWZwXRgUOI+Z97T5QShzVSEIY/0ImRTYRjgBuA7rH3j/808yK\n3UxvzszGlyYi0k0nXaWqEShmEpI8PgasMyezEFGAWV9cKGnugc6fSSh2+XZproEA\nCH4Y/yjONwpDDrDv9R+JEYEM+kjWicdz7FxPVNa/M4fGIHNzWI2+jpLLzAbfTz/a\n9B1Lg8N8EfVo5RHZ8HjV7n3UGTa6TYENp6NGdNCIDlQGmXphMjfnuqMovnkcuwEi\ns1r4rfWzLU1h6jyTK1+aTKfA7maIKcs1hlkMp4LlAy6WbDNDSqJrbuSNciFqpqVd\n4zhCMSp9kpIeauysCKTu\n=zG9P\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T10:58:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/17ad3e6f66a6fb4a5cf9514e47e905ed9df4b615","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDE3YWQzZTZmNjZhNmZiNGE1Y2Y5NTE0ZTQ3ZTkwNWVkOWRmNGI2MTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/261432a07b89c9f725d19cef2195ead4dff57e6d","sha":"261432a07b89c9f725d19cef2195ead4dff57e6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/261432a07b89c9f725d19cef2195ead4dff57e6d"}],"sha":"17ad3e6f66a6fb4a5cf9514e47e905ed9df4b615","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/17ad3e6f66a6fb4a5cf9514e47e905ed9df4b615"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18286430?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ivan-kalachikov","id":18286430,"login":"ivan-kalachikov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Mjg2NDMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/261432a07b89c9f725d19cef2195ead4dff57e6d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T17:32:15Z","email":"ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com","name":"Ivan Kalachikov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T17:32:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VCST-5733): all customer orders (#2444)\n\n## Description\n\nGives Sales Reps their customers'' **complete order history** inside the\nhub, instead of sending them to the\nbuyer-facing `/account/orders`. Backed by the new\n`salesRepCustomerOrders` / `salesRepCustomerOrder` queries,\nso the list is no longer limited to orders the rep personally placed.\n\nBackend PR: https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-module-sales-rep/pull/14\n\n### Routes\n\n| Route | Shows |\n|---|---|\n| `/company/customer-orders` | Every order of every customer the rep\nserves, with a **Customer** column and customer filter |\n| `/company/my-customers/:organizationId/orders` | The same list scoped\nto one customer. Breadcrumbs `Account / Sales Rep hub / My customers /\n{customer} / Orders` |\n| `/company/my-customers/:organizationId/orders/:orderId` | One order,\n**read-only** — Print is the only action |\n\nOne component serves both list routes; the customer column and filter\nappear only where more than one\ncustomer is in scope.\n\n### Behaviour\n\n- **List** — paging (`first` + offset-as-cursor `after`), keyword search\ncommitted on Enter or the search\n  button, and column sorting on Date and Total, each reversible.\n- **Filters panel** — order status (multi-select, with per-status\ncounts) and created-date (presets or custom\nrange with validation). The status and customer options come back with\nthe page as facets, so every option\n  offered has orders behind it and its count follows the other filters.\n- **Opening an order** — an order the **rep placed** opens on the buyer\npage `/account/orders/:orderId`, where\nthe actions they are entitled to (Pay now, Reorder) still work.\n**Everyone else''s** opens read-only in the\nhub. A rep can therefore see and print a colleague''s order but never act\non it.\n- **Dashboard** — the widget is renamed **\"My recent orders\"** (all 13\nlocales) to make explicit that it, and\nthe statistics beside it, remain scoped to orders the rep placed. Its\n\"All orders\" link now opens\n  `/company/customer-orders`.\n\n### Notable changes to shared code\n\n- `shared/account/composables/useOrderView.ts` — **new**. The\norder-derived state (item splits, currency\ngrouping, first shipment and payment, their addresses) lifted out of\n`useUserOrder`, which now delegates to\n  it, so the same order renders identically whichever endpoint read it.\n- `scripts/graphql-codegen/generator.ts` — the SalesRep entry gained\n`requiredCommonFragments`; codegen does\nnot follow `#import` outside a module''s own `apiPath`, and the read-only\norder page reuses the storefront''s\n  `fullOrderFields`.\n\n### Known limitations\n\n- The hub order page duplicates most of\n`pages/account/order-details.vue`''s template. Extracting a shared\n`OrderDetailsView` component is deferred; until then a BOPIS order''s\npickup-point action is missing from the\n  hub page.\n- The filters panel carries its own date presets rather than reusing\n`shared/account/components/date-filter-select.vue` — the shared presets\nare calendar-aligned and these are a\nrolling window, so adopting it is a deliberate behaviour change rather\nthan a refactor.\n\n### Screenshots\n<img width=\"1510\" height=\"883\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ea8a05f8-7736-4eac-b64e-b1bc98365202\"\n/>\n\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5733\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.57.0-pr-2444-d5ba-d5ba9b69.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: yuskithedeveloper <yuskianywhere@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: yuskithedeveloper <126832118+yuskithedeveloper@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"1cfcb18e77d1d276b5e0e9245507273fe1db2883","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/1cfcb18e77d1d276b5e0e9245507273fe1db2883"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/261432a07b89c9f725d19cef2195ead4dff57e6d","verification":{"payload":"tree 1cfcb18e77d1d276b5e0e9245507273fe1db2883\nparent b61e9398a331b650c345b33bc6736e4fa7c477da\nauthor Ivan Kalachikov <ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com> 1788543135 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788543135 -0500\n\nfeat(VCST-5733): all customer orders (#2444)\n\n## Description\n\nGives Sales Reps their customers'' **complete order history** inside the\nhub, instead of sending them to the\nbuyer-facing `/account/orders`. Backed by the new\n`salesRepCustomerOrders` / `salesRepCustomerOrder` queries,\nso the list is no longer limited to orders the rep personally placed.\n\nBackend PR: https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-module-sales-rep/pull/14\n\n### Routes\n\n| Route | Shows |\n|---|---|\n| `/company/customer-orders` | Every order of every customer the rep\nserves, with a **Customer** column and customer filter |\n| `/company/my-customers/:organizationId/orders` | The same list scoped\nto one customer. Breadcrumbs `Account / Sales Rep hub / My customers /\n{customer} / Orders` |\n| `/company/my-customers/:organizationId/orders/:orderId` | One order,\n**read-only** — Print is the only action |\n\nOne component serves both list routes; the customer column and filter\nappear only where more than one\ncustomer is in scope.\n\n### Behaviour\n\n- **List** — paging (`first` + offset-as-cursor `after`), keyword search\ncommitted on Enter or the search\n  button, and column sorting on Date and Total, each reversible.\n- **Filters panel** — order status (multi-select, with per-status\ncounts) and created-date (presets or custom\nrange with validation). The status and customer options come back with\nthe page as facets, so every option\n  offered has orders behind it and its count follows the other filters.\n- **Opening an order** — an order the **rep placed** opens on the buyer\npage `/account/orders/:orderId`, where\nthe actions they are entitled to (Pay now, Reorder) still work.\n**Everyone else''s** opens read-only in the\nhub. A rep can therefore see and print a colleague''s order but never act\non it.\n- **Dashboard** — the widget is renamed **\"My recent orders\"** (all 13\nlocales) to make explicit that it, and\nthe statistics beside it, remain scoped to orders the rep placed. Its\n\"All orders\" link now opens\n  `/company/customer-orders`.\n\n### Notable changes to shared code\n\n- `shared/account/composables/useOrderView.ts` — **new**. The\norder-derived state (item splits, currency\ngrouping, first shipment and payment, their addresses) lifted out of\n`useUserOrder`, which now delegates to\n  it, so the same order renders identically whichever endpoint read it.\n- `scripts/graphql-codegen/generator.ts` — the SalesRep entry gained\n`requiredCommonFragments`; codegen does\nnot follow `#import` outside a module''s own `apiPath`, and the read-only\norder page reuses the storefront''s\n  `fullOrderFields`.\n\n### Known limitations\n\n- The hub order page duplicates most of\n`pages/account/order-details.vue`''s template. Extracting a shared\n`OrderDetailsView` component is deferred; until then a BOPIS order''s\npickup-point action is missing from the\n  hub page.\n- The filters panel carries its own date presets rather than reusing\n`shared/account/components/date-filter-select.vue` — the shared presets\nare calendar-aligned and these are a\nrolling window, so adopting it is a deliberate behaviour change rather\nthan a refactor.\n\n### Screenshots\n<img width=\"1510\" height=\"883\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ea8a05f8-7736-4eac-b64e-b1bc98365202\"\n/>\n\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5733\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.57.0-pr-2444-d5ba-d5ba9b69.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-