ontend/commit/71d20ea97b807579027fe5dbff31118f038398f5","sha":"71d20ea97b807579027fe5dbff31118f038398f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/71d20ea97b807579027fe5dbff31118f038398f5"}],"sha":"c4046f560a35fe0b9f260f2ef353129792b45c98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/c4046f560a35fe0b9f260f2ef353129792b45c98"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18286430?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ivan-kalachikov","id":18286430,"login":"ivan-kalachikov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Mjg2NDMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/71d20ea97b807579027fe5dbff31118f038398f5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T15:54:00Z","email":"ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com","name":"Ivan Kalachikov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T15:54:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VCST-5750): add SSO support to the login on behalf page (#2448)\n\n## Description\n\nThe login on behalf page (`/account/impersonate/:userId`) only offered\nusername/password verification, so an operator of a store that\nauthenticates through identity providers had no way to start an\nimpersonation session.\n\nIdentity providers now render on that page, with the same layout the\nsign-in page uses:\n\n- **Password + providers** — the verification form stays in place, the\nproviders are shown next to it behind the `Or` divider.\n- **Providers only** — the form is hidden and the providers are rendered\nin the content column.\n- The providers return to the impersonation URL (`returnUrl`), where the\nalready existing authenticated flow picks the session up and starts the\nimpersonation automatically. No backend change is involved: the\n`impersonate` grant is requested with the operator''s token, exactly as\nfor an operator who was already signed in.\n\nParts shared by the sign-in and the impersonate pages:\n\n- `useIdentityProviders()` — the enabled-providers logic.\n- `identity-providers.vue` — the provider buttons.\n- `sign-in-divider.vue` — the `Or` divider, which each page composes\nwith the providers.\n- `useIdentityProvider()` takes the return URL as a required input; the\nprovider components pass it down as a prop.\n- `useReturnUrl()` resolves that URL — the requested page, then the\nstore default — and the `openReturnUrl` handler reads it from there too.\n\nThe heading of the verification step lives on the page rather than in\n`impersonate-form.vue`, so it is also shown when the store has no\npassword authentication — the same split the sign-in page already has.\n\n`openReturnUrl` navigates through `toSameOriginPath`, the guard\n`useImpersonate` already applies. A `returnUrl` of the same host but a\ndifferent origin (other port or scheme) used to be followed and now\nfalls back to the home page. Nothing in the app produces such a value —\nthe router guard and the callback both pass paths.\n\n`getReturnUrlValue` returns `null` for a `returnUrl` that does not\nparse, the same as for one that points to another host: the value falls\nthrough to the next key and then to the default. It threw a `TypeError`\nbefore, on the sign-in page render, the router guard, the push-message\npage and the `openReturnUrl` handler.\n\nThe provider components are memoized with `useMemoize`. A component\nwhose chunk fails to load is no longer dropped from the cache: a\nprovider this theme does not ship never loads, and a chunk that fails to\nfetch is handled by the `vite:preloadError` recovery.\n\nTests cover the providers logic, the return URL resolution, the provider\nprop plumbing and both pages.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5750\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.57.0-pr-2448-243a-243a0c42.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Elena Kutasina <kutasina.elena@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"13cf85d993243062fb6561e5e5be71b3205f6e6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/13cf85d993243062fb6561e5e5be71b3205f6e6c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/71d20ea97b807579027fe5dbff31118f038398f5","verification":{"payload":"tree 13cf85d993243062fb6561e5e5be71b3205f6e6c\nparent 60f8edff0876005107b7f3d11a056f08b49bb1f3\nauthor Ivan Kalachikov <ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com> 1788450840 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788450840 +0200\n\nfeat(VCST-5750): add SSO support to the login on behalf page (#2448)\n\n## Description\n\nThe login on behalf page (`/account/impersonate/:userId`) only offered\nusername/password verification, so an operator of a store that\nauthenticates through identity providers had no way to start an\nimpersonation session.\n\nIdentity providers now render on that page, with the same layout the\nsign-in page uses:\n\n- **Password + providers** — the verification form stays in place, the\nproviders are shown next to it behind the `Or` divider.\n- **Providers only** — the form is hidden and the providers are rendered\nin the content column.\n- The providers return to the impersonation URL (`returnUrl`), where the\nalready existing authenticated flow picks the session up and starts the\nimpersonation automatically. No backend change is involved: the\n`impersonate` grant is requested with the operator''s token, exactly as\nfor an operator who was already signed in.\n\nParts shared by the sign-in and the impersonate pages:\n\n- `useIdentityProviders()` — the enabled-providers logic.\n- `identity-providers.vue` — the provider buttons.\n- `sign-in-divider.vue` — the `Or` divider, which each page composes\nwith the providers.\n- `useIdentityProvider()` takes the return URL as a required input; the\nprovider components pass it down as a prop.\n- `useReturnUrl()` resolves that URL — the requested page, then the\nstore default — and the `openReturnUrl` handler reads it from there too.\n\nThe heading of the verification step lives on the page rather than in\n`impersonate-form.vue`, so it is also shown when the store has no\npassword authentication — the same split the sign-in page already has.\n\n`openReturnUrl` navigates through `toSameOriginPath`, the guard\n`useImpersonate` already applies. A `returnUrl` of the same host but a\ndifferent origin (other port or scheme) used to be followed and now\nfalls back to the home page. Nothing in the app produces such a value —\nthe router guard and the callback both pass paths.\n\n`getReturnUrlValue` returns `null` for a `returnUrl` that does not\nparse, the same as for one that points to another host: the value falls\nthrough to the next key and then to the default. It threw a `TypeError`\nbefore, on the sign-in page render, the router guard, the push-message\npage and the `openReturnUrl` handler.\n\nThe provider components are memoized with `useMemoize`. A component\nwhose chunk fails to load is no longer dropped from the cache: a\nprovider this theme does not ship never loads, and a chunk that fails to\nfetch is handled by the `vite:preloadError` recovery.\n\nTests cover the providers logic, the return URL resolution, the provider\nprop plumbing and both pages.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5750\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.57.0-pr-2448-243a-243a0c42.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Elena Kutasina <kutasina.elena@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmZgYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwuMQAF5rLmCVfdl2RrC1bveThiqf\nPOwXYcNalwLfug22weeWh4FqlIEpGJjhVcaZcfvBhLEA0zZk0XYpiean1ewPa7Pn\ndFTpVHkzj9yIuDUHm1179nTQkgM7/raDvT2SRYj6wBhTmn4dMF5olau5cM1Gd0qR\nOP4eKLCpF5hwlRof4qOhuk+ruLQEGjUS8QY3FYNmmiV+qwdTtCNYiDuFuacA5FLT\nESpSGsLrZ3fgqKQsU7ouLK4ZU7unBlq/rlUAUQfeLKlqMPhIwRv3nq4n92rvZups\nUGGBYXd71uyLmNLF2gZFzaVbeAkvHa6Rf1YwLypaWFHfyRTN2wXQFyGX011y4tOg\nlA5Yz7XqM83Ln9k9zhBC3ti7LX89taPfBtP/fK2jH4UO/ZCUoKI35MdhKzgEe5ha\nlRF+4KLVEFxub2bvl0CAAbmXC1LTj9MMcdjjR+1SgPJRwhuonEhjyNl5+28D+Ctm\nOjki7f0WSG5B4AR6IwdbijbcvAF0OCsMApQyY6CqCHz88gL90VcXADegtXtgLgvI\n2WCVW9Q7f4nqd3MU+LUx8ZgMqWeTP7FmE/sReMQOx/XTlVd6jspMjU8ZXj/9ynH2\nezXZVQbLuFpMxBBNoM27GhDDycq+buCYj6Oj/1ngoUznoNONQ9shyN0/yj/9BGwP\nyhC+ZuLdn3omg6Z4AKhj\n=36ah\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-03T15:54:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/r