b.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/60f8edff0876005107b7f3d11a056f08b49bb1f3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/330693?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilkot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilkot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilkot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilkot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/basilkot","id":330693,"login":"basilkot","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMDY5Mw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilkot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilkot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilkot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilkot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilkot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilkot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/9505580e2aff8920eab1c2b22fc0ea03f37fcc86/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:48:53Z","email":"basilkot@gmail.com","name":"Basil Kotov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:48:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VCST-5704): render page anchors and scroll to them on load (#2441)\n\nAdd an anchor setting to the shared section and block schemas so a\ncontent manager can give an item a readable link target, and render it\nas the element id in place of the generated one.\n\nScroll to the hash on the initial load: Page Builder content is parsed\nafter the route resolves, so the browser has already given up on the\nanchor by the time it exists in the DOM.\n\nThe slug rules mirror generateAnchor in the Page Builder designer, which\noffers these values in the rich text link dialog — the two sides must\nderive the same string or the links it produces would resolve to\nnothing.\n\n## Description\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\n<!-- Put link to your task in Jira here -->\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.57.0-pr-2441-a5b6-a5b6b23b.zip\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Hash scrolling and header height CSS variables affect multiple\nhigh-traffic routes; behavior is complex but covered by new unit tests.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Adds **in-page anchor links** for Page Builder blocks/sections and\nproduct template blocks: merchants can set an optional **Anchor** in\nblock/section settings; rendered DOM ids come from `getAnchorId`\n(authored slug or fallback block id), aligned with the Page Builder\ndesigner’s `generateAnchor` rules.\n> \n> Introduces **`scrollToAnchor`** and **`useAnchorScroll`** so `#hash`\nnavigation works after async content mounts (static pages, Virto page\nbuilder, product page). Scroll waits for the target, respects user\nwheel/keyboard takeover, manages focus for a11y, and cancels stale waits\non route or unmount. **VP page builder** now watches `content` instead\nof only parsing on mount so client-side navigations re-render and scroll\nat the right time.\n> \n> **Layout:** desktop and mobile headers publish\n**`--vc-app-header-height`**, and global **`scroll-padding-top`** uses\nit so anchored sections aren’t hidden under the fixed header. Product\n**description** block template is flattened so parent `:id` falls\nthrough to the visible root.\n> \n> Removes redundant `id` props from several static-content block\ncomponents now that parents set `:id` via `getAnchorId`.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\na5b6b23b262009cac53b723a88fd669dea844781. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Elena Kutasina <kutasina.elena@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"f045918ebf33d61c4f4aad452fe991fe2221c167","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/f045918ebf33d61c4f4aad452fe991fe2221c167"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/9505580e2aff8920eab1c2b22fc0ea03f37fcc86","verification":{"payload":"tree f045918ebf33d61c4f4aad452fe991fe2221c167\nparent 282eaeef04e6a2a9e7a458690c667a7cf750adf3\nauthor Basil Kotov <basilkot@gmail.com> 1788274133 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788274133 +0100\n\nfeat(VCST-5704): render page anchors and scroll to them on load (#2441)\n\nAdd an anchor setting to the shared section and block schemas so a\ncontent manager can give an item a readable link target, and render it\nas the element id in place of the generated one.\n\nScroll to the hash on the initial load: Page Builder content is parsed\nafter the route resolves, so the browser has already given up on the\nanchor by the time it exists in the DOM.\n\nThe slug rules mirror generateAnchor in the Page Builder designer, which\noffers these values in the rich text link dialog — the two sides must\nderive the same string or the links it produces would resolve to\nnothing.\n\n## Description\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\n<!-- Put link to your task in Jira here -->\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.57.0-pr-2441-a5b6-a5b6b23b.zip\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Hash scrolling and header height CSS variables affect multiple\nhigh-traffic routes; behavior is complex but covered by new unit tests.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Adds **in-page anchor links** for Page Builder blocks/sections and\nproduct template blocks: merchants can set an optional **Anchor** in\nblock/section settings; rendered DOM ids come from `getAnchorId`\n(authored slug or fallback block id), aligned with the Page Builder\ndesigner’s `generateAnchor` rules.\n> \n> Introduces **`scrollToAnchor`** and **`useAnchorScroll`** so `#hash`\nnavigation works after async content mounts (static pages, Virto page\nbuilder, product page). Scroll waits for the target, respects user\nwheel/keyboard takeover, manages focus for a11y, and cancels stale waits\non route or unmount. **VP page builder** now watches `content` instead\nof only parsing on mount so client-side navigations re-render and scroll\nat the right time.\n> \n> **Layout:** desktop and mobile headers publish\n**`--vc-app-header-height`**, and global **`scroll-padding-top`** uses\nit so anchored sections aren’t hidden under the fixed header. Product\n**description** block template is flattened so parent `:id` falls\nthrough to the visible root.\n> \n> Removes redundant `id` props from several static-content block\ncomponents now that parents set `:id` via `getAnchorId`.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\na5b6b23b262009cac53b723a88fd669dea844781. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Elena Kutasina <kutasina.elena@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqluXVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFVwQAEESdfPbhcab9cf7cOqEjVUv\nazJMHk87wwa+QdpkN/gRArvZoINlgs9vToDfq4yxQdK+denGHaEBGZWa/SOP7/S4\nbYvc2GSh1dOQY6LI7DkAof/ctWMEp2fqF8XJqYml/BDQIn0FgzCyT0IE0VGQYbNd\n8A/sn2/vqbjRviIxc+eRaOnQsn0fXwp4dF7BTzUGrZxnglyDuGxQFM1kz3EBJyX/\n+jTdZcAaBxQQNR/w0Rlav4/H4qzUe2A0sB9RNyZsyJ9aQ8o5c/5DPmOWBUTVaSWW\nj21oHWZHrYvy+PfqXGPrs6fJ32et8RvA4zQiDFlIeWoZkZginLRMYGc18A0dG+la\nAtbdmxH6FgciqbUx7bP20zb8RFlwQNbnQVGJtiyydfLY8u6j2ZJBnQ+Cb3P5gYsi\n5Sc0ikKt1qIAq9aJ0YaR2JjmrOvNf/xuE4+FRrlCS0Xgkxg0G3sgZmJ1b9JOElxJ\nywr/kG13D8j9CyRTe1q+J2FhLg0zJi0RSGsblzN9jchy+0FB1jrdhBa+cIBPHuCg\nM5NCRMmyCEFKiwGZiPgHMPeO8Mj3dsB+2Ci+ZUYu0K2w0B2UT8wh+/vl5Ctt6Pav\ntVPTM7L0fHL9VpCpxMDEzE6W1ki5LL5IUoacf+fpIfiSr5VYpXeZvbUl0mAFVVru\np6xDOudYTaSrcNuaJLDV\n=PVYL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T14:48:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/9505580e2aff8920eab1c2b22fc0ea03f37fcc86","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDk1MDU1ODBlMmFmZjg5MjBlYWIxYzJiMjJmYzBlYTAzZjM3ZmNjODY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/282eaeef04e6a2a9e7a458690c667a7cf750adf3","sha":"282eaeef04e6a2a9e7a458690c667a7cf750adf3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/282eaeef04e6a2a9e7a458690c667a7cf750adf3"}],"sha":"9505580e2aff8920eab1c2b22fc0ea03f37fcc86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/9505580e2aff8920eab1c2b22fc0ea03f37fcc86"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/279651339?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks","id":279651339,"login":"DmitryGrishinVirtoworks","node_id":"U_kgDOEKskCw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DmitryGrishinVirtoworks","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/282eaeef04e6a2a9e7a458690c667a7cf750adf3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:35:35Z","email":"Dmitry.Grishin@virtoworks.com","name":"DmitryGrishinVirtoworks"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T14:35:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VCST-5450): use configurable company roles for invite, filters, and change role (#2426)\n\n## Description\nStorefront now sources company member roles from the new\n`Customer.MembershipRolesWhitelist` store setting instead of a hardcoded\nrole list, for the invite, change-role, and member-filter UIs.\n\n## What was added\n- **New composable `useCompanyMemberRoles`**: reads the public module\nsetting and maps configured role ids/names to display objects; falls\nback to the same 3 default roles (Organization employee / Purchasing\nagent / Organization maintainer) the UI showed before this feature, when\nthe setting is unconfigured or unparseable.\n- **`invite-member-modal.vue`** and **`members.vue`** (Change role\nmodal): source their role list from `useCompanyMemberRoles()` instead of\nthe removed `B2B_ROLES` constant.\n- **New composable `useOrganizationContactRoles`** + GraphQL query\n`getOrganizationContactRoles`: powers the \"role\" filter facet on the\ncompany members list with roles actually assigned within the\norganization, replacing a static hardcoded 5-role list.\n- Removed dead code: the unused `permissions` field on role constants in\n`security.ts` (real permission checks go through the server session, not\nthese constants), the now-unused `B2B_ROLES` constant, and\n`role-icon.vue`.\n- Added `no_company_roles_available` translated message across all\nlocales for the empty-state case.\n\n## Breaking changes\nNone — this is an application, not a consumed library; no public API\nsurface changes.\n\n## Verification\n- `vue-tsc --build --force` clean, ESLint clean\n- Manually exercised invite / change-role / filter flows in the browser\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\n<!-- Put link to your task in Jira here -->\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.57.0-pr-2426-8ae2-8ae22416.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Elena Kutasina <kutasina.elena@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"da5ae9d96d564cc7268da9b695524c408f8cf664","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/da5ae9d96d564cc7268da9b695524c408f8cf664"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/282eaeef04e6a2a9e7a458690c667a7cf750adf3","verification":{"payload":"tree da5ae9d96d564cc7268da9b695524c408f8cf664\nparent b22635d8099c468f034c0ca140b9c7c02a7ffe7a\nauthor DmitryGrishinVirtoworks <Dmitry.Grishin@virtoworks.com> 1788273335 +0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788273335 +0400\n\nfeat(VCST-5450): use configurable company roles for invite, filters, and change role (#2426)\n\n## Description\nStorefront now sources company member roles from the new\n`Customer.MembershipRolesWhitelist` store setting instead of a hardcoded\nrole list, for the invite, change-role, and member-filter UIs.\n\n## What was added\n- **New composable `useCompanyMemberRoles`**: reads the public module\nsetting and maps configured role ids/names to display objects; falls\nback to the same 3 default roles (Organization employee / Purchasing\nagent / Organization maintainer) the UI showed before this feature, when\nthe setting is unconfigured or unparseable.\n- **`invite-member-modal.vue`** and **`members.vue`** (Change role\nmodal): source their role list from `useCompanyMemberRoles()` instead of\nthe removed `B2B_ROLES` constant.\n- **New composable `useOrganizationContactRoles`** + GraphQL query\n`getOrganizationContactRoles`: powers the \"role\" filter facet on the\ncompany members list with roles actually assigned within the\norganization, replacing a static hardcoded 5-role list.\n- Removed dead code: the unused `permissions` field on role constants in\n`security.ts` (real permission checks go through the server session, not\nthese constants), the now-unused `B2B_ROLES` constant, and\n`role-icon.vue`.\n- Added `no_company_roles_available` translated message across all\nlocales for the empty-state case.\n\n## Breaking changes\nNone — this is an application, not a consumed library; no public API\nsurface changes.\n\n## Verification\n- `vue-tsc --build --force` clean, ESLint clean\n- Manually exercised invite / change-role / filter flows in the browser\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\n<!-- Put link to your task in Jira here -->\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.57.0-pr-2426-8ae2-8ae22416.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Elena Kutasina <kutasina.elena@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqluK3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALJEQAI/cj4Gg5sRwa1vzxWem+FPJ\nkMXQQZO91Qn4ExDhj5GGCYRXQLPxvJtXYm0LBBiNHH3dhqPadEFaJsHZgNo1LuwV\nJHwEg2AHd5Grx0K37ofc5iLkuS8E703EEtJs9S5qEF7ZeW/MgWrKClYMko+TbmSw\nwEAQzSR7NiYw/j4vSS+2OlRvUhzIgNnu/puvOm6ZWv7Uvh+CRdnqYMevE3s7mZ+s\npi62P21tekYDNqkWVE3mUasD36e7UyyjWlL+6/26OeYjxeapUfn6QLslWnycr2M0\nOdJ1YWW+08+HSbLf6e42NibeQ1ewnBaAVFn+EY5zYasbN1/tas4QaNjAP207umoT\namwjLXxG7702L/QFGqIYNr9gFf/e2cZypZei6Oz9aB1nBleOVT5+9ykNzi73HNDv\nQ3eijTlIDlCFsFrKPFD4jcdgvQnAh1VBX4q5QyqyGnhF0f37eaE49iBYDu5XzjIs\nyf9dfo2NVi8dm3R/1gedLpW1y3fe7LILjeYlLeyRgPI4Kh/hQ4Zvk4G2s2pR53CE\nRz9pxS5JDJugkMmodeSzF1EgM4LTpWjDasGHaiuHwGrGWAEnAmT2bxVENdXO1xdY\nEdoYTjb/Yn6Q8dIGwDA42V1A4koA9o1J9kgjyJw6lAt1bZ2cesgAcnvwTlOsYbkc\nGvE4fW87n75Elg53u7PU\n=ULu4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T14:35:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/282eaeef04e6a2a9e7a458690c667a7cf750adf3","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDI4MmVhZWVmMDRlNmEyYTllN2E0NTg2OTBjNjY3YTdjZjc1MGFkZjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/b22635d8099c468f034c0ca140b9c7c02a7ffe7a","sha":"b22635d8099c468f034c0ca140b9c7c02a7ffe7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/b22635d8099c468f034c0ca140b9c7c02a7ffe7a"}],"sha":"282eaeef04e6a2a9e7a458690c667a7cf750adf3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/282eaeef04e6a2a9e7a458690c667a7cf750adf3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18286430?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ivan-kalachikov","id":18286430,"login":"ivan-kalachikov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Mjg2NDMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/b22635d8099c468f034c0ca140b9c7c02a7ffe7a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T13:32:31Z","email":"ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com","name":"Ivan Kalachikov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T13:32:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(VCST-5770): update dompurify and swiper, the two vulnerable runtime dependencies (#2457)\n\n## Description\n\n**Why:** two open security advisories sit on packages that ship in the\nstorefront bundle — a **critical prototype pollution** in `swiper` and\nan **XSS** in `dompurify`. Unlike the rest of our open alerts, these two\nrun in the customer''s browser, so they are actually reachable. Both are\nalready fixed upstream; this PR only moves to the patched versions.\n\n`swiper` has no fix on the 11.x line, which is the sole reason for the\nmajor bump. `dompurify` is lockfile-only. No application code changes,\ntwo commits, independently revertable.\n\n| Alert | Package | Fix | Change |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|\n[#108](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/security/code-scanning/108)\ncritical, prototype pollution | swiper 11.2.10 | 12.1.2, no 11.x\nbackport | major bump + 2 stylesheets |\n|\n[#288](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/security/code-scanning/288)\nXSS via detached subtree | dompurify 3.4.12 | 3.4.13 | `^3.4.12` →\n`^3.4.14`, lockfile only |\n\n### swiper 12\n\nOnly one v12 breaking change reaches us: **LESS/SCSS sources were\ndropped**, so `_swiper.scss` and `storybook-styles/swiper.scss` now\n`@use \"swiper/css\"` instead of `swiper/scss`. Both keep their place in\nthe import chain — our `.image-gallery` and `.vc-carousel` overrides\nstill win the cascade (verified by computed style, see below).\n\n**The shipped `.css` files use native CSS nesting** (`&`, nested blocks)\nwhere the old `.scss` sources were flat. This matters and is worth a\nreviewer''s attention: `tailwindcss/nesting` in `postcss.config.js`\nflattens them to **plain descendant selectors, not `:is()`** — so\nspecificity is unchanged and our overrides are unaffected. Confirmed\nagainst the browser''s resolved stylesheet: 0 nested rules survive, and\nselectors emit as `.swiper-horizontal .swiper-button-prev`, not\n`:is(.swiper-horizontal) .swiper-button-prev`. Had postcss emitted\n`:is()`, vendor rules would have gained specificity and could have\nclobbered our overrides. Browserslist resolves to Chrome 118+ / Safari\n26.3+ / iOS 18.5+, all of which support native nesting natively anyway.\n\nTwo new params appear in v12, both inert here:\n\n- **`navigation.addIcons: true`** — cannot inject into our buttons.\n`navigation.mjs:102` guards on\n`el.matches(''.swiper-button-next,.swiper-button-prev'') &&\n!el.querySelector(''svg'')`; our `VcNavButton` / `vc-carousel__btn` carry\nneither class and always contain a `VcIcon` svg, so both conditions\nfail. 0 `.swiper-navigation-icon` in the DOM on every page checked,\nincluding a deliberate test against bare `<button>` elements with no\nsvg.\n- **`snapToSlideEdge: false`** — opt-in, off. `cssMode: false`\neverywhere too, so v12''s new `.swiper-css-mode` `margin-inline` rules\nare dead code.\n\nAlso noted, no action needed:\n\n- **`.swiper-button-*` is not styled by us, but swiper does stamp its\nown classes onto our custom nav elements** (`swiper-button-disabled`,\n`swiper-button-lock`). Checked whether v12''s `.swiper-button-lock {\ndisplay: none }` could hide them — the rule is identical in v11, and\ncomputed `display: flex` on both versions.\n- **Vendor CSS defaults that changed are unreachable**:\n`--swiper-navigation-sides-offset` 10px → 4px, and the `swiper-icons`\n`@font-face` + `::after` arrows replaced by `.swiper-navigation-icon`\nSVG. All apply only to `.swiper-button-*` elements, of which the app\nrenders none.\n- **v12 emits the same slide classes in a different order** (e.g.\n`swiper-slide-active` before rather than after `swiper-slide-visible`).\n0 set differences; nothing in `client-app` matches swiper slide classes\nor depends on `className` order.\n- **RTL / effects / scrollbar / a11y CSS rewrites are unreachable**: the\ntheme ships 13 locales with no RTL language and no `dir=\"rtl\"` handling,\nand only `Navigation`, `Pagination`, `Thumbs` are imported.\n\n### dompurify\n\nTwo call sites: `icons.ts` (`sanitize(raw)`) and\n`vc-markdown-render.vue` (`USE_PROFILES: { html: true }`). Neither uses\nhooks or `IN_PLACE`, which is all 3.4.13/3.4.14 changed.\n\nDiffed 3.4.12 against 3.4.14 directly, 47 payloads × both real configs =\n**94 comparisons, 2 differ**: 3.4.14 *preserves* `vector-effect` and\n`pointer-events`, i.e. strictly more permissive on two benign SVG\npresentation attributes. **0 of the 2796 SVGs in `client-app` use either\nattribute**, so the only behavioural delta in the upgrade is\nunreachable. 21 XSS vectors (script, `onload`/`onerror`, `javascript:`\nhrefs, xlink, mXSS via `mglyph`/`noscript`/`noembed`, the\ndetached-subtree CVE class, DOM clobbering, `srcdoc`, `base`) are\nstripped identically by both.\n\n## Verified\n\nRetested in real Chrome via DevTools, this branch against\n`vcst-qa-storefront` (same backend), after confirming by CSS/param\nfingerprint that QA runs swiper 11 and the branch runs 12.\n\n**Prod build vs prod build** (`yarn build` + `yarn preview` against QA\nprod, so build mode is not a variable) — the headline result: across 49\nnodes at ~1400 computed properties each, **0 standard CSS properties\ndiffer in value, 0 exist on only one side, 0 root CSS vars differ**. The\nonly remaining entries are the two new params above and Vue''s\nper-instance `v-bind()` hash names.\n\n| Surface | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Homepage: banner slider + 20 product-card carousels | 21/21\ninitialized, banner next/prev `-1185px` both |\n| Catalog: 16 carousels × 6 steps (next/next/prev/slideTo-last/back) |\n0/16 differ |\n| PDP gallery + thumbs, 2-slide and 4-slide,\nNavigation+Pagination+Thumbs | identical incl. every computed property |\n| Thumb click → main gallery (trusted click) | both `-438px`,\nactiveIndex 1, thumb-active synced |\n| Lightbox (tw-elements via swiper attr forwarding) | both open, overlay\nopacity 1, 800px image, scroll locked |\n| Reviews modal (`VcCarousel` + custom prev/next) | identical |\n| Real pointer drag (touch, 8-step move) | identical snap to `-216px` |\n| Mobile 390×844×2, and 1440→390→1440 round-trip | identical; 4 bullets\nat mobile, 0 at desktop, no stale bullets either direction |\n| 66 slides, `slidesPerView: 4`, `spaceBetween` breakpoints, Navigation\n| 0/8 steps differ — snapGrid 63, 282px slides, 24px gaps, end clamp,\n`swiper-button-disabled` at both boundaries |\n| `/compare`, search dropdown (32 cards) | identical |\n| Icon rendering (dompurify) | 205/205, 149/149, 72/72, 60/60, 59/59\nrendered SVG, 0 empty, byte-identical per icon name |\n| Live markdown (dompurify `USE_PROFILES`) | 4/4 blocks on `/news`\n**SHA-256 identical**; only `alt`/`href`/`src`/`title` survive; 0 event\nhandlers, 0 script/iframe/object/embed |\n\nNo console errors on either side attributable to swiper or dompurify.\n`vue-tsc --build --force` 0 errors · 135 test files / 2106 tests · `yarn\nbuild` · `yarn storybook:build`.\n\n**Advisory closed — reproduced both ways.** The CVE-2026-27212 PoC\n(`Array.prototype.indexOf = () => -1`, then\n`Swiper.extendDefaults(JSON.parse(''{\"__proto__\":{\"polluted\":\"yes\"}}''))`)\npollutes `Object.prototype` on 11.2.10 and does **not** on 12.1.2. Fix\ncommit `d3e6633` replaced the `noExtend.indexOf(key) < 0` guard in\n`shared/utils.mjs` with direct key comparisons.\n\n**Residual note, not a blocker.** A variant that overrides\n`Array.prototype.filter` instead still gets through on the whole 12.x\nline (12.1.2 through 12.2.0), because `extend()` still builds its key\nlist with `.filter()`. It requires the attacker to already hold\n`Array.prototype` write access — i.e. prototype pollution is already\nachieved before Swiper is involved — so it grants nothing new. Swiper 14\nremoves the exposure by dropping `.filter()` and checking keys inline;\nworth a look whenever a v14 migration is on the table.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5770\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.57.0-pr-2457-4116-41164c3f.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9233a6d941d893b885aaca0663b1ee60bdf4a9c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/9233a6d941d893b885aaca0663b1ee60bdf4a9c4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/b22635d8099c468f034c0ca140b9c7c02a7ffe7a","verification":{"payload":"tree 9233a6d941d893b885aaca0663b1ee60bdf4a9c4\nparent f4560ccb9f34f70962e3676878332083813d3766\nauthor Ivan Kalachikov <ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com> 1787923951 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787923951 +0100\n\nfix(VCST-5770): update dompurify and swiper, the two vulnerable runtime dependencies (#2457)\n\n## Description\n\n**Why:** two open security advisories sit on packages that ship in the\nstorefront bundle — a **critical prototype pollution** in `swiper` and\nan **XSS** in `dompurify`. Unlike the rest of our open alerts, these two\nrun in the customer''s browser, so they are actually reachable. Both are\nalready fixed upstream; this PR only moves to the patched versions.\n\n`swiper` has no fix on the 11.x line, which is the sole reason for the\nmajor bump. `dompurify` is lockfile-only. No application code changes,\ntwo commits, independently revertable.\n\n| Alert | Package | Fix | Change |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|\n[#108](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/security/code-scanning/108)\ncritical, prototype pollution | swiper 11.2.10 | 12.1.2, no 11.x\nbackport | major bump + 2 stylesheets |\n|\n[#288](https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/security/code-scanning/288)\nXSS via detached subtree | dompurify 3.4.12 | 3.4.13 | `^3.4.12` →\n`^3.4.14`, lockfile only |\n\n### swiper 12\n\nOnly one v12 breaking change reaches us: **LESS/SCSS sources were\ndropped**, so `_swiper.scss` and `storybook-styles/swiper.scss` now\n`@use \"swiper/css\"` instead of `swiper/scss`. Both keep their place in\nthe import chain — our `.image-gallery` and `.vc-carousel` overrides\nstill win the cascade (verified by computed style, see below).\n\n**The shipped `.css` files use native CSS nesting** (`&`, nested blocks)\nwhere the old `.scss` sources were flat. This matters and is worth a\nreviewer''s attention: `tailwindcss/nesting` in `postcss.config.js`\nflattens them to **plain descendant selectors, not `:is()`** — so\nspecificity is unchanged and our overrides are unaffected. Confirmed\nagainst the browser''s resolved stylesheet: 0 nested rules survive, and\nselectors emit as `.swiper-horizontal .swiper-button-prev`, not\n`:is(.swiper-horizontal) .swiper-button-prev`. Had postcss emitted\n`:is()`, vendor rules would have gained specificity and could have\nclobbered our overrides. Browserslist resolves to Chrome 118+ / Safari\n26.3+ / iOS 18.5+, all of which support native nesting natively anyway.\n\nTwo new params appear in v12, both inert here:\n\n- **`navigation.addIcons: true`** — cannot inject into our buttons.\n`navigation.mjs:102` guards on\n`el.matches(''.swiper-button-next,.swiper-button-prev'') &&\n!el.querySelector(''svg'')`; our `VcNavButton` / `vc-carousel__btn` carry\nneither class and always contain a `VcIcon` svg, so both conditions\nfail. 0 `.swiper-navigation-icon` in the DOM on every page checked,\nincluding a deliberate test against bare `<button>` elements with no\nsvg.\n- **`snapToSlideEdge: false`** — opt-in, off. `cssMode: false`\neverywhere too, so v12''s new `.swiper-css-mode` `margin-inline` rules\nare dead code.\n\nAlso noted, no action needed:\n\n- **`.swiper-button-*` is not styled by us, but swiper does stamp its\nown classes onto our custom nav elements** (`swiper-button-disabled`,\n`swiper-button-lock`). Checked whether v12''s `.swiper-button-lock {\ndisplay: none }` could hide them — the rule is identical in v11, and\ncomputed `display: flex` on both versions.\n- **Vendor CSS defaults that changed are unreachable**:\n`--swiper-navigation-sides-offset` 10px → 4px, and the `swiper-icons`\n`@font-face` + `::after` arrows replaced by `.swiper-navigation-icon`\nSVG. All apply only to `.swiper-button-*` elements, of which the app\nrenders none.\n- **v12 emits the same slide classes in a different order** (e.g.\n`swiper-slide-active` before rather than after `swiper-slide-visible`).\n0 set differences; nothing in `client-app` matches swiper slide classes\nor depends on `className` order.\n- **RTL / effects / scrollbar / a11y CSS rewrites are unreachable**: the\ntheme ships 13 locales with no RTL language and no `dir=\"rtl\"` handling,\nand only `Navigation`, `Pagination`, `Thumbs` are imported.\n\n### dompurify\n\nTwo call sites: `icons.ts` (`sanitize(raw)`) and\n`vc-markdown-render.vue` (`USE_PROFILES: { html: true }`). Neither uses\nhooks or `IN_PLACE`, which is all 3.4.13/3.4.14 changed.\n\nDiffed 3.4.12 against 3.4.14 directly, 47 payloads × both real configs =\n**94 comparisons, 2 differ**: 3.4.14 *preserves* `vector-effect` and\n`pointer-events`, i.e. strictly more permissive on two benign SVG\npresentation attributes. **0 of the 2796 SVGs in `client-app` use either\nattribute**, so the only behavioural delta in the upgrade is\nunreachable. 21 XSS vectors (script, `onload`/`onerror`, `javascript:`\nhrefs, xlink, mXSS via `mglyph`/`noscript`/`noembed`, the\ndetached-subtree CVE class, DOM clobbering, `srcdoc`, `base`) are\nstripped identically by both.\n\n## Verified\n\nRetested in real Chrome via DevTools, this branch against\n`vcst-qa-storefront` (same backend), after confirming by CSS/param\nfingerprint that QA runs swiper 11 and the branch runs 12.\n\n**Prod build vs prod build** (`yarn build` + `yarn preview` against QA\nprod, so build mode is not a variable) — the headline result: across 49\nnodes at ~1400 computed properties each, **0 standard CSS properties\ndiffer in value, 0 exist on only one side, 0 root CSS vars differ**. The\nonly remaining entries are the two new params above and Vue''s\nper-instance `v-bind()` hash names.\n\n| Surface | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Homepage: banner slider + 20 product-card carousels | 21/21\ninitialized, banner next/prev `-1185px` both |\n| Catalog: 16 carousels × 6 steps (next/next/prev/slideTo-last/back) |\n0/16 differ |\n| PDP gallery + thumbs, 2-slide and 4-slide,\nNavigation+Pagination+Thumbs | identical incl. every computed property |\n| Thumb click → main gallery (trusted click) | both `-438px`,\nactiveIndex 1, thumb-active synced |\n| Lightbox (tw-elements via swiper attr forwarding) | both open, overlay\nopacity 1, 800px image, scroll locked |\n| Reviews modal (`VcCarousel` + custom prev/next) | identical |\n| Real pointer drag (touch, 8-step move) | identical snap to `-216px` |\n| Mobile 390×844×2, and 1440→390→1440 round-trip | identical; 4 bullets\nat mobile, 0 at desktop, no stale bullets either direction |\n| 66 slides, `slidesPerView: 4`, `spaceBetween` breakpoints, Navigation\n| 0/8 steps differ — snapGrid 63, 282px slides, 24px gaps, end clamp,\n`swiper-button-disabled` at both boundaries |\n| `/compare`, search dropdown (32 cards) | identical |\n| Icon rendering (dompurify) | 205/205, 149/149, 72/72, 60/60, 59/59\nrendered SVG, 0 empty, byte-identical per icon name |\n| Live markdown (dompurify `USE_PROFILES`) | 4/4 blocks on `/news`\n**SHA-256 identical**; only `alt`/`href`/`src`/`title` survive; 0 event\nhandlers, 0 script/iframe/object/embed |\n\nNo console errors on either side attributable to swiper or dompurify.\n`vue-tsc --build --force` 0 errors · 135 test files / 2106 tests · `yarn\nbuild` · `yarn storybook:build`.\n\n**Advisory closed — reproduced both ways.** The CVE-2026-27212 PoC\n(`Array.prototype.indexOf = () => -1`, then\n`Swiper.extendDefaults(JSON.parse(''{\"__proto__\":{\"polluted\":\"yes\"}}''))`)\npollutes `Object.prototype` on 11.2.10 and does **not** on 12.1.2. Fix\ncommit `d3e6633` replaced the `noExtend.indexOf(key) < 0` guard in\n`shared/utils.mjs` with direct key comparisons.\n\n**Residual note, not a blocker.** A variant that overrides\n`Array.prototype.filter` instead still gets through on the whole 12.x\nline (12.1.2 through 12.2.0), because `extend()` still builds its key\nlist with `.filter()`. It requires the attacker to already hold\n`Array.prototype` write access — i.e. prototype pollution is already\nachieved before Swiper is involved — so it grants nothing new. Swiper 14\nremoves the exposure by dropping `.filter()` and checking keys inline;\nworth a look whenever a v14 migration is on the table.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5770\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.57.0-pr-2457-4116-41164c3f.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkY3vCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxwkQAGXV794xgTXEC+Sk0zM4YBnY\nURQrxNNWL7i/9+eR/Jkoqw25ogvSb8rT7xzhFuqIdTAhcwoFhkzciF5JDvjtp/Og\nmhdDZog6kqOL7To+aIIpQzMAq/zDNNXBJ2w7fyZRlQBxPIvzvES2y2LxXs/nflwV\nfi2F0OVYqm6gj3K0WrzCJdE4u0jsLS+0xyJYoJbHH6Kc0Q2HpvYeRlti6Ms1F9Ap\nVPdHjJx0sxkJEDNIcd0ISD/HM+3XBMYQFQN27Td13nUYby4+/QMsJQNZlF3E01Fz\n76zNeX/tjgniurV6hOc6xFbE5BpgBSgq7tvNZdJ+71jwZd6t1jEtJh2RXdASMD9t\naiCKR6KR3XzfJ+zoH6M+MZ8vLhlqf7yjqXmkkNEAp3mi8OFWFJ8yJcZi4Bt75B3s\nItrmgodzhq2cd3Qp4mQGjVxX37zvp2AKaQuOFJUxaI9vv946cwdcIyH7OSKqlI3T\n6YH1q9jvyC/jBtbcnLOWW4gjzJJ73RcXGVxsiSZpzpadSovB8E8Cl5Z8wEUC+rdm\nDWye9ayUOrBrhjy9FixZ/k10R0v2n04BgSz7HP6AyFl5jh+fL4okAaMxKmO9u656\nB+JliI38tArWZ0CA9bn3LAP5t4mjM552WcbIssAydaEwithSev8hMVOtUXGCHohQ\nrWIMzq1US4Yxw6flSOw7\n=H9Vs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-28T13:32:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/b22635d8099c468f034c0ca140b9c7c02a7ffe7a","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKGIyMjYzNWQ4MDk5YzQ2OGYwMzRjMGNhMTQwYjljN2MwMmE3ZmZlN2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/f4560ccb9f34f70962e3676878332083813d3766","sha":"f4560ccb9f34f70962e3676878332083813d3766","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/f4560ccb9f34f70962e3676878332083813d3766"}],"sha":"b22635d8099c468f034c0ca140b9c7c02a7ffe7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/b22635d8099c468f034c0ca140b9c7c02a7ffe7a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18286430?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ivan-kalachikov","id":18286430,"login":"ivan-kalachikov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Mjg2NDMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/f4560ccb9f34f70962e3676878332083813d3766/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T13:16:55Z","email":"ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com","name":"Ivan Kalachikov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T13:16:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(VCST-5769): close build-only dependency advisories (#2456)\n\n## Description\n\nCloses **70 osv-scanner advisories**. Lockfile only — no app code.\n\n**Removed 3 unused devDependencies** — each was the only path to a\nvulnerable subtree:\n\n| Removed | Unused because | Drops |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `@types/dompurify` | dompurify self-types since v3 | dompurify 3.4.8 →\n#289 #251 #247 #246 |\n| `@storybook/cli` | no dependents, no script uses `sb` | giget → tar\n6.2.1 → #283 #237 #234 #232 #225 #112 #111 #109 #103 #102 #101 #98 |\n| `@graphql-codegen/near-operation-file-preset` | codegen uses plugins,\nno preset | relay-compiler 12 → immutable 3.7.6 (no 3.x fix exists) →\n#244 #242 #114 |\n\n**`yarn up -R` the rest** — all fixes were already inside the ranges\ntheir parents allow:\ntar 7.5.22 · undici 6.28.0 / 7.29.0 · brace-expansion 1.1.18 / 2.1.4 /\n5.0.9 · immutable 5.1.9 · postcss 8.5.26 · nanoid 3.3.18 · js-yaml 4.3.2\n· fast-uri 3.1.6 · protobufjs 7.6.6 · shell-quote 1.10.0 · form-data\n4.0.6\n\n`-R` (`--recursive`) re-resolves **every** descriptor for a package —\ntransitive ones included — each to the newest version its own parent''s\nrange allows. Plain `yarn up` only touches the descriptor declared in\nour `package.json`, which leaves nested copies untouched: that is where\nall of these advisories live (e.g. postcss 8.5.15 pulled by\nvite/tailwind, 8.5.20 by `@vue/compiler-sfc`). No manifest edits, no\noverrides — just newer patches yarn was already allowed to pick.\n\n**4 parent-scoped `resolutions`** — no in-range fix exists, so each is\npinned at the parent that blocks it:\n\n| Resolution | Blocked by | Note |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `skyflow-js/lodash` `^4.18.1` | pins 4.17.21 exactly | not bundled —\nskyflow-js ships a self-contained dist |\n| `@graphql-codegen/plugin-helpers/lodash` `^4.18.1` | wants `~4.17.0`,\nfix is 4.18.0 | |\n| `@module-federation/dts-plugin/undici` `^7.29.0` | pins 7.28.0 exactly\n| version dts-plugin 2.8.2 ships; MF runtime stays 2.8.0 |\n| `@module-federation/dts-plugin/adm-zip` `^0.6.0` | pins 0.5.10 exactly\n| same |\n\nNo `yarn dedupe` — it moves 45 unrelated packages.\n\n### Verified\n\n- **Bundle unchanged** — base and head builds emit the same 3579 dist\nfiles with identical content-hashed names\n- **Console unchanged** — `yarn dev` against a live backend: same 4\nmessages on home, same 10 on a category page as `dev`, no errors, no\noverlay\n- `yarn dev` · `yarn build` · `yarn preview` · `yarn storybook:build` ·\nMF-host build — all clean from a fresh `node_modules`\n- `vue-tsc --build --force` 0 errors · 130 test files / 2034 tests ·\n`yarn install --immutable` · graphql codegen\n- **OSV scan of the new lock**: 1483 packages, 0 in-scope advisories\nleft\n\n### Out of scope\n\n`swiper` 11.2.10 (#108) and `dompurify` 3.4.12 (#288) — runtime bumps,\nseparate WI.\n\nFollow-up: enable **Dependabot security updates** in repo settings.\n`.github/dependabot.yml` groups only `minor`/`patch`, which is why\ntransitive advisories never closed on their own.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5769\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.57.0-pr-2456-7564-7564c89a.zip\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e7230704c685c2c33a6d052c36975f3492c7efa7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/e7230704c685c2c33a6d052c36975f3492c7efa7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/f4560ccb9f34f70962e3676878332083813d3766","verification":{"payload":"tree e7230704c685c2c33a6d052c36975f3492c7efa7\nparent 7f5716e15dfc9149dc5172aae790f03ad5b5c62d\nauthor Ivan Kalachikov <ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com> 1787923015 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787923015 +0100\n\nchore(VCST-5769): close build-only dependency advisories (#2456)\n\n## Description\n\nCloses **70 osv-scanner advisories**. Lockfile only — no app code.\n\n**Removed 3 unused devDependencies** — each was the only path to a\nvulnerable subtree:\n\n| Removed | Unused because | Drops |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `@types/dompurify` | dompurify self-types since v3 | dompurify 3.4.8 →\n#289 #251 #247 #246 |\n| `@storybook/cli` | no dependents, no script uses `sb` | giget → tar\n6.2.1 → #283 #237 #234 #232 #225 #112 #111 #109 #103 #102 #101 #98 |\n| `@graphql-codegen/near-operation-file-preset` | codegen uses plugins,\nno preset | relay-compiler 12 → immutable 3.7.6 (no 3.x fix exists) →\n#244 #242 #114 |\n\n**`yarn up -R` the rest** — all fixes were already inside the ranges\ntheir parents allow:\ntar 7.5.22 · undici 6.28.0 / 7.29.0 · brace-expansion 1.1.18 / 2.1.4 /\n5.0.9 · immutable 5.1.9 · postcss 8.5.26 · nanoid 3.3.18 · js-yaml 4.3.2\n· fast-uri 3.1.6 · protobufjs 7.6.6 · shell-quote 1.10.0 · form-data\n4.0.6\n\n`-R` (`--recursive`) re-resolves **every** descriptor for a package —\ntransitive ones included — each to the newest version its own parent''s\nrange allows. Plain `yarn up` only touches the descriptor declared in\nour `package.json`, which leaves nested copies untouched: that is where\nall of these advisories live (e.g. postcss 8.5.15 pulled by\nvite/tailwind, 8.5.20 by `@vue/compiler-sfc`). No manifest edits, no\noverrides — just newer patches yarn was already allowed to pick.\n\n**4 parent-scoped `resolutions`** — no in-range fix exists, so each is\npinned at the parent that blocks it:\n\n| Resolution | Blocked by | Note |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `skyflow-js/lodash` `^4.18.1` | pins 4.17.21 exactly | not bundled —\nskyflow-js ships a self-contained dist |\n| `@graphql-codegen/plugin-helpers/lodash` `^4.18.1` | wants `~4.17.0`,\nfix is 4.18.0 | |\n| `@module-federation/dts-plugin/undici` `^7.29.0` | pins 7.28.0 exactly\n| version dts-plugin 2.8.2 ships; MF runtime stays 2.8.0 |\n| `@module-federation/dts-plugin/adm-zip` `^0.6.0` | pins 0.5.10 exactly\n| same |\n\nNo `yarn dedupe` — it moves 45 unrelated packages.\n\n### Verified\n\n- **Bundle unchanged** — base and head builds emit the same 3579 dist\nfiles with identical content-hashed names\n- **Console unchanged** — `yarn dev` against a live backend: same 4\nmessages on home, same 10 on a category page as `dev`, no errors, no\noverlay\n- `yarn dev` · `yarn build` · `yarn preview` · `yarn storybook:build` ·\nMF-host build — all clean from a fresh `node_modules`\n- `vue-tsc --build --force` 0 errors · 130 test files / 2034 tests ·\n`yarn install --immutable` · graphql codegen\n- **OSV scan of the new lock**: 1483 packages, 0 in-scope advisories\nleft\n\n### Out of scope\n\n`swiper` 11.2.10 (#108) and `dompurify` 3.4.12 (#288) — runtime bumps,\nseparate WI.\n\nFollow-up: enable **Dependabot security updates** in repo settings.\n`.github/dependabot.yml` groups only `minor`/`patch`, which is why\ntransitive advisories never closed on their own.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5769\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.57.0-pr-2456-7564-7564c89a.zip\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkYpHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQ44QAKVc7cM1unePNDvcrnquW4jB\ny10Dk/LKsmBjAvOx3olEuhAvnlqPDNGJmiyuO6ilFpOBIID/hZgkXYvj7MSUx4uo\nYwNV7w4OKJ7cOhHPCjQJmOl4oAMtH88C4EpTe59TL3j2uFYsAvK9lzSSMjHPGWFQ\nrgjNcucE2tQIDPolWQUtSmxm3PW4ftCIxUAaPlxpoyLWtfDg4RVBlbUgTu+YmoUN\nP+nPxfJ1wDPyCp1Dbr7pHgRavAw+3FL1REyYCNUxalcgW1Y3EEyB/Xi2gmeOAjha\nsfLUtVFzquTX4uWV2bUUWxZULnhnOPRfm8GEXFxh4tdAofBVJZcSOrUCnN0RQBsD\n3W+U76CTdldKND36PE6sixNRgoRvTurj8lXCOBl5cD8La/+CiH39BkJXtFBi2JZB\nygMjMzg5qgiMrt4ZH3XKVbp78WB46DpKr3W3R1cBEjVMBowVtckWGRL3+/ksVut9\nBPZ2E9nVj85qtyAFOCjuGxBZJO1LCNK9FmFYKdgm8cedJ+SOFV2GC5N5vtKEOwVM\n3Jy2Oe9B3Q0cjD+41heD1fXxoIpJE075JdU0/OM/4eyba5qKTfm0AzlkvgfN2VwN\n85DmB8W2u3mnuxO7/LyGK0lL3PmwYyp48Ix5nWr5Xhad3DHNWa4gFMikBXqRW0VH\nJOt48R0V8MNi9K/czkoW\n=LWcL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-28T13:16:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/f4560ccb9f34f70962e3676878332083813d3766","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKGY0NTYwY2NiOWYzNGY3MDk2MmUzNjc2ODc4MzMyMDgzODEzZDM3NjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/7f5716e15dfc9149dc5172aae790f03ad5b5c62d","sha":"7f5716e15dfc9149dc5172aae790f03ad5b5c62d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/7f5716e15dfc9149dc5172aae790f03ad5b5c62d"}],"sha":"f4560ccb9f34f70962e3676878332083813d3766","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/f4560ccb9f34f70962e3676878332083813d3766"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46611511?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/muller39","id":46611511,"login":"muller39","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NjExNTEx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/muller39","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/7f5716e15dfc9149dc5172aae790f03ad5b5c62d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T09:45:08Z","email":"46611511+muller39@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alexander Kurilin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T09:45:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(search-bar): show only one category scope indicator while the scope is loading (#2436)\n\n## Description\n\n**Symptom.** On a category page, clicking a parent breadcrumb link makes\nthe search bar''s category-scope area show **two indicators at once** for\nthe whole duration of the new category''s fetch: the loading chip *and*\nthe previous (child) category''s stale chip. Only one indicator should\never be visible — the chip for the category being left should not linger\nuntil the new category''s data arrives.\n\n**Root cause.** `search-bar.vue` rendered the two indicators\nindependently, with no mutual exclusion:\n\n```html\n<VcButton v-if=\"preparingScope\" ... />          <!-- loading chip -->\n<VcButton v-for=\"item in searchScopeData.searchScope\" ... />  <!-- scope chips -->\n```\n\nBoth conditions are true at the same time during navigation. In\n`category.vue`, the `watch(() => props.categoryId, ...)` handler sets\n`preparingScope.value = true` synchronously when `categoryId` changes,\nbut the previous category''s scope item is removed only later — by the\nseparate `watch(() => currentCategory.value?.id, ...)` →\n`changeSearchBarScope()` → `clearCategoryScope()`, which runs after\n`fetchCategory` resolves. So for the entire fetch window\n`preparingScope` is `true` while the old scope item is still in\n`searchScope`, and both render.\n\n**Fix.** Make the two indicators mutually exclusive in the template: the\nscope-item `v-for` moves into a `<template v-else>` of the existing\n`v-if=\"preparingScope\"`. Template-only change — no script changes, no\nnew imports.\n\n**Why fixed in the template rather than by clearing the scope state\nearlier.** The alternative — calling `removeScopeItemByType(\"category\")`\nin `category.vue` where `preparingScope` is set — looks smaller but is\nnot behaviour-preserving. Today `changeSearchBarScope()` clears and\nre-adds the scope item **synchronously in one block**, so the\n`isCategoryScope` computed never observably changes and the\n`watch(isCategoryScope, ...)` in `search-bar.vue` never fires. Clearing\nearly and re-adding only after the `await` breaks that atomicity and\nmakes the computed flip `true → false → true`, which would fire that\nwatch, flip `searchScopeFilterExpression` to the whole-catalog fallback\nmid-navigation, and flicker the placeholder. The template fix leaves\n`searchScopeData`, `isCategoryScope` and `searchScopeFilterExpression`\nsemantics completely untouched.\n\n## Update: fixes for review feedback\n\n@ivan-kalachikov reviewed the first version and found the template-only\nfix left two things unaddressed. Both are now fixed:\n\n1. **Placeholder still named the old category.** `searchPlaceholder`\n(`search-bar.vue`) read `isCategoryScope` alone, so during the fetch\nwindow the chip was hidden but the input placeholder still read \"Search\nwithin Child category\" — same stale info, different pixels. Now gated\nthe same way as the chip: `isCategoryScope.value &&\n!preparingScope.value`.\n\n2. **The scope became unreachable after a failed category fetch.**\n`useCategory.fetchCategory` rethrows on error, and `category.vue` reset\n`preparingScope.value = false` only after the `await`, with no\n`try`/`finally`. A failed fetch left `preparingScope` stuck `true`\nforever — and now that the chips live in `v-else`, that meant the chips\nnever render again while the category filter is still live, with no way\nfor the user to clear it (the remove button lives in the\nnow-permanently-hidden branch). Fixed by wrapping the `fetchCategory`\ncall in `try/finally` so `preparingScope` always resets, success or\nfailure.\n\n3. **The tests couldn''t see either bug.** The `VcInput` stub rendered\nonly the `prepend` slot (placeholder is a separate attr, never\nrendered), and `SearchDropdown` was stubbed to `null` (so\n`filterExpression`/`isCategoryScope` props were never observable).\nReworked both stubs — `VcInput`''s stub now renders the placeholder it''s\ngiven, and `SearchDropdown`''s stub is a real component that surfaces its\nscope-related props as data attributes — and added tests asserting on\nboth. Also fixed the \"shows the scope chip once preparation finished\"\ntest, which previously never set `preparingScope` to `true`, so it only\nasserted the idle default rather than the actual loading → finished\ntransition.\n\n4. **Test file location.** Moved from `__tests__/search-bar.test.ts` to\na colocated `search-bar.test.ts` next to `search-bar.vue`, matching the\nrepo convention (111 of 116 spec files are colocated, only 4 live under\n`__tests__/`).\n\n## Tests\n\n\n`client-app/shared/layout/components/header/_internal/search-bar/search-bar.test.ts`\n(6 tests, no existing test or story modified):\n\n- `hides the scope chips while the category scope is being prepared`\n- `hides the scope chips as soon as preparation starts`\n- `shows the scope chip once preparation finished` — now genuinely\ndrives `preparingScope` `true → false` and asserts both sides of the\ntransition\n- `falls back to the generic placeholder while the category scope is\nbeing prepared` — new, covers fix #1\n- `shows the category placeholder once the scope is no longer being\nprepared` — new\n- `keeps the dropdown scoped to the category filter while preparing the\nnext category` — new, asserts `SearchDropdown`''s\n`filterExpression`/`isCategoryScope` props directly instead of a\n`null`-rendering stub\n\nVerified the placeholder test is genuinely red→green by reverting the\n`search-bar.vue` fix locally and re-running: it fails with the\nplaceholder rendering `enter_keyword_placeholder_category` (the\nstale-category string) instead of the generic fallback.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `vitest` (updated spec): 6/6 green.\n- `eslint` + `prettier --check` on all changed files: clean.\n- `vue-tsc --noEmit`: 0 errors.\n\n## Notes for reviewers\n\n- **Not visually re-verified on a running storefront** — the change is\nunit-proven only. Worth a quick look at the search bar''s scope area\nduring category navigation (including a simulated fetch failure) before\nmerge.\n- `mobile-search-bar.vue` does not use `useSearchScore` or\n`preparingScope` (it builds a plain catalog-wide scope expression), so\nthere is no mobile variant of this bug left unfixed.\n\n> **DO NOT MERGE until human review.**\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\n<!-- n/a — found during storefront QA, tracked in an internal tracker\n(ref. 8472) rather than Jira -->\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.57.0-pr-2436-f3bf-f3bffc67.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"c47dfb73541583ac776d0d62c97128cfbffa7e70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/c47dfb73541583ac776d0d62c97128cfbffa7e70"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/7f5716e15dfc9149dc5172aae790f03ad5b5c62d","verification":{"payload":"tree c47dfb73541583ac776d0d62c97128cfbffa7e70\nparent 21cde9a1bed624cd806c14c0143bb952f99c84fb\nauthor Alexander Kurilin <46611511+muller39@users.noreply.github.com> 1787823908 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787823908 +0200\n\nfix(search-bar): show only one category scope indicator while the scope is loading (#2436)\n\n## Description\n\n**Symptom.** On a category page, clicking a parent breadcrumb link makes\nthe search bar''s category-scope area show **two indicators at once** for\nthe whole duration of the new category''s fetch: the loading chip *and*\nthe previous (child) category''s stale chip. Only one indicator should\never be visible — the chip for the category being left should not linger\nuntil the new category''s data arrives.\n\n**Root cause.** `search-bar.vue` rendered the two indicators\nindependently, with no mutual exclusion:\n\n```html\n<VcButton v-if=\"preparingScope\" ... />          <!-- loading chip -->\n<VcButton v-for=\"item in searchScopeData.searchScope\" ... />  <!-- scope chips -->\n```\n\nBoth conditions are true at the same time during navigation. In\n`category.vue`, the `watch(() => props.categoryId, ...)` handler sets\n`preparingScope.value = true` synchronously when `categoryId` changes,\nbut the previous category''s scope item is removed only later — by the\nseparate `watch(() => currentCategory.value?.id, ...)` →\n`changeSearchBarScope()` → `clearCategoryScope()`, which runs after\n`fetchCategory` resolves. So for the entire fetch window\n`preparingScope` is `true` while the old scope item is still in\n`searchScope`, and both render.\n\n**Fix.** Make the two indicators mutually exclusive in the template: the\nscope-item `v-for` moves into a `<template v-else>` of the existing\n`v-if=\"preparingScope\"`. Template-only change — no script changes, no\nnew imports.\n\n**Why fixed in the template rather than by clearing the scope state\nearlier.** The alternative — calling `removeScopeItemByType(\"category\")`\nin `category.vue` where `preparingScope` is set — looks smaller but is\nnot behaviour-preserving. Today `changeSearchBarScope()` clears and\nre-adds the scope item **synchronously in one block**, so the\n`isCategoryScope` computed never observably changes and the\n`watch(isCategoryScope, ...)` in `search-bar.vue` never fires. Clearing\nearly and re-adding only after the `await` breaks that atomicity and\nmakes the computed flip `true → false → true`, which would fire that\nwatch, flip `searchScopeFilterExpression` to the whole-catalog fallback\nmid-navigation, and flicker the placeholder. The template fix leaves\n`searchScopeData`, `isCategoryScope` and `searchScopeFilterExpression`\nsemantics completely untouched.\n\n## Update: fixes for review feedback\n\n@ivan-kalachikov reviewed the first version and found the template-only\nfix left two things unaddressed. Both are now fixed:\n\n1. **Placeholder still named the old category.** `searchPlaceholder`\n(`search-bar.vue`) read `isCategoryScope` alone, so during the fetch\nwindow the chip was hidden but the input placeholder still read \"Search\nwithin Child category\" — same stale info, different pixels. Now gated\nthe same way as the chip: `isCategoryScope.value &&\n!preparingScope.value`.\n\n2. **The scope became unreachable after a failed category fetch.**\n`useCategory.fetchCategory` rethrows on error, and `category.vue` reset\n`preparingScope.value = false` only after the `await`, with no\n`try`/`finally`. A failed fetch left `preparingScope` stuck `true`\nforever — and now that the chips live in `v-else`, that meant the chips\nnever render again while the category filter is still live, with no way\nfor the user to clear it (the remove button lives in the\nnow-permanently-hidden branch). Fixed by wrapping the `fetchCategory`\ncall in `try/finally` so `preparingScope` always resets, success or\nfailure.\n\n3. **The tests couldn''t see either bug.** The `VcInput` stub rendered\nonly the `prepend` slot (placeholder is a separate attr, never\nrendered), and `SearchDropdown` was stubbed to `null` (so\n`filterExpression`/`isCategoryScope` props were never observable).\nReworked both stubs — `VcInput`''s stub now renders the placeholder it''s\ngiven, and `SearchDropdown`''s stub is a real component that surfaces its\nscope-related props as data attributes — and added tests asserting on\nboth. Also fixed the \"shows the scope chip once preparation finished\"\ntest, which previously never set `preparingScope` to `true`, so it only\nasserted the idle default rather than the actual loading → finished\ntransition.\n\n4. **Test file location.** Moved from `__tests__/search-bar.test.ts` to\na colocated `search-bar.test.ts` next to `search-bar.vue`, matching the\nrepo convention (111 of 116 spec files are colocated, only 4 live under\n`__tests__/`).\n\n## Tests\n\n\n`client-app/shared/layout/components/header/_internal/search-bar/search-bar.test.ts`\n(6 tests, no existing test or story modified):\n\n- `hides the scope chips while the category scope is being prepared`\n- `hides the scope chips as soon as preparation starts`\n- `shows the scope chip once preparation finished` — now genuinely\ndrives `preparingScope` `true → false` and asserts both sides of the\ntransition\n- `falls back to the generic placeholder while the category scope is\nbeing prepared` — new, covers fix #1\n- `shows the category placeholder once the scope is no longer being\nprepared` — new\n- `keeps the dropdown scoped to the category filter while preparing the\nnext category` — new, asserts `SearchDropdown`''s\n`filterExpression`/`isCategoryScope` props directly instead of a\n`null`-rendering stub\n\nVerified the placeholder test is genuinely red→green by reverting the\n`search-bar.vue` fix locally and re-running: it fails with the\nplaceholder rendering `enter_keyword_placeholder_category` (the\nstale-category string) instead of the generic fallback.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `vitest` (updated spec): 6/6 green.\n- `eslint` + `prettier --check` on all changed files: clean.\n- `vue-tsc --noEmit`: 0 errors.\n\n## Notes for reviewers\n\n- **Not visually re-verified on a running storefront** — the change is\nunit-proven only. Worth a quick look at the search bar''s scope area\nduring category navigation (including a simulated fetch failure) before\nmerge.\n- `mobile-search-bar.vue` does not use `useSearchScore` or\n`preparingScope` (it builds a plain catalog-wide scope expression), so\nthere is no mobile variant of this bug left unfixed.\n\n> **DO NOT MERGE until human review.**\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\n<!-- n/a — found during storefront QA, tracked in an internal tracker\n(ref. 8472) rather than Jira -->\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.57.0-pr-2436-f3bf-f3bffc67.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Elena Mutykova <56412054+Lenajava1@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkAckCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqaUQACmzcpuxyqkd7N97xUAffvfY\nx33/flYwtWNevvHKCuFq8x5zOf2TMaKDrii3egIVzgMxncYQ2wMI8hA9+E2TKAdy\npJ4Nz3hFqBDeCXBdDDhVhIPDB8iZsdh/SIu6rLiYAeese4oQnZdD8tSfpU3Q0Ckq\nC8Ct2vi7Fp5IKHoV4dBzgOUuXf3RQhv1k0m2ydLGB4wZZIesBxyTcr67PyqjOQi/\nv6t7+724wcsusHlo3LJg8lbHqPfIJYkSpHtGJEDO1WYrYdy8/9o9BCk7wGv4ZQ8t\nM6IFrjZnoFJD5iaANDzE8Vca7kLXiXJ7VI9/rvy3Ce+zkb6iVj+1zGQSE/U+EwyN\n5UqZrUQBmIy3Vnse/dgpWszkD2F+i742mo8uZBTLu7tBWEJv+LCfgrA/VpKMnInX\n+AGkaEzFsFDZHkM3VyHYJ7fAlrfcBVHzLEqdMPZmfazN7P8z4W8EwGRehUwitfei\nzgX615NGOnI5kS7BkhiCRI+NOHXWT4M7OeFnHF