SbboQ2rkX6c51Lt6ITFmuEtys0domGRU+KTyJTuk6V+kVjFJxR4\n5ickVDiKcgRd2mBJRcEShROvcZ+wEszDBIV/+jV3zaaEqiRtEmRRaX5i+/o9QGf1\nubyJQBgAXb+Jv/fZsTwlyhIG9scMuvmYxPQMps6JCDCkhiqQEuAI0Zls+0IU+JPo\nBcJT9RDHoGW0PHg4o768DO25P9T/qE+rt9rV10YlSc4vOb6FFBQg+wpRh0qbsivE\nfpH8mWY3PRRrneyb3paA\n=dADc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T14:48:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/da6b1496ad284f5f1e2fc121c1abb0bba3d95185","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKGRhNmIxNDk2YWQyODRmNWYxZTJmYzEyMWMxYWJiMGJiYTNkOTUxODU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/912d2d3e337865c7a45bb2718e50cade837afe19","sha":"912d2d3e337865c7a45bb2718e50cade837afe19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/912d2d3e337865c7a45bb2718e50cade837afe19"}],"sha":"da6b1496ad284f5f1e2fc121c1abb0bba3d95185","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/da6b1496ad284f5f1e2fc121c1abb0bba3d95185"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18286430?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ivan-kalachikov","id":18286430,"login":"ivan-kalachikov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Mjg2NDMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/912d2d3e337865c7a45bb2718e50cade837afe19/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T10:20:33Z","email":"ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com","name":"Ivan Kalachikov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T10:20:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(VCST-5682): keep a failure signal where the toast was suppressed (#2443)\n\n## Description\n\nQA verified #2432 on `vcptcore-qa` and confirmed the reported defect is\nfixed — a single failing hub query now renders only its inline error.\nBut suppressing the toast left some surfaces with **no** failure signal:\nthe toast had been their only one. This is that follow-up (BL-SR-012 — a\nfailure state must stay distinguishable from \"no data\").\n\n| Failing operation | After #2432 | This PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| `SalesRepCustomer` (`/company/my-customers/<id>`) | the same **\"not\nfound\"** verdict — a transient server error read as \"this customer isn''t\nyours\" | its own load-failure wording, with the error illustration |\n| `SalesRepOrderFilterRules` and its five sibling rule ops | the status\ntabs / category chips / segment chips and the sortable headers\n**silently disappear** | an inline alert naming what degraded: the\nfilters, the sorting options, or both |\n\n**The change.** Both reads have an `error` the surface never saw, so\neach composable now exposes `failed`:\n\n- `useSalesRepCustomer` — `failed` is excluded from `notFound`, so \"the\nrep doesn''t serve this customer\" and \"the read died\" are no longer the\nsame state. The page words them separately; the back button is\nunchanged.\n- `useSalesRepRules` — an empty catalog and a dead read look identical\nin `rules`. The new `sales-rep-rule-alert.vue` (the `VcAlert` shape\n`useSalesRepLayout` already uses for `load_failed`) renders on Recent\norders, Top sellers and My customers, so all six rule ops are covered —\nthe one QA named plus `SalesRepOrderSortRules`,\n`SalesRepTopSellerFilterRules`, `SalesRepTopSellerSortRules` and the\ncustomer segment/sort pair. The message names only what actually failed;\nreporting sorting as broken when only the filters died would be the same\nclass of untruth this PR removes.\n\nFour keys in 13 locales. Every change is inside `modules/sales-rep`.\n\n**Two deliberate limits:**\n\n1. **The customers-count badge is left as is.** QA also flagged\n`SalesRepCustomersCount`: on failure the account-rail badge drops its\nnumber silently. Not worth a signal — the count is decorative, nothing\nis blocked, and a refresh fixes it. Marking the mobile menu''s badge\nwould additionally mean changing shared layout code for a module\nconcern. `error-notifications.test.ts` records this as the one\nintentional exception.\n2. A filter-rules failure stays silent in the orders widget on the\ncustomer profile (`filterable={false}`) — no chips are offered there, so\nnothing was lost. Sort-rule failures still speak, since the headers are\nsortable on both surfaces.\n\n### Verification\n\n- New `pages/customer-profile.test.ts` (3) — the profile words a failed\nread as a load failure, keeps \"not found\" for a real null, and renders\nthe layout in neither case.\n- 9 new degraded-control cases across `sales-rep-orders.test.ts`,\n`top-sellers.test.ts` and `my-customers.test.ts` assert which message\neach surface carries, including the `filterable={false}` silence, plus\none in `useSalesRepCustomer.test.ts` for the `notFound` split.\n- `yarn vitest run --dir client-app` — 126 files, 1974 tests passed\n- `yarn vue-tsc --build --force` — clean\n- `eslint` on the changed files — 0 errors (the remaining `sonarjs`\nwarnings in `useSalesRepRules.ts` are pre-existing, on lines this PR\ndoes not touch)\n- `prettier --check` on the changed files — clean\n\nNot verified in a browser: reproducing needs a Sales Rep account on a\nlive backend with one named `POST /graphql` operation forced to fail.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5682\n### Artifact URL:\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"068201951a2e7be543e488ca353f5aae1af614d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/068201951a2e7be543e488ca353f5aae1af614d7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/912d2d3e337865c7a45bb2718e50cade837afe19","verification":{"payload":"tree 068201951a2e7be543e488ca353f5aae1af614d7\nparent 7b727a37737f1fbb6fda9c8467d26043dbc5034e\nauthor Ivan Kalachikov <ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com> 1787307633 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787307633 +0100\n\nfix(VCST-5682): keep a failure signal where the toast was suppressed (#2443)\n\n## Description\n\nQA verified #2432 on `vcptcore-qa` and confirmed the reported defect is\nfixed — a single failing hub query now renders only its inline error.\nBut suppressing the toast left some surfaces with **no** failure signal:\nthe toast had been their only one. This is that follow-up (BL-SR-012 — a\nfailure state must stay distinguishable from \"no data\").\n\n| Failing operation | After #2432 | This PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| `SalesRepCustomer` (`/company/my-customers/<id>`) | the same **\"not\nfound\"** verdict — a transient server error read as \"this customer isn''t\nyours\" | its own load-failure wording, with the error illustration |\n| `SalesRepOrderFilterRules` and its five sibling rule ops | the status\ntabs / category chips / segment chips and the sortable headers\n**silently disappear** | an inline alert naming what degraded: the\nfilters, the sorting options, or both |\n\n**The change.** Both reads have an `error` the surface never saw, so\neach composable now exposes `failed`:\n\n- `useSalesRepCustomer` — `failed` is excluded from `notFound`, so \"the\nrep doesn''t serve this customer\" and \"the read died\" are no longer the\nsame state. The page words them separately; the back button is\nunchanged.\n- `useSalesRepRules` — an empty catalog and a dead read look identical\nin `rules`. The new `sales-rep-rule-alert.vue` (the `VcAlert` shape\n`useSalesRepLayout` already uses for `load_failed`) renders on Recent\norders, Top sellers and My customers, so all six rule ops are covered —\nthe one QA named plus `SalesRepOrderSortRules`,\n`SalesRepTopSellerFilterRules`, `SalesRepTopSellerSortRules` and the\ncustomer segment/sort pair. The message names only what actually failed;\nreporting sorting as broken when only the filters died would be the same\nclass of untruth this PR removes.\n\nFour keys in 13 locales. Every change is inside `modules/sales-rep`.\n\n**Two deliberate limits:**\n\n1. **The customers-count badge is left as is.** QA also flagged\n`SalesRepCustomersCount`: on failure the account-rail badge drops its\nnumber silently. Not worth a signal — the count is decorative, nothing\nis blocked, and a refresh fixes it. Marking the mobile menu''s badge\nwould additionally mean changing shared layout code for a module\nconcern. `error-notifications.test.ts` records this as the one\nintentional exception.\n2. A filter-rules failure stays silent in the orders widget on the\ncustomer profile (`filterable={false}`) — no chips are offered there, so\nnothing was lost. Sort-rule failures still speak, since the headers are\nsortable on both surfaces.\n\n### Verification\n\n- New `pages/customer-profile.test.ts` (3) — the profile words a failed\nread as a load failure, keeps \"not found\" for a real null, and renders\nthe layout in neither case.\n- 9 new degraded-control cases across `sales-rep-orders.test.ts`,\n`top-sellers.test.ts` and `my-customers.test.ts` assert which message\neach surface carries, including the `filterable={false}` silence, plus\none in `useSalesRepCustomer.test.ts` for the `notFound` split.\n- `yarn vitest run --dir client-app` — 126 files, 1974 tests passed\n- `yarn vue-tsc --build --force` — clean\n- `eslint` on the changed files — 0 errors (the remaining `sonarjs`\nwarnings in `useSalesRepRules.ts` are pre-existing, on lines this PR\ndoes not touch)\n- `prettier --check` on the changed files — clean\n\nNot verified in a browser: reproducing needs a Sales Rep account on a\nlive backend with one named `POST /graphql` operation forced to fail.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5682\n### Artifact URL:\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiCZxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABMAQACDkqi6aDRR+fPhKHaNB+BvZ\nrHDgATTGK0dtnZdaGwErb2Rn2kTTTcvF3vqvQnuta3hAQ1gGekfZacT0Hp4Bg1Ry\nax4ViVcakzyOs2QaU5efcM0n8lGXEKCkQZQ+ZVQfZPiJPNXApJMts1L7PofGCKUN\nShNRU54CLw7HWhzgUGePoVfHqYQTbbkbw6751WwrAmnli3f6KLIorxi2Idq5hqeh\neiSXbT3PJtLxEkHxcK9/qLP3rkY4rMw5YHHnVZi9DmkFHKOaSxi8ODCPnO+hydm0\nTgzQ9EY4gheJNZhNz2BNm+kxqbuhdvaNTdVRak5ECKQ4tgJHs9XtzEpew3HPwhe9\n9UFjYu4ysiJOlEAqKBJLcZ6HPhkvl/PewKQART03HzP0vyVTLC02et1C4MFunJb8\n5ET3I7pvjbI8ZW1IWC4rOnNK+04RyY8tBvgo1Y9DsUMVYi/8BR660w1pHk8zRf+N\njiHko/HPau79MI5jfo7oFeocM7aymnVBiLsY9M3zFA8J5cDXXl7o+ZfPfrOOyH5+\n6Pk+eYbxPXF80Ta5hqr0RKhyxUv5DnXCPAzzxIBGyUPPyZ5NVo/GMtFk/ra1fnga\nZhuwRT1CqoxQQ1KI7k/w7TJMMToF/DFMxX+9DDjpvPiBL5GkoYPqEQCh8XUM2xRl\nJAV2rYx4BgA0KyR1CIF6\n=Mvc9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-21T10:20:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/912d2d3e337865c7a45bb2718e50cade837afe19","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDkxMmQyZDNlMzM3ODY1YzdhNDViYjI3MThlNTBjYWRlODM3YWZlMTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/7b727a37737f1fbb6fda9c8467d26043dbc5034e","sha":"7b727a37737f1fbb6fda9c8467d26043dbc5034e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/7b727a37737f1fbb6fda9c8467d26043dbc5034e"}],"sha":"912d2d3e337865c7a45bb2718e50cade837afe19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/912d2d3e337865c7a45bb2718e50cade837afe19"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18286430?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ivan-kalachikov","id":18286430,"login":"ivan-kalachikov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Mjg2NDMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/7b727a37737f1fbb6fda9c8467d26043dbc5034e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T19:56:45Z","email":"ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com","name":"Ivan Kalachikov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T19:56:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(VCST-5683): pluralize sales-rep count messages (#2430)\n\n## Description\n\nThe **My Customers** table rendered `\"1 orders\"`. The call site already\npassed vue-i18n''s plural-choice index, but\n`sales_rep.my_customers.table.orders_count` carried a single form\n(`\"{count} orders\"`), so there was no singular to select. The dashboard\nstat sub-lines (`ordered_this_month`, `new_customers`, `new_this_week`,\n`of_recent_orders`) had the same shape.\n\n**What changed** — `client-app/modules/sales-rep/locales/*.json` and\nnothing else: 11 files, 44 lines. No component change; the plumbing was\nalready correct.\n\n| Forms | Locales | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| one | `ja`, `zh` | Neither marks number — untouched. Same for keys\nthat read the same either way (en `\"{count} ordered this month\"`, de\n`\"{count} in diesem Monat bestellt\"`). |\n| two | `de`, `en`, `es`, `fi`, `it`, `no`, `sv` | The built-in selector\npicks between them, and their plural is what zero takes. |\n| three | `fr`, `pt` | A leading **zero** slot, whose copy is the\nsingular — see below. |\n| four | `ru`, `pl` | The width at which `createIntlPluralRule`\n(VCST-5487, now on `dev`) consults the CLDR data. Three forms would fall\nback to index counting and render `\"5 заказа\"`. Their leading slot keeps\nthe numeric many form, which is what both languages take at zero. |\n\n**Agreement at zero (QA reopen).** French renders `\"0 nouveau client\"`,\nnot `\"0 nouveaux clients\"` — it files zero under CLDR `one`. A two-form\nmessage can''t express that: below four forms the rule defers to\nvue-i18n''s locale-blind `count === 1 ? 0 : 1`, so zero can only ever\nland on the plural. Three forms give zero a slot of its own, which is\nhow `reviews_count` is already written in these locales.\n\n`pt` gets the same treatment, as QA asked. CLDR files zero under `one`\nfor region-less `pt` and for `pt-BR`, and under `other` only for\n`pt-PT`. It reads correctly on the QA store purely because that store is\nconfigured `pt-PT` — switching to `pt-BR` would make `\"0 novos\nclientes\"` the same defect with no code change. One file serves both\nspellings and the rule short-circuits zero to slot 0 for every locale,\nso this picks a side: the file''s wording is Brazilian (`pedido`, `Meu\núltimo pedido`), so the zero slot is singular. `pt-PT` now reads `\"0\nnovo cliente\"` where CLDR would say plural.\n\n**Merged `dev` in.** VCST-5587 (#2433) replaced the \"placed today\" card\nwith `of_recent_orders`, deleting `placed_today`; its plural forms went\nwith the key. Everything `dev` added to these files since — `ytd`\n(#2429), `table.load_failed` (#2432), `of_recent_orders` (#2433) — is\npreserved: key sets are identical to `dev` in all 13 files, and the only\nvalues that differ are the 44 above.\n\n`of_recent_orders` came in with that merge carrying the same defect, so\nit is fixed here too: a participle agreeing with the elided \"orders\" in\n`es`/`fr`/`it`/`pt`/`sv`, the genitive after `из`/`z` in `ru`/`pl`.\n`de`, `en`, `fi` and `no` keep one form — nothing in them agrees.\n\n**No tests.** This is locale data; the repo has 117 locale JSONs and no\ntests over any of them, and `client-app/i18n.test.ts` already covers the\nrule these messages feed — including `rule(0, 3) === 0`, the path the\n`fr`/`pt` zero slot rides on. Asserting that `\"{count} order | {count}\norders\"` renders `\"1 order\"` would be testing vue-i18n, not this change.\n\nOne property of the convention worth knowing, since this PR is the first\nto lean on it: a **Slavic** message written with exactly three forms\nsilently loses the CLDR path and renders `\"1 заказа\"` with no error,\nbecause `createIntlPluralRule` only consults `Intl` at four. A repo-wide\nguard would belong alongside the rule, not here.\n\n**Verification** — every message rendered through the real `createI18n`\nat counts 0 / 1 / 2 / 5 / 21 in all 13 locales (65 cells, no `|` leak,\nno raw key): `fr` `0 nouveau client`, `pt` `0 novo cliente`, `ru` `21\nзаказ`, `pl` `2 zamówienia`. Full `vitest` suite green (125 files / 1995\ntests), `vue-tsc --build --force` clean, `eslint` and `prettier` clean.\n\n**Note for reviewers:** the non-English forms are my best-effort\ntranslations. `ru`/`pl` would particularly benefit from a native check —\n`new_this_week` assumes the elided subject is the cart (корзина /\nkoszyk), which is what the widget counts.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5683\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.56.0-pr-2430-469e-469ed074.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Maiia Diachkovskaia <mayapavlovna@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bf5cdbf700429d4a94c817cf8a519b89d912b2ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/bf5cdbf700429d4a94c817cf8a519b89d912b2ec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/7b727a37737f1fbb6fda9c8467d26043dbc5034e","verification":{"payload":"tree bf5cdbf700429d4a94c817cf8a519b89d912b2ec\nparent 12b0112e671a842f9886d4d544b9065e03822ad3\nauthor Ivan Kalachikov <ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com> 1787255805 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787255805 +0100\n\nfix(VCST-5683): pluralize sales-rep count messages (#2430)\n\n## Description\n\nThe **My Customers** table rendered `\"1 orders\"`. The call site already\npassed vue-i18n''s plural-choice index, but\n`sales_rep.my_customers.table.orders_count` carried a single form\n(`\"{count} orders\"`), so there was no singular to select. The dashboard\nstat sub-lines (`ordered_this_month`, `new_customers`, `new_this_week`,\n`of_recent_orders`) had the same shape.\n\n**What changed** — `client-app/modules/sales-rep/locales/*.json` and\nnothing else: 11 files, 44 lines. No component change; the plumbing was\nalready correct.\n\n| Forms | Locales | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| one | `ja`, `zh` | Neither marks number — untouched. Same for keys\nthat read the same either way (en `\"{count} ordered this month\"`, de\n`\"{count} in diesem Monat bestellt\"`). |\n| two | `de`, `en`, `es`, `fi`, `it`, `no`, `sv` | The built-in selector\npicks between them, and their plural is what zero takes. |\n| three | `fr`, `pt` | A leading **zero** slot, whose copy is the\nsingular — see below. |\n| four | `ru`, `pl` | The width at which `createIntlPluralRule`\n(VCST-5487, now on `dev`) consults the CLDR data. Three forms would fall\nback to index counting and render `\"5 заказа\"`. Their leading slot keeps\nthe numeric many form, which is what both languages take at zero. |\n\n**Agreement at zero (QA reopen).** French renders `\"0 nouveau client\"`,\nnot `\"0 nouveaux clients\"` — it files zero under CLDR `one`. A two-form\nmessage can''t express that: below four forms the rule defers to\nvue-i18n''s locale-blind `count === 1 ? 0 : 1`, so zero can only ever\nland on the plural. Three forms give zero a slot of its own, which is\nhow `reviews_count` is already written in these locales.\n\n`pt` gets the same treatment, as QA asked. CLDR files zero under `one`\nfor region-less `pt` and for `pt-BR`, and under `other` only for\n`pt-PT`. It reads correctly on the QA store purely because that store is\nconfigured `pt-PT` — switching to `pt-BR` would make `\"0 novos\nclientes\"` the same defect with no code change. One file serves both\nspellings and the rule short-circuits zero to slot 0 for every locale,\nso this picks a side: the file''s wording is Brazilian (`pedido`, `Meu\núltimo pedido`), so the zero slot is singular. `pt-PT` now reads `\"0\nnovo cliente\"` where CLDR would say plural.\n\n**Merged `dev` in.** VCST-5587 (#2433) replaced the \"placed today\" card\nwith `of_recent_orders`, deleting `placed_today`; its plural forms went\nwith the key. Everything `dev` added to these files since — `ytd`\n(#2429), `table.load_failed` (#2432), `of_recent_orders` (#2433) — is\npreserved: key sets are identical to `dev` in all 13 files, and the only\nvalues that differ are the 44 above.\n\n`of_recent_orders` came in with that merge carrying the same defect, so\nit is fixed here too: a participle agreeing with the elided \"orders\" in\n`es`/`fr`/`it`/`pt`/`sv`, the genitive after `из`/`z` in `ru`/`pl`.\n`de`, `en`, `fi` and `no` keep one form — nothing in them agrees.\n\n**No tests.** This is locale data; the repo has 117 locale JSONs and no\ntests over any of them, and `client-app/i18n.test.ts` already covers the\nrule these messages feed — including `rule(0, 3) === 0`, the path the\n`fr`/`pt` zero slot rides on. Asserting that `\"{count} order | {count}\norders\"` renders `\"1 order\"` would be testing vue-i18n, not this change.\n\nOne property of the convention worth knowing, since this PR is the first\nto lean on it: a **Slavic** message written with exactly three forms\nsilently loses the CLDR path and renders `\"1 заказа\"` with no error,\nbecause `createIntlPluralRule` only consults `Intl` at four. A repo-wide\nguard would belong alongside the rule, not here.\n\n**Verification** — every message rendered through the real `createI18n`\nat counts 0 / 1 / 2 / 5 / 21 in all 13 locales (65 cells, no `|` leak,\nno raw key): `fr` `0 nouveau client`, `pt` `0 novo cliente`, `ru` `21\nзаказ`, `pl` `2 zamówienia`. Full `vitest` suite green (125 files / 1995\ntests), `vue-tsc --build --force` clean, `eslint` and `prettier` clean.\n\n**Note for reviewers:** the non-English forms are my best-effort\ntranslations. `ru`/`pl` would particularly benefit from a native check —\n`new_this_week` assumes the elided subject is the cart (корзина /\nkoszyk), which is what the widget counts.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5683\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.56.0-pr-2430-469e-469ed074.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Maiia Diachkovskaia <mayapavlovna@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqh1v9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAU9oQAEpmtdzT1viXWeNZyE1g/znc\nbf3lSWTbvtLJ5g2el158JOJ8Y4J3PSW7ragTeR6v8vLt8bD7zaFLgFD8yroWhlUY\nwtcAUEfaz0b8VEwcq9HxVIlj+gzZeqPa5O3blC7XuAxedNGjNHX9tTrEKYM/Kgf1\nN13k7vR6Ywx9WbESAz/YKjvd7xrCtNv+ZYHnTLgtGdqQC8QJkE1x7uKTWMDNySSh\nTKrXLAiauihfgetkzsnKe85aYz1v1I4LeWjr4ot0djkxrI3Q6VTMTk8NlPpO9DaL\ntjPvrvJzeUooNDVSdVK/+SiCWNj15ZpPFIqbWvJmgZLP+3M5DobX+2xvSojoJCUK\nPDIRPjq6QbvSJ+faxC3TEB7pVyIezBGiMb4cR6Mav1gzvuSecigrzeXraqjkExql\niiUGEEJGpnJDliNbKaFHZQY7nZy5pyhuW0mbUeE2Zf8NyVG/ZEUUVbRas+zar89j\nr4F9WeIUtinSRg4xBFnHiUviURUff8Zsev16niAhOp+oVqIOj8qMZUtqojLb1vZh\nsLdpOjRx0nMTbeLJZgZ8UsvwZRyTC2GagCtbkxgtV6fvgh8ytV4r+5//c/rQS81d\nHQCu/MbJlP7e2H0NxDISf82vk86Gg3PlWvG2lyy/Ui0hRbmgwSeUVP4N7l9S8B5C\ndqkELB7AkTyPkdip1OQu\n=t/NP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T19:56:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/7b727a37737f1fbb6fda9c8467d26043dbc5034e","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDdiNzI3YTM3NzM3ZjFmYmI2ZmRhOWM4NDY3ZDI2MDQzZGJjNTAzNGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/12b0112e671a842f9886d4d544b9065e03822ad3","sha":"12b0112e671a842f9886d4d544b9065e03822ad3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/12b0112e671a842f9886d4d544b9065e03822ad3"}],"sha":"7b727a37737f1fbb6fda9c8467d26043dbc5034e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/7b727a37737f1fbb6fda9c8467d26043dbc5034e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18286430?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ivan-kalachikov","id":18286430,"login":"ivan-kalachikov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Mjg2NDMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/12b0112e671a842f9886d4d544b9065e03822ad3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T16:58:19Z","email":"ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com","name":"Ivan Kalachikov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T16:58:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VCST-5724): always notify a shared list on both channels (#2438)\n\n## Description\n\nRemoves the notification-channel choice from the Sales Rep \"Share list\nwith customer\" dialog. Publishing a list to a customer now always\nnotifies over both email and push, so the behavior is identical for a\nnew share and for editing an existing one (where the checkboxes used to\ndisappear).\n\n- `wishlist-customer-sharing.vue`: dropped the \"Send via\" fieldset and\nits two checkboxes; `sendCommunication` is called with `sendEmail: true,\nsendPush: true`, and the post-save notify no longer short-circuits on\n\"no channel selected\".\n- Removed the now-unused `share_channels_label` / `share_email_label` /\n`share_push_label` keys from all 14 locales.\n- Specs updated: the dialog asserts the checkboxes are absent and that\nboth channels are always requested.\n\nVerified: `vitest` sales-rep module 340/340 (25/25 in the sharing spec),\n`eslint` clean on the touched files, `prettier --check` clean, `vue-tsc\n--build --force` clean.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5724\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.56.0-pr-2438-ef16-ef1624b4.zip\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"38e25b0a480604cc9595cd7c034e8e4de42700b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/38e25b0a480604cc9595cd7c034e8e4de42700b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/12b0112e671a842f9886d4d544b9065e03822ad3","verification":{"payload":"tree 38e25b0a480604cc9595cd7c034e8e4de42700b7\nparent ab9f0a5ea21a37a028cb8565624e7917ba40a36c\nauthor Ivan Kalachikov <ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com> 1787245099 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787245099 +0100\n\nfeat(VCST-5724): always notify a shared list on both channels (#2438)\n\n## Description\n\nRemoves the notification-channel choice from the Sales Rep \"Share list\nwith customer\" dialog. Publishing a list to a customer now always\nnotifies over both email and push, so the behavior is identical for a\nnew share and for editing an existing one (where the checkboxes used to\ndisappear).\n\n- `wishlist-customer-sharing.vue`: dropped the \"Send via\" fieldset and\nits two checkboxes; `sendCommunication` is called with `sendEmail: true,\nsendPush: true`, and the post-save notify no longer short-circuits on\n\"no channel selected\".\n- Removed the now-unused `share_channels_label` / `share_email_label` /\n`share_push_label` keys from all 14 locales.\n- Specs updated: the dialog asserts the checkboxes are absent and that\nboth channels are always requested.\n\nVerified: `vitest` sales-rep module 340/340 (25/25 in the sharing spec),\n`eslint` clean on the touched files, `prettier --check` clean, `vue-tsc\n--build --force` clean.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5724\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.56.0-pr-2438-ef16-ef1624b4.zip\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhzIrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5HYQADJRNrSuEzY76sFgkPAAYi9I\nb3I4PxfZbMIWAVbdWW8Kk9Z+kJf1bDbN2i5zC9m/OqR38iV6rA9nqSWtBpR2ms9C\n5vlTUmjmB7aaInhdPzl9lQ1LWwSDMgn5J27sAv+kMyJrUmMgPy72GGC1PdRlp5b6\npcQdooABgDWh0RvQbK+f2AUCfNXJqZby12jmBrp7no5svHwfvPE1NZTXrIN/caRL\nzvXTsTGCxCYEleBenzcNg+j8m00nULFORkznpUwWNZttMnwIR3H82SyAsgxC5E48\n8kK+zt4BP2VkLNKA7nc4rg0cTvaw6L2twmqBHSZ81YIadOj3ltLJwzsFlaA4+PJw\nM7Wq3nK2Ou6f56mlp0qmBVAgLvWpUVZE8DlMf+iOIhPIrozhcT1Q0V76BCrg+Mkx\nF1Q+o4D+LHjSQkWvkyQeK/txVnBTZ9xUY3KiAi98LESPfqZ2F/UlzoLfVWiDfExZ\nkCgrSCqgp7b7MwwT3spYoVUCf4960ZE6hIER2Qet48B5PEjMicGgRwTPB9VaFjMn\n0LAxZC8gXb3c0X1705Gyh6y753XEqTu+oc/onJtWNF5GmoRaIqsj0kIfUEGxZQTe\nqM+IgMZ9EV5P6gmq3RMDplm2e4UdJ91HNqt02Qb96pfzwt4tIPS0vDFYguch66Jj\nkmN1rf30y+mOpMQP3AN+\n=r59G\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T16:58:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/12b0112e671a842f9886d4d544b9065e03822ad3","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDEyYjAxMTJlNjcxYTg0MmY5ODg2ZDRkNTQ0YjkwNjVlMDM4MjJhZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/ab9f0a5ea21a37a028cb8565624e7917ba40a36c","sha":"ab9f0a5ea21a37a028cb8565624e7917ba40a36c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/ab9f0a5ea21a37a028cb8565624e7917ba40a36c"}],"sha":"12b0112e671a842f9886d4d544b9065e03822ad3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/12b0112e671a842f9886d4d544b9065e03822ad3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/126832118?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yuskithedeveloper","id":126832118,"login":"yuskithedeveloper","node_id":"U_kgDOB49N9g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/ab9f0a5ea21a37a028cb8565624e7917ba40a36c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T15:34:21Z","email":"126832118+yuskithedeveloper@users.noreply.github.com","name":"yuskithedeveloper"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T15:34:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VCST-5647): SRH queries optimization (#2437)\n\n## Description\n\nStorefront half of VCST-5647: the Sales Rep Hub''s three statistics\nqueries are now **shaped from the cards the rep can actually see**,\ninstead of one hand-kept union selection serving both surfaces. Each\ncard declares its data sources (`needs`) in `layout/stat-cards.ts`; a\npure mapping turns the visible card set into `@include(if:)` flags plus\na per-query enabled/disabled decision. Declare a card''s `needs` and both\nthe document and the run/don''t-run decision follow — the two surfaces\ncan no longer pay for each other''s slices.\n\nPairs with the backend PR (money figures aggregated only when selected):\n<backend PR link>\n\n**Before → after**\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| customer profile, order buckets | 8 — including the `week` bucket and\nthe previous-week / previous-month baselines, for cards the profile does\nnot have | 5 |\n| dashboard, `mtd.average` | fetched, read by nothing | deleted outright\n|\n| dashboard, `ytd.average` | fetched on both surfaces | selected only\nwhere an Avg-order-value card exists (the profile) |\n| a hidden card | its slices fetched anyway | its slices drop out of the\ndocument; a query with no visible card left **does not run at all**\n(cart statistics and customer counts each exist for one card) |\n| cart statistics selection | quantities + `currencyCode` | quantities\nonly — with the backend PR, one grouped SQL per bucket instead of two |\n\n### Behaviour\n\n* **Per-card `needs` declarations.** Tokens name whole aggregation\nbuckets — the unit of backend cost, since the backend''s batch loader\nruns one grouped query per distinct date range. `averageOrderValue` is\nthe one field-level token: it rides inside the `ytd` bucket, so it is\ngated for bytes, not for a query.\n* **`@include(if:)` with required `Boolean!` flags, not separate\nper-surface documents** — a visibility-driven selection is variable at\nruntime, and N static documents can only express N static selections.\nOne document also keeps the two surfaces from drifting. Precedent:\n`searchProductsQuery`; unlike there the flags are required, so a\nforgotten one is a compile error rather than a surface quietly\nover-fetching.\n* **One-way publish/subscribe, not provide/inject.** `useSalesRepLayout`\npublishes the visible card set (`useStatDataNeeds`, module-local and\nscope-keyed like `layout/registry.ts`); the statistics composables read\nit. The layout is resolved inside `<LayoutSurface>`, a child of the page\nthat owns the composables, so it cannot be injected upwards.\n* **No new wait.** Queries hold until the layout read settles, but\n`salesRepLayout` is `no-cache` (~4 ms) and `<LayoutSurface>` already\nrenders nothing but a skeleton until it lands — figures fetched earlier\ncould not have been painted. A failed layout read settles too (registry\ndefaults), so the cards stay fed rather than empty behind an alert.\n`loading` includes the not-yet-settled phase, so cards never read as\nzeros in the meantime.\n* **Layout-edit mode widens the set back to every card**, because the\nparked zone renders the hidden ones.\n* **Honest scale** (measured while researching the ticket, localhost\nagainst the perf dataset): trimming buckets alone is hygiene, not a\nspeed-up — ~0.4 ms marginal per bucket, response payload 972 → 569\nbytes, and buckets run under `Task.WhenAll`. The prize is the dropped\nround trips: hiding one card can delete an entire query, and up to 8\naggregations.\n* **`types.ts` is hand-updated** to match the new schema — `yarn\ngenerate:graphql-types` needs a running backend carrying the new module\nbuild. A codegen run after the backend PR lands should be a no-op.\n* **Tests**: the visible-cards → flags mapping has its own suite\n(`layout/stat-data-needs.test.ts`), including the exact VCST-5647\nfinding (profile leaves week + month-over-month out) and a guard that\nevery registered card declares at least one source — a card nothing\nfetches would render a permanent zero. Sales-rep module suite: 355\npassing.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5647\n\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5648?focusedCommentId=105908\n(follow-up #2)\n\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.56.0-pr-2437-3b30-3b305f41.zip\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.56.0-pr-2437-315c-315cd30c.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8d7b545ecbd78708a9b8d8b976e7f06df76a59cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/8d7b545ecbd78708a9b8d8b976e7f06df76a59cc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/ab9f0a5ea21a37a028cb8565624e7917ba40a36c","verification":{"payload":"tree 8d7b545ecbd78708a9b8d8b976e7f06df76a59cc\nparent d57e3ad8b80c9de2f38b2f50b2540d04e0e001eb\nauthor yuskithedeveloper <126832118+yuskithedeveloper@users.noreply.github.com> 1787240061 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787240061 -0500\n\nfeat(VCST-5647): SRH queries optimization (#2437)\n\n## Description\n\nStorefront half of VCST-5647: the Sales Rep Hub''s three statistics\nqueries are now **shaped from the cards the rep can actually see**,\ninstead of one hand-kept union selection serving both surfaces. Each\ncard declares its data sources (`needs`) in `layout/stat-cards.ts`; a\npure mapping turns the visible card set into `@include(if:)` flags plus\na per-query enabled/disabled decision. Declare a card''s `needs` and both\nthe document and the run/don''t-run decision follow — the two surfaces\ncan no longer pay for each other''s slices.\n\nPairs with the backend PR (money figures aggregated only when selected):\n<backend PR link>\n\n**Before → after**\n\n| | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| customer profile, order buckets | 8 — including the `week` bucket and\nthe previous-week / previous-month baselines, for cards the profile does\nnot have | 5 |\n| dashboard, `mtd.average` | fetched, read by nothing | deleted outright\n|\n| dashboard, `ytd.average` | fetched on both surfaces | selected only\nwhere an Avg-order-value card exists (the profile) |\n| a hidden card | its slices fetched anyway | its slices drop out of the\ndocument; a query with no visible card left **does not run at all**\n(cart statistics and customer counts each exist for one card) |\n| cart statistics selection | quantities + `currencyCode` | quantities\nonly — with the backend PR, one grouped SQL per bucket instead of two |\n\n### Behaviour\n\n* **Per-card `needs` declarations.** Tokens name whole aggregation\nbuckets — the unit of backend cost, since the backend''s batch loader\nruns one grouped query per distinct date range. `averageOrderValue` is\nthe one field-level token: it rides inside the `ytd` bucket, so it is\ngated for bytes, not for a query.\n* **`@include(if:)` with required `Boolean!` flags, not separate\nper-surface documents** — a visibility-driven selection is variable at\nruntime, and N static documents can only express N static selections.\nOne document also keeps the two surfaces from drifting. Precedent:\n`searchProductsQuery`; unlike there the flags are required, so a\nforgotten one is a compile error rather than a surface quietly\nover-fetching.\n* **One-way publish/subscribe, not provide/inject.** `useSalesRepLayout`\npublishes the visible card set (`useStatDataNeeds`, module-local and\nscope-keyed like `layout/registry.ts`); the statistics composables read\nit. The layout is resolved inside `<LayoutSurface>`, a child of the page\nthat owns the composables, so it cannot be injected upwards.\n* **No new wait.** Queries hold until the layout read settles, but\n`salesRepLayout` is `no-cache` (~4 ms) and `<LayoutSurface>` already\nrenders nothing but a skeleton until it lands — figures fetched earlier\ncould not have been painted. A failed layout read settles too (registry\ndefaults), so the cards stay fed rather than empty behind an alert.\n`loading` includes the not-yet-settled phase, so cards never read as\nzeros in the meantime.\n* **Layout-edit mode widens the set back to every card**, because the\nparked zone renders the hidden ones.\n* **Honest scale** (measured while researching the ticket, localhost\nagainst the perf dataset): trimming buckets alone is hygiene, not a\nspeed-up — ~0.4 ms marginal per bucket, response payload 972 → 569\nbytes, and buckets run under `Task.WhenAll`. The prize is the dropped\nround trips: hiding one card can delete an entire query, and up to 8\naggregations.\n* **`types.ts` is hand-updated** to match the new schema — `yarn\ngenerate:graphql-types` needs a running backend carrying the new module\nbuild. A codegen run after the backend PR lands should be a no-op.\n* **Tests**: the visible-cards → flags mapping has its own suite\n(`layout/stat-data-needs.test.ts`), including the exact VCST-5647\nfinding (profile leaves week + month-over-month out) and a guard that\nevery registered card declares at least one source — a card nothing\nfetches would render a permanent zero. Sales-rep module suite: 355\npassing.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5647\n\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5648?focusedCommentId=105908\n(follow-up #2)\n\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.56.0-pr-2437-3b30-3b305f41.zip\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.56.0-pr-2437-315c-315cd30c.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhx59CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEZkQAFU4la3EOy9VuCMIopclwT/b\nd9Err4c82MftIioIo3MvRkYBVfOAGdOebhMI2du92Jo5Y8TqDcXrEBSkzg/Wh9/f\n70QAl9efd+2/5kb2YlCgq+nhowCC7Ii29WIP7fXWojJB0/LgjTz7x+524NrfhZSO\nGzLTEKFJBVoOvo3BIne8FCPHpv74LMZfpS5BpXKF2ajJ8jY01zbH5d20F2sAmEA7\nkLhKXwRfdS2jY8tJgeduq2eOaFmVdJJk4fIpWUbBxqfFc9bG7SYLO1W05kn8qQPW\n19McysTOBkeJ0zZyPA2kMtsPlOhoPf3jW/rfMIdbsOQzr52bx5m55LYaA4TmF5dz\nTWgQlF8oO9gGyI07t85/Mg8NIRDLCLJilgOYf0H0m4ZVks4DqzAzZJhgJ30m4PCV\nArwxZR4QQZy/N/HQmIpHKbk7FgO56inFl5CAAi16wxA4bYAb76izAWllrURqayOe\nkQvOl8y8RpKFqVeK22N3SzycgB/Do/VBlbDETy5cSFSm6jA9Dco/CBgUh0vJf0J8\nU8wz3fhxKm3B6gimab5I+tslz1lFijRj/itf2IOjTVzvS0cln6pUchXgHaUhhVBw\n6VRQXYXWxNtfCD1Lti5BHUmXHzbBzZneSgzVhJigNi/KvpJA0KqoJrk+Qc3KANqM\n1g0noHg5PNiZZaxRBWSk\n=T2Su\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T15:34:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/ab9f0a5ea21a37a028cb8565624e7917ba40a36c","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKGFiOWYwYTVlYTIxYTM3YTAyOGNiODU2NTYyNGU3OTE3YmE0MGEzNmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/d57e3ad8b80c9de2f38b2f50b2540d04e0e001eb","sha":"d57e3ad8b80c9de2f38b2f50b2540d04e0e001eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/d57e3ad8b80c9de2f38b2f50b2540d04e0e001eb"}],"sha":"ab9f0a5ea21a37a028cb8565624e7917ba40a36c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/ab9f0a5ea21a37a028cb8565624e7917ba40a36c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/126832118?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yuskithedeveloper","id":126832118,"login":"yuskithedeveloper","node_id":"U_kgDOB49N9g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/d57e3ad8b80c9de2f38b2f50b2540d04e0e001eb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T12:22:57Z","email":"126832118+yuskithedeveloper@users.noreply.github.com","name":"yuskithedeveloper"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T12:22:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VCST-5588): sales rep hub active carts (#2416)\n\n## Description\n\nStorefront half of VCST-5588: the **Active carts** stat card now shows\n**item quantities** instead of a cart count + money total, and the Hub\ndashboard and the customer page render it from **one shared source**\ninstead of two hand-written copies.\n\nRequires the backend PR (new `selectedItemQuantity` /\n`unselectedItemQuantity` fields):\nhttps://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-module-sales-rep/pull/10\n\n**Before → after**\n\n| slot | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| value | `3` (number of carts) | `3` **items** (quantity selected for\ncheckout) |\n| sub-figure | `$0.00` (cart total) | `12 not for checkout` (quantity\n*not* selected) |\n| delta | `2 new this week` (carts created this week) | `3 items this\nweek` (**selected** items whose line was touched this week) |\n| customer page | its own card: the cart''s money total, no sub, no delta\n| the same card, scoped to that organization |\n\n### What the three figures mean, precisely\n\n* **Value** — summed `Quantity` of the cart lines with\n`SelectedForCheckout = true`, across the carts in scope.\n* **Sub** — the same sum for `SelectedForCheckout = false` (the parked\nremainder).\n* **Delta** — the **value''s own metric, windowed**: still only\n*selected* lines, restricted to those whose `ModifiedDate` falls in the\ncurrent week. It is **not** \"all items touched this week\" — an\nunselected line touched this week is counted nowhere in this card''s\ndelta. The selected flag is read as of *now*, not as of the window, so a\nline selected on Monday and deselected on Thursday does not appear.\n* **Scope** — the dashboard aggregates every organization the rep\nserves; the customer page passes `organizationId` and the backend\nnarrows to it. Same builder, different payloads; sharing code does\n**not** make the two surfaces show the same numbers.\n\n### Behaviour\n\n* **One card definition, two surfaces.** New\n`useSalesRepActiveCartsCard(organizationId?)` owns the card *and* its\ndata source; `useSalesRepDashboardWidgets` and\n`useSalesRepCustomerWidgets` each drop it in. This is the ticket''s\n\"single shared calculation source — no page-specific logic\" on the\nclient side, and it removed the duplicated `useSalesRepCartStatistics`\nwiring. Card position on both pages is unchanged.\n* **Customer page scoping is data-only** — the composable takes the\norganization and the backend authorizes + narrows to it; verified\nagainst three of the rep''s organizations (the one with a cart returns\nits quantities, the others return zero).\n* **`<StatWidget>` gained an optional `valueSuffix`** — a de-emphasized\nunit rendered after the value (\"3 **items**\") so the number stays the\nfocal point. Generic on purpose: the same widget renders orders and\ncustomer counts.\n* **i18n:** added `items_unit`, `not_for_checkout`, `items_this_week`;\nremoved the now-unused `new_this_week` and the singular `active_cart`\nlabel. All 13 locales, each matching that locale''s existing checkout\nwording (de \"nicht zur Kasse\", fr \"hors paiement\", ru \"не к оформлению\",\nzh \"件不结账\", …). `items_unit` / `items_this_week` use vue-i18n plural\nforms (`\"item | items\"`, house style per `locales/*.json`\n`products_found_message`), so a count of 1 reads \"1 item\", not \"1\nitems\"; single form for ja/zh/de.\n* **Query trimmed** — with both cards reading only quantities, `count`\nand `total` are no longer selected, which also drops the storefront''s\nlast dependency on the persisted `Cart.Total` (unreliable for carts\nbuilt through short-cart mutations).\n* **`types.ts` is hand-updated** to match the new schema — `yarn\ngenerate:graphql-types` needs a running backend carrying the new module\nbuild, so it could not be run here. A codegen run after the backend PR\nlands should be a no-op; the schema-level `CustomerCartStatisticsPeriod`\n/ `…Comparison` types were updated in both `core` and the module for\nthat reason.\n\n### Breaking changes\n\n* **Card meaning changed** on both surfaces: the customer page tile was\na money total and is now a quantity. Layout **block ids are unchanged**\n— dashboard `active_carts`, profile `active_cart` (kept singular\ndeliberately so saved customer-profile layouts keep matching); only the\nprofile''s caption changed to \"Active carts\".\n\n### Screenshots\n<img width=\"1436\" height=\"243\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b597cf7c-3d1f-4e8a-9358-c5391d4d4886\"\n/>\n\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5588\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.56.0-pr-2416-efad-efadb479.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"48a4a39a68e2960872e91ddb245019d5014a44db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/48a4a39a68e2960872e91ddb245019d5014a44db"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/d57e3ad8b80c9de2f38b2f50b2540d04e0e001eb","verification":{"payload":"tree 48a4a39a68e2960872e91ddb245019d5014a44db\nparent cf276947c575d376005c138373d78f0b92f8fa18\nauthor yuskithedeveloper <126832118+yuskithedeveloper@users.noreply.github.com> 1787228577 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787228577 -0500\n\nfeat(VCST-5588): sales rep hub active carts (#2416)\n\n## Description\n\nStorefront half of VCST-5588: the **Active carts** stat card now shows\n**item quantities** instead of a cart count + money total, and the Hub\ndashboard and the customer page render it from **one shared source**\ninstead of two hand-written copies.\n\nRequires the backend PR (new `selectedItemQuantity` /\n`unselectedItemQuantity` fields):\nhttps://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-module-sales-rep/pull/10\n\n**Before → after**\n\n| slot | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| value | `3` (number of carts) | `3` **items** (quantity selected for\ncheckout) |\n| sub-figure | `$0.00` (cart total) | `12 not for checkout` (quantity\n*not* selected) |\n| delta | `2 new this week` (carts created this week) | `3 items this\nweek` (**selected** items whose line was touched this week) |\n| customer page | its own card: the cart''s money total, no sub, no delta\n| the same card, scoped to that organization |\n\n### What the three figures mean, precisely\n\n* **Value** — summed `Quantity` of the cart lines with\n`SelectedForCheckout = true`, across the carts in scope.\n* **Sub** — the same sum for `SelectedForCheckout = false` (the parked\nremainder).\n* **Delta** — the **value''s own metric, windowed**: still only\n*selected* lines, restricted to those whose `ModifiedDate` falls in the\ncurrent week. It is **not** \"all items touched this week\" — an\nunselected line touched this week is counted nowhere in this card''s\ndelta. The selected flag is read as of *now*, not as of the window, so a\nline selected on Monday and deselected on Thursday does not appear.\n* **Scope** — the dashboard aggregates every organization the rep\nserves; the customer page passes `organizationId` and the backend\nnarrows to it. Same builder, different payloads; sharing code does\n**not** make the two surfaces show the same numbers.\n\n### Behaviour\n\n* **One card definition, two surfaces.** New\n`useSalesRepActiveCartsCard(organizationId?)` owns the card *and* its\ndata source; `useSalesRepDashboardWidgets` and\n`useSalesRepCustomerWidgets` each drop it in. This is the ticket''s\n\"single shared calculation source — no page-specific logic\" on the\nclient side, and it removed the duplicated `useSalesRepCartStatistics`\nwiring. Card position on both pages is unchanged.\n* **Customer page scoping is data-only** — the composable takes the\norganization and the backend authorizes + narrows to it; verified\nagainst three of the rep''s organizations (the one with a cart returns\nits quantities, the others return zero).\n* **`<StatWidget>` gained an optional `valueSuffix`** — a de-emphasized\nunit rendered after the value (\"3 **items**\") so the number stays the\nfocal point. Generic on purpose: the same widget renders orders and\ncustomer counts.\n* **i18n:** added `items_unit`, `not_for_checkout`, `items_this_week`;\nremoved the now-unused `new_this_week` and the singular `active_cart`\nlabel. All 13 locales, each matching that locale''s existing checkout\nwording (de \"nicht zur Kasse\", fr \"hors paiement\", ru \"не к оформлению\",\nzh \"件不结账\", …). `items_unit` / `items_this_week` use vue-i18n plural\nforms (`\"item | items\"`, house style per `locales/*.json`\n`products_found_message`), so a count of 1 reads \"1 item\", not \"1\nitems\"; single form for ja/zh/de.\n* **Query trimmed** — with both cards reading only quantities, `count`\nand `total` are no longer selected, which also drops the storefront''s\nlast dependency on the persisted `Cart.Total` (unreliable for carts\nbuilt through short-cart mutations).\n* **`types.ts` is hand-updated** to match the new schema — `yarn\ngenerate:graphql-types` needs a running backend carrying the new module\nbuild, so it could not be run here. A codegen run after the backend PR\nlands should be a no-op; the schema-level `CustomerCartStatisticsPeriod`\n/ `…Comparison` types were updated in both `core` and the module for\nthat reason.\n\n### Breaking changes\n\n* **Card meaning changed** on both surfaces: the customer page tile was\na money total and is now a quantity. Layout **block ids are unchanged**\n— dashboard `active_carts`, profile `active_cart` (kept singular\ndeliberately so saved customer-profile layouts keep matching); only the\nprofile''s caption changed to \"Active carts\".\n\n### Screenshots\n<img width=\"1436\" height=\"243\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b597cf7c-3d1f-4e8a-9358-c5391d4d4886\"\n/>\n\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5588\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.56.0-pr-2416-efad-efadb479.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhvGhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkiUQAIUgMem3IyMC2WgAmw6UCuR5\nljdraPQa+dSQVWzYVrG+L3ac8FvLHfzO6rEtx2gu7Wl5ZJWNv9fyQUjzAusX+8Xc\nHIclP3SCFztign3KQHqI9vR01X/jIzsJU0Su/5kWqPIMiy7rkh/ukLbVR1kZzS7Y\nst+bxWMVqMLVA+ORTVicshpZOShYi3oNqfq1F5CGPQPQfLBhflltuIM3PX27hGuc\nE3sQQrXxIV+wBuexQDHVZxdiR2TdDgN24FFmHw7bHfIzqaR9ODtOzFE/cowVxNWL\nfB+1cY3DBWgm/nhTH/UlWE+xHC693iak7vq0NfDvOQWMI2lMrhjCSDVpyreViwxa\ndDrdMeTKZWdZVfgkHMVEUR6VpICtWA/zEq278NNXgsrSE65/6fqBllg7Qx//JUzu\nqpMmVc4idQvMbGB7HO/aeARtMI6aO7KGF0jgNnqvi+gS6RMOGT3xgWwClgJ8Ulp0\ngRxXOz4A9UwwbY8eWnq/LrpfXBcOIeIEq1dq8FfdHcD1hoQcw6kyLxhqydJiigxu\neeGsQp5jj+eegP+623YYWh4aMEkIZJPEq2y8628HxpTnERXgBiAJdykCNfBppSJB\nfhUiQP9sSACEWrc3ZbnVJ5F7aaLG85aaeImg3EDWm3oQ4Aqxv9LhmU706I8R+yIT\n2lAL6g7pmUGuNYW6p5z5\n=wfAD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T12:22:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/d57e3ad8b80c9de2f38b2f50b2540d04e0e001eb","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKGQ1N2UzYWQ4YjgwYzlkZTJmMzhiMmY1MGIyNTQwZDA0ZTBlMDAxZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/cf276947c575d376005c138373d78f0b92f8fa18","sha":"cf276947c575d376005c138373d78f0b92f8fa18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/cf276947c575d376005c138373d78f0b92f8fa18"}],"sha":"d57e3ad8b80c9de2f38b2f50b2540d04e0e001eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/d57e3ad8b80c9de2f38b2f50b2540d04e0e001eb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16372194?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/goldenmaya","id":16372194,"login":"goldenmaya","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzcyMTk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/cf276947c575d376005c138373d78f0b92f8fa18/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T09:28:50Z","email":"mayapavlovna@gmail.com","name":"Maiia Diachkovskaia"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T09:28:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VCST-5487): update customer-reviews design (#2417)\n\n## Description\n<img width=\"1177\" height=\"627\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-08-03 at 08 40 28\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e4520a5f-161d-4fe0-b0ea-d5bc4f772e97\"\n/>\n<img width=\"855\" height=\"538\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-08-03 at 08 38 23\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ca20095e-9e4a-49e3-86ab-fb5cf2fbda21\"\n/>\n<img width=\"876\" height=\"397\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-08-03 at 08 43 27\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c66cbdee-43bd-4da3-b75a-b3e273cc79a3\"\n/>\n<img width=\"943\" height=\"625\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-08-03 at 08 45 58\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6d1f00b5-8558-4ab1-ab07-9df747ee29fb\"\n/>\n<img width=\"865\" height=\"615\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-08-03 at 08 38 59\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0d9fd830-8a68-479c-8f29-1c688730eb9e\"\n/>\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\n<!-- Put link to your task in Jira here -->\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5487\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.55.0-pr-2417-00fc-00fcc90e.zip\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Global i18n plural behavior and a shared VcRating change can affect\nstorefront copy and any rating UI; review submission flow is unchanged\nbut is user-visible.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> **Customer reviews (VCST-5487)** gets a layout refresh:\n`ProductRating` shows stars, a one-decimal score, and optional\npluralized review count; the product page enables that count. The\nreviews list moves to BEM styling, smaller controls, and **photo\nthumbnails** that open a new **`ReviewImagesModal`** (carousel, keyboard\nnav) instead of inline Swiper strips.\n> \n> **`VcRating`** switches from shape masks to **outline star icons**\nwith **per-star fractional fill** (not just half-stars), plus larger\ntouch targets and focus styles for interactive mode.\n> \n> **i18n** adds **`createIntlPluralRule`** via `Intl.PluralRules` for\nfour-form messages (e.g. Russian/Polish review counts), registers rules\nfor both culture names and two-letter locale keys at boot, and keeps\nvue-i18n’s default behavior for two- and three-form legacy strings.\n**`@vc-frontend/core`** bumps to **1.2.0** with an optional\n`pluralRuleLocales` on `createI18n` and regenerated GraphQL types\n(`StoreAssetUrl`, `sectionName`).\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n00fcc90e60b5f19fd98e1f5516ebcfdf0cc87eaa. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Ivan Kalachikov <ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"4fd9eca44152da0497f218323467bc0371cc0d13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/4fd9eca44152da0497f218323467bc0371cc0d13"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/cf276947c575d376005c138373d78f0b92f8fa18","verification":{"payload":"tree 4fd9eca44152da0497f2183