n> **`VcRating`** switches from shape masks to **outline star icons**\nwith **per-star fractional fill** (not just half-stars), plus larger\ntouch targets and focus styles for interactive mode.\n> \n> **i18n** adds **`createIntlPluralRule`** via `Intl.PluralRules` for\nfour-form messages (e.g. Russian/Polish review counts), registers rules\nfor both culture names and two-letter locale keys at boot, and keeps\nvue-i18n’s default behavior for two- and three-form legacy strings.\n**`@vc-frontend/core`** bumps to **1.2.0** with an optional\n`pluralRuleLocales` on `createI18n` and regenerated GraphQL types\n(`StoreAssetUrl`, `sectionName`).\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n00fcc90e60b5f19fd98e1f5516ebcfdf0cc87eaa. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Ivan Kalachikov <ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhCXSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvdAQAEeYrr7SeEANYip0TL6HBZ4U\nu7+5+PVnvtgYxfYwt2OX9fJx1oOk1I9wJfZqMmznXEKPaOMMDo7t6XMkWe+zDlJ5\nLc5k1dKTjN12xdpuzD7k76Uf4ZfUDWVPG0g+sZdMHoIdrnXdx1djGmwZv8w893C9\nYYqMw4DZ57HpCE/hIgxItbgrwreOYVQ8Ed7uT+PeJpYpS8okPTB/AaYwYNUtGbvU\nR0Yu7HjJ7QwcEuNuArWOy2MHb9qXfAiLJu/LanngyMrmyjGXxoh0+1ep2xVFKp+V\nKkDFa+/jkDLUqK373yNalOvVHv+zLZPgjfVYQpRZc29rrgX6kwultQXUazdhV8qF\n+L5RlTF7YfvwA5edr9IcfCOd8riFnB8wkHu4kdf4WQx+ZCsy3PfVYAtYR17THuW1\nk0qVUgSbmo5Ho0288AtfQUdWWlf6tfqFwD9YwD0FykC6LX/51E++TcKTjVMchr+h\nhtD2ebbzZPYqQO+vp3umHFXtoYAitB0PTw54bAqUO6j4+46xNPQtvL/n+8msQMhK\nD/uTka2n25pyPZ4blSZ0molvDL2UgeQWLGTNRfq8p2njxib0e6saAWOU3t3YztY7\nWAXzWQSqv4pDZ/1xmzGCemim8RSaGVedwHiu/vnXHzdsYBgYytf382ynfAVvikSb\nLvhLy0g9X8GNZ0tIYQfj\n=lqkJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T09:28:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/cf276947c575d376005c138373d78f0b92f8fa18","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKGNmMjc2OTQ3YzU3NWQzNzYwMDVjMTM4MzczZDc4ZjBiOTJmOGZhMTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/8c91aedd17954560f2eca5db90ecfc18871a7aa6","sha":"8c91aedd17954560f2eca5db90ecfc18871a7aa6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/8c91aedd17954560f2eca5db90ecfc18871a7aa6"}],"sha":"cf276947c575d376005c138373d78f0b92f8fa18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/cf276947c575d376005c138373d78f0b92f8fa18"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18286430?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ivan-kalachikov","id":18286430,"login":"ivan-kalachikov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Mjg2NDMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/8c91aedd17954560f2eca5db90ecfc18871a7aa6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T09:22:25Z","email":"ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com","name":"Ivan Kalachikov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T09:22:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(VCST-5682): no page-level error toast for a failed Sales Rep hub widget (#2432)\n\n## Description\n\nA failing Sales Rep statistics query rendered its inline \"Couldn''t\nload…\" state **and** raised the global _\"Apologies for the\ninconvenience. Our server is currently experiencing technical issues.\"_\ntoast, so one degraded card read as a page-level outage.\n\n**Why the module couldn''t fix this itself.** Every sales-rep composable\nalready declares \"No toast; the widget/page names the failure instead\"\nin its own `onError` — but the toast is emitted from `errorHandlerLink`,\nan Apollo `onError` link in the shared chain, below the composable. Four\nescape hatches were checked and all dead-end:\n\n| Attempt | Why it doesn''t work |\n|---|---|\n| `errorPolicy: \"ignore\"` / `\"all\"` on the query | Only changes what the\n*observable* surfaces; the link still runs beneath it |\n| Module-scoped link / second `ApolloClient` | The chain is assembled in\n`core/api/graphql/config/links/index.ts`, the client provided at\nbootstrap — both core |\n| Intercepting the broadcast event | `broadcast.on` only *adds*\nlisteners; it can''t cancel core''s `unhandledErrorEvent` → toast handler\n|\n| Muting the `\"GenericError\"` notification group while the hub is\nmounted | Would also swallow genuinely page-level failures from\nunrelated queries (cart, user) |\n\nSo the seam has to be in core, which is what the ticket suggests. Core\nfootprint is kept to two files.\n\n**The change.** A per-operation opt-out carried in the Apollo operation\ncontext:\n\n```ts\n// client-app/core/api/graphql/consts.ts\nexport const SUPPRESS_ERROR_NOTIFICATIONS_CONTEXT: ErrorNotificationsContextType = {\n  suppressErrorNotifications: true,\n};\n```\n\n`errorHandlerLink` honours it in its **two generic-toast branches only**\n— `ServerError.Unhandled` and the unrecognized-`graphQLErrors` fallback.\n`Unauthorized`, `Forbidden`, `UserLocked` and `PasswordExpired` drive\nnavigation (sign-in redirect, no-access page, `/blocked`,\nchange-password) rather than a notification, so they still fire for an\nopted-out operation.\n\n**Scope.** Set on all twelve hub reads, not just the three statistics\nqueries named in the ticket — QA reproduced the toast on\n`/company/my-customers` and on the search-active path too, and every one\nof these composables already claims its failure inline: order/cart\nstatistics, customer counts, my-customers list, customers-count badge,\norders, top sellers, customer profile header, share-customer picker,\nreps list, rule discovery, saved layout.\n\nMutations are deliberately untouched — a failed user action still\ndeserves a toast. That includes `saveSalesRepLayout`, which shows\n`saveFailed` inline as well; worth a separate UX call if the double\nsignal there is unwanted.\n\n### Review follow-up\n\nThree review findings, all verified against the code before fixing:\n\n1. **Auth outcomes under suppression.** `toServerError()` maps `code ===\n\"\"` to `Unhandled` and resolves it ahead of the auth codes, so an\nopted-out response carrying both hit the early return and emitted\nnothing — contradicting this file''s own comment. An opted-out operation\nnow drops the two inputs that can only mean `Unhandled` (a network\nerror, and the `\"\"`-coded errors) and classifies what is left, so all\nfour auth outcomes survive: `Unauthorized`, `Forbidden`, `UserLocked`,\n`PasswordExpired`. That includes a 401/403, which arrives as a network\nerror carrying its GraphQL errors on `result` — the only shape where the\ntwo co-occur, and the one the test harness previously could not produce.\nWith notifications on, the computation is the untouched\n`toServerError(networkError, graphQLErrors)`, so `dev` behaviour outside\nthe opt-out is byte-identical.\n2. **My Sales Reps had no failure signal.** The page rendered\n`variant=\"empty\"` for a dead fetch and for a legitimately empty list\nalike, and this PR removed the fallback toast that was its only other\nsignal. `useSalesReps` now returns `error` and the page shows the\n`variant=\"error\"` failure view with a new `sales_rep.table.load_failed`\n(13 locales), the same shape My Customers got in VCST-5586.\n3. **The opt-in was a bare constant.** All twelve reads now go through\n`useSalesRepHubQuery`, which bakes the context in (a caller context\nmerges, but cannot switch the opt-out off), and `no-restricted-syntax`\nkeeps direct `useQuery` / `useLazyQuery` out of `modules/sales-rep` —\nthe wrapper and the tests are the only exemptions. The ambiguous\nmutation is resolved rather than documented: `sendCustomerCommunication`\nopts out too, because its modal already raises an error toast naming the\nchannel that failed, so the generic one only stacked a second toast on\none action. `saveSalesRepLayout` keeps the generic toast and now records\nwhy.\n\n### Verification\n\n- New `client-app/core/api/graphql/config/error-handler.test.ts` (4\ntests) drives the real link: notifies on a network failure and on an\nunrecognized GraphQL error, stays silent for all three suppressible\nshapes when opted out, and still emits all four auth events when opted\nout. Proven red on `dev`''s handler — it emitted `unhandled_error`,\n`unhandled_error`, `graphql_error` where the fix emits nothing.\n- New\n`client-app/modules/sales-rep/composables/error-notifications.test.ts`\n(13 tests) mounts each of the twelve hub composables against a real\n`ApolloClient` whose link chain is `[errorHandlerLink,\nalwaysFailingLink]` and asserts no broadcast emit. A thirteenth case\nruns the same query *without* the context and asserts the toast still\nfires, so the suite can''t pass by never firing at all.\n- `yarn vitest run --dir client-app` — 119 files, 1898 tests passed\n(new: `pages/sales-reps.test.ts` for the four states,\n`useSalesRepHubQuery.test.ts` for the option merge, plus the mixed-code\nauth case and the opted-out mutation in the two suites above; each new\ncase was proven red against the code it guards)\n- `yarn vue-tsc --build --force` — clean\n- `yarn eslint <changed files>` — no new errors or warnings (one\npre-existing `no-unnecessary-type-assertion` on\n`serializeError(networkError as Error)` was auto-fixed by the pre-commit\nhook)\n- `yarn build` — clean, no new circular-dependency or chunk warnings\n\nNot verified in a browser — reproducing needs a Sales Rep account on a\nlive backend with one `POST /graphql` operation forced to fail.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5682\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.56.0-pr-2432-fbea-fbead07b.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ceb0d3d7d6bb656fee513056f24be492ac916ebe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/ceb0d3d7d6bb656fee513056f24be492ac916ebe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/8c91aedd17954560f2eca5db90ecfc18871a7aa6","verification":{"payload":"tree ceb0d3d7d6bb656fee513056f24be492ac916ebe\nparent a8f4578eee26e88d40f72a7502396fe9423f1fad\nauthor Ivan Kalachikov <ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com> 1787044945 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787044945 +0100\n\nfix(VCST-5682): no page-level error toast for a failed Sales Rep hub widget (#2432)\n\n## Description\n\nA failing Sales Rep statistics query rendered its inline \"Couldn''t\nload…\" state **and** raised the global _\"Apologies for the\ninconvenience. Our server is currently experiencing technical issues.\"_\ntoast, so one degraded card read as a page-level outage.\n\n**Why the module couldn''t fix this itself.** Every sales-rep composable\nalready declares \"No toast; the widget/page names the failure instead\"\nin its own `onError` — but the toast is emitted from `errorHandlerLink`,\nan Apollo `onError` link in the shared chain, below the composable. Four\nescape hatches were checked and all dead-end:\n\n| Attempt | Why it doesn''t work |\n|---|---|\n| `errorPolicy: \"ignore\"` / `\"all\"` on the query | Only changes what the\n*observable* surfaces; the link still runs beneath it |\n| Module-scoped link / second `ApolloClient` | The chain is assembled in\n`core/api/graphql/config/links/index.ts`, the client provided at\nbootstrap — both core |\n| Intercepting the broadcast event | `broadcast.on` only *adds*\nlisteners; it can''t cancel core''s `unhandledErrorEvent` → toast handler\n|\n| Muting the `\"GenericError\"` notification group while the hub is\nmounted | Would also swallow genuinely page-level failures from\nunrelated queries (cart, user) |\n\nSo the seam has to be in core, which is what the ticket suggests. Core\nfootprint is kept to two files.\n\n**The change.** A per-operation opt-out carried in the Apollo operation\ncontext:\n\n```ts\n// client-app/core/api/graphql/consts.ts\nexport const SUPPRESS_ERROR_NOTIFICATIONS_CONTEXT: ErrorNotificationsContextType = {\n  suppressErrorNotifications: true,\n};\n```\n\n`errorHandlerLink` honours it in its **two generic-toast branches only**\n— `ServerError.Unhandled` and the unrecognized-`graphQLErrors` fallback.\n`Unauthorized`, `Forbidden`, `UserLocked` and `PasswordExpired` drive\nnavigation (sign-in redirect, no-access page, `/blocked`,\nchange-password) rather than a notification, so they still fire for an\nopted-out operation.\n\n**Scope.** Set on all twelve hub reads, not just the three statistics\nqueries named in the ticket — QA reproduced the toast on\n`/company/my-customers` and on the search-active path too, and every one\nof these composables already claims its failure inline: order/cart\nstatistics, customer counts, my-customers list, customers-count badge,\norders, top sellers, customer profile header, share-customer picker,\nreps list, rule discovery, saved layout.\n\nMutations are deliberately untouched — a failed user action still\ndeserves a toast. That includes `saveSalesRepLayout`, which shows\n`saveFailed` inline as well; worth a separate UX call if the double\nsignal there is unwanted.\n\n### Review follow-up\n\nThree review findings, all verified against the code before fixing:\n\n1. **Auth outcomes under suppression.** `toServerError()` maps `code ===\n\"\"` to `Unhandled` and resolves it ahead of the auth codes, so an\nopted-out response carrying both hit the early return and emitted\nnothing — contradicting this file''s own comment. An opted-out operation\nnow drops the two inputs that can only mean `Unhandled` (a network\nerror, and the `\"\"`-coded errors) and classifies what is left, so all\nfour auth outcomes survive: `Unauthorized`, `Forbidden`, `UserLocked`,\n`PasswordExpired`. That includes a 401/403, which arrives as a network\nerror carrying its GraphQL errors on `result` — the only shape where the\ntwo co-occur, and the one the test harness previously could not produce.\nWith notifications on, the computation is the untouched\n`toServerError(networkError, graphQLErrors)`, so `dev` behaviour outside\nthe opt-out is byte-identical.\n2. **My Sales Reps had no failure signal.** The page rendered\n`variant=\"empty\"` for a dead fetch and for a legitimately empty list\nalike, and this PR removed the fallback toast that was its only other\nsignal. `useSalesReps` now returns `error` and the page shows the\n`variant=\"error\"` failure view with a new `sales_rep.table.load_failed`\n(13 locales), the same shape My Customers got in VCST-5586.\n3. **The opt-in was a bare constant.** All twelve reads now go through\n`useSalesRepHubQuery`, which bakes the context in (a caller context\nmerges, but cannot switch the opt-out off), and `no-restricted-syntax`\nkeeps direct `useQuery` / `useLazyQuery` out of `modules/sales-rep` —\nthe wrapper and the tests are the only exemptions. The ambiguous\nmutation is resolved rather than documented: `sendCustomerCommunication`\nopts out too, because its modal already raises an error toast naming the\nchannel that failed, so the generic one only stacked a second toast on\none action. `saveSalesRepLayout` keeps the generic toast and now records\nwhy.\n\n### Verification\n\n- New `client-app/core/api/graphql/config/error-handler.test.ts` (4\ntests) drives the real link: notifies on a network failure and on an\nunrecognized GraphQL error, stays silent for all three suppressible\nshapes when opted out, and still emits all four auth events when opted\nout. Proven red on `dev`''s handler — it emitted `unhandled_error`,\n`unhandled_error`, `graphql_error` where the fix emits nothing.\n- New\n`client-app/modules/sales-rep/composables/error-notifications.test.ts`\n(13 tests) mounts each of the twelve hub composables against a real\n`ApolloClient` whose link chain is `[errorHandlerLink,\nalwaysFailingLink]` and asserts no broadcast emit. A thirteenth case\nruns the same query *without* the context and asserts the toast still\nfires, so the suite can''t pass by never firing at all.\n- `yarn vitest run --dir client-app` — 119 files, 1898 tests passed\n(new: `pages/sales-reps.test.ts` for the four states,\n`useSalesRepHubQuery.test.ts` for the option merge, plus the mixed-code\nauth case and the opted-out mutation in the two suites above; each new\ncase was proven red against the code it guards)\n- `yarn vue-tsc --build --force` — clean\n- `yarn eslint <changed files>` — no new errors or warnings (one\npre-existing `no-unnecessary-type-assertion` on\n`serializeError(networkError as Error)` was auto-fixed by the pre-commit\nhook)\n- `yarn build` — clean, no new circular-dependency or chunk warnings\n\nNot verified in a browser — reproducing needs a Sales Rep account on a\nlive backend with one `POST /graphql` operation forced to fail.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5682\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.56.0-pr-2432-fbea-fbead07b.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhCRRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAboUQAJBUWG+ITm0WU1C5NeHxbJM/\nOOVPMzdjsOcXvdp7aa7o+7tngsydnQ+uQJsdOzmAoldI4h0NR3DWQMj793HgJ06k\nsqZieMQDRkcRP0MJxZoNouuBxtdmgg5xbpjpbp2ssuyaJ9EzWK/ZUnX0PiromyEU\nsWaldHnhvAKN0FYTh+M8/ZJNDdrEVofIrEmUQ+OiqBmsvs9ZTgjePRpORwvm6fa8\nFkKqZEmZD+Srybu9brybzmh21qLR4vSvTEEg6Ibe6XL+cKc9bU680s6VQalTL1eD\nEEqo+oQVBsAZRvCx4FFOpSwL3rSEDJ9z9W+hEMZlHAZ5QNuTPiFvmURHIkBDxKvt\nbMlZ9gSWQI2ZVkqKylP+ZX3PaZPpVuIgoGAu3KmfoLlwAQD2oyp3m9SwUm/yko+S\n0NEZT5SjcxdEe8BGUeWip+eA62R9AYeEmO4XkV8UG1AqTxIaMwHUT1nZ/lizlv2g\nswMmCrZUFML9JOIYnivvcMFBXDWwvwOKyZyt3wTIQT9dv0V0Ah6sdObGDRc4ab8M\n2J26JqaSu4ZyZKy3v0b13ypSmf4x++4yQoB7CKgAWAycVHyqavp6R4LE1ChDzp87\n648K1hbzT/hYZoSPULFrVyRIHYElzHkEPd58v4Kk6PofhmL43X65ec3dolkZ3kkC\n6xPambOgA+8KWDzctNC9\n=hLcX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T09:22:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/8c91aedd17954560f2eca5db90ecfc18871a7aa6","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDhjOTFhZWRkMTc5NTQ1NjBmMmVjYTVkYjkwZWNmYzE4ODcxYTdhYTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/a8f4578eee26e88d40f72a7502396fe9423f1fad","sha":"a8f4578eee26e88d40f72a7502396fe9423f1fad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/a8f4578eee26e88d40f72a7502396fe9423f1fad"}],"sha":"8c91aedd17954560f2eca5db90ecfc18871a7aa6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/8c91aedd17954560f2eca5db90ecfc18871a7aa6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18286430?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ivan-kalachikov","id":18286430,"login":"ivan-kalachikov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Mjg2NDMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/a8f4578eee26e88d40f72a7502396fe9423f1fad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T07:33:01Z","email":"ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com","name":"Ivan Kalachikov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T07:33:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(VCST-5684): translate YTD acronym in sales-rep locales (#2429)\n\n## Description\n\n`YTD` is an English-only abbreviation, so every non-English locale that\nkept it\nrendered a half-translated string. On a German Sales Rep customer\nprofile the\n_Average order value_ widget subtitle read `Durchschnitt pro Bestellung\n(YTD)`.\n\nSwept all 13 sales-rep locales and fixed the two keys that still leaked\nthe\nacronym in 6 of them:\n\n| Key | Where it renders | Locales fixed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `sales_rep.customer_profile.stats.per_order` | AOV widget subtitle |\nde, es, fr, it, pl, pt |\n| `sales_rep.my_customers.table.ytd` | \"YTD purchases\" column header |\nes, fr, it, pl, pt |\n\nEach replacement reuses the year-to-date phrasing that locale already\nuses for\n`sales_rep.hub.dashboard.widgets.orders_placed_ytd`, so the wording\nstays\ninternally consistent. The column headers use the shorter variant to\nstay\ncomparable in width to the adjacent `last_year` header. German only\nneeded the\nsubtitle — its column header was already `Jahresumsatz`.\n\n`en.json` is unchanged: `YTD` / `MTD` are standard business\nabbreviations in the\nsource language, and `mtd_of_ytd` plus the other `*_mtd` keys were\nalready\nlocalized everywhere else.\n\nNo code change — data only. The stat widget''s `__sub` element is\n`text-xs` with\nno truncation or `nowrap`, so the longer German string wraps rather than\nclips.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `vitest run --dir client-app/modules/sales-rep` — 33 files, 340 tests\npass.\n  The existing assertions read the English strings, which are untouched.\n- All 13 locale files parse as valid JSON; `prettier --check` clean on\nthe 6 changed files.\n- `grep \"YTD\\|MTD\"` over `client-app/modules/sales-rep/locales/` now\nmatches `en.json` only.\n\nNot visually verified in a browser against a German store — the change\nis a\nstring swap in the locale data with no layout impact.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5684\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.56.0-pr-2429-796d-796dc06c.zip\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"c3508fc5606969ac5ab553298994978ce6bfbc5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/c3508fc5606969ac5ab553298994978ce6bfbc5e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/a8f4578eee26e88d40f72a7502396fe9423f1fad","verification":{"payload":"tree c3508fc5606969ac5ab553298994978ce6bfbc5e\nparent 6e52bdeed892565b66125a524e502db5542a1d5f\nauthor Ivan Kalachikov <ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com> 1787038381 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787038381 +0100\n\nfix(VCST-5684): translate YTD acronym in sales-rep locales (#2429)\n\n## Description\n\n`YTD` is an English-only abbreviation, so every non-English locale that\nkept it\nrendered a half-translated string. On a German Sales Rep customer\nprofile the\n_Average order value_ widget subtitle read `Durchschnitt pro Bestellung\n(YTD)`.\n\nSwept all 13 sales-rep locales and fixed the two keys that still leaked\nthe\nacronym in 6 of them:\n\n| Key | Where it renders | Locales fixed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `sales_rep.customer_profile.stats.per_order` | AOV widget subtitle |\nde, es, fr, it, pl, pt |\n| `sales_rep.my_customers.table.ytd` | \"YTD purchases\" column header |\nes, fr, it, pl, pt |\n\nEach replacement reuses the year-to-date phrasing that locale already\nuses for\n`sales_rep.hub.dashboard.widgets.orders_placed_ytd`, so the wording\nstays\ninternally consistent. The column headers use the shorter variant to\nstay\ncomparable in width to the adjacent `last_year` header. German only\nneeded the\nsubtitle — its column header was already `Jahresumsatz`.\n\n`en.json` is unchanged: `YTD` / `MTD` are standard business\nabbreviations in the\nsource language, and `mtd_of_ytd` plus the other `*_mtd` keys were\nalready\nlocalized everywhere else.\n\nNo code change — data only. The stat widget''s `__sub` element is\n`text-xs` with\nno truncation or `nowrap`, so the longer German string wraps rather than\nclips.\n\n### Verification\n\n- `vitest run --dir client-app/modules/sales-rep` — 33 files, 340 tests\npass.\n  The existing assertions read the English strings, which are untouched.\n- All 13 locale files parse as valid JSON; `prettier --check` clean on\nthe 6 changed files.\n- `grep \"YTD\\|MTD\"` over `client-app/modules/sales-rep/locales/` now\nmatches `en.json` only.\n\nNot visually verified in a browser against a German store — the change\nis a\nstring swap in the locale data with no layout impact.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5684\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.56.0-pr-2429-796d-796dc06c.zip\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhAqtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5FwQAJAQ6fSgl2SGhmAdFCiP/0UO\nGD6kEPz4lDTZxREDPZfxYSGE4+XctbJs6UXVdfXYnAdspOoOkbdg+fxfkv066kJt\nn9xQTrevUeVgDIyxmOTC0sYaMbbJJAm06gBIa5gRmt5vlg4YBnZ8AcPLP/rxFcLN\nzLxEEOsiekjBpStJro0BZY++V9vbv+nd4lDmMZZRmJeL/Ba+Tl2CKS+LGV/1FFkK\nhCnyujxSNTm3FwzSujgXSiPFz/KYdZhDToe4KLXifrxwXrWSj3J5cqnwJjryTzOc\nfpb/UwEpoYvEIvf/fAD/qE5je2td2YtrBRV7VyfkNupNR9AyujqEkCSi83/dOB0T\npwlIhL4xKahqHzjeKOkSuEqpXA64O25EQVSlvTkXxZ3KI57AuZiY0Jn3fORrXKoK\noWeABazPvPXkxKWEm04+P8vWfrqR9JI7cS98WKa58GToV3hW7Ac/Ot+olhLfCHxf\nBaWIfxm0S4KYszktxXTeb/vKp/8IPeZB1aED/EqZSmwipWuD2c7Vi3wGWNHfPoE6\na7EB0Gw6YTf7WIj97FvRKWi7ckU++j6V2UBHvWCpNliUGhmjishdU3FIwwfP21d2\nShMs8PEXNmq07GEhDIVddIX1XD7etCYkIC6hj6D0pNi0FO/RigmjiAAo3B1vblUz\n2vWV3PH6ABaYwAdmzpn0\n=ZYjz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T07:33:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/a8f4578eee26e88d40f72a7502396fe9423f1fad","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKGE4ZjQ1NzhlZWUyNmU4OGQ0MGY3MmE3NTAyMzk2ZmU5NDIzZjFmYWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/6e52bdeed892565b66125a524e502db5542a1d5f","sha":"6e52bdeed892565b66125a524e502db5542a1d5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/6e52bdeed892565b66125a524e502db5542a1d5f"}],"sha":"a8f4578eee26e88d40f72a7502396fe9423f1fad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/a8f4578eee26e88d40f72a7502396fe9423f1fad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/126832118?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yuskithedeveloper","id":126832118,"login":"yuskithedeveloper","node_id":"U_kgDOB49N9g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/6e52bdeed892565b66125a524e502db5542a1d5f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T12:16:21Z","email":"126832118+yuskithedeveloper@users.noreply.github.com","name":"yuskithedeveloper"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T12:16:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VCST-5587): sales rep hub new orders metric (#2433)\n\n## Description\n\nThe **New orders** stat card stops reporting a **lifetime** backlog of\n`New`-status orders and reports the **rolling last 7 days** instead,\nwith the all-status volume of that same window as its context figure.\nThe label now names the status explicitly, so \"new\" can no longer be\nread as \"recently created\".\n\nNo backend PR is required.\n\n**Before → after**\n\n| slot | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| label | `NEW ORDERS` | `ORDERS IN “NEW” STATUS` |\n| value | `6` — every `New`-status order ever placed | `6` —\n`New`-status orders **created in the last 7 days** |\n| sub-figure | `$12,345 total` (lifetime) | `$12,345 total` (same window\nas the value) |\n| delta | `2 placed today` — green, a second status-filtered count | `of\n48 created in the last 7 days` — gray, the all-status volume the value\nis a slice of |\n| window | none (lifetime, unbounded) | rolling 7 days: today + the 6\npreceding UTC days |\n\n**Agreed definition** — the six questions the ticket asks:\n\n| # | question | answer |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `stat-widget__value`: all statuses or only `new`? | Only `New` — a\nsingle raw order status (`NEW_ORDERS_FILTER`), resolved server-side\nthrough the `salesRepOrderFilterRules` name → `Order.Status` dictionary.\nNot a subset of several statuses. |\n| 2 | `stat-widget__delta`: baseline period and status set? | **Not a\nperiod-over-period comparison.** It is a denominator: the same 7-day\nwindow, **all** statuses. So the card reads \"6 of 48\" — how much of the\nrecent flow still needs the rep. Rendered `neutral` (gray, no chevron),\nwhich is this widget''s existing convention for an informational count. |\n| 3 | cancelled / refunded / draft / test orders? | Excluded from\n**both** figures, by the rep scope itself\n(`RepOrderScopeQueryExtensions.ApplyRepScope`: `!IsPrototype &&\n!IsCancelled`) — no per-card exclusion needed. Refunds are not a status\nin VC''s stock dictionary. Note the exclusion is by the `IsCancelled`\n**flag**: an order parked in a `Cancelled` *status* without that flag\nwould still count in the all-status figure. |\n| 4 | which timestamp defines the period? | `CustomerOrder.CreatedDate`\n— the only date the statistics query filters on. Never the status-change\ndate. The delta wording (\"…created in the last 7 days\") states this on\nthe card. |\n| 5 | Dashboard vs Customer page: identical logic? | Yes — one\noperation, one set of aliases, both mappers reading the same fields. The\nonly difference is scope: the customer page passes `organizationId`, the\ndashboard omits it and spans every organization assigned to the rep. |\n| 6 | does the label need to change? | Yes, changed. `New orders` →\n`Orders in “New” status`. |\n\n### Behaviour\n\n* **Rolling 7 days, not week-to-date.** A Monday-start window would\nreset the card every Monday morning, exactly when the actionable backlog\nis largest, so `buildStatisticsWindows` gained `recentFrom`/`recentTo`\n(`todayFrom`/`todayTo` are gone — nothing else used them). Both bounds\nkeep the existing day-granularity rounding, so the backend statistics\ncache keys stay stable within a day.\n* **The status token stays `New` in every locale — deliberately.**\n`vc-module-order`''s localization files translate the `Order.Status`\nsetting''s title/description but **not** its values, and the storefront\nships no `sales_rep.rules.order.filter.*` overrides, so every other\nstatus label a rep sees (the Orders widget''s tabs, its filter chips)\nrenders the raw key. Translating the token here would have desynced the\ncard from the tab beside it. Only the frame is localized, using each\nlocale''s own quote convention: de `Bestellungen im Status „New“`, fr\n`Commandes au statut « New »`, ru `Заказы в статусе «New»`, ja\n`ステータス「New」の注文`, zh `状态为“New”的订单`, pl `Zamówienia w statusie „New”`,\nfi/sv `”New”`, es/it/pt/no `«New»`.\n* **i18n:** `widgets.new_orders` relabelled and `stats.placed_today`\nreplaced by `stats.of_recent_orders` across all 13 locales, each phrased\nnaturally for \"created in the last 7 days\" (de reads `von {count} aus\nden letzten 7 Tagen`, where the participle would be clumsy). The count\nis still passed as vue-i18n''s plural selector alongside the formatted\nstring, so locales that need plural forms can add them later.\n`placed_today` had no other consumer and is removed rather than left\ndangling.\n* **Query:** `newOrders` gained the window bounds; `newOrdersToday` was\nreplaced by `recentOrders: period(from:, to:)` with no filter. Bucket\ncount per request is unchanged (two, batched in one DataLoader\ndispatch), but the unbounded lifetime aggregate — the most expensive\nscan on the dashboard, growing with the rep''s whole order history — is\ngone.\n* **`types.ts` is hand-updated**, as in #2416: `yarn\ngenerate:graphql-types` diverges in this repo. Correctness was proven\nmechanically rather than by eye — printing the hand-edited\n`DocumentNode` and the parsed `.graphql` operation yields byte-identical\noutput, so a later codegen run should be a no-op.\n* **Tests:** the whole sales-rep suite is green (342 tests / 33 files).\nTwo new window cases pin the behaviour the design rests on: the window\nspans 7 calendar days including today, and it stays full on a Monday\nwhile week-to-date is nearly empty. Card assertions now read the real\nlocalized strings, as before.\n\n### Deliberately not in this PR\n\n* **The tooltip named in the acceptance criteria.** `<StatWidget>` has\nno tooltip affordance, and adding one is a component-level change with\nits own a11y surface. The delta line states the window in plain text\ninstead. Happy to follow up if the AC should be met literally.\n* **`NEW_ORDERS_FILTER` is still the hard-coded `\"New\"`.** An\nunrecognized status name fails closed — the resolver returns no rule and\nthe card silently reads `0` — and the label now quotes this status in 13\nlocale strings, so the coupling is documented at the constant. Sourcing\nit from `salesRepOrderFilterRules` (or a per-widget setting) would\nremove both problems; out of scope here.\n* **`Orders placed · WEEK` is untouched.** It stays all-status\nweek-to-date; this card is status-filtered on a different, rolling\nwindow, so the two no longer report the same number.\n\n### Screenshots\n\n<img width=\"1469\" height=\"321\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d56b3d32-11db-4aad-bfbd-a135c005dff8\"\n/>\n\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5587\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.56.0-pr-2433-c4d6-c4d67a4d.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"19968d1308490233bcd727f24ee5b2b0c8f9f625","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/19968d1308490233bcd727f24ee5b2b0c8f9f625"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/6e52bdeed892565b66125a524e502db5542a1d5f","verification":{"payload":"tree 19968d1308490233bcd727f24ee5b2b0c8f9f625\nparent 9941a96dc4fa0df01252eae665c4fdf745ffeb2e\nauthor yuskithedeveloper <126832118+yuskithedeveloper@users.noreply.github.com> 1786968981 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786968981 -0500\n\nfeat(VCST-5587): sales rep hub new orders metric (#2433)\n\n## Description\n\nThe **New orders** stat card stops reporting a **lifetime** backlog of\n`New`-status orders and reports the **rolling last 7 days** instead,\nwith the all-status volume of that same window as its context figure.\nThe label now names the status explicitly, so \"new\" can no longer be\nread as \"recently created\".\n\nNo backend PR is required.\n\n**Before → after**\n\n| slot | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| label | `NEW ORDERS` | `ORDERS IN “NEW” STATUS` |\n| value | `6` — every `New`-status order ever placed | `6` —\n`New`-status orders **created in the last 7 days** |\n| sub-figure | `$12,345 total` (lifetime) | `$12,345 total` (same window\nas the value) |\n| delta | `2 placed today` — green, a second status-filtered count | `of\n48 created in the last 7 days` — gray, the all-status volume the value\nis a slice of |\n| window | none (lifetime, unbounded) | rolling 7 days: today + the 6\npreceding UTC days |\n\n**Agreed definition** — the six questions the ticket asks:\n\n| # | question | answer |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `stat-widget__value`: all statuses or only `new`? | Only `New` — a\nsingle raw order status (`NEW_ORDERS_FILTER`), resolved server-side\nthrough the `salesRepOrderFilterRules` name → `Order.Status` dictionary.\nNot a subset of several statuses. |\n| 2 | `stat-widget__delta`: baseline period and status set? | **Not a\nperiod-over-period comparison.** It is a denominator: the same 7-day\nwindow, **all** statuses. So the card reads \"6 of 48\" — how much of the\nrecent flow still needs the rep. Rendered `neutral` (gray, no chevron),\nwhich is this widget''s existing convention for an informational count. |\n| 3 | cancelled / refunded / draft / test orders? | Excluded from\n**both** figures, by the rep scope itself\n(`RepOrderScopeQueryExtensions.ApplyRepScope`: `!IsPrototype &&\n!IsCancelled`) — no per-card exclusion needed. Refunds are not a status\nin VC''s stock dictionary. Note the exclusion is by the `IsCancelled`\n**flag**: an order parked in a `Cancelled` *status* without that flag\nwould still count in the all-status figure. |\n| 4 | which timestamp defines the period? | `CustomerOrder.CreatedDate`\n— the only date the statistics query filters on. Never the status-change\ndate. The delta wording (\"…created in the last 7 days\") states this on\nthe card. |\n| 5 | Dashboard vs Customer page: identical logic? | Yes — one\noperation, one set of aliases, both mappers reading the same fields. The\nonly difference is scope: the customer page passes `organizationId`, the\ndashboard omits it and spans every organization assigned to the rep. |\n| 6 | does the label need to change? | Yes, changed. `New orders` →\n`Orders in “New” status`. |\n\n### Behaviour\n\n* **Rolling 7 days, not week-to-date.** A Monday-start window would\nreset the card every Monday morning, exactly when the actionable backlog\nis largest, so `buildStatisticsWindows` gained `recentFrom`/`recentTo`\n(`todayFrom`/`todayTo` are gone — nothing else used them). Both bounds\nkeep the existing day-granularity rounding, so the backend statistics\ncache keys stay stable within a day.\n* **The status token stays `New` in every locale — deliberately.**\n`vc-module-order`''s localization files translate the `Order.Status`\nsetting''s title/description but **not** its values, and the storefront\nships no `sales_rep.rules.order.filter.*` overrides, so every other\nstatus label a rep sees (the Orders widget''s tabs, its filter chips)\nrenders the raw key. Translating the token here would have desynced the\ncard from the tab beside it. Only the frame is localized, using each\nlocale''s own quote convention: de `Bestellungen im Status „New“`, fr\n`Commandes au statut « New »`, ru `Заказы в статусе «New»`, ja\n`ステータス「New」の注文`, zh `状态为“New”的订单`, pl `Zamówienia w statusie „New”`,\nfi/sv `”New”`, es/it/pt/no `«New»`.\n* **i18n:** `widgets.new_orders` relabelled and `stats.placed_today`\nreplaced by `stats.of_recent_orders` across all 13 locales, each phrased\nnaturally for \"created in the last 7 days\" (de reads `von {count} aus\nden letzten 7 Tagen`, where the participle would be clumsy). The count\nis still passed as vue-i18n''s plural selector alongside the formatted\nstring, so locales that need plural forms can add them later.\n`placed_today` had no other consumer and is removed rather than left\ndangling.\n* **Query:** `newOrders` gained the window bounds; `newOrdersToday` was\nreplaced by `recentOrders: period(from:, to:)` with no filter. Bucket\ncount per request is unchanged (two, batched in one DataLoader\ndispatch), but the unbounded lifetime aggregate — the most expensive\nscan on the dashboard, growing with the rep''s whole order history — is\ngone.\n* **`types.ts` is hand-updated**, as in #2416: `yarn\ngenerate:graphql-types` diverges in this repo. Correctness was proven\nmechanically rather than by eye — printing the hand-edited\n`DocumentNode` and the parsed `.graphql` operation yields byte-identical\noutput, so a later codegen run should be a no-op.\n* **Tests:** the whole sales-rep suite is green (342 tests / 33 files).\nTwo new window cases pin the behaviour the design rests on: the window\nspans 7 calendar days including today, and it stays full on a Monday\nwhile week-to-date is nearly empty. Card assertions now read the real\nlocalized strings, as before.\n\n### Deliberately not in this PR\n\n* **The tooltip named in the acceptance criteria.** `<StatWidget>` has\nno tooltip affordance, and adding one is a component-level change with\nits own a11y surface. The delta line states the window in plain text\ninstead. Happy to follow up if the AC should be met literally.\n* **`NEW_ORDERS_FILTER` is still the hard-coded `\"New\"`.** An\nunrecognized status name fails closed — the resolver returns no rule and\nthe card silently reads `0` — and the label now quotes this status in 13\nlocale strings, so the coupling is documented at the constant. Sourcing\nit from `salesRepOrderFilterRules` (or a per-widget setting) would\nremove both problems; out of scope here.\n* **`Orders placed · WEEK` is untouched.** It stays all-status\nweek-to-date; this card is status-filtered on a different, rolling\nwindow, so the two no longer report the same number.\n\n### Screenshots\n\n<img width=\"1469\" height=\"321\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d56b3d32-11db-4aad-bfbd-a135c005dff8\"\n/>\n\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5587\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.56.0-pr-2433-c4d6-c4d67a4d.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqgvuVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbL0QAI5Avv7zfagVt9E3uOhHYoB3\nlTaMXWgYM/BmigL7lMiDST4jGRdGEH6a6Z55n6QP3Od5BsKtnyM8IBakfCUnIqzf\nuQ2chFCFsynLZ3FQTqufv5zeS/riA9mlND60U9B0SBORRToxhe3kxkZzdRDyZN0H\nCoJ5lrGGupQpUapOVsJM+bh8zPEPw+Lv1NlnLIQf/6PpYa2yYIYiMLBBP8XpK+M+\nZs2+QzX/8N7bCcUU/Dl6Mt4l3U+N7koTFDALYJkYLJwK+1eBfPsfzPtvBh0lEOze\nyhGmSKhq6ZO1QqtHLSc5dSM86Xsc8tUFmuiVY5Qsb3dZDIgu5fEHQatfILZReJaS\nqZx0Nq4vKuXsf1mqGN+m4kOyprbguRcbztldEgqRhG1ghAXn3f36B1nHUzi9I+sd\nJK4aPsMjZEt12vydX7RC+FM+pVg+/IHs/IPR9YNXpj1iNS7f42oE1Hzb19sFcwQ5\n5CHuznr0eGoEqVyJ5ATkHJgC4CLhIzzYBY+RFQQ34ezwU2+cHjqmoIN49Fxmc3ow\nlvzJ5NQ97pKhZu7ZKVzcZ0FuaoXma8rsO9e5Kf6T5nTF+GyJVn654YVpLOm4ueQD\ni0IDPv9Em4/N1IzJprhmocvTqtjilFfos040kVthZMOEJuQ5KKLpTZnh71oxXW8h\nkJXlJkfRVPelojvUEtZS\n=zX8j\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-17T12:16:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/6e52bdeed892565b66125a524e502db5542a1d5f","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDZlNTJiZGVlZDg5MjU2NWI2NjEyNWE1MjRlNTAyZGI1NTQyYTFkNWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/9941a96dc4fa0df01252eae665c4fdf745ffeb2e","sha":"9941a96dc4fa0df01252eae665c4fdf745ffeb2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/9941a96dc4fa0df01252eae665c4fdf745ffeb2e"}],"sha":"6e52bdeed892565b66125a524e502db5542a1d5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/6e52bdeed892565b66125a524e502db5542a1d5f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/126832118?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yuskithedeveloper","id":126832118,"login":"yuskithedeveloper","node_id":"U_kgDOB49N9g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/9941a96dc4fa0df01252eae665c4fdf745ffeb2e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T11:45:55Z","email":"126832118+yuskithedeveloper@users.noreply.github.com","name":"yuskithedeveloper"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T11:45:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(VCST-5592): Using local time instead of UTC for sales rep hub statistics filters (#2414)\n\n## Description\nThe sales-rep statistics widgets on the Dashboard and Customer page\nbuilt their today/week/MTD/YTD windows from UTC calendar parts, so the\nday boundary didn''t match the user''s own day: an order placed at 23:00\nUTC on Jul 27 (Jul 28 02:00 for a UTC+3 rep) appeared in the\nrecent-orders list and in the unbounded \"new orders\" counter, but was\nmissing from the \"created today\" badge.\n`buildStatisticsWindows()` — the single place periods are computed,\nfeeding both surfaces and the orders/top-sellers period chips — now\nanchors every boundary to the user''s local midnight while still sending\nplain UTC instants to the API, so the widgets agree with the dates\nrendered beside them; no backend change was needed.\n\n**Note for testing:** order numbers are still minted from the UTC date\n(`CO{0:yyMMdd}-…`), so a near-midnight order can be numbered `…0727…`\nwhile the UI consistently shows Jul 28 — that mismatch is expected, not\na regression.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5592\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.56.0-pr-2414-332d-332d12cb.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4ec6315f8ec4b7c178ee40f72f11079fb5b7fb89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/4ec6315f8ec4b7c178ee40f72f11079fb5b7fb89"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/9941a96dc4fa0df01252eae665c4fdf745ffeb2e","verification":{"payload":"tree 4ec6315f8ec4b7c178ee40f72f11079fb5b7fb89\nparent 984972c41fb5db19f183f894f1ec28fb0b264ab4\nauthor yuskithedeveloper <126832118+yuskithedeveloper@users.noreply.github.com> 1786967155 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786967155 -0500\n\nfix(VCST-5592): Using local time instead of UTC for sales rep hub statistics filters (#2414)\n\n## Description\nThe sales-rep statistics widgets on the Dashboard and Customer page\nbuilt their today/week/MTD/YTD windows from UTC calendar parts, so the\nday boundary didn''t match the user''s own day: an order placed at 23:00\nUTC on Jul 27 (Jul 28 02:00 for a UTC+3 rep) appeared in the\nrecent-orders list and in the unbounded \"new orders\" counter, but was\nmissing from the \"created today\" badge.\n`buildStatisticsWindows()` — the single place periods are computed,\nfeeding both surfaces and the orders/top-sellers period chips — now\nanchors every boundary to the user''s local midnight while still sending\nplain UTC instants to the API, so the widgets agree with the dates\nrendered beside them; no backend change was needed.\n\n**Note for testing:** order numbers are still minted from the UTC date\n(`CO{0:yyMMdd}-…`), so a near-midnight order can be numbered `…0727…`\nwhile the UI consistently shows Jul 28 — that mismatch is expected, not\na regression.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5592\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.56.0-pr-2414-332d-332d12cb.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqgvRzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+v8QAGKvzgNgXDTVWdwp7OYuP+2t\nOv0POLrDV/CMo3vEqO6CoQ6O4XrlGl9UEL1g1HoezkGfRJaXbterm2USaWeZob9v\norRZmqnpUCYVCPej81icgIlTYx3t408bLLDzcfBfm83yzrHknv58b+mpu4rLKMns\nJ2PL6Cb9MD92sr/ZBRNRj+p8YILPMLAtg47P+OhjOxk1XNOa7LsC3XXyZ9TI/lMh\noW9U9YC9lhqGPOEU8cnZdUyXpjZhQto59Ypr94bxEE4xd3jrqaATNBSBqf9CJ3SJ\nqR9qI5cesy4Ib9qfhGD0jHIj1mW6yZuSRdT+OCjI0XDlJ2W7XROTSKTPHWU7Ey/6\nBH6PEK9px+Iodr1DJZuiryxpwDnwDRHv/9a2E9LadyE89KyaOqKu8IG0lv0PysCT\nSq0XPVLAjiGBr3Y8I1ffY7xRRTShpCTuKtQUQnHrmaVoaCuuRpyYHrUl280zQ0oV\ndEWjuWNssOgXN3WQRRwCCyzJ7Tr8bJOgxNLeAHJDiJD3zwbcgrrcZ0UI5xkRthCZ\nisRk3dw9hW5KJMr4qcv9HWg9kWgA1ZGP1cquwlI8K7C5213yHBDdcvHOg1n8vKWZ\nx9bf1hanjiu9LNoCM3MR6mkYd2N0I4U1Un/f7r4T0pbCTonkRj2Q0TP5uzkw34A7\nQN+scPqj8vmTN6zvoe6U\n=nMgw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-17T11:45:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/9941a96dc4fa0df01252eae665c4fdf745ffeb2e","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDk5NDFhOTZkYzRmYTBkZjAxMjUyZWFlNjY1YzRmZGY3NDVmZmViMmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/984972c41fb5db19f183f894f1ec28fb0b264ab4","sha":"984972c41fb5db19f183f894f1ec28fb0b264ab4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/984972c41fb5db19f183f894f1ec28fb0b264ab4"}],"sha":"9941a96dc4fa0df01252eae665c4fdf745ffeb2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/9941a96dc4fa0df01252eae665c4fdf745ffeb2e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18286430?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ivan-kalachikov","id":18286430,"login":"ivan-kalachikov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Mjg2NDMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/984972c41fb5db19f183f894f1ec28fb0b264ab4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T13:57:06Z","email":"ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com","name":"Ivan Kalachikov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T13:57:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(VCST-5537): publish a default /llms.txt brand brief (#2419)\n\n## Description\n\nAdds a default `/llms.txt` to the theme — a plain-text brief that AI\ndiscovery agents read for brand context. It is the ticket''s draft text\nverbatim, placed in `client-app/public/`, so it is served at the site\nroot the same way `robots.txt` already is.\n\nThis is **AC 1** (\"Frontend should have default\"). **AC 2**, the\nper-store Store Assets override, is backend work and is not in this\nrepo. That looks like an extension of an existing mechanism rather than\nnew work: `robots.txt` is already overridden server-side — the theme''s\ncopy says \"demo environments\" while `vcst-qa` serves \"backend\nenvironments\" from the same path. Probably worth a linked backend\nticket.\n\nThe placeholders (`Yourstore`, `Category one`, `support@yourstore.com`)\nare the intended default. Per AC 2, the merchant override is what fills\nthem in.\n\n## Verification\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `/llms.txt` on the dev server | `200 text/plain`, body matches the\nfile |\n| `/llms.txt` on `vcst-qa` | `404` before this change — the gap being\nclosed |\n| `/robots.txt` on `vcst-qa` | `200 text/plain`, already overridden\nserver-side |\n\nNo test: a static text asset with no behaviour to assert. No TypeScript,\nlint or test surface is touched.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5537\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.55.0-pr-2419-e52f-e52f4269.zip\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"556d7ab6732093d30d08f45c21fe1ccb60161840","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/556d7ab6732093d30d08f45c21fe1ccb60161840"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/984972c41fb5db19f183f894f1ec28fb0b264ab4","verification":{"payload":"tree 556d7ab6732093d30d08f45c21fe1ccb60161840\nparent a28847282499d1486164aa3656237d77342024cd\nauthor Ivan Kalachikov <ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com> 1786629426 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786629426 +0100\n\nfeat(VCST-5537): publish a default /llms.txt brand brief (#2419)\n\n## Description\n\nAdds a default `/llms.txt` to the theme — a plain-text brief that AI\ndiscovery agents read for brand context. It is the ticket''s draft text\nverbatim, placed in `client-app/public/`, so it is served at the site\nroot the same way `robots.txt` already is.\n\nThis is **AC 1** (\"Frontend should have default\"). **AC 2**, the\nper-store Store Assets override, is backend work and is not in this\nrepo. That looks like an extension of an existing mechanism rather than\nnew work: `robots.txt` is already overridden server-side — the theme''s\ncopy says \"demo environments\" while `vcst-qa` serves \"backend\nenvironments\" from the same path. Probably worth a linked backend\nticket.\n\nThe placeholders (`Yourstore`, `Category one`, `support@yourstore.com`)\nare the intended default. Per AC 2, the merchant override is what fills\nthem in.\n\n## Verification\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `/llms.txt` on the dev server | `200 text/plain`, body matches the\nfile |\n| `/llms.txt` on `vcst-qa` | `404` before this change — the gap being\nclosed |\n| `/robots.txt` on `vcst-qa` | `200 text/plain`, already overridden\nserver-side |\n\nNo test: a static text asset with no behaviour to assert. No TypeScript,\nlint or test surface is touched.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5537\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.55.0-pr-2419-e52f-e52f4269.zip\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfc0yCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzbAQAKXQ9RqghDWAd4spyOewvcBw\nFb/14KImOx5zl5oPK3uxCFwDYYaNVliM9Nhn1Y/Oqm7/3Fq2gRNzKa661Dm8Kgfu\nuC/rJh/bL6y3lTf8mqu53kLUSp48UfRpIR42guoA5nuFPb23gxrL8z+RNThA+8yn\nwUDTW1ou2pwbkfOfkWLRUDiMVnsclpAdEgwd0jNpLrFRuWSgS3YBXXAYTkaf+/cW\ny4kYNM5uCbKhoSX7EJE1ELBs+u1hyMNZcEEKiLWY+XGXPzIleYfLcF2zdrMsci2K\neOTbqdyxEcCivd7lPvzV9i9Rptci5O4Z7tO+dEWpWuPyESe2acBv+CvrWBzSyLva\n/9G8YB/ea+gZDkvkyKPMyXOCvATbjVzedwywERuLmfrrlOUlONQs03vUBuS7xZ2R\n/pvLwx/aXrJ15NR+17IkpGaWWj8CkoqobbvMcvLW3IB/MU++xQ86exyXo5FWYwVe\nlUM5YODVHnGb0XquusZCBl3USk3kHnv81nHwirOweTMZOCM6dBn2KW66qaIvJxpn\nr38/1Vtkm37RqHubL83XgYH2dJgJ3T+5FC3SSF7dT03C7x1ru1G6nIABSjWGye6b\nYa4aFoRB4XkV2xDcpbAz/zhRHALzETQejMDfpmbKp12R+6xaHUGOSPrDvBvgpYiu\nYeJsCMRrnjUmmAP3SqNu\n=WpGo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-13T13:57:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/984972c41fb5db19f183f894f1ec28fb0b264ab4","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDk4NDk3MmM0MWZiNWRiMTlmMTgzZjg5NGYxZWMyOGZiMGIyNjRhYjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/a28847282499d1486164aa3656237d77342024cd","sha":"a28847282499d1486164aa3656237d77342024cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/a28847282499d1486164aa3656237d77342024cd"}],"sha":"984972c41fb5db19f183f894f1ec28fb0b264ab4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/984972c41fb5db19f183f894f1ec28fb0b264ab4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16372194?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/goldenmaya","id":16372194,"login":"goldenmaya","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzcyMTk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goldenmaya","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/a28847282499d1486164aa3656237d77342024cd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T13:04:18Z","email":"mayapavlovna@gmail.com","name":"Maiia Diachkovskaia"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T13:04:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(VCST-5533): coupons sidebar — WCAG 2.2 AA gaps (#2421)\n\n## Description\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\n<!-- Put link to your task in Jira here -->\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5533\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.55.0-pr-2421-1e94-1e949ce0.zip\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Changes cart coupon apply/remove semantics and shared `VcInput` ARIA\nmerging, which can affect checkout UX and any consumer passing custom\n`aria-describedby`; behavior is well covered by new tests but touches\ncore cart flows.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Addresses **VCST-5533** by fixing WCAG 2.2 AA gaps in the cart coupons\nsidebar and tightening coupon apply/remove behavior.\n> \n> **Coupon cards** now expose proper names and errors: visible labels\nget stable `id`s wired via `aria-labelledby` / `aria-label`, rejected\ncodes set `aria-invalid` and `aria-describedby` on the input, and errors\nkeep `role=\"alert\"`. **`VcInput`** merges consumer `aria-describedby`\nwith its internal details id instead of overwriting it.\n> \n> **Coupons section** adds a screen-reader-only `aria-live=\"polite\"`\nregion that announces apply/remove (including swap and partial-failure\ncases), discount, and new total when cart figures exist. Apply/remove go\nthrough handlers that rely on **boolean results** from `useCoupon` so\nannouncements are not skewed by shared module-level `couponError`.\n> \n> **Coupon logic** introduces `isSameCouponCode` (trim +\ncase-insensitive) for loading, applied/error UI, and swaps; re-applying\nthe same code in a different case no longer removes the working coupon.\n**`applyCoupon` / `removeCoupon`** return whether the cart actually\nchanged after mutations, with extra validation when add/remove resolves\nbut the cart does not reflect the code.\n> \n> New i18n strings for announcements and fallback input labeling; broad\nunit/integration tests cover a11y wiring, live region behavior, and edge\ncases.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n1e949ce0c33f77bf56cc90942feb87df5003db92. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Ivan Kalachikov <ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"efe972955a81d3a57ce1ff766059cfd516dcea18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/efe972955a81d3a57ce1ff766059cfd516dcea18"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/a28847282499d1486164aa3656237d77342024cd","verification":{"payload":"tree efe972955a81d3a57ce1ff766059cfd516dcea18\nparent 49165430ff56ee2cd6e2aac6ca260322431fda82\nauthor Maiia Diachkovskaia <mayapavlovna@gmail.com> 1786626258 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786626258 +0100\n\nfix(VCST-5533): coupons sidebar — WCAG 2.2 AA gaps (#2421)\n\n## Description\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\n<!-- Put link to your task in Jira here -->\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5533\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.55.0-pr-2421-1e94-1e949ce0.zip\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Changes cart coupon apply/remove semantics and shared `VcInput` ARIA\nmerging, which can affect checkout UX and any consumer passing custom\n`aria-describedby`; behavior is well covered by new tests but touches\ncore cart flows.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Addresses **VCST-5533** by fixing WCAG 2.2 AA gaps in the cart coupons\nsidebar and tightening coupon apply/remove behavior.\n> \n> **Coupon cards** now expose proper names and errors: visible labels\nget stable `id`s wired via `aria-labelledby` / `aria-label`, rejected\ncodes set `aria-invalid` and `aria-describedby` on the input, and errors\nkeep `role=\"alert\"`. **`VcInput`** merges consumer `aria-describedby`\nwith its internal details id instead of overwriting it.\n> \n> **Coupons section** adds a screen-reader-only `aria-live=\"polite\"`\nregion that announces apply/remove (including swap and partial-failure\ncases), discount, and new total when cart figures exist. Apply/remove go\nthrough handlers that rely on **boolean results** from `useCoupon` so\nannouncements are not skewed by shared module-level `couponError`.\n> \n> **Coupon logic** introduces `isSameCouponCode` (trim +\ncase-insensitive) for loading, applied/error UI, and swaps; re-applying\nthe same code in a different case no longer removes the working coupon.\n**`applyCoupon` / `removeCoupon`** return whether the cart actually\nchanged after mutations, with extra validation when add/remove resolves\nbut the cart does not reflect the code.\n> \n> New i18n strings for announcements and fallback input labeling; broad\nunit/integration tests cover a11y wiring, live region behavior, and edge\ncases.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit\n1e949ce0c33f77bf56cc90942feb87df5003db92. Bugbot is set up for automated\ncode reviews on this repo. Configure\n[here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Ivan Kalachikov <ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfcDSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmoMQAD4sMe3SfcOWFoq7+oX40w4P\nJWmVFyXv5Uq7RcpYi1ovYeqPDSJj+X7uckwQc4R7DSQqbWXAzjUN/DfVB+V4fxWx\nYFj5mq1J1e/4dwK45OcUKLzX0YRN4U+X61ApnYIdI4XW303KEwM+lWwFJEPaS00w\nClvdcMJDTtMdL4UzZAPuzNobfHuBzqAVvMQ7UnlJW/N/UM+HhAXU0PA4Cg+BGwW8\nIy09Yw/JQEYItIqhN6J7q54pa0+v8oKAvuRwO1FHoq1Cr4GkqzCJYEo0qpsqh4Kh\nOdylwsy0FBHnO0z2PH7XtNSF+UJeYrHrMku5LBGA2ht3F9E0Efp+q480gI2Kn1IU\nByfQIHAiyR0ldWOpjfRaNuFG0BPXcGTcTOUrpYiEXo2N4gETi8rhV66bjpg+3HBm\nZqyaX/Lzc9ImpmyQnf/6QAHOKB5Xjdp7aQ9Ov9CbxzWX8vdlRM/6/z2sw4ljtta3\n3sUEQCDaqBiil3giTiiWenx0peIheHcX3TKPtdrxK5FjBeo0uAj6+2q+Rxc9+g/Y\nKB2EQ3AzVZ9f/WF1SSplUPAPfeD6WW+AURnK1RtCWKhTFI80Vxc6T2Wo8i37y4bK\nZim8tDvPo2eBswrdPXH4pKadWtCbvRr3YRPGRfm7zfs2rMMiWoALMrlwx3FRWJ81\nN3j3nlddihF3TBqF8M5k\n=qSdm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-13T13:04:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/a28847282499d1486164aa3656237d77342024cd","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKGEyODg0NzI4MjQ5OWQxNDg2MTY0YWEzNjU2MjM3ZDc3MzQyMDI0Y2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/49165430ff56ee2cd6e2aac6ca260322431fda82","sha":"49165430ff56ee2cd6e2aac6ca260322431fda82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/49165430ff56ee2cd6e2aac6ca260322431fda82"}],"sha":"a28847282499d1486164aa3656237d77342024cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/a28847282499d1486164aa3656237d77342024cd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18286430?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ivan-kalachikov","id":18286430,"login":"ivan-kalachikov","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Mjg2NDMw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ivan-kalachikov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/49165430ff56ee2cd6e2aac6ca260322431fda82/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T09:58:03Z","email":"ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com","name":"Ivan Kalachikov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T09:58:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(VCST-5654): recover from failed chunk loads (#2431)\n\n## Description\n\n**Deploy while someone has the tab open → lazy components break for the\nrest of their session, silently.**\n\n### What happens today\n\n1. **10:00** — a user has the storefront open and is browsing.\n2. **10:05** — we deploy. Every chunk is renamed by its new content\nhash, so the filenames their already-loaded document knows about start\nreturning **404**.\n3. **10:06** — cart full, they click **Checkout**. `/checkout`\nlazy-loads `@/pages/checkout/index.vue`; that chunk 404s, the navigation\ndies, and they are left sitting on the cart with no message. Same for\n`/account/orders`, `/account/lists`, and every other lazy route.\n4. They click **Checkout** again. Same nothing — `defineAsyncComponent`\ncaches the rejected loader promise and replays it on every later mount.\n5. Only a full page reload recovers, and nothing on screen tells them\nthat.\n\nWorst case is a lazy component that gates a control: the wishlist\nsharing-scope element renders an empty area and **Save stays disabled**,\nbecause the parent reads `canSave` off a component instance that never\nmounted.\n\nThere is no retry path today: `retry()` is only reachable through\n`onError`, and none of the 25 `defineAsyncComponent` call sites pass it.\n\n### The fix — one listener\n\nVite dispatches `vite:preloadError` for a failed dependency preload\n**and** for the failed base `import()`. So a single handler covers every\nlazy site at once: 45 lazy routes, 25 `defineAsyncComponent` call sites,\nplain `import()` calls.\n\nNew `client-app/chunk-load-recovery.ts`, installed from `main.ts` before\nthe app runner so nothing can slip past it:\n\n| When it fails | What the user gets |\n|---|---|\n| App is rendered | Toast — *\"Part of the site could not be loaded.\nPlease reload the page to continue.\"* — with a **Reload page** button.\nNothing they were typing is discarded. |\n| Before the app renders (blank page) | One automatic reload. A\ntimestamp guard stops a permanently missing chunk from looping. |\n\nThe event is left un-prevented on purpose: preventing it makes the\nfailed import resolve with `undefined` instead of rejecting, which would\nhide the failure from Vue and the router.\n\nThe message says what happened, not why. A failed chunk is *usually* a\ndeploy, but it is also a flaky network, a proxy, or a poisoned cache —\nso the copy states the fact and the fix rather than guessing at a cause.\n\n### Cost and blast radius\n\nMeasured against `origin/dev` (same base commit, both built clean):\n\n| | Base | This PR | Delta |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Entry chunk, gzip | 333,964 B | 334,219 B | **+255 B (+0.08%)** |\n| Entry chunk, raw | 1,850,260 B | 1,851,010 B | +750 B |\n| Chunk count | 362 | 362 | 0 |\n| Locale chunk (one per session) | — | — | +~150 B |\n\nNo runtime cost on the happy path: Vite already dispatched this event,\nnothing listened. Registration is one `addEventListener`; everything\nelse runs only after a chunk has already failed. The module ships in\nexactly one chunk — no duplication.\n\nExisting behaviour is untouched: the event is not prevented, so a failed\nimport rejects exactly as it does today. This only adds a message and a\nrecovery path on top.\n\nStorage access is wrapped: `sessionStorage` throws where it is denied\n(sandboxed preview iframes, blocked cookies), and without a record of\nthe previous attempt the automatic reload cannot be kept from looping —\nso it is skipped there rather than risking one.\n\n### Deliberately not included\n\n- **`onError` retry wrapper** — retrying cannot help the deploy case,\nthe hashed filename is gone. A wrapper with no call sites is dead code.\n- **Federated remotes** — they load through the Module Federation\nruntime, not Vite''s preload helper, so they never emit this event.\n\n### Testing\n\n- 6 new tests in `client-app/chunk-load-recovery.test.ts`: toast when\nrendered, single reload when blank, no second reload inside the\ncooldown, reload again after it, no reload when storage is denied, event\nleft un-prevented.\n- `yarn vitest run --dir client-app` — 116 files / 1877 tests pass.\n- `vue-tsc --build --force`, `eslint`, `prettier --check` on changed\nfiles — clean.\n- `yarn build` — succeeds; `depcruise` reports no new violations.\n\nVerified live against the production build (`yarn preview` + real\nbackend), by deleting a route chunk from `dist/` while the tab was open\n— the actual deploy scenario:\n\n- **Client-side navigation** — clicked a link to the missing route:\nnavigation aborted, page stayed put, toast appeared with the **Reload\npage** button, no automatic reload. Console: `TypeError: Failed to fetch\ndynamically imported module: …/sign-in-BrTah6Dc.js`.\n- **Boot-time failure** — hard-loaded the same route: `#app` stayed\nempty, the handler reloaded once\n(`performance.getEntriesByType(\"navigation\")[0].type === \"reload\"`),\nthen the guard held — no loop.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5654\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.55.0-pr-2431-14ba-14ba8d48.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f3f382027dd89d2918f6fb57103ceadcfd247836","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/f3f382027dd89d2918f6fb57103ceadcfd247836"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/49165430ff56ee2cd6e2aac6ca260322431fda82","verification":{"payload":"tree f3f382027dd89d2918f6fb57103ceadcfd247836\nparent af7db0802de6654f92a4587cd24612397f572b8f\nauthor Ivan Kalachikov <ivan.kalachikov@gmail.com> 1786615083 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786615083 +0100\n\nfix(VCST-5654): recover from failed chunk loads (#2431)\n\n## Description\n\n**Deploy while someone has the tab open → lazy components break for the\nrest of their session, silently.**\n\n### What happens today\n\n1. **10:00** — a user has the storefront open and is browsing.\n2. **10:05** — we deploy. Every chunk is renamed by its new content\nhash, so the filenames their already-loaded document knows about start\nreturning **404**.\n3. **10:06** — cart full, they click **Checkout**. `/checkout`\nlazy-loads `@/pages/checkout/index.vue`; that chunk 404s, the navigation\ndies, and they are left sitting on the cart with no message. Same for\n`/account/orders`, `/account/lists`, and every other lazy route.\n4. They click **Checkout** again. Same nothing — `defineAsyncComponent`\ncaches the rejected loader promise and replays it on every later mount.\n5. Only a full page reload recovers, and nothing on screen tells them\nthat.\n\nWorst case is a lazy component that gates a control: the wishlist\nsharing-scope element renders an empty area and **Save stays disabled**,\nbecause the parent reads `canSave` off a component instance that never\nmounted.\n\nThere is no retry path today: `retry()` is only reachable through\n`onError`, and none of the 25 `defineAsyncComponent` call sites pass it.\n\n### The fix — one listener\n\nVite dispatches `vite:preloadError` for a failed dependency preload\n**and** for the failed base `import()`. So a single handler covers every\nlazy site at once: 45 lazy routes, 25 `defineAsyncComponent` call sites,\nplain `import()` calls.\n\nNew `client-app/chunk-load-recovery.ts`, installed from `main.ts` before\nthe app runner so nothing can slip past it:\n\n| When it fails | What the user gets |\n|---|---|\n| App is rendered | Toast — *\"Part of the site could not be loaded.\nPlease reload the page to continue.\"* — with a **Reload page** button.\nNothing they were typing is discarded. |\n| Before the app renders (blank page) | One automatic reload. A\ntimestamp guard stops a permanently missing chunk from looping. |\n\nThe event is left un-prevented on purpose: preventing it makes the\nfailed import resolve with `undefined` instead of rejecting, which would\nhide the failure from Vue and the router.\n\nThe message says what happened, not why. A failed chunk is *usually* a\ndeploy, but it is also a flaky network, a proxy, or a poisoned cache —\nso the copy states the fact and the fix rather than guessing at a cause.\n\n### Cost and blast radius\n\nMeasured against `origin/dev` (same base commit, both built clean):\n\n| | Base | This PR | Delta |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Entry chunk, gzip | 333,964 B | 334,219 B | **+255 B (+0.08%)** |\n| Entry chunk, raw | 1,850,260 B | 1,851,010 B | +750 B |\n| Chunk count | 362 | 362 | 0 |\n| Locale chunk (one per session) | — | — | +~150 B |\n\nNo runtime cost on the happy path: Vite already dispatched this event,\nnothing listened. Registration is one `addEventListener`; everything\nelse runs only after a chunk has already failed. The module ships in\nexactly one chunk — no duplication.\n\nExisting behaviour is untouched: the event is not prevented, so a failed\nimport rejects exactly as it does today. This only adds a message and a\nrecovery path on top.\n\nStorage access is wrapped: `sessionStorage` throws where it is denied\n(sandboxed preview iframes, blocked cookies), and without a record of\nthe previous attempt the automatic reload cannot be kept from looping —\nso it is skipped there rather than risking one.\n\n### Deliberately not included\n\n- **`onError` retry wrapper** — retrying cannot help the deploy case,\nthe hashed filename is gone. A wrapper with no call sites is dead code.\n- **Federated remotes** — they load through the Module Federation\nruntime, not Vite''s preload helper, so they never emit this event.\n\n### Testing\n\n- 6 new tests in `client-app/chunk-load-recovery.test.ts`: toast when\nrendered, single reload when blank, no second reload inside the\ncooldown, reload again after it, no reload when storage is denied, event\nleft un-prevented.\n- `yarn vitest run --dir client-app` — 116 files / 1877 tests pass.\n- `vue-tsc --build --force`, `eslint`, `prettier --check` on changed\nfiles — clean.\n- `yarn build` — succeeds; `depcruise` reports no new violations.\n\nVerified live against the production build (`yarn preview` + real\nbackend), by deleting a route chunk from `dist/` while the tab was open\n— the actual deploy scenario:\n\n- **Client-side navigation** — clicked a link to the missing route:\nnavigation aborted, page stayed put, toast appeared with the **Reload\npage** button, no automatic reload. Console: `TypeError: Failed to fetch\ndynamically imported module: …/sign-in-BrTah6Dc.js`.\n- **Boot-time failure** — hard-loaded the same route: `#app` stayed\nempty, the handler reloaded once\n(`performance.getEntriesByType(\"navigation\")[0].type === \"reload\"`),\nthen the guard held — no loop.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5654\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.55.0-pr-2431-14ba-14ba8d48.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfZUrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYk0QAFMtYU0txzdKwJszzlAx5z7m\n0nnkJByg/Uno+Ds9ijwBCOyYh80cMLZwSJQMzl5ftjQ8lGrQwFfCIkX7Zv42LL/f\nf18O9ppqn60SF6dCMO90Kw7XcFCWhWnbezAWFAMWes3EoVVoLD8OX8pF3G8/zcqN\nHwQpYc/OguL5I3D8R08zzGM+/soEKOGfMKlmjvvpQm4vHQfO8RaVMF/bsoPUChUX\nr7Y9UNJlHY+Wz/TUlbowFSocgyItnfd9w/n8D6wHKsflvOkQWvnkUwutyyEt3Z2F\nDbjxFsShgHfVc1MrHbaC/TiC+EvAQHsZw4efl8nAudeVqMjqKy2PYHO5Yc+ldhoq\ngFY8VYYPpnEuS3mjZHXw1job6WjM8BG2XuAmFARzpJ3IuN+hNI04jHGbNPCYddnO\nkTynAH8MLOZuiUZGJcjB/QfRRirKvQbmeUxiKtflFyZ5GYd8+IrWKHfIukqIz1Tx\nwjAuPvMFsWIGDaz3N3k6IWFv/mplPGldwr4f5MtIgnAWpyUZmhz2ybc0OO7U0ey2\nTdy8Z4nhSnFn7/aPUnk6dZkf7Eo6X8TnTmmIvlgo1yDuxH+zChTGktAtOVWX9qZK\nnLfgdYnkAFDBH4YXWDf4HhApzeB4ayfAavMQTphjVNqEVv1utlQTajTfbVM31uja\nRYWfPk1Rir6WoTkP1cG0\n=5AKO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-13T09:58:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/49165430ff56ee2cd6e2aac6ca260322431fda82","node_id":"C_kwDOEam6btoAKDQ5MTY1NDMwZmY1NmVlMmNkNmUyYWFjNmNhMjYwMzIyNDMxZmRhODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commit/af7db0802de6654f92a4587cd24612397f572b8f","sha":"af7db0802de6654f92a4587cd24612397f572b8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/af7db0802de6654f92a4587cd24612397f572b8f"}],"sha":"49165430ff56ee2cd6e2aac6ca260322431fda82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/49165430ff56ee2cd6e2aac6ca260322431fda82"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/126832118?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/yuskithedeveloper","id":126832118,"login":"yuskithedeveloper","node_id":"U_kgDOB49N9g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuskithedeveloper","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/commits/af7db0802de6654f92a4587cd24612397f572b8f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-12T12:20:35Z","email":"126832118+yuskithedeveloper@users.noreply.github.com","name":"yuskithedeveloper"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T12:20:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"VCST-5590: Dashboard statuses and categories filter (#2409)\n\n## Description\nSends the **list''s own scope** to the sales-rep filter-rule discovery\nqueries, so the chip rows match the records on screen. The backend\nvocabularies are now data-derived (the statuses/categories that actually\nexist in the records being shown), which only holds if the storefront\nasks for them with the same `organizationId` and `period` its list uses\n— otherwise a chip appears that the list has no rows for (\"No orders\nmatch this filter\").\n\nAlso stops a stale selection from staying applied invisibly: when the\nscope changes and the selected rule is no longer offered, the chip row\nfalls back to the baseline instead of leaving a filter active with no\nchip showing it.\n\n**Requires the matching `vc-module-sales-rep` PR\nhttps://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-module-sales-rep/pull/9, which adds\nthe `organizationId` / `period` arguments — merge after, or together\nwith, the module release.\n\n**Behavior**\n- **`useSalesRepRules(domain, kind, scope?)`** — the third argument\ncarries the scope: `{ organizationId, periodFrom, periodTo }`, each a\nvalue, ref or getter. Option values are expanded rather than\n`MaybeRefOrGetter<… | undefined>`, matching `useSalesRepOrders` and\nkeeping Sonar S4782 quiet. Surfaces with a static vocabulary (sort\nrules, customer segments) pass nothing and are unaffected.\n- **Recent Orders** (`sales-rep-orders.vue`) passes its `organizationId`\nand period, so the status chips on a customer page reflect that customer\nwhile the dashboard reflects the rep''s whole book.\n- **Top Sellers** (`top-sellers.vue`) passes its `organizationId` and\nperiod (year-to-date), so the category chips are the categories sold\ninto in that window.\n- **A vanished selection resets** (`sales-rep-rule-chips.vue`) — if the\nselected rule is absent from the offered rules, the model falls back to\n`undefined` (the \"All\" baseline). Gated on a `loading` prop so an\nin-flight refetch isn''t mistaken for \"the rule is gone\". Applies to\nevery chip surface at once.\n- **Operations updated:** `SalesRepOrderFilterRules` and\n`SalesRepTopSellerFilterRules` declare and pass `$organizationId`,\n`$periodFrom`, `$periodTo` (`period: { from, to }`, mirroring\n`SalesRepOrders`).\n- **No visual change** — same chips, labels and layout. Statuses unknown\nto the theme (e.g. from an ERP sync) already render correctly:\n`OrderStatus` falls back to `displayValue || status` with a neutral\ncolor.\n\n> **Note (generated types):** `types.ts` was updated **by hand** —\nvariables, `Query…Args`, and the two document ASTs (produced with the\n`graphql` parser rather than hand-written JSON) — because `yarn\ngenerate:graphql-types` diverges in this repo and needs a backend that\nalready exposes the new arguments. ⚠️ Running codegen against a backend\n**without** the module update will drop `organizationId` / `period`\nagain and the operations will then fail schema validation; regenerate\nonly after the module is deployed.\n\n## References\n### Jira-link:\nhttps://virtocommerce.atlassian.net/browse/VCST-5590\n### Artifact URL:\n\nhttps://vc3prerelease.blob.core.windows.net/packages/vc-theme-b2b-vue-2.56.0-pr-2409-be59-be59212a.zip\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Aleksandra-Mitricheva <54628043+Aleksandra-Mitricheva@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"73a8c0c0cd944fe31614b235e1f5ac59a81a1477","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/trees/73a8c0c0cd944fe31614b235e1f5ac59a81a1477"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/VirtoCommerce/vc-frontend/git/commits/af7db0802de6654f92a4587cd24612397f572b8f","verification":{"payload":"tree 73a8c0c0cd944fe31614b235e1f5ac59a81a1477\nparent 42d5faaf5a3d967ffa2c34fabc3c7c4bc69394e5\nauthor yuskithedeveloper <126832118+yuskithedeveloper@users.noreply.github.com> 1786537235 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786537235 -0500\n\nVCST-5590: Dashboard statuses and categories filter (#2409)\n\n## Description\nSends the **list''s own scope** to the sales-rep filter-rule discovery\nqueries, so the chip rows match the records on screen. The backend\nvocabularies are now data-derived (the statuses/categories that actually\nexist in the records being shown), which only holds if the storefront\nasks for them with the same `organizationId` and `period` its list uses\n— otherwise a chip appears that the list has no rows for (\"No orders\nmatch this filter\").\n\nAlso stops a stale selection from staying applied invisibly: when the\nscope changes and the selected rule is no longer offered, the chip row\nfalls back to the baseline instead of leaving a filter active with no\nchip showing it.\n\n**Requires the matching `vc-module-sales-rep` PR\nhttps://github.com/VirtoCommerce/vc-module-sales-rep/pull/9, which adds\nthe `organizationId` / `period` arguments — merge after, or together\nwith, the module release.\n\n**Behavior**\n- **`useSalesRepRules(domain, kind, scope?)`** — the third argument\ncarries the scope: `{ organizationId, periodFrom, periodTo }`, each a\nvalue, ref or getter. Option values are expanded rather than\n`MaybeRefOrGetter<… | undefined>`, matching `useSalesRepOrders` and\nkeeping Sonar S4782 quiet. Surfaces with a static vocabulary (sort\nrules, customer segments) pass nothing and are unaffected.\n- **Recent Orders** (`sales-rep-orders.vue`) passes its `organizationId`\nand period, so the status chips on a customer page reflect that customer\nwhile the dashboard reflects the rep''s whole book.\n- **Top Sellers** (`top-sellers.vue`) passes its `organizationId` and\nperiod (year-to-date), so the category chips are the categories sold\ninto in that window.\n- **A vanished selection resets** (`sales-rep-rule-chips.vue`) — if the\nselected rule is absent from the offered rules, the model falls back to\n`undefined` (the \"All\" baseline). Gated on a `loading` prop so an\nin-flight refetch isn''t mistaken for \"the rule is gone\". Applies to\nevery chip surface at once.\n- **Operations updated:** `SalesRepOrderFilterRules` and\n`SalesRepTopSellerFilterRules` declare and pass `$organizationId`,\n`$periodFrom`, `$periodTo` (`period: { from, to }`, mirroring\n`SalesRepOrders`).\n- **No visual change** — same chips, labels and layout. Statuses unknown\nto the theme (e.g. from an ERP sync) already render correctly:\n`OrderStatus` falls back to `displayValue || status` with a neutral\ncolor.\n\n> **Note (generated types):** `types.ts` was updated **by hand** —\nvariables, `Query…Args`, and the two document ASTs (produced with the\n`graphql` parser rather than hand-written JSON) — because `yarn\ngenerate:graphql-types` diverges in this repo and needs a backend that\nalready exposes the new arguments. ⚠️ Running codegen against a backend\n**without** the 