s","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/navikt/esyfovarsel/commits/bf591720742dc5f557b98a0b75dd7a419008de0d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T14:38:20Z","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dependabot[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T14:38:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(deps): bump io.netty:netty-handler from 4.2.17.Final to 4.2.18.Final (#1103)\n\nBumps [io.netty:netty-handler](https://github.com/netty/netty) from\n4.2.17.Final to 4.2.18.Final.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/releases\">io.netty:netty-handler''s\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>netty-4.2.18.Final</h2>\n<h2>Security fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-rmcw-9fcq-wjq7\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: unbounded resource usage in <code>io.netty:netty-codec-http</code>\n(SPDY)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-pvjx-v7vp-62vq\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: unbounded resource usage in <code>io.netty:netty-codec-http</code>\n(HTTP/1.1)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-8352-h356-c9qh\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: denial of service vector in\n<code>io.netty:netty-codec-http2</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-jj3c-mwvr-9g52\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: improper certificate validation in\n<code>io.netty:netty-handler-ssl-ocsp</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-ghg5-c4jg-8q5j\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: memory leak in <code>io.netty:netty-codec-stomp</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-2g37-3h88-55hc\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: unbounded resource usage in\n<code>io.netty:netty-codec-http</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-q9pg-8h3j-8hvm\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: improper header validation in\n<code>io.netty:netty-codec-http3</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-hmf3-49g9-g7qq\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: denial of service vector in\n<code>io.netty:netty-codec-stomp</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-wxrh-4rgq-pjcg\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: parser desync/response smuggling in\n<code>io.netty:netty-codec-memcache</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-495p-pchh-r4mc\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: unbounded resource usage in\n<code>io.netty:netty-codec-http3</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-v5p2-hmgx-3xrx\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: unbounded resource usage in\n<code>io.netty:netty-codec-http3</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-f64r-x647-cg8w\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: unbounded resource usage in\n<code>io.netty:netty-codec-http3</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-hcvj-94mj-jp5c\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: improper header validation in\n<code>io.netty:netty-codec-http</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-pq4x-537v-r54q\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: unbounded resource usage in\n<code>io.netty:netty-codec-smtp</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-j58c-g352-8h4p\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: memory leak in <code>io.netty:netty-codec-haproxy</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-h75q-xqrh-59rf\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: request smuggling in <code>io.netty:netty-codec-http</code>\n(RTSP)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-rq4j-fc47-9698\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: request smuggling in <code>io.netty:netty-codec-http</code>\n(HTTP/1)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-45h4-vhwh-fmhg\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: improper header validation in\n<code>io.netty:netty-codec-http2</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-jgph-cgq3-c627\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: improper header validation in <code>io.netty:netty-codec-http</code>\n(HTTP/1)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-hfr2-x62w-v49h\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: improper header validation in\n<code>io.netty:netty-codec-http3</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-w6j8-x45j-w75f\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: improper header validation in <code>io.netty:netty-codec-http3</code>\nand in <code>io.netty:netty-codec-http2</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-cg2g-fxr4-mg8m\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: improper header validation in\n<code>io.netty:netty-codec-http2</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-mj35-3qqm-q387\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: improper hostname verification in\n<code>io.netty:netty-codec-classes-quic</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-r4xx-7fpg-j8xg\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: unbounded resource usage in\n<code>io.netty:netty-codec-redis</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-3jrc-fchc-59pw\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: improper header validation in <code>io.netty:netty-codec-http</code>\n(HTTP/1.1)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-j4mg-hqgv-34qc\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: request smuggling vector in <code>io.netty:netty-codec-http</code>\n(HTTP/1.1)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-jqf3-r9ww-c5x8\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: unbounded resource usage in\n<code>io.netty:netty-codec-mqtt</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-5vh9-c45f-rf7p\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: improper CRLF neutralization in\n<code>io.netty:netty-codec-smtp</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-jhjp-5q4f-8wr2\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: improper certificate validation in\n<code>io.netty:netty-handler-ssl-ocsp</code></li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/security/advisories/GHSA-8whp-c7w8-2m72\">CVE-2026-XXXXX</a>\n: improper header validation in\n<code>io.netty:netty-codec-http2</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Compatibility Notes</h2>\n<p>A number of security fixes have added additional validation and\nimpose new resource usage limits, which may cause existing workloads to\nfail or be rejected. We recommend that you test your systems thoroughly\nas part of your Netty upgrade.</p>\n<p>Two specific changes are worth calling out:</p>\n<p><strong>QUIC now explicitly requires\n<code>X509ExtendedTrustManager</code> when hostname verification is\nenabled.</strong>\nPreviously, when configuring QUIC with an endpoint identification\nalgorithm and an <code>X509TrustManager</code>, hostname verification\nwould be silently skipped.\nThis is now considered a misconfiguration and an exception will be\nthrown.</p>\n<p><strong>HTTP/2 header <em>value</em> validation is now enabled by\ndefault.</strong>\nHTTP/2 header <em>name</em> validation has always been enabled by\ndefault, with an option to disable it, but HTTP/2 header <em>value</em>\nvalidation has been disabled by default until now. Configuration options\nstill exist to disable this, but validation of HTTP header names and\nvalues are now both opt-in by default rather than opt-out.</p>\n<h2>What''s Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Use X509ExtendedTrustManager in SSLErrorTest by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/normanmaurer\"><code>@​normanmaurer</code></a>\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/netty/netty/pull/17221\">netty/netty#17221</a></li>\n<li>Update setup-testlens to v1.9.4 by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/marcphilipp\"><code>@​marcphilipp</code></a> in\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/netty/netty/pull/17223\">netty/netty#17223</a></li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/commit/2521f494432e27415a567d3a81a9eb907abf20b3\"><code>2521f49</code></a>\n[maven-release-plugin] prepare release netty-4.2.18.Final</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/commit/6fd53272cbce5c461b8b4e15101687fedce30fd7\"><code>6fd5327</code></a>\nHTTP/1 absolute-form Host mismatch is translated to HTTP/3 :authority,\noverri...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/commit/c44a052228bc4e5aa816686a6628410f037dad7c\"><code>c44a052</code></a>\nSPDY: SpdySessionHandler must limit the concurrent streams</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/commit/374d965d6f7f63318adcddbb474c0d5198bfaa53\"><code>374d965</code></a>\nHTTP: Limit the maximum number of concurrent pipelined requests</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/commit/7e8b325cd2d5dc04eaa5a0c13ebfec173b9bedf7\"><code>7e8b325</code></a>\nHTTP/2: Limit HPACK encoding table size</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/commit/e3ebf70348918febe7cda9bfa1c0ee040a157c07\"><code>e3ebf70</code></a>\nOCSP: Correctly handle that <code>nextUpdate</code> is optional</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/commit/5388535e1d0c285b6081f53c054bee0e6536a610\"><code>5388535</code></a>\nSTOMP: Correctly release partial content on handler removal</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/commit/3a80f5a3b1f3fdc14e5269c27aac0d67075db245\"><code>3a80f5a</code></a>\nWebSockets: Enforce a limit for the max pipelined requests in\nWebSocketServer...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/commit/1b6ea48c89a32f36edbc717861580bc563389b63\"><code>1b6ea48</code></a>\nHTTP3: Correctly handle &quot;:authority&quot; and &quot;host&quot;\nheaders</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/commit/3630659c817e848e4cc4f11703dc36adc80d537a\"><code>3630659</code></a>\nSTOMP codec content-length long-to-int truncation causes infinite decode\nloop...</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/netty/netty/compare/netty-4.2.17.Final...netty-4.2.18.Final\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=io.netty:netty-handler&package-manager=gradle&previous-version=4.2.17.Final&new-version=4.2.18.Final)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don''t\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or