</code>, the\n<code>put(ILoggingEvent)</code> method now has the protected modifier to\nallow access from derived classes. This change was requested by Thomas\nSkjølberg in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/qos-ch/logback/pull/1053\">pr#1053</a>.</p>\n<p>• Bump SLF4J dependency to version 2.0.18.</p>\n<p>• <strong>See also the overview of the <a\nhref=\"https://logback.qos.ch/news.html#latest_stable\">1.6.x\nseries</a>.</strong></p>\n<p>• A bit-wise identical binary of this version can be reproduced by\nbuilding from source code at commit\nb07adf36019b51a10f824fdd94009985c587b1d3 associated with the tag\nv_1.6.0. The release was built using Java &quot;21&quot; 2023-10-17 LTS\nbuild 21.0.1.+12-LTS-29 under Linux Debian 11.6.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/qos-ch/logback/commit/b07adf36019b51a10f824fdd94009985c587b1d3\"><code>b07adf3</code></a>\nsynronized logback-access with future 2.0.14</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/qos-ch/logback/commit/8381cdc3b3202a33293092dbd6cbf905a6235ac2\"><code>8381cdc</code></a>\nprepare release 1.6.0</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/qos-ch/logback/commit/15db759d78e7f694b6b1a53485d041c8415c8a8f\"><code>15db759</code></a>\nnotes on removed deprecated classes, methods and variables.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/qos-ch/logback/commit/90ced5a15f1a288b87bf64071081a8a5206da03b\"><code>90ced5a</code></a>\nrevert removal of support for packaing data</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/qos-ch/logback/commit/64c5d3fcf9f97c88a3efd6cf9d7ee24f42dafd63\"><code>64c5d3f</code></a>\nPackaging data is no longer supported. It was rarely used.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/qos-ch/logback/commit/54740446b227e52215210e11b0195d9f43564d21\"><code>5474044</code></a>\nfix failing tests</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/qos-ch/logback/commit/ac484c2fd453adcc69b7e36cc46b39e682c29c97\"><code>ac484c2</code></a>\nin version 1.6.x target JDK 11</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/qos-ch/logback/commit/01eaa90c4cca5a9c8245347a54aaad7b704a3194\"><code>01eaa90</code></a>\nstart work on version 1.6.0-SNAPSHOT</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/qos-ch/logback/commit/d5e658cd30f2513c508ebc0cf005f5a011a5748b\"><code>d5e658c</code></a>\nAllow subclasses to use put(ILoggingEvent) by making method access\nprotected</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/qos-ch/logback/commit/94ba1a07acb6ebfa15043c1bbf701b4c3a634616\"><code>94ba1a0</code></a>\nimprove message in case of version mismatch</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/qos-ch/logback/compare/v_1.5.38...v_1.6.0\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=ch.qos.logback:logback-classic&package-manager=gradle&previous-version=1.5.38&new-version=1.6.0)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don''t\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot crea