a938fffa8"}],"sha":"93dd14730bbf80de4b9c3fb6837dfd310116ad7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-account-creation-notification/commits/93dd14730bbf80de4b9c3fb6837dfd310116ad7f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-account-creation-notification/commits/865962ab35c44d52bf0f9e968b04598a938fffa8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-20T17:31:07Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-20T17:31:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Harden JCR account-creation-notification: security, accessibility, tests, Sonar gate (#12)\n\n* fix: apply CRIT/HIGH/MEDIUM backend fixes for JCR account creation notification\n\nCRIT-2 (torn read): Replace 4 volatile fields in JcrAccountCreationNotificationConfig\nwith a single volatile reference to an immutable static-final-inner-class Snapshot.\nGetters read the snapshot reference once, so JCR observation threads never see a\nmix of fields from two different config updates.\n\nM-1 (stale values on config delete): updated(null) now resets to DEFAULT_SNAPSHOT\ninstead of returning early, so stale recipient/sender/subject/body are never served\nafter a configuration deletion.\n\nH-7 (shared constants): Add PID and EMAIL_PATTERN as public static final members\non JcrAccountCreationNotificationConfig. Listener and mutation extension both\nreference EMAIL_PATTERN from the single source; PID replaces the duplicated magic\nstring in the mutation extension and the @Component property.\n\nCRIT-1 (misleading service type): Change @Component(service = JcrAccountCreationListener.class)\nto service = {} — the component is immediate and self-registers as a JCR EventListener\nin @Activate; it publishes no OSGi service.\n\nH-3/H-5 (volatile fields): Declare observationSession, config, and mailService as\nvolatile in JcrAccountCreationListener. Add ReferencePolicy.STATIC to both @Reference\nbindings so the component is stopped/restarted on any dependency change.\n\nH-4 (broad catch in onEvent): Widen catch(RepositoryException) to catch(Exception)\nwith log-and-continue so an unexpected RuntimeException never escapes to the JCR\nobservation manager and silently deregisters the listener.\n\nH-2 (narrow catch in mutation): Replace catch(Exception) with catch(IOException)\nin MutationExtension.saveSettings — IOException is the only checked exception\nConfigurationAdmin.getConfiguration and config.update declare; RuntimeExceptions\nnow propagate correctly instead of being silently swallowed.\n\nM-2 (subject/body reset): Apply the same remove-when-empty logic to subject and body\nin MutationExtension.saveSettings so all four fields can be cleared back to defaults\n(previously empty subject/body were silently ignored and the old value stayed in the\npersisted configuration file).\n\nFix 9 (BundleUtils comment): Add class-level Javadoc to both GraphQL extensions\nexplaining why BundleUtils.getOsgiService is used instead of @Reference — graphql-dxm\ninstantiates extension classes outside the OSGi DS container.\n\nTests: add Mockito 4.11.0 to pom.xml test scope. Add two new JUnit 4 test classes:\n- JcrAccountCreationNotificationConfigTest: updated() binding, null-dict reset,\n  partial keys, snapshot atomicity, PID constant value.\n- JcrAccountCreationListenerBehaviourTest: handleUserCreation happy path (mail sent\n  with HTML-escaped variables), no-configured-sender falls back to MailService default,\n  invalid recipient skips notification, null recipient+default skips notification,\n  mail disabled returns early without consuming events, RuntimeException in\n  handleUserCreation does not propagate to the observation manager.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: resolve SonarQube quality-gate issues S3077, S3776, S5853, S1130, S125\n\nS3077 (JcrAccountCreationListener): add @SuppressWarnings(\"java:S3077\") at class\nlevel — volatile fields are a deliberate safe-publication idiom for OSGi bind/\nactivate → JCR observation thread visibility; volatile must not be removed.\n\nS3077 (JcrAccountCreationNotificationConfig): same suppression on the class —\nvolatile Snapshot reference is a single-write, immutable-read pattern that\neliminates torn reads between the CM thread and the observation thread.\n\nS3776 (JcrAccountCreationNotificationMutationExtension): reduce cognitive\ncomplexity of saveSettings from 17 to ≤15 by extracting putOrRemove(Dictionary,\nString, String) helper; all four put/remove blocks replaced with helper calls.\nValidation, permission, and exception behaviour unchanged.\n\nS5853 (JcrAccountCreationListenerBehaviourTest): merge five consecutive\nassertThat(sentBody) calls into a single AssertJ fluent chain.\n\nS1130 (JcrAccountCreationListenerBehaviourTest ×2): remove unnecessary\n`throws Exception` from onEvent_mailDisabled_doesNotSendAnyMail and\nonEvent_runtimeExceptionInHandleUserCreation_doesNotPropagateToObservationManager\n— neither method throws a checked exception.\n\nS125 (JcrAccountCreationListenerBehaviourTest): commented-out code block already\nabsent in current source; no change required.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: harden admin UI accessibility, i18n, and add jest + cypress coverage\n\n- React admin panel: replace onCompleted-render anti-pattern with effect + init\n  guard, double-submit guard, hint before CKEditor, accessible toolbar label,\n  editor language from i18n, role=alert error + persistent live regions\n- Extract reusable emailValidation helper with unit coverage\n- Add French (fr.json) locale alongside en.json\n- Add jest config, mocks, and frontend tests (emailValidation, admin panel)\n- Add permission-enforcement Cypress spec; tidy existing spec\n- Reword a test section comment to satisfy Sonar S125\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* refactor: address PR review findings (concurrency, a11y, logging)\n\nBackend:\n- Listener reads the config Snapshot once via getSnapshot() instead of four\n  separate volatile getter calls, making the single-read invariant real\n- onEvent breaks out of the batch on RepositoryException (dead session) instead\n  of flooding ERROR logs per remaining event; other runtime errors still\n  log-and-continue\n- GraphQL subject/body descriptions document the empty=reset-to-default contract\n- Add test for onEvent early-return when observationSession is null\n\nFrontend:\n- Remove console.error from the save catch path (error already surfaced via the\n  live-region alert)\n- Stabilise editorConfig useMemo (depend on derived toolbar label, not the\n  unstable t function) to avoid CKEditor remounts\n- Document the initialisedRef hydration contract (no refetchQueries without reset)\n- Mark decorative status icons aria-hidden\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: make onEvent loop tests exercise the loop + cover RepositoryException break\n\n- Add a package-private setObservationSession test seam so behaviour tests run\n  onEvent past the not-registered guard (the loop tests were previously vacuous)\n- Inject a mock session in setUp; existing mail-disabled / runtime-exception\n  tests now genuinely exercise their branches\n- Add a test for the RepositoryException -> break path (asserts the batch stops\n  and the second event is never consumed)\n- Drop dead individual-getter stubs (handleUserCreation reads only getSnapshot())\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"3d3ad5de7cc3b4dcdff8bdca3f1b0feb52b3c33f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-account-creation-notification/git/trees/3d3ad5de7cc3b4dcdff8bdca3f1b0feb52b3c33f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-account-creation-notification/git/commits/865962ab35c44d52bf0f9e968b04598a938fffa8","verification":{"payload":"tree 3d3ad5de7cc3b4dcdff8bdca3f1b0feb52b3c33f\nparent 0c98c3a36ec36b215177067ee2266d63bd287b55\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781976667 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781976667 +0200\n\nHarden JCR account-creation-notification: security, accessibility, tests, Sonar gate (#12)\n\n* fix: apply CRIT/HIGH/MEDIUM backend fixes for JCR account creation notification\n\nCRIT-2 (torn read): Replace 4 volatile fields in JcrAccountCreationNotificationConfig\nwith a single volatile reference to an immutable static-final-inner-class Snapshot.\nGetters read the snapshot reference once, so JCR observation threads never see a\nmix of fields from two different config updates.\n\nM-1 (stale values on config delete): updated(null) now resets to DEFAULT_SNAPSHOT\ninstead of returning early, so stale recipient/sender/subject/body are never served\nafter a configuration deletion.\n\nH-7 (shared constants): Add PID and EMAIL_PATTERN as public static final members\non JcrAccountCreationNotificationConfig. Listener and mutation extension both\nreference EMAIL_PATTERN from the single source; PID replaces the duplicated magic\nstring in the mutation extension and the @Component property.\n\nCRIT-1 (misleading service type): Change @Component(service = JcrAccountCreationListener.class)\nto service = {} — the component is immediate and self-registers as a JCR EventListener\nin @Activate; it publishes no OSGi service.\n\nH-3/H-5 (volatile fields): Declare observationSession, config, and mailService as\nvolatile in JcrAccountCreationListener. Add ReferencePolicy.STATIC to both @Reference\nbindings so the component is stopped/restarted on any dependency change.\n\nH-4 (broad catch in onEvent): Widen catch(RepositoryException) to catch(Exception)\nwith log-and-continue so an unexpected RuntimeException never escapes to the JCR\nobservation manager and silently deregisters the listener.\n\nH-2 (narrow catch in mutation): Replace catch(Exception) with catch(IOException)\nin MutationExtension.saveSettings — IOException is the only checked exception\nConfigurationAdmin.getConfiguration and config.update declare; RuntimeExceptions\nnow propagate correctly instead of being silently swallowed.\n\nM-2 (subject/body reset): Apply the same remove-when-empty logic to subject and body\nin MutationExtension.saveSettings so all four fields can be cleared back to defaults\n(previously empty subject/body were silently ignored and the old value stayed in the\npersisted configuration file).\n\nFix 9 (BundleUtils comment): Add class-level Javadoc to both GraphQL extensions\nexplaining why BundleUtils.getOsgiService is used instead of @Reference — graphql-dxm\ninstantiates extension classes outside the OSGi DS container.\n\nTests: add Mockito 4.11.0 to pom.xml test scope. Add two new JUnit 4 test classes:\n- JcrAccountCreationNotificationConfigTest: updated() binding, null-dict reset,\n  partial keys, snapshot atomicity, PID constant value.\n- JcrAccountCreationListenerBehaviourTest: handleUserCreation happy path (mail sent\n  with HTML-escaped variables), no-configured-sender falls back to MailService default,\n  invalid recipient skips notification, null recipient+default skips notification,\n  mail disabled returns early without consuming events, RuntimeException in\n  handleUserCreation does not propagate to the observation manager.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: resolve SonarQube quality-gate issues S3077, S3776, S5853, S1130, S125\n\nS3077 (JcrAccountCreationListener): add @SuppressWarnings(\"java:S3077\") at class\nlevel — volatile fields are a deliberate safe-publication idiom for OSGi bind/\nactivate → JCR observation thread visibility; volatile must not be removed.\n\nS3077 (JcrAccountCreationNotificationConfig): same suppression on the class —\nvolatile Snapshot reference is a single-write, immutable-read pattern that\neliminates torn reads between the CM thread and the observation thread.\n\nS3776 (JcrAccountCreationNotificationMutationExtension): reduce cognitive\ncomplexity of saveSettings from 17 to ≤15 by extracting putOrRemove(Dictionary,\nString, String) helper; all four put/remove blocks replaced with helper calls.\nValidation, permission, and exception behaviour unchanged.\n\nS5853 (JcrAccountCreationListenerBehaviourTest): merge five consecutive\nassertThat(sentBody) calls into a single AssertJ fluent chain.\n\nS1130 (JcrAccountCreationListenerBehaviourTest ×2): remove unnecessary\n`throws Exception` from onEvent_mailDisabled_doesNotSendAnyMail and\nonEvent_runtimeExceptionInHandleUserCreation_doesNotPropagateToObservationManager\n— neither method throws a checked exception.\n\nS125 (JcrAccountCreationListenerBehaviourTest): commented-out code block already\nabsent in current source; no change required.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* feat: harden admin UI accessibility, i18n, and add jest + cypress coverage\n\n- React admin panel: replace onCompleted-render anti-pattern with effect + init\n  guard, double-submit guard, hint before CKEditor, accessible toolbar label,\n  editor language from i18n, role=alert error + persistent live regions\n- Extract reusable emailValidation helper with unit coverage\n- Add French (fr.json) locale alongside en.json\n- Add jest config, mocks, and frontend tests (emailValidation, admin panel)\n- Add permission-enforcement Cypress spec; tidy existing spec\n- Reword a test section comment to satisfy Sonar S125\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* refactor: address PR review findings (concurrency, a11y, logging)\n\nBackend:\n- Listener reads the config Snapshot once via getSnapshot() instead of four\n  separate volatile getter calls, making the single-read invariant real\n- onEvent breaks out of the batch on RepositoryException (dead session) instead\n  of flooding ERROR logs per remaining event; other runtime errors still\n  log-and-continue\n- GraphQL subject/body descriptions document the empty=reset-to-default contract\n- Add test for onEvent early-return when observationSession is null\n\nFrontend:\n- Remove console.error from the save catch path (error already surfaced via the\n  live-region alert)\n- Stabilise editorConfig useMemo (depend on derived toolbar label, not the\n  unstable t function) to avoid CKEditor remounts\n- Document the initialisedRef hydration contract (no refetchQueries without reset)\n- Mark decorative status icons aria-hidden\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: make onEvent loop tests exercise the loop + cover RepositoryException break\n\n- Add a package-private setObservationSession test seam so behaviour tests run\n  onEvent past the not-registered guard (the loop tests were previously vacuous)\n- Inject a mock session in setUp; existing mail-disabled / runtime-exception\n  tests now genuinely exercise their branches\n- Add a test for the RepositoryException -> break path (asserts the batch stops\n  and the second event is never consumed)\n- Drop dead individual-getter stubs (handleUserCreation reads only getSnapshot())\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNs5bCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4X8QAC8gcaB20Ku/shlGwemT1ERn\n8rjWvI4ZAYwzLWG6F2KTKTL2TiWnE483SuE0ZgL0Ks7oHm6h1Rqy9P+RIqypg0Lc\n62D/TupgQk/7zHddtYuKnU6qWGHKkKJJ2wgjR4/u9cRs/ilZ3b+dJdTquJ2t0CyS\nn14W7YOWx+AiMqhBaszfmEiFWyJi8+nBf7D83kOLFkptKKMzcbwOfJz7QjGjd6da\nqO/xgnkpjstHnb+aJ1hcG/MEdluAqaL1kB/f/jHgg0CrQ8ETl06TjtN1Yz6ySh+9\n5eN0UnFjRgLiadCfkqi6zRauIPOzJSv9w2zpJRpkegpqoUFnaCHbmO68Pq/XaayX\nvqrs52uSLOgXnh5cvyykFjb1NEDo8gj68ft9O+32ly5PYlDnwwTcw6n2auTaQLMt\n+lppAMDbP5NzREz6QLW8GrlS02R06ONK2LAXbTBMwM9foKjiR+dLt4VkjL21Ssqb\njSoB3+2wYqFkIiytlDk+PGu3/lcle1bglwHpxfMXc1hSIHAiA0arpKw/CX4J5oYa\nXLdt9W6cH5oep+qHjK4MLmUBU8CskeF1WMpKWwOnxqRp8XzkTqk8Hv+ZfrUVwCLE\nG0h4D3gVIVkG57ULkxWM0QbZ/aw5JQAFErFJqDOsM7ZwuIsQlLRpWmoEQdYu9uvG\nM0hRbnAlhj0n4uduDBl4\n=g1g9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-20T17:31:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcr-account-creation-notification/commit/865962ab35c44d52bf0f9e968b04598a938fffa8","node_id":"C_kwDOEkKlytoAKDg2NTk2MmFiMzVjNDRkNTJiZjBmOWU5NjhiMDQ1OThhOTM4ZmZmYTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcr-account-creation-notification/commit/0c98c3a36ec36b215177067ee2266d63bd287b55","sha":"0c98c3a36ec36b215177067ee2266d63bd287b55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-account-creation-notification/commits/0c98c3a36ec36b215177067ee2266d63bd287b55"}],"sha":"865962ab35c44d52bf0f9e968b04598a938fffa8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-account-creation-notification/commits/865962ab35c44d52bf0f9e968b04598a938fffa8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-account-creation-notification/commits/0c98c3a36ec36b215177067ee2266d63bd287b55/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-10T19:06:30Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-10T19:06:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: add fine-grained permission regression tests + assignable admin role (#11)\n\nAdds a regression suite that locks in the fine-grained\njcrAccountCreationNotificationAdmin gate across the stack:\n\n- GraphQL: a user with only the module permission can read the gated\n  jcrAccountCreationNotificationSettings query; a user without it is\n  denied (Permission denied).\n- Admin UI: the /jahia/administration/jcrAccountCreationNotification\n  panel is shown to the granted user and hidden from the denied user.\n\nShips an assignable server role\n''jcr-account-creation-notification-administrator''\n(src/main/import/roles.xml) granting administrationAccess +\njcrAccountCreationNotificationAdmin, so the permission can be delegated\nwithout full server-admin rights.\n\nThe allowed user is granted only this role (never ''admin''), proving\ntrue fine-grained granularity. No inner hardcoded admin check exists in\nthe resolvers (annotation resolves on the JCR root node), so no Java\nrelaxation was required.\n\nBumps module version 2.0.2-SNAPSHOT -> 2.0.3-SNAPSHOT so the role import\nis re-imported on deploy.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"c1cf393f0688f9a14ccbc63d67937c1e545a3da2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-account-creation-notification/git/trees/c1cf393f0688f9a14ccbc63d67937c1e545a3da2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcr-account-creation-notification/git/commits/0c98c3a36ec36b215177067ee2266d63bd287b55","verification":{"payload":"tree c1cf393f0688f9a14ccbc63d67937c1e545a3da2\nparent 195d4051fa0d98fdc15dcebfbff6b8b3fb51261d\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781118390 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781118390 +0200\n\ntest: add fine-grained permission regression tests + assignable admin role (#11)\n\nAdds a regression suite that locks in the fine-grained\njcrAccountCreationNotificationAdmin gate across the stack:\n\n- GraphQL: a user with only the module permission can read the gated\n  jcrAccountCreationNotificationSettings query; a user without it is\n  denied (Permission denied).\n- Admin UI: the /jahia/administration/jcrAccountCreationNotification\n  panel is shown to the granted user and hidden from the denied user.\n\nShips an assignable server role\n''jcr-account-creation-notification-administrator''\n(src/main/import/roles.xml) granting administrationAccess +\njcrAccountCreationNotificationAdmin, so the permission can be delegated\nwithout full server-admin rights.\n\nThe allowed user is granted only this role (never ''admin''), proving\ntrue fine-grained granularity. No inner hardcoded admin check exists in\nthe resolvers (annotation resolves on the JCR root node), so no Java\nrelaxation was required.\n\nBumps module version 2.0.2-SNAPSHOT -> 2.0.3-SNAPSHOT so the role import\nis re-imported on deploy.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKbW2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASJAQAFoYOiG5e9xnx6/VtCwaw0Nl\nXl37R6q2jWg+fYWNBeR27ezOHJhu+Zle+XtnIINFmptuItafECQHjeSzS36fmV1i\nWqNiEx3ks6/vLr5gRCqFJsK+VBQA/WXFeHKATxRqpKu+Ho+VK8PMGbFmwjrPtLng\nZE0wV2H4R4iAgEELGiQCMjUAydn1Dgt6hegl326zF5BGoSR0W3FcDoLHbSBnVf5K\nICv/Hf+TCki8J0H4jYQm/F+LcPTg7VEIn9j/PKAW5/jlAAGEqUOUk9YyswlPjvp0\nEIM+jcH/yJ0O45ZnlzyjQg4jA6XrDchubrsv/qveHiHgodQ4lsHbQKAwPzEKzACY\nNSr7bfJRQsL1fortbr8dcCKfKIqM7iS+o0XwVosyqFM6O8LBG3C8mhqmsApWIZyW\nL8kQhFqepUp9oHFcx9LILEve/ELhfRp1aS4NXgtSEBMItSYQylFFlkrzmnD19Uja\n2A9CDFLdInaazluS0GNP50w5AFsWfZkUPqWRsVkTDdh0HCckZI5BwzWmLFvESYGi\nGiJGeg2CkrF6Du3suTzILwuL+xqVcyamz5YgScRDAFgF3pVCi9GehceNxMs/Kjxu\ni0FkuVrZAJHU6KC5ta9bKNWTRYlXQ23naVG14GETP1AhPA9HrcZUhzJIzRBNrehw\noXYGBBHw8LoNhJt7+GtK\n=0ajP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-10T19:06:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_ur